setupEmacs
**********

  * Usage: 
        setupEmacs()
  * Consequences:
      * The initialization file for Emacs (.emacs in your home directory) will
        have lines added to allow the Macaulay2 Emacs mode to operate. The user
        is prompted before the file is modified and offered the opportunity to
        review or reject the change.

Description
===========

A backup files is made carefully, and if a mangled initialization file is
detected, it will not be modified. The lines added are bracketed by comment
lines containing the phrases Macaulay 2 start and Macaulay 2 end.

The function *note setup: setup, does all this and more.

See also
========

  * *note setup: setup,

Ways to use setupEmacs:
=======================

  * "setupEmacs()"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note setupEmacs: setupEmacs, is a *note method function:
MethodFunction,.

