+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : headlines about firstFunction                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = 0.  "FirstPackage :: firstFunction"       -- a silly first function     |
|     1.  "FirstPackage :: firstFunction(ZZ)"   -- a silly first function     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : help 0                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = FirstPackage::firstFunction -- a silly first function                   |
|     *****************************************************                   |
|                                                                             |
|       * Usage:                                                              |
|             firstFunction n                                                 |
|       * Inputs:                                                             |
|           * n, an "integer",                                                |
|       * Outputs:                                                            |
|           * a "string", a silly string, depending on the value of n         |
|                                                                             |
|     Here we show an example.                                                |
|                                                                             |
|     +------------------------+                                              |
|     |  i1 : firstFunction 1  |                                              |
|     |                        |                                              |
|     |  o1 = Hello World!     |                                              |
|     +------------------------+                                              |
|     |  i2 : firstFunction 0  |                                              |
|     |                        |                                              |
|     |  o2 = D'oh!            |                                              |
|     +------------------------+                                              |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                                                             |
|     The source of this document is in FirstPackage.m2:53:0.                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This is also true for a list of symbols generated using the function *note
apropos: apropos,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : headlines apropos "hilbert"                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = 0.  "Polyhedra :: hilbertBasis"           --                            |
|     1.  "Macaulay2Doc :: hilbertFunction"     --                            |
|     2.  "Macaulay2Doc :: hilbertPolynomial"   --                            |
|     3.  "Macaulay2Doc :: hilbertSeries"       --                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|computes the Hilbert basis of a Cone                                         |
|the Hilbert function                                                         |
|compute the Hilbert polynomial                                               |
|compute the Hilbert series                                                   |
