help -- view documentation nodes
********************************

Description
===========

Various ways to get help:

+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help                       | -- display the *note initial help: initial help,                            |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help "Macaulay2"           | -- display the top of the documentation tree                                |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help "matrices"            | -- display an overview of matrices in Macaulay2                             |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help X                     | -- display the documentation node whose key is X                            |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help res                   | -- documentation for the function *note res: (Complexes)freeResolution, and |
|                           |ways to use it                                                               |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help(res, Module)          | -- documentation for the method *note resolution(Module):                   |
|                           |(OldChainComplexes)resolution_lpModule_rp,                                   |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help Module                | -- documentation for the type *note Module: Module, and methods that take   |
|                           |one as input                                                                 |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help symbol **             | -- documentation for the operator *note **: _st_st, and its various uses and|
|                           |meanings                                                                     |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help(symbol **, Ring, Ring)| -- documentation for the method *note Ring ** Ring:                         |
|                           |tensor_lpMonoid_cmMonoid_rp,                                                 |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help[gb, DegreeLimit]      | -- documentation for the optional argument *note gb(...,DegreeLimit=>...):  |
|                           |gb,                                                                          |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help methods(map, Module)  | -- documentation for various ways to use the function *note map: map, and a |
|                           |module                                                                       |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help methods(symbol **, T) | -- documentation for various ways to use the operator *note **: _st_st, and |
|                           |an object of class T                                                         |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help methods(X, Y)         | -- documentation for the methods that take an object of class X and an      |
|                           |object of class Y                                                            |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help apropos "hilbert"     | -- documentation about all functions whose name contains the string hilbert |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help about X               | -- documentation nodes from all installed packages whose keys contain X     |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|help about(X, Body => true)| -- documentation nodes from all installed packages whose keys or contents   |
|                           |contain X                                                                    |
+---------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The help command is used to display online documentation, as in the following
suggestions.

+-----------------+
|help             |
+-----------------+
|help ideal       |
+-----------------+
|help(ideal, List)|
+-----------------+

Some other potential help topics:

+----------------------------------------------+
|help "monomial orderings"                     |
+----------------------------------------------+
|help "Gröbner bases"                          |
+----------------------------------------------+
|help "graded and multigraded polynomial rings"|
+----------------------------------------------+

Use *note viewHelp: viewHelp, to display the corresponding documentation in
your web browser.

See also
========

  * *note initial help: initial help, -- Welcome to Macaulay2
  * *note ? Symbol: ? Symbol, -- view brief documentation of a symbol
  * *note viewHelp: viewHelp, -- view online documentation in a web browser
  * *note infoHelp: infoHelp, -- view documentation in Info format
  * *note apropos: apropos, -- symbols matching a pattern
  * *note about: about, -- search the documentation
  * *note code: code, -- display source code
  * *note methods: methods, -- list methods
  * *note examples: examples, -- list the examples in documentation

Ways to use help:
=================

  * "help"
  * "help(ZZ)" -- see *note headlines: headlines, -- display a table of
    documentation headlines
  * "help(Array)"
  * "help(DocumentTag)"
  * "help(List)"
  * "help(Sequence)"
  * "help(String)"
  * "help(Symbol)"
  * "help(Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note help: help, is a *note command: Command,.

