viewHelp -- view online documentation in a web browser
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        viewHelp
        viewHelp X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note thing: Thing,, a descriptor for a documentation node (see
        below for examples)
  * Consequences:
      * The given documentation page is displayed using the function *note
        show: show, which opens the page in the default web browser.
      * If no argument is given to viewHelp, then ~/.Macaulay2/index.html
        opens, which contains a list of all packages installed locally.

Description
===========

Some example uses:

+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|viewHelp                       | -- open the list of local packages and their documentation                |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|viewHelp "Macaulay2"           | -- open the top of the online documentation tree                          |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|viewHelp "matrices"            | -- open an overview of matrices in Macaulay2                              |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|viewHelp X                     | -- open the documentation node whose key is X                             |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|viewHelp ideal                 | -- documentation for the function *note ideal: ideal, and ways to use it  |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|viewHelp(ideal, List)          | -- documentation for the method *note ideal(List): ideal_lpList_rp,       |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|viewHelp[gb, DegreeLimit]      | -- documentation for the optional argument *note gb(...,DegreeLimit=>...):|
|                               |gb,                                                                        |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|viewHelp(symbol **, Ring, Ring)| -- documentation for the method *note Ring ** Ring:                       |
|                               |tensor_lpMonoid_cmMonoid_rp,                                               |
+-------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The *note help: help, command allows other possible arguments, such as help
methods ideal, but for viewHelp the argument must refer to only one web page.
Note that the Safari browser may prevent loading of the style files for the
online documentation.

See also
========

  * *note infoHelp: infoHelp, -- view documentation in Info format
  * *note help: help, -- view documentation nodes
  * *note about: about, -- search the documentation
  * *note apropos: apropos, -- symbols matching a pattern
  * *note makePackageIndex: makePackageIndex, -- create an index of installed
    packages

Ways to use viewHelp:
=====================

  * "viewHelp"
  * "viewHelp(ZZ)" -- see *note headlines: headlines, -- display a table of
    documentation headlines
  * "viewHelp(DocumentTag)"
  * "viewHelp(String)"
  * "viewHelp(Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note viewHelp: viewHelp, is a *note command: Command,.

