? Symbol -- view brief documentation of a symbol
************************************************

  * Operator: *note ?: ?,

Description
===========

A question mark followed by a symbol representing a function, type, option
name, or package prints a brief, compact list of various ways to use the given
symbol.

+-----------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|? BGG      | -- brief information about the package *note BGG: (BGG)Top,                |
+-----------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|? Tally    | -- brief information about ways to use objects of class *note Tally: Tally,|
+-----------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|? betti    | -- brief information about ways to use the function *note betti: betti,    |
+-----------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|? Weights  | -- brief information about ways to use the option *note Weights: Weights,  |
+-----------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|? symbol >>| -- brief information about ways to use the operator *note >>: >>,          |
+-----------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|? HH       | -- brief information about ways to use the scripted functor HH             |
+-----------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If the object is defined by the user, brief information about the object and
its class are printed.

When using Macaulay2 in Emacs, moving the cursor to each line of the output
beginning with '*' and pressing Enter results in showing the full documentation
node corresponding to that line.

See also
========

  * *note initial help: initial help, -- Welcome to Macaulay2
  * *note methods: methods, -- list methods
  * *note help: help, -- view documentation nodes
  * *note code: code, -- display source code
  * *note about: about, -- search the documentation

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "? Function"
  * "? Keyword"
  * "? Package"
  * "? ScriptedFunctor"
  * *note ? Symbol: ? Symbol, -- view brief documentation of a symbol
  * "? Type"
