select(String,String,String) -- select and reformat substrings matching a regular expression
********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note select: select,
  * Usage: 
        select(re, replacement, str)
        select(re, str)
  * Inputs:
      * re, a *note string: String,, a *note regular expression: regular
        expressions, describing a pattern
      * replacement, a *note string: String,, following the *note formatting
        syntax: regular expressions,
      * str, a *note string: String,, a subject string to be searched
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * POSIX => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value false, if true,
        interpret the re using the POSIX Extended flavor, otherwise the Perl
        flavor
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: List,, of mutually exclusive substrings of str matching
        the pattern re; if replacement is given, the matching substrings are
        formatted based on it.

Description
===========

For an introduction to regular expressions, see *note regular expressions:
regular expressions,.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : select("[[:alpha:]]+", "Dog, cat, and deer.")|
|                                                  |
|o1 = {Dog, cat, and, deer}                        |
|                                                  |
|o1 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : select("^.*$", "ABC\nDEF\r\nGHI")            |
|                                                  |
|o2 = {ABC, DEF, GHI}                              |
|                                                  |
|o2 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+

The replacement string may contain *note formatting syntax: regular
expressions, such as backreferences $1 or \\1, which will be replaced by the
string matching the corresponding parenthesized subexpression of re.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : select("([a-zA-Z]+);", "$1", "Dog; cat, deer;")|
|                                                    |
|o3 = {Dog, deer}                                    |
|                                                    |
|o3 : List                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+

Special operators such as the lowercase operator \\L may also be used to
manipulate the replacement substring.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : select("([a-zA-Z]+);", "\\L$1", "Dog; cat, deer;")|
|                                                       |
|o4 = {dog, deer}                                       |
|                                                       |
|o4 : List                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

Lookaheads and lookbehinds can be used to precisely control the regular
expression matches.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : s = "catfish cats dogs";                |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i6 : select("cat(?!fish)s?", s)              |
|                                             |
|o6 = {cats}                                  |
|                                             |
|o6 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i7 : select("\\w+(?=s\\b)", s)               |
|                                             |
|o7 = {cat, dog}                              |
|                                             |
|o7 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i8 : s = "goldfish swordfish catfish catdog";|
+---------------------------------------------+
|i9 : select("\\w+(?=fish)", s)               |
|                                             |
|o9 = {gold, sword, cat}                      |
|                                             |
|o9 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i10 : select("(?<=cat)\\w+", s)              |
|                                             |
|o10 = {fish, dog}                            |
|                                             |
|o10 : List                                   |
+---------------------------------------------+

The POSIX => true option can be used to specify the POSIX Extended flavor for
the regular expression used to match. Note that only the Perl flavor allows the
use of lookaheads and lookbehinds.

See also
========

  * *note regular expressions: regular expressions, -- syntax for regular
    expressions
  * *note strings and nets: strings and nets, -- an overview of strings and
    nets in Macaulay2
  * *note regex: regex, -- evaluate a regular expression search
  * *note separate: separate, -- split a string into substrings using a regular
    expression
  * *note replace(String,String,String): replace_lpString_cmString_cmString_rp,
    -- replace substrings matching a regular expression

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "select(String,String)"
  * *note select(String,String,String): select_lpString_cmString_cmString_rp,
    -- select and reformat substrings matching a regular expression
