concatenate -- join strings
***************************

Description
===========

concatenate(s,t,...,u) yields the concatenation of the strings s,t,...,u.


The arguments may also be lists or sequences of strings and symbols, in which
case they are concatenated recursively.  Additionally, an integer may be used
to represent a number of spaces, and *note null: null, will be represented by
the empty string.
+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : concatenate {"a",("s",3,"d",),"f"}|
|                                       |
|o1 = as   df                           |
+---------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note String: String, -- the class of all strings

