format -- format a string or real number
****************************************

Description
===========

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        format s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: String,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: String,, obtained from s by inserting escape sequences,
        thereby preparing it for printing in a format suitable for reading in
        again
+------------------+
|i1 : s = "a\"b\"c"|
|                  |
|o1 = a"b"c        |
+------------------+
|i2 : t = format s |
|                  |
|o2 = "a\"b\"c"    |
+------------------+
|i3 : u = value t  |
|                  |
|o3 = a"b"c        |
+------------------+
|i4 : u == s       |
|                  |
|o4 = true         |
+------------------+

The characters that are escaped are double quotes, backslashes, and all control
characters (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/control_characters ).  In
particular, the outputted string will be valid JSON (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSON ).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : format(ascii(0..31) | "\"\\")                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = "\u0000\u0001\u0002\u0003\u0004\u0005\u0006\u0007\b\t\n\u000b\f\r\u000e\|
|     u000f\u0010\u0011\u0012\u0013\u0014\u0015\u0016\u0017\u0018\u0019\u001a\|
|     u001b\u001c\u001d\u001e\u001f\"\\"                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        format(s,k,l,t,e,x)
  * Inputs:
      * s, an *note integer: ZZ,, the maximum number of significant decimal
        digits (default: *note printingPrecision: printingPrecision,). The
        special value 0 imposes no limit.
      * k, an *note integer: ZZ,, how far to the right of the decimal point to
        go, at most (default: *note printingAccuracy: printingAccuracy,). The
        special value -1 imposes no limit.
      * l, an *note integer: ZZ,, maximum number of leading zeroes (default:
        *note printingLeadLimit: printingLeadLimit,).
      * t, an *note integer: ZZ,, maximum number of trailing zeroes (default:
        *note printingTrailLimit: printingTrailLimit,)
      * e, a *note string: String,, the separator between the mantissa and the
        exponent (default: *note printingSeparator: printingSeparator,)
      * x, a *note real number: RR,, the number to be converted to a string
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: String,, the decimal representation of the number x,
        prepared according to the parameters above
+------------------------------------+
|i6 : format(10,1/3000.)             |
|                                    |
|o6 = .0003333333333                 |
+------------------------------------+
|i7 : format(10,6,1/3000.)           |
|                                    |
|o7 = .000333                        |
+------------------------------------+
|i8 : format(10,6,2,1/3000.)         |
|                                    |
|o8 = 3.33e-4                        |
+------------------------------------+
|i9 : format(10,300000.)             |
|                                    |
|o9 = 300000                         |
+------------------------------------+
|i10 : format(10,-1,10,5,300000.)    |
|                                    |
|o10 = 300000                        |
+------------------------------------+
|i11 : format(10,-1,10,4,300000.)    |
|                                    |
|o11 = 3e5                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i12 : format(10,-1,10,4,"E",300000.)|
|                                    |
|o12 = 3E5                           |
+------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note toExternalString: toExternalString, -- convert to a readable string

Ways to use format:
===================

  * "format(DocumentTag)" -- see *note DocumentTag: DocumentTag, -- the class
    of all document tags
  * "format(CC)"
  * "format(RR)"
  * "format(String)"

For the programmer
==================

