Net || Net -- join nets or strings vertically
*********************************************

  * Operator: *note ||: ||,

Description
===========

m||n -- joins nets or strings by concatenating them vertically.  The baseline
of the result is the baseline of the first one.


In this example, we build a large net with arrows to indicate the location of
the baseline.
+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : x = "x" | "3"^1                     |
|                                         |
|      3                                  |
|o1 = x                                   |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : "<--- " | ( x || "" || x ) | " --->"|
|                                         |
|           3                             |
|o2 = <--- x  --->                        |
|                                         |
|           3                             |
|          x                              |
+-----------------------------------------+

