BasicList -- the class of all basic lists
*****************************************

Description
===========

For an overview of lists and sequences, see *note lists and sequences: lists
and sequences,.

A basic list is a sequence of expressions indexed by a sequence of consecutive
integers of the form 0, 1, ..., N-1.  The number N is called the length of the
list.


There are various types of basic lists, depending on the application, and they
are displayed in different ways. The types first encountered are those of type
*note VisibleList: VisibleList,, but new types are easy to introduce. In the
following example we introduce a new type of basic list called L.
+------------------------------+
|i1 : L = new Type of BasicList|
|                              |
|o1 = L                        |
|                              |
|o1 : Type                     |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : x = new L from {a,b,c,d} |
|                              |
|o2 = L{a, b, c, d}            |
|                              |
|o2 : L                        |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : join(x,x)                |
|                              |
|o3 = L{a, b, c, d, a, b, c, d}|
|                              |
|o3 : L                        |
+------------------------------+
Here are the core types that inherit from BasicList:
* Menu:

* FilePosition::                the class of all file positions
* Command::                     the class of all commands
* URL::                         a type representing a URL
* RingElement::                 the class of all ring elements handled by the engine
