Command -- the class of all commands
************************************

  * Usage: 
        Command g
  * Inputs:
      * g, a function or a string
  * Outputs:
      * a new command that will evaluate g() if g is a function, and will
        evaluate run g if g is a string

Description
===========

A command behaves as a function does if it is followed by an adjacent
expression that can serve as its argument or argument list.  In addition, if it
appears as the value of an expression typed by the user at top level (i.e., not
in a file), then it gets executed with empty argument list.
+----------------------------------+
|i1 : (f = Command ( () -> 2^30 );)|
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : f                            |
|                                  |
|o2 = 1073741824                   |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : (c = Command "date";)        |
+----------------------------------+
|i4 : c                            |
|Fri Aug  7 01:43:57 UTC 2026      |
|                                  |
|o4 = 0                            |
+----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note run: run, -- run an external command
  * *note AfterEval: AfterEval, -- top level method applied after evaluation

