isUnit -- whether a ring element is a unit
******************************************

  * Usage: 
        isUnit r
  * Inputs:
      * r, a *note ring element: RingElement,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, *note true: true, if the *note ring
        element: RingElement, r generates an ideal containing the
        multiplicative identity 1 and false otherwise

Description
===========

+---------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[z]/(z^2+1);          |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : isUnit z                    |
|                                 |
|o2 = true                        |
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : S = QQ[x,y]/(1-(x-1)*(y-1));|
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : isUnit (x^2 - 2*x + 1)      |
|                                 |
|o4 = true                        |
+---------------------------------+
|i5 : isUnit x                    |
|                                 |
|o5 = false                       |
+---------------------------------+

Ways to use isUnit:
===================

  * "isUnit(Number)"
  * "isUnit(RingElement)"
  * "isUnit(ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isUnit: isUnit, is a *note method function: MethodFunction,.

