leadTerm(RingElement) -- get the greatest term
**********************************************

  * Function: *note leadTerm: leadTerm,
  * Usage: 
        leadTerm f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: RingElement,, in a polynomial ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: RingElement,, the lead term of f

Description
===========

Each polynomial ring comes equipped with a *note monomial ordering: monomial
orderings, and this routine returns the lead (greatest) monomial and its
coefficient. Recall that the default monomial order is the graded reverse
lexicographic order.
+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                     |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : leadTerm (3*b*c^2-d^3-1)          |
|                                       |
|         2                             |
|o2 = 3b*c                              |
|                                       |
|o2 : R                                 |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = QQ[a..d, MonomialOrder => Lex]|
|                                       |
|o3 = S                                 |
|                                       |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                    |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : leadTerm (3*b*c^2-d^3-1)          |
|                                       |
|         2                             |
|o4 = 3b*c                              |
|                                       |
|o4 : S                                 |
+---------------------------------------+
Coefficients are included in the result:
+------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = ZZ[a..d][x,y,z];           |
+------------------------------------+
|i6 : leadTerm((a+b)*y^2 + (b+c)*x*z)|
|                                    |
|             2                      |
|o6 = (a + b)y                       |
|                                    |
|o6 : R                              |
+------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note leadCoefficient: leadCoefficient, -- the coefficient of the leading
    term
  * *note leadMonomial: leadMonomial, -- the leading monomial of a ring element
