factor(RingElement) -- factor a ring element
********************************************

  * Function: *note factor: factor,
  * Usage: 
        factor x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note ring element: RingElement,, or a *note rational number: QQ,
        or an *note integer: ZZ,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note product expression: Product,, the factorization of x

Description
===========

The result is a *note Product: Product, each of whose factors is a *note Power:
Power, whose base is one of the factors found and whose exponent is an integer.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : factor 124744878111332355674003415153753485211381849014286981744945|
|                                                                        |
|                7                                                       |
|o1 = 3*5*53*2819 10861*10212222054939737109085868749                    |
|                                                                        |
|o1 : Expression of class Product                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : y = (2^15-4)/(2^15-5)                                              |
|                                                                        |
|     32764                                                              |
|o2 = -----                                                              |
|     32763                                                              |
|                                                                        |
|o2 : QQ                                                                 |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : x = factor y                                                       |
|                                                                        |
|       2                                                                |
|      2 8191                                                            |
|o3 = --------                                                           |
|     3*67*163                                                           |
|                                                                        |
|o3 : Expression of class Divide                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : value x                                                            |
|                                                                        |
|     32764                                                              |
|o4 = -----                                                              |
|     32763                                                              |
|                                                                        |
|o4 : QQ                                                                 |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

We may *note peek: peek, inside x to a high depth to see its true structure as
*note Expression: Expression,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : peek'(100,x)                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = Divide{Product{Power{2, 2}, Power{8191, 1}}, Product{Power{3, 1},       |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Power{67, 1}, Power{163, 1}}}                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

For integers, factorization is done by *note FLINT: FLINT,, and the factors $x$
are actually just probably prime, as described in the documentation of *note
isPseudoprime: isPseudoprime_lpZZ_rp,.

For multivariate polynomials the factorization is done with code of Michael
Messollen (see *note Singular-Factory: Singular-Factory,).  For univariate
polynomials the factorization is in turn done with code of Gert-Martin Greuel
and Ruediger Stobbe (see *note Singular-Factory: Singular-Factory,).

+--------------------------------+
|i6 : R = ZZ/101[u]              |
|                                |
|o6 = R                          |
|                                |
|o6 : PolynomialRing             |
+--------------------------------+
|i7 : factor (u^3-1)             |
|                                |
|              2                 |
|o7 = (u - 1)(u  + u + 1)        |
|                                |
|o7 : Expression of class Product|
+--------------------------------+
The constant term is provided as the last factor, if it's not equal to 1.
+-------------------------------+
|i8 : F = frac(ZZ/101[t])       |
|                               |
|o8 = F                         |
|                               |
|o8 : FractionField             |
+-------------------------------+
|i9 : factor ((t^3-1)/(t^3+1))  |
|                               |
|              2                |
|     (t - 1)(t  + t + 1)       |
|o9 = -------------------       |
|              2                |
|     (t + 1)(t  - t + 1)       |
|                               |
|o9 : Expression of class Divide|
+-------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "factor(QQ)"
  * *note factor(RingElement): factor_lpRingElement_rp, -- factor a ring
    element
  * "factor(ZZ)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/functions/factor-doc.m2:70:0.

