indices(RingElement) -- indices of variables occurring in a polynomial
**********************************************************************

  * Function: *note indices: indices,
  * Usage: 
        indices f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: RingElement,, or a *note matrix: Matrix,over a
        polynomial ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: List,, of integers, the indices of the variables
        occurring in the polynomial or matrix

Description
===========

The first variable in a polynomial ring has index 0, the second has index 1,
etc. This function returns a list (in ascending order) of the indices of all of
the variables that occur in f.
+---------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..g]                |
|                                 |
|o1 = R                           |
|                                 |
|o1 : PolynomialRing              |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : F = a^3+b^2*c+3*f^10*d-1+e-e|
|                                 |
|         10    3    2            |
|o2 = 3d*f   + a  + b c - 1       |
|                                 |
|o2 : R                           |
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : indices F                   |
|                                 |
|o3 = {0, 1, 2, 3, 5}             |
|                                 |
|o3 : List                        |
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : index a                     |
|                                 |
|o4 = 0                           |
+---------------------------------+
|i5 : support F                   |
|                                 |
|o5 = {a, b, c, d, f}             |
|                                 |
|o5 : List                        |
+---------------------------------+
The same works for matrices.
+-----------------------------------+
|i6 : M = matrix"a+b,c+e;2a-e,3b-c4"|
|                                   |
|o6 = | a+b  c+e    |               |
|     | 2a-e -c4+3b |               |
|                                   |
|             2      2              |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R               |
+-----------------------------------+
|i7 : indices M                     |
|                                   |
|o7 = {0, 1, 2, 4}                  |
|                                   |
|o7 : List                          |
+-----------------------------------+
|i8 : support M                     |
|                                   |
|o8 = {a, b, c, e}                  |
|                                   |
|o8 : List                          |
+-----------------------------------+
This use of *note indices: indices, has no relationship with the use for
specifying parts of a direct sum

See also
========

  * *note index: index, -- numeric index of a ring variable
  * *note support: support, -- list of variables occurring in a polynomial or
    matrix
  * *note indices: indices, -- indices of a polynomial; also components for a
    direct sum
  * *note Ring _ ZZ: get a ring variable by index, -- get a ring variable by
    index

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "indices(Matrix)"
  * *note indices(RingElement): indices_lpRingElement_rp, -- indices of
    variables occurring in a polynomial
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/functions/indices-doc.m2:46:0.

