RingElement ^ ZZ -- power
*************************

  * Operator: *note ^: ^,
  * Usage: 
        f^n
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: RingElement,
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: RingElement,, f^n

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/7[x]/(x^46-x-1);                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : (x+4)^(7^100)                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|        45    43    42     41     38     37     36     35    34     33     32|
|o2 = - x   - x   - x   + 3x   + 3x   - 2x   + 2x   + 3x   + x   - 3x   + 3x  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|         31     30    29    28    27     26     25    23     22    21     20 |
|     - 2x   + 2x   + x   - x   + x   - 3x   + 2x   + x   + 3x   - x   - 2x   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|         19    18     17     16     15     14    13     12     11    10     9|
|     - 2x   - x   + 3x   - 3x   - 3x   + 2x   + x   + 2x   - 3x   - x   - 3x |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|         8     7     6     5    4     2                                      |
|     - 2x  + 3x  - 2x  + 3x  - x  + 2x  - 3x + 3                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+


If the ring allows inverses, negative values may be used.
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = ZZ[t,Inverses=>true,MonomialOrder=>RevLex];|
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : t^-1                                           |
|                                                    |
|      -1                                            |
|o4 = t                                              |
|                                                    |
|o4 : S                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : T = frac(ZZ[a,b,c]);                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : (a+b+c)^-1                                     |
|                                                    |
|         1                                          |
|o6 = ---------                                      |
|     a + b + c                                      |
|                                                    |
|o6 : T                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note frac: frac, -- construct a fraction field
  * *note polynomial rings: polynomial rings,

