Vector ** Vector -- tensor product
**********************************

  * Operator: *note **: _st_st,
  * Usage: 
        v ** w
        tensor(v, w)
  * Inputs:
      * v, a *note vector: Vector,, 
      * w, a *note vector: Vector,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note vector: Vector,, the tensor product of $v$ and $w$

Description
===========

If $v$ is in the module $M$ and $w$ is in the module $N$, then $v\otimes w$ is
in the module $M\otimes N$.

+-----------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[a..d];           |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : F = R^3                 |
|                             |
|      3                      |
|o2 = R                       |
|                             |
|o2 : R-module, free          |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : G = coker vars R        |
|                             |
|o3 = cokernel | a b c d |    |
|                             |
|                            1|
|o3 : R-module, quotient of R |
+-----------------------------+
|i4 : v = (a-37)*F_1          |
|                             |
|o4 = |   0  |                |
|     | a-37 |                |
|     |   0  |                |
|                             |
|      3                      |
|o4 : R                       |
+-----------------------------+
|i5 : v ** G_0                |
|                             |
|o5 = |  0  |                 |
|     | -37 |                 |
|     |  0  |                 |
|                             |
|o5 : Vector                  |
+-----------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note flip: flip, -- isomorphism map of commutativity of tensor product
  * *note tensor(Module,Module): tensor_lpModule_cmModule_rp, -- tensor product
    of modules
  * *note tensor(Matrix,Module): tensor_lpMatrix_cmModule_rp, -- tensor product
  * *note tensor(Matrix,Matrix): tensor_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, -- tensor product

Ways to use this method:
========================

