Manipulator -- the class of all file manipulators
*************************************************

Description
===========

A file manipulator is a type of list that, when put out to a file with *note
<<: <<, causes a chosen function to be applied to the file.  Alternatively, a
manipulator can be used the way a function is used.
+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : f = new Manipulator from identity|
|                                      |
|o1 = f                                |
|                                      |
|o1 : Manipulator                      |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : stdio << f                       |
|                                      |
|o2 = stdio                            |
|                                      |
|o2 : File                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : f stdio                          |
|                                      |
|o3 = stdio                            |
|                                      |
|o3 : File                             |
+--------------------------------------+

Functions and methods returning a manipulator:
==============================================

  * "new Manipulator from Function"

Methods that use a manipulator:
===============================

  * "Manipulator Database"
  * "Manipulator File"
  * "Manipulator Nothing"
  * "methods(Manipulator)" -- see *note methods: methods, -- list methods
  * "Manipulator NetFile" -- see *note NetFile: NetFile, -- the class of all
    net files
  * "NetFile << Manipulator" -- see *note NetFile: NetFile, -- the class of all
    net files
  * "File << Manipulator" -- see *note printing to a file: printing to a file,
    -- print to a file
  * "Nothing << Manipulator" -- see *note printing to a file: printing to a
    file, -- print to a file

Protected objects of class Manipulator:
=======================================

  * *note close: close, -- close a file
  * *note closeIn: closeIn, -- close an input file
  * *note closeOut: closeOut, -- close an output file
  * *note endl: endl, -- end an output line
  * *note flush: flush, -- flush output to file

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Manipulator: Manipulator, is a *note type: Type,, with
ancestor classes *note BasicList: BasicList, < *note Thing: Thing,.

