File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: IndexedVariable, Prev: Manipulator, Up: BasicList

IndexedVariable -- the class of all indexed variables
*****************************************************

Description
===========

Indexed variables provide the possibility of producing polynomial rings R[x_0,
x_1, ..., x_(n-1)] in n variables, where n is not known in advance.  If x is an
symbol, and i is an integer, then x_i produces an indexed variable. After this
has been done, an assignment x_i=v will assign another value to it.  A new
sequence of indexed variables of length n assigned to the symbol x can be
produced with x_1 .. x_n and that sequence can be used in constructing a
polynomial ring.
+------------------------------+
|i1 : ZZ/101[t_0 .. t_4]       |
|                              |
|      ZZ                      |
|o1 = ---[t ..t ]              |
|     101  0   4               |
|                              |
|o1 : PolynomialRing           |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : (t_0 -  2*t_1)^3         |
|                              |
|      3     2          2     3|
|o2 = t  - 6t t  + 12t t  - 8t |
|      0     0 1      0 1     1|
|                              |
|      ZZ                      |
|o2 : ---[t ..t ]              |
|     101  0   4               |
+------------------------------+
Warning: the values of the indexed variables t_i are stored in a global
location, behind the scenes, so may not get garbage collected, even if t is a
local variable.
* Menu:

* value(IndexedVariable): value_lpIndexedVariable_rp.  retrieve the value of an indexed variable
* IndexedVariable .. IndexedVariable: IndexedVariable _pd_pd IndexedVariable.  sequences of consecutive indexed variables
* IndexedVariable ..< IndexedVariable: IndexedVariable _pd_pd< IndexedVariable.  sequences of consecutive indexed variables
* baseName::                    the base name of a generator

Methods that use an indexed variable:
=====================================

  * "IndexedVariable <- Thing" -- see *note <-: <-, -- assignment with left
    side evaluated
  * "IndexedVariable ? IndexedVariable" -- see *note ?: ?, -- comparison
    operator
  * "Symbol ? IndexedVariable" -- see *note ?: ?, -- comparison operator
  * "baseName(IndexedVariable)" -- see *note baseName: baseName, -- the base
    name of a generator
  * *note IndexedVariable .. IndexedVariable: IndexedVariable _pd_pd
    IndexedVariable, -- sequences of consecutive indexed variables
  * *note IndexedVariable ..< IndexedVariable: IndexedVariable _pd_pd<
    IndexedVariable, -- sequences of consecutive indexed variables
  * *note IndexedVariable _ Ring: IndexedVariable _us Ring, -- get a ring
    variable by name
  * promote(IndexedVariable,type of RingElement) (missing documentation)
  * *note value(IndexedVariable): value_lpIndexedVariable_rp, -- retrieve the
    value of an indexed variable

For the programmer
==================

