File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: List, Next: Sequence, Up: VisibleList

List -- the class of all lists -- {...}
***************************************

Description
===========

Lists in Macaulay2 consist of elements of any type, enclosed in braces, and
separated by commas.
+------------------+
|i1 : L = {a,1,b,2}|
|                  |
|o1 = {a, 1, b, 2} |
|                  |
|o1 : List         |
+------------------+
The length of a list has two notations, the version with the # is faster when
writing programs.
+-----------------+
|i2 : #L, length L|
|                 |
|o2 = (4, 4)      |
|                 |
|o2 : Sequence    |
+-----------------+
The first entry of the list has index 0.  Indexing is performed using *note #:
#,.
+-----------+
|i3 : L#2   |
|           |
|o3 = b     |
|           |
|o3 : Symbol|
+-----------+

Lists in Macaulay2 are immutable. See *note MutableList: MutableList, for
making and using lists that you may modify.

To convert lists to and from other types of *note BasicList: BasicList,, in
addition to *note toList: toList,, one may use *note new: new,.

+---------------------------+
|i4 : new Array from {a,b,c}|
|                           |
|o4 = [a, b, c]             |
|                           |
|o4 : Array                 |
+---------------------------+
|i5 : new List from [a,b,c] |
|                           |
|o5 = {a, b, c}             |
|                           |
|o5 : List                  |
+---------------------------+

For an overview of lists and sequences, see *note lists and sequences: lists
and sequences,.

* Menu:

* VerticalList::                a type of visible self-initializing list that prints vertically

Types of list:
==============

  * *note VerticalList: VerticalList, -- a type of visible self-initializing
    list that prints vertically

Functions and methods returning a list:
=======================================

  * "List * Thing" -- see *note *: _st, -- a binary operator, usually used for
    multiplication
  * "Thing * List" -- see *note *: _st, -- a binary operator, usually used for
    multiplication
  * "- List" -- see *note -: -, -- a unary or binary operator, usually used for
    negation or subtraction
  * "List // Number" -- see *note //: //, -- a binary operator, usually used
    for quotient
  * "List // RingElement" -- see *note //: //, -- a binary operator, usually
    used for quotient
  * *note apply(ZZ,Function): apply_lpZZ_cmFunction_rp, -- apply a function to
    {0,..., n-1}
