drop -- drop some elements from a list or sequence
**************************************************

  * Usage: 
        drop(L, i)
        drop(L, {j,k})
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note basic list: BasicList,, 
      * i, an *note integer: ZZ,, 
      * j, an *note integer: ZZ,, 
      * k, an *note integer: ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * L2, a *note basic list: BasicList,, the list or sequence obtained by
        dropping the first i elements of L, (if i positive), or the last i
        elements of L (if i negative), or, if given the pair j,k, the list or
        sequence obtained by dropping the elements of L with indices j through
        k

Description
===========

+---------------------------------+
|i1 : drop({a,b,c,d,e,f,g}, 3)    |
|                                 |
|o1 = {d, e, f, g}                |
|                                 |
|o1 : List                        |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : drop({a,b,c,d,e,f,g}, -3)   |
|                                 |
|o2 = {a, b, c, d}                |
|                                 |
|o2 : List                        |
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : drop({a,b,c,d,e,f,g}, {1,3})|
|                                 |
|o3 = {a, e, f, g}                |
|                                 |
|o3 : List                        |
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : drop({a,b,c,d,e,f,g}, {2,2})|
|                                 |
|o4 = {a, b, d, e, f, g}          |
|                                 |
|o4 : List                        |
+---------------------------------+

The pair \{j,k\} must be given with both entries non-negative, and $j\le k$.
Otherwise the original list is returned.

+----------------------------------+
|i5 : drop({a,b,c,d,e,f,g}, {3,1}) |
|                                  |
|o5 = {a, b, c, d, e, f, g}        |
|                                  |
|o5 : List                         |
+----------------------------------+
|i6 : drop({a,b,c,d,e,f,g}, {4,-1})|
|                                  |
|o6 = {a, b, c, d, e, f, g}        |
|                                  |
|o6 : List                         |
+----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note take: take, -- take some elements from a list or sequence
  * *note delete: delete, -- delete some elements of a list
  * *note position: position, -- the first element of a list satisfying a
    condition
  * *note positions: positions, -- which elements of a list satisfy a condition
  * *note select: select, -- select from a list, hash table, or string
  * *note lists and sequences: lists and sequences, -- a detailed overview of
    lists and sequences in Macaulay2

Ways to use drop:
=================

  * "drop(BasicList,List)"
  * "drop(BasicList,ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note drop: drop, is a *note compiled function: CompiledFunction,.

