VisibleList // Function -- apply a function
*******************************************

  * Operator: *note //: //,
  * Usage: 
        x // f
        f \\ x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note visible list: VisibleList,
      * f, a *note function: Function,, a *note command: Command,, or a *note
        self initializing type: SelfInitializingType,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note visible list: VisibleList,, the result of applying f to x,
        i.e., f x

Description
===========

The parsing precedence of the operators // and \\ is rather low, which makes
them useful for avoiding parentheses.  See *note precedence of operators:
precedence of operators,.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : toList \\ sin \ ( 1 .. 5 )                    |
|                                                   |
|o1 = {.841471, .909297, .14112, -.756802, -.958924}|
|                                                   |
|o1 : List                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : ( 1 .. 5 ) / sin // toList                    |
|                                                   |
|o2 = {.841471, .909297, .14112, -.756802, -.958924}|
|                                                   |
|o2 : List                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (x -> (x,x)) \ (a,b,c,d)                      |
|                                                   |
|o3 = ((a, a), (b, b), (c, c), (d, d))              |
|                                                   |
|o3 : Sequence                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : splice \\ (x -> (x,x)) \ (a,b,c,d)            |
|                                                   |
|o4 = (a, a, b, b, c, c, d, d)                      |
|                                                   |
|o4 : Sequence                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------+

