ultimate -- ultimate value for an iteration
*******************************************

Description
===========

ultimate(f,x) -- yields the value ultimately obtained by applying the function
f to x.


Iteration ceases when an error occurs during application of the function, or
the result is the same.  Errors are not reported.


It's a bad idea to use this function, because unexpected errors will produce
unexpected results silently.

Ways to use ultimate:
=====================

  * "ultimate(Function,Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note ultimate: ultimate, is a *note method function:
MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

