File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: iterator, Next: next, Up: Iterator

iterator -- get an iterator
***************************

  * Usage: 
        iterator x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note thing: Thing,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note thing: Thing,, likely an *note Iterator: Iterator,; 

Description
===========

An iterator is an object that is used to traverse through x. Usually, but not
necessarily, this will be an instance of the *note Iterator: Iterator, class.

+------------------------------+
|i1 : iter = iterator {1, 2, 3}|
|                              |
|o1 = iter                     |
|                              |
|o1 : Iterator                 |
+------------------------------+

The class of an iterator should have a *note next: next, method installed that
gets the next element of x.

+--------------+
|i2 : next iter|
|              |
|o2 = 1        |
+--------------+
|i3 : next iter|
|              |
|o3 = 2        |
+--------------+
|i4 : next iter|
|              |
|o4 = 3        |
+--------------+

If x contains only a finite number of elements, then *note next: next, should
return the symbol *note StopIteration: StopIteration, after exhausting them
all.

+------------------+
|i5 : next iter    |
|                  |
|o5 = StopIteration|
|                  |
|o5 : Symbol       |
+------------------+

Instances of classes with this method installed can be used like lists in *note
for: for, loops and *note scan: scan,.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : lookup(iterator, String)                                             |
|                                                                          |
|o6 = FunctionClosure[../../../../../Macaulay2/m2/iterators.m2:20:24-27:16]|
|                                                                          |
|o6 : FunctionClosure                                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : for i in "foo" list i                                                |
|                                                                          |
|o7 = {f, o, o}                                                            |
|                                                                          |
|o7 : List                                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : scan("foo", print)                                                   |
|f                                                                         |
|o                                                                         |
|o                                                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

They can also be passed to *note apply: apply, and *note select: select,.  In
each case, an *note Iterator: Iterator, object will be returned that is an
iterator for itself.

+----------------------------------+
|i9 : apply("foo", toUpper)        |
|                                  |
|o9 = (F, O, O)                    |
|                                  |
|o9 : Sequence                     |
+----------------------------------+
|i10 : for i in oo list i          |
|                                  |
|o10 = {F, O, O}                   |
|                                  |
|o10 : List                        |
+----------------------------------+
|i11 : select("foo", i -> i == "o")|
|                                  |
|o11 = iterator "foo"              |
|                                  |
|o11 : Iterator                    |
+----------------------------------+
|i12 : for i in oo list i          |
|                                  |
|o12 = {o, o}                      |
|                                  |
|o12 : List                        |
+----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Iterator: Iterator, -- class for iterators
  * *note next: next, -- get the next object from an iterator
  * *note StopIteration: StopIteration, -- stop iteration

Ways to use iterator:
=====================

  * "iterator(Iterator)"
  * "iterator(String)"
  * "iterator(VisibleList)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note iterator: iterator, is a *note method function with a single
argument: MethodFunctionSingle,.

