next -- get the next object from an iterator
********************************************

  * Usage: 
        next x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note thing: Thing,, an iterator; 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note thing: Thing,, the next object from x; 

Description
===========

This gets the next object from an iterator, i.e., something returned by *note
iterator: iterator,.

+------------------------------+
|i1 : iter = iterator {1, 2, 3}|
|                              |
|o1 = iter                     |
|                              |
|o1 : Iterator                 |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : next iter                |
|                              |
|o2 = 1                        |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : next iter                |
|                              |
|o3 = 2                        |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : next iter                |
|                              |
|o4 = 3                        |
+------------------------------+

If the iterator is exhausted, then the symbol *note StopIteration:
StopIteration, is returned.

+------------------+
|i5 : next iter    |
|                  |
|o5 = StopIteration|
|                  |
|o5 : Symbol       |
+------------------+

