uniform -- whether all elements of a list are the same class
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        uniform L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: List,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, whether all elements of L are of the
        same *note class: class,

Description
===========

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : uniform {2, 5, 0}          |
|                                |
|o1 = true                       |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : uniform {2*0.5, 5*0.5, 0/2}|
|                                |
|o2 = false                      |
+--------------------------------+

The second list is not uniform because 0/2 is represented as a rational number
(of class *note QQ: QQ,), while 2*0.5 and 5*0.5 are represented as real numbers
(of class *note RR: RR,).

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : uniform {hi, "hello"}                       |
|                                                 |
|o3 = false                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : uniform {"hi", "hello"}                     |
|                                                 |
|o4 = true                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                              |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : uniform {x^2*y*z, 5*y, 12/7}                |
|                                                 |
|o6 = false                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : uniform {x^2*y*z, 5*y, (12/7)_R}            |
|                                                 |
|o7 = true                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : S = ZZ[t];                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : uniform {monomialIdeal(x), monomialIdeal(t)}|
|                                                 |
|o9 = true                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : uniform {monomialIdeal(t), ideal(t)}       |
|                                                 |
|o10 = false                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : uniform {S/monomialIdeal(t), S/ideal(t)}   |
|                                                 |
|o11 = true                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------+

