select(Thing,Function) -- select elements from an object with an iterator
*************************************************************************

  * Function: *note select: select,
  * Usage: 
        select(x, f)
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note thing: Thing,, an instance of a class with the *note
        iterator: iterator, method installed;
      * f, a *note function: Function,, returning either *note true: true, or
        *note false: false,;
  * Outputs:
      * an *note iterator: Iterator,, 

Description
===========

Suppose x is an instance of a class with the *note iterator: iterator, method
installed, e.g., a string, and suppose iter is the output of iterator x.  Then
a new *note Iterator: Iterator, object is returned whose *note next: next,
method returns the next output of next iter for which f next iter is true,
unless next iter returns *note StopIteration: StopIteration,, in which case
this new iterator does the same.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : selectiter = select("foo", i -> i == "o")|
|                                              |
|o1 = selectiter                               |
|                                              |
|o1 : Iterator                                 |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : next selectiter                          |
|                                              |
|o2 = o                                        |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : next selectiter                          |
|                                              |
|o3 = o                                        |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : next selectiter                          |
|                                              |
|o4 = StopIteration                            |
|                                              |
|o4 : Symbol                                   |
+----------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note iterator: iterator, -- get an iterator
  * *note Iterator: Iterator, -- class for iterators
  * *note next: next, -- get the next object from an iterator
  * *note StopIteration: StopIteration, -- stop iteration
  * *note apply(Thing,Function): apply_lpThing_cmFunction_rp, -- apply a
    function to an object with an iterator

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note select(Thing,Function): select_lpThing_cmFunction_rp, -- select
    elements from an object with an iterator
