positions -- which elements of a list satisfy a condition
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        positions(A, f)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note visible list: VisibleList,, 
      * f, a *note function: Function,, 
  * Outputs:
      * p, a *note list: List,, the list of indices i such that f(A#i) is true

Description
===========

The indices are listed in ascending order. If no element satisfies the
condition, an empty list is returned.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : positions((10,20,43,105,6,93), odd)     |
|                                             |
|o1 = {2, 3, 5}                               |
|                                             |
|o1 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : positions((10,20,43,105,6,93), i -> i<0)|
|                                             |
|o2 = {}                                      |
|                                             |
|o2 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : positions(100..110, isPrime)            |
|                                             |
|o3 = {1, 3, 7, 9}                            |
|                                             |
|o3 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+

To find the first or last index of an element satisfying the condition, see
*note position: position,. To return the elements, rather than their indices,
see *note select: select,. The function *note number: number, counts the number
of elements satisfying the condition.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : position((10,20,43,105,6), odd)                 |
|                                                     |
|o4 = 2                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : position((10,20,43,105,6), odd, Reverse => true)|
|                                                     |
|o5 = 3                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : select((10,20,43,105,6), odd)                   |
|                                                     |
|o6 = (43, 105)                                       |
|                                                     |
|o6 : Sequence                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : number((10,20,43,105,6), odd)                   |
|                                                     |
|o7 = 2                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

