min -- get the minimum element in a list or sequence
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        min X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note visible list: VisibleList,, 
  * Outputs:
      * m, a *note thing: Thing,, 

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = for i from 1 to 10 list random(100) |
|                                             |
|o1 = {24, 65, 71, 72, 19, 19, 91, 72, 93, 79}|
|                                             |
|o1 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : min X                                   |
|                                             |
|o2 = 19                                      |
+---------------------------------------------+

If L contains elements in a polynomial ring, the *note MonomialOrder:
MonomialOrder, of the ring is used for comparisons.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R1 = QQ[x, y, z, MonomialOrder => Lex];    |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : min {x*y^2, x*y^2 + z^2, y^4, y*z^5}       |
|                                                |
|        5                                       |
|o4 = y*z                                        |
|                                                |
|o4 : R1                                         |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R2 = QQ[x, y, z, MonomialOrder => GRevLex];|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : min (x*y^2, x*y^2 + z^2, y^4, y*z^5)       |
|                                                |
|        2                                       |
|o6 = x*y                                        |
|                                                |
|o6 : R2                                         |
+------------------------------------------------+

More generally, the order of the elements is determined using the *note ?: ?,
operator.

If X is a list of lists, min acts on the outermost level.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : min {{3, 1, 2}, {2, 9, 6}, {3, 7, 5}}        |
|                                                  |
|o7 = {2, 9, 6}                                    |
|                                                  |
|o7 : List                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : min flatten {{3, 1, 2}, {2, 9, 6}, {3, 7, 5}}|
|                                                  |
|o8 = 1                                            |
+--------------------------------------------------+

