mingle -- mingle elements of several lists
******************************************

  * Usage: 
        mingle(L)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note basic list: BasicList,, a list of lists L=\{L1, L2, ...,
        Ln\}
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note list: List,, a new list mingling the elements of all lists
        in L

Description
===========

The output list M takes the first element of each Li, i=1,...,n, followed by
the second element of Li, i=1,...,n, and so forth.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : mingle {{a1, a2, a3}, {b1, b2, b3}, {c1, c2, c3}}|
|                                                      |
|o1 = {a1, b1, c1, a2, b2, c2, a3, b3, c3}             |
|                                                      |
|o1 : List                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+

The lists can have different lengths. After a list is exhausted, it will be
silently ignored.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : mingle {{a1, a2, a3, a4}, {b1, b2}, {c1}}|
|                                              |
|o2 = {a1, b1, c1, a2, b2, a3, a4}             |
|                                              |
|o2 : List                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+

To transpose a nested list (thinking of it as a matrix), try using mingle with
*note pack: pack,.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : pack(3, mingle ((a1, a2, a3), (b1, b2, b3), (c1, c2, c3)))|
|                                                               |
|o3 = {{a1, b1, c1}, {a2, b2, c2}, {a3, b3, c3}}                |
|                                                               |
|o3 : List                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

Notice from the previous example that mingle accepts sequences and other types
of *note BasicList: BasicList,s as input, but the output will always be a *note
List: List,.

Further examples:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : concatenate mingle( {"a","b","c"} , {",",","} )                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = a,b,c                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : netList pack(3, mingle( (0..5), apply(6, i -> i^2), apply(6, i -> i^3)))|
|                                                                             |
|     +-+--+---+                                                              |
|o5 = |0|0 |0  |                                                              |
|     +-+--+---+                                                              |
|     |1|1 |1  |                                                              |
|     +-+--+---+                                                              |
|     |2|4 |8  |                                                              |
|     +-+--+---+                                                              |
|     |3|9 |27 |                                                              |
|     +-+--+---+                                                              |
|     |4|16|64 |                                                              |
|     +-+--+---+                                                              |
|     |5|25|125|                                                              |
|     +-+--+---+                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

