runLengthEncode -- run length encoding
**************************************

  * Usage: 
        runLengthEncode x
  * Inputs:
      * x
  * Outputs:
      * a list equivalent to x, in which runs and sequences have been expressed
        symbolically as *note expressions: Expression,

Description
===========

The result is useful in printed displays, as a way of making them more compact.
The original list can be recovered by applying *note value: value, to the
elements of the result, and then using *note deepSplice: deepSplice,, provided
that x contains no entries that are sequences.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : x = {1,2,3,a,b,c,a,b,c,4,4,4,"asdf"};                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : y = runLengthEncode x                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {1..3, 2:a..c, 3:4, asdf}                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : peek y                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {BinaryOperation{.., 1, 3}, BinaryOperation{:, 2, a..c},                |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     BinaryOperation{:, 3, 4}, Holder{asdf}}                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : value \ y                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {(1, 2, 3), ((a, b, c), (a, b, c)), (4, 4, 4), asdf}                    |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : deepSplice \\ oo                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {1, 2, 3, a, b, c, a, b, c, 4, 4, 4, asdf}                              |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : x === oo                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note BinaryOperation: BinaryOperation, -- the class of all binary
    operation expressions
  * *note Holder: Holder, -- the class of all holder expressions

Ways to use runLengthEncode:
============================

  * "runLengthEncode(VisibleList)"

