File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: HashTable, Next: MutableHashTable, Up: hash tables

HashTable -- the class of all hash tables
*****************************************

Description
===========

A hash table consists of: a class type, a parent type, and a set of key-value
pairs.  The keys and values can be anything. The access functions below accept
a key and return the corresponding value.  For details of the mechanism
underlying this, see *note hashing: hashing,.

One important feature of hash tables that when the keys are consecutive
integers starting at 0, the keys are scanned in the natural order.

There is a subclass of HashTable called *note MutableHashTable:
MutableHashTable, which consists of those hash tables whose entries can be
changed.

This node is currently in progress!!!

See also
========

  * *note #: #, -- length or access to elements
  * *note .: _pd, -- access to elements whose key is a symbol
  * *note #?: #?, -- check existence of value in a list, hash table, database,
    or string
  * *note .?: _pd?, -- check for presence of elements whose key is a symbol
* Menu:

* VirtualTally::
* OptionTable::                 the class of hash tables for optional arguments

Types of hash table:
====================

  * *note DocumentTag: DocumentTag, -- the class of all document tags
  * *note Ideal: Ideal, -- the class of all ideals
  * *note ImmutableType: ImmutableType, -- the class of all immutable types
  * *note Matrix: Matrix, -- the class of all matrices
  * *note MonoidElement: MonoidElement, -- the class of all monoid elements
  * *note MutableHashTable: MutableHashTable, -- the class of all mutable hash
    tables
  * *note MutableMatrix: MutableMatrix, -- the class of all mutable matrices
  * *note OptionTable: OptionTable, -- the class of hash tables for optional
