BettiTally -- the class of all Betti tallies
********************************************

Description
===========

A Betti tally is a special type of *note Tally: Tally, that is printed as a
display of graded Betti numbers. The class was created so the function *note
betti: betti, could return something that both prints nicely and from which
information can be extracted.  The keys are triples (i,d,h) encoding:

 i, the column labels, representing the homological degree;

 d, a list of integers giving a multidegree; and

 h, the row labels, representing the dot product of a weight covector and d.

Only i and h are used in printing, and the weight covector can be modified by
specifying the *note betti(...,Weights=>...): betti_lpBettiTally_rp, option to
*note betti(BettiTally): betti_lpBettiTally_rp,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : t = new BettiTally from { (0,{0},0) => 1, (1,{1},1) => 2, (2,{3},3) =>  |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1 2                                                            |
|o1 = total: 1 2 7                                                            |
|         0: 1 2 .                                                            |
|         1: . . 3                                                            |
|         2: . . 4                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : BettiTally                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3, (2,{4},4) => 4 }                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : betti(t, Weights => {2})                                                |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1 2                                                            |
|o2 = total: 1 2 7                                                            |
|         0: 1 . .                                                            |
|         1: . 2 .                                                            |
|         2: . . .                                                            |
|         3: . . .                                                            |
|         4: . . 3                                                            |
|         5: . . .                                                            |
|         6: . . 4                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : BettiTally                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : peek oo                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = BettiTally{(0, {0}, 0) => 1}                                            |
|                (1, {1}, 2) => 2                                             |
|                (2, {3}, 6) => 3                                             |
|                (2, {4}, 8) => 4                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

For convenience, the operations of direct sum (*note ++: ++,), tensor product
(*note **: _st_st,), *note codim: codim,, *note degree: degree,, *note dual:
dual,, *note pdim: pdim,, *note poincare: poincare,, *note regularity:
regularity,, and degree shifting (numbers in brackets or parentheses), have
been implemented for Betti tallies.  These operations mimic the corresponding
operations on chain complexes.

+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : t(5)                             |
|                                      |
|            0 1 2                     |
|o4 = total: 1 2 7                     |
|        -5: 1 2 .                     |
|        -4: . . 3                     |
|        -3: . . 4                     |
|                                      |
|o4 : BettiTally                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : t[-5]                            |
|                                      |
|            5 6 7                     |
|o5 = total: 1 2 7                     |
|        -5: 1 2 .                     |
|        -4: . . 3                     |
|        -3: . . 4                     |
|                                      |
|o5 : BettiTally                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : dual oo                          |
|                                      |
|            -7 -6 -5                  |
|o6 = total:  7  2  1                  |
|         3:  4  .  .                  |
|         4:  3  .  .                  |
|         5:  .  2  1                  |
|                                      |
|o6 : BettiTally                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i7 : t ++ oo                          |
|                                      |
|            -7 -6 -5 -4 -3 -2 -1 0 1 2|
|o7 = total:  7  2  1  .  .  .  . 1 2 7|
|         0:  .  .  .  .  .  .  . 1 2 .|
|         1:  .  .  .  .  .  .  . . . 3|
|         2:  .  .  .  .  .  .  . . . 4|
|         3:  4  .  .  .  .  .  . . . .|
|         4:  3  .  .  .  .  .  . . . .|
|         5:  .  2  1  .  .  .  . . . .|
|                                      |
|o7 : BettiTally                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i8 : t ** t                           |
|                                      |
|            0 1  2  3  4              |
|o8 = total: 1 4 18 28 49              |
|         0: 1 4  4  .  .              |
|         1: . .  6 12  .              |
|         2: . .  8 16  9              |
|         3: . .  .  . 24              |
|         4: . .  .  . 16              |
|                                      |
|o8 : BettiTally                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i9 : pdim t                           |
|                                      |
|o9 = 2                                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i10 : codim t                         |
|                                      |
|o10 = 0                               |
+--------------------------------------+
|i11 : degree t                        |
|                                      |
|o11 = 6                               |
+--------------------------------------+
|i12 : poincare t                      |
|                                      |
|                 3     4              |
|o12 = 1 - 2T + 3T  + 4T               |
|                                      |
|o12 : ZZ[T]                           |
+--------------------------------------+
|i13 : regularity t                    |
|                                      |
|o13 = 2                               |
+--------------------------------------+

If the Betti tally represents the Betti numbers of a resolution of a module $M$
on a polynomial ring $R = K[x_0,...,x_n]$, then while the data does not
uniquely determine $M$, it suffices to compute the *note Hilbert polynomial:
hilbertPolynomial, and *note Hilbert series: hilbertSeries, of $M$.

+---------------------------------+
|i14 : n = 3                      |
|                                 |
|o14 = 3                          |
+---------------------------------+
|i15 : hilbertSeries(n, t)        |
|                                 |
|                 3     4         |
|      1 - 2T + 3T  + 4T          |
|o15 = ------------------         |
|                  3              |
|           (1 - T)               |
|                                 |
|o15 : Expression of class Divide |
+---------------------------------+
|i16 : hilbertPolynomial(n, t)    |
|                                 |
|o16 = 33*P  - 23*P  + 6*P        |
|          0       1      2       |
|                                 |
|o16 : ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial|
+---------------------------------+

A Betti tally can be multiplied by an integer or by a rational number, and the
values can be lifted to integers, when possible.

+------------------+
|i17 : (1/2) * t   |
|                  |
|             0 1 2|
|             1   7|
|o17 = total: - 1 -|
|             2   2|
|             1    |
|          0: - 1 .|
|             2    |
|                 3|
|          1: . . -|
|                 2|
|          2: . . 2|
|                  |
|o17 : BettiTally  |
+------------------+
|i18 : 2 * oo      |
|                  |
|             0 1 2|
|o18 = total: 1 2 7|
|          0: 1 2 .|
|          1: . . 3|
|          2: . . 4|
|                  |
|o18 : BettiTally  |
+------------------+
|i19 : lift(oo,ZZ) |
|                  |
|             0 1 2|
|o19 = total: 1 2 7|
|          0: 1 2 .|
|          1: . . 3|
|          2: . . 4|
|                  |
|o19 : BettiTally  |
+------------------+
* Menu:

* MultigradedBettiTally::       the class of all multigraded Betti tallies

Types of Betti tally:
=====================

