hashTable -- make a hash table
******************************

Description
===========

hashTable(h,v) -- produce a hash table from a list v of key-value pairs, with
an optional collision handler function h.


The pairs may be of the form a=>b, {a,b}, or (a,b).


Missing entries in the list, represented by *note null: null,, will be silently
ignored.


+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : x = hashTable {a=>b, c=>d, }         |
|                                          |
|o1 = HashTable{a => b}                    |
|               c => d                     |
|                                          |
|o1 : HashTable                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : x#a                                  |
|                                          |
|o2 = b                                    |
|                                          |
|o2 : Symbol                               |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : hashTable(plus, {(a,3),(b,4),(a,10)})|
|                                          |
|o3 = HashTable{a => 13}                   |
|               b => 4                     |
|                                          |
|o3 : HashTable                            |
+------------------------------------------+

