copy -- copy an object
**********************

Description
===========

copy x yields a copy of x.


If x is an hash table, array, list or sequence, then the elements are placed
into a new copy. If x is a hash table, the copy is mutable if and only if x is.


It is not advisable to copy such things as modules and rings, for: (1) the
operations that have already been installed for them will return values in the
original object, rather than in the copy; and (2) the copy operation is
shallow, not copying keys and values that happen to be hash tables.


See also
========

  * *note newClass: newClass, -- set the class and parent of an object

For the programmer
==================

The object *note copy: copy, is a *note compiled function: CompiledFunction,.

