applyPairs -- apply a function to each pair in a hash table
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        applyPairs(H, f)
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note hash table: HashTable,, a *note basic list: BasicList,, or a
        *note dictionary: Dictionary,, or any instance of a class with an *note
        iterator: iterator, method installed
      * f, a *note function: Function,, of two arguments, returning a pair or
        *note null: null,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: HashTable,, obtained by applying f to each
        key/value pair in H

Description
===========

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : H = new HashTable from {1 => 10, 2 => 15, 3 => 20}|
|                                                       |
|o1 = HashTable{1 => 10}                                |
|               2 => 15                                 |
|               3 => 20                                 |
|                                                       |
|o1 : HashTable                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : applyPairs(H, (k,v) -> (k+1, v+10))               |
|                                                       |
|o2 = HashTable{2 => 20}                                |
|               3 => 25                                 |
|               4 => 30                                 |
|                                                       |
|o2 : HashTable                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : applyPairs(H, (k,v) -> (v,k))                     |
|                                                       |
|o3 = HashTable{10 => 1}                                |
|               15 => 2                                 |
|               20 => 3                                 |
|                                                       |
|o3 : HashTable                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

If H is not a hash table, then apply(pairs H, f) is called.

+-------------------------------------------+
|i4 : applyPairs({4, 5, 6}, (i, x) -> i * x)|
|                                           |
|o4 = {0, 5, 12}                            |
|                                           |
|o4 : List                                  |
+-------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

It is an error for the function f to return two pairs with the same key.

