selectValues -- select part of a hash table by values
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        selectValues(v,f)
        selectValues(n,v,f)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,
      * v, a *note hash table: HashTable,
      * f, returning either *note true: true, or *note false: false,
  * Outputs:
      * whose pairs are those key-value pairs (k,w) of the hash table v that
        yield true when the function f is applied to the value w.If n is
        provided, at most n pairs will be selected.

Description
===========

The hash table v should be immutable: to scan the values in a mutable hash
table, use scan(values x, f).
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : x = new HashTable from { x => 1, y => 2, z => 3 }|
|                                                      |
|o1 = HashTable{x => 1}                                |
|               y => 2                                 |
|               z => 3                                 |
|                                                      |
|o1 : HashTable                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : select(x,odd)                                    |
|                                                      |
|o2 = HashTable{x => 1}                                |
|               z => 3                                 |
|                                                      |
|o2 : HashTable                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : select(1,x,odd)                                  |
|                                                      |
|o3 = HashTable{x => 1}                                |
|                                                      |
|o3 : HashTable                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------+

