- -- a unary or binary operator, usually used for negation or subtraction
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        -y 
        x-y

Description
===========

In most cases, this operator refers to standard negation or subtraction.


In many cases, the integer 1 can be used as the identity, and scalars function
as multiples of the identity. For example, the 1 below refers to the identity
matrix and the 2 to twice the identity matrix.
+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matrix{{1,2,3},{2,3,4},{3,4,6}}|
|                                        |
|o1 = | 1 2 3 |                          |
|     | 2 3 4 |                          |
|     | 3 4 6 |                          |
|                                        |
|              3       3                 |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : M-1, M-2                           |
|                                        |
|o2 = (| 0 2 3 |, | -1 2 3 |)            |
|      | 2 2 4 |  | 2  1 4 |             |
|      | 3 4 5 |  | 3  4 4 |             |
|                                        |
|o2 : Sequence                           |
+----------------------------------------+

Intervals
---------

If one of the inputs is an *note RRi: RRi, or a *note CCi: CCi,, the output is
an interval containing all differences of pairs in the inputs.

+----------------------------------+
|i3 : 2-interval(1,3)              |
|                                  |
|o3 = [-1,1]                       |
|                                  |
|o3 : RRi (of precision 53)        |
+----------------------------------+
|i4 : interval(1,3)-interval(-1,2) |
|                                  |
|o4 = [-1,4]                       |
|                                  |
|o4 : RRi (of precision 53)        |
+----------------------------------+
|i5 : interval(-1,1)-interval(-1,1)|
|                                  |
|o5 = [-2,2]                       |
|                                  |
|o5 : RRi (of precision 53)        |
+----------------------------------+
|i6 : interval(1,2+3*ii)-(2+ii)    |
|                                  |
|o6 = [-1,-0]+[-1,2]*ii            |
|                                  |
|o6 : CCi (of precision 53)        |
+----------------------------------+

