/ -- a binary operator, usually used for division
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        x / y

Description
===========

This operator is currently used in several ways in Macaulay2.
  * division in a ring, yielding a fraction
  * division in unevaluated expressions
  * quotient rings, modules and sheaves
  * applying a function or ring map to every element of a list or set
+-------------------------+
|i1 : 2/3                 |
|                         |
|     2                   |
|o1 = -                   |
|     3                   |
|                         |
|o1 : QQ                  |
+-------------------------+
|i2 : 2./3                |
|                         |
|o2 = .6666666666666666   |
|                         |
|o2 : RR (of precision 53)|
+-------------------------+

Intervals
---------

If one of the inputs is an *note RRi: RRi, or a *note CCi: CCi,, the output is
an interval containing all quotients of pairs in the inputs.

+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : 2/interval(1,3)                    |
|                                        |
|o3 = [.6666666666666666,2]              |
|                                        |
|o3 : RRi (of precision 53)              |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : interval(-1,2)/interval(1,3)       |
|                                        |
|o4 = [-1,2]                             |
|                                        |
|o4 : RRi (of precision 53)              |
+----------------------------------------+
|i5 : interval(1,2)/interval(1,2)        |
|                                        |
|o5 = [.5,2]                             |
|                                        |
|o5 : RRi (of precision 53)              |
+----------------------------------------+
|i6 : interval(1,2+3*ii)/(1+2*ii)        |
|                                        |
|o6 = [.2,1.6]+[-.8,.2000000000000001]*ii|
|                                        |
|o6 : CCi (of precision 53)              |
+----------------------------------------+

