; -- expression separator
*************************

  * Usage: 
        (e;f;...;g;h)

Description
===========

The semicolon can be used for evaluating a sequence of expressions.  The value
of the sequence is the value of its last expression, unless it is omitted, in
which case the value is *note null: null,.

+-------------+
|i1 : (3;4;5) |
|             |
|o1 = 5       |
+-------------+
|i2 : (3;4;5;)|
+-------------+

Putting expressions on separate lines is not a substitute for the semicolons.

For the programmer
==================

The object *note ;: ;, is a *note keyword: Keyword,.

