continue -- continue with the next iteration of a loop
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        continue x
  * Inputs:
      * x
  * Consequences:
      * the currently executing list-clause of a *note for: for,-loop or *note
        while: while,-loop is finished, and iteration continues with the *note
        do: do,-clause or the next iteration of the loop, if any.  The value x
        is added to the list being accumulated. If x is omitted, then no value
        is added to the list, and the statement may be used in a do-clause.
      * Alternatively, as a debugger command, causes execution to be resumed,
        starting with the current expression.

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : for i from 1 to 4 list (continue 4; print ho) do print hi             |
|hi                                                                         |
|hi                                                                         |
|hi                                                                         |
|hi                                                                         |
|                                                                           |
|o1 = {4, 4, 4, 4}                                                          |
|                                                                           |
|o1 : List                                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : for i from 1 to 4 list (continue ; 14) do print hi                    |
|hi                                                                         |
|hi                                                                         |
|hi                                                                         |
|hi                                                                         |
|                                                                           |
|o2 = {}                                                                    |
|                                                                           |
|o2 : List                                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : for i from 1 to 4 list 14 do print hi                                 |
|hi                                                                         |
|hi                                                                         |
|hi                                                                         |
|hi                                                                         |
|                                                                           |
|o3 = {14, 14, 14, 14}                                                      |
|                                                                           |
|o3 : List                                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : i = 0 ; while i < 10 do ( i = i+1; if i == 5 then continue ; print i )|
|1                                                                          |
|2                                                                          |
|3                                                                          |
|4                                                                          |
|6                                                                          |
|7                                                                          |
|8                                                                          |
|9                                                                          |
|10                                                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Here is an example of the use of *note continue: continue, in the debugger
after altering a value so continuation will not cause the error to recur.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : load "Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.m2"                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : code g                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = /usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.                    |
|     m2:11:4-14:9: --source code:                                            |
|     g = y -> (                                                              |
|          c := f(y-1);                                                       |
|          d := f(y-2);                                                       |
|          c+d)                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : g 2                                                                     |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.m2:8:11:(3):[3]: error   |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.m2:8:11:(3): entering    |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.m2:8:                    |
|10-8:13: --source code:                                                      |
|     b := 1/x;                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|: division by zero                                                           |
|debugger (enter 'help' to see commands)                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii9 : code f                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|oo9 = /usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.                   |
|      m2:6:5-9:9: --source code:                                             |
|      f := x -> (                                                            |
|           a := "hi there";                                                  |
|           b := 1/x;                                                         |
|           b+1)                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii10 : x                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|oo10 = 0                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii11 : x = 11                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|oo11 = 11                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii12 : continue                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|      34                                                                     |
|o12 = --                                                                     |
|      11                                                                     |
