File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: caching computation results, Next: using hooks, Prev: making new functions with optional arguments, Up: The Macaulay2 language

caching computation results
***************************

Here is a simple example of caching a computation in a *note CacheTable:
CacheTable,, using the augmented null coalescing operator *note ??=: ??=,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : pdim' = M -> M.cache.pdim' ??= ( printerr "computing pdim'"; pdim M );  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = coker vars R;                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : elapsedTime pdim' M                                                     |
| -- computing pdim'                                                          |
| -- .00311415s elapsed                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 3                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : elapsedTime pdim' M                                                     |
| -- .000001012s elapsed                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 3                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : peek M.cache                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = CacheTable{cache => MutableHashTable{}                                  |
|                isHomogeneous => true                                        |
|                minimalPresentation => (OptionTable{Exclude => {}}) =>       |
|                pdim' => 3                                                   |
|                presentation => | x y z |                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                  }                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|cokernel | z y x |                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In the example above, the function is only executed if M.cache.pdim' is not
already defined, and once it is executed the result is stored there for future
reference.

In more complicated situations, one may need to create a new table under *note
cache: cache, first.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : code(hh, Sequence, ProjectiveVariety)                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = -- code for method: hh(Sequence,ProjectiveVariety)                      |
|     ../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/Varieties.m2:784:34-793:7: --source   |
|     code:                                                                   |
|     hh(Sequence,ProjectiveVariety) := (pq,X) -> if X.cache.?hh and X.cache  |
|          (p,q) := pq;                                                       |
|          if class p =!= ZZ or class q =!= ZZ then error "expected integer   |
|          d := dim X;                                                        |
|          pqs := { (p,q), (q,p), (d-p,d-q), (d-q,d-p) };                     |
|          (p,q) = min { (p,q), (q,p), (d-p,d-q), (d-q,d-p) };                |
|          h := rank HH^q cotangentSheaf(p,X);                                |
|          if not X.cache.?hh then X.cache.hh = new MutableHashTable;         |
|          scan(pqs, pq -> X.cache.hh#pq = h);                                |
|          h)                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|.hh#?pq then X.cache.hh#pq else (                                            |
|                                                                             |
|superscripts";                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

