installing assignment methods -- install methods assignment to the value of an operator
***************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        installAssignmentMethod(op,X,Y,f)
  * Inputs:
      * op, a *note keyword: Keyword,, the symbol for a binary operator
      * X, a *note type: Type,, the type of the left-hand operand
      * Y, a *note type: Type,, the type of the right-hand operand
      * f, a *note function: Function,, the method function that will perform
        the assignment
  * Consequences:
      * If the operator to be used is **, say, then op should be symbol **.
        After installing the assignment method, assignments of the form x**y=v
        will be handled by evaluating f(x,y,v).

If the operator is a unary operator, just omit X and its comma.

We illustrate this function by defining a type of mutable list whose elements
can be both extracted and replaced using the operator _.  We also install a
method for *note net: net, so objects of the class can be printed.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = new Type of MutableList                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = M                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Type                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : net M := m -> peek m                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = FunctionClosure[stdio:2:9-2:20]                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : FunctionClosure                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M _ ZZ := (x,i) -> x#i                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = FunctionClosure[stdio:3:10-3:22]                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : FunctionClosure                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : installAssignmentMethod(symbol _, M, ZZ, (x,i,v) -> x#i = v);           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : y = new M from (a..z)                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = M{a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, i, j, k, l, m, n, o, p, q, r, s, t, u, v, w,  |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : M                                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x, y, z}                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : y_12                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = m                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Symbol                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : y_12 = foo                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = foo                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : Symbol                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : y                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = M{a, b, c, d, e, f, g, h, i, j, k, l, foo, n, o, p, q, r, s, t, u, v, w,|
|                                                                             |
|o8 : M                                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x, y, z}                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : y_12                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = foo                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : Symbol                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
For sample applications of this facility, see *note Symbol _ Thing = Thing:
Symbol _us Thing = Thing, and *note MutableMatrix _ Sequence = Thing:
MutableMatrix _us Sequence = Thing,.

Caveat
======

The syntax involved here is not pleasant, so we may change it to something
briefer, something involving yet another assignment operator, distinct from =
and :=.

