installing augmented assignment methods
***************************************

In most cases, the default behavior of *note augmented assignment: augmented
assignment, gives the desired result.  But in some situations, it may be useful
to override this behavior and install a custom method for a given type.

Consider the following example.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Foo = new SelfInitializingType of MutableList;|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : net Foo := x -> net x#0;                      |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Foo + Foo := (x, y) -> Foo {x#0 + y#0};       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : x = Foo {1}                                   |
|                                                   |
|o4 = 1                                             |
|                                                   |
|o4 : Foo                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : y = Foo {2}                                   |
|                                                   |
|o5 = 2                                             |
|                                                   |
|o5 : Foo                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : x += y                                        |
|                                                   |
|o6 = 3                                             |
|                                                   |
|o6 : Foo                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------+

Note that an intermediate Foo object was created and then assigned to x.
Instead, it would be more efficient if x was modified directly.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : installMethod(symbol +=, Foo, (x, y) -> (x#0 += y#0; x));|
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : x += y                                                   |
|                                                              |
|o8 = 5                                                        |
|                                                              |
|o8 : Foo                                                      |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

In some cases, it may be useful to fall back on the default behavior of the
given operator.  When this is desired, the installed method should return the
*note Default: Default, symbol.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : Bar = new SelfInitializingType of List;                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : net Bar := x -> net x#0#0;                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : Bar * Bar := (x, y) -> Bar {{x#0#0 * y#0#0}};                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : installMethod(symbol *=, Bar, (x, y) -> if isMutable x#0 then (|
|              print "using custom method";                           |
|              x#0#0 *= y#0#0; x) else Default)                       |
|                                                                     |
|o12 = FunctionClosure[stdio:12:30-14:39]                             |
|                                                                     |
|o12 : FunctionClosure                                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : x = Bar {new MutableList from {3}}                             |
|                                                                     |
|o13 = 3                                                              |
|                                                                     |
|o13 : Bar                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : y = Bar {{4}}                                                  |
|                                                                     |
|o14 = 4                                                              |
|                                                                     |
|o14 : Bar                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : x *= y                                                         |
|using custom method                                                  |
|                                                                     |
|o15 = 12                                                             |
|                                                                     |
|o15 : Bar                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : y *= x                                                         |
|                                                                     |
|o16 = 48                                                             |
|                                                                     |
|o16 : Bar                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

