File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: lookup, Up: inheritance

lookup -- look up methods
*************************

Description
===========

lookup(M,A) -- provides the unary method named M for class A. The first place
to look is A#M.  The search proceeds with the parent of A, and so on.


lookup(M,A,B) -- provides the binary method named M for (A,B). The first place
to look is Y#(M,A,B) where Y is the younger of A and B.  The search proceeds
next with the parent of B, and so on.


lookup(M,A,B,C) -- provides the ternary method named M for (A,B,C).  The first
place to look is Y#(M,A,B,C) where Y is the youngest of A, B, and C.  The
search proceeds with the parent of C, and so on.


lookup(M,A,B,C,D) -- provides the quaternary method named M for (A,B,C,D).  The
first place to look is Y#(M,A,B,C,D) where Y is the youngest of A, B, C, and D.
The search proceeds with the parent of D, and so on.


lookup x -- where x is a symbol or function, returns x.


If no method is found, then *note null: null, is returned.


See also
========

  * *note #: #, -- length or access to elements
  * *note installMethod: installMethod, -- install methods
  * *note youngest: youngest, -- the youngest member of a sequence

For the programmer
==================

The object *note lookup: lookup, is a *note compiled function:
CompiledFunction,.

