|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/                               |
|demo1.m2:6:0-6:1                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
We see that the value of x is 0, and that explains the error message about
division by zero. The other local symbols are the ones defined in the body of
the function f, whose code can now be displayed with *note code: code,.
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|ii8 : code f                                              |
|                                                          |
|oo8 = /usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.|
|      m2:6:5-9:9: --source code:                          |
|      f := x -> (                                         |
|           a := "hi there";                               |
|           b := 1/x;                                      |
|           b+1)                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
We can use *note step: step, with argument 0 to bypass the current expression.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii9 : step 0                                                                 |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.m2:8:11:(3):[            |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.m2:8:11:(3):             |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.m2:8:                    |
|10-8:13: --source code:                                                      |
|     b := 1/x;                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3]: --stepping limit reached                                                 |
|entering debugger (enter 'help' to see commands)                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
If we decide the problem is one level up, we can use end or the end-of-file
character (which often is CTRL-D) to quit this instance of the debugger.  In
this case, the debugger will be entered again (triggered by the same error
indication that caused it to be entered originally) at the point inside the
function g from which the function f was called.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii10 : end                                                                   |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.m2:13:11:(3): entering   |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo1.m2:13:                   |
|10-13:16: --source code:                                                     |
|     d := f(y-2);                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|debugger (enter 'help' to see commands)                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
We can use *note listLocalSymbols: listLocalSymbols, again to see the local
variables of g.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii11 : listLocalSymbols                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|oo11 = symbol  class                                                         |
|       ------  -----                                                         |
|       c       QQ                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|       d       Nothing                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|       y       ZZ                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|       f       FunctionClosure                                               |
|                                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|value                                                                        |
|-----                                                                        |
|2                                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|null                                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|2                                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|FunctionClosure[/home/m2user/work/M2/M2/M2/Macaulay2/p.                      |
|                                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|location of symbol                                                           |
|------------------                                                           |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/                               |
|demo1.m2:12:5-12:6                                                           |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/                               |
|demo1.m2:13:5-13:6                                                           |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/                               |
|demo1.m2:11:4-11:5                                                           |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/                               |
|demo1.m2:6:0-6:1                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
After we are done debugging, we can quit the debugger entirely and return to
