step -- step by single lines in the debugger
********************************************

  * Usage: 
        step n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,
  * Consequences:
      * This command is active within the debugger.  The current expression is
        executed and execution is continued until n lines of source code whose
        load depth is as large as *note errorDepth: errorDepth, have been
        encountered.  If n is omitted, then 1 is used.  If n is negative then
        instead, n microsteps in the inner interpreter are executed and traced.

Description
===========

One useful way to debug code suspected of being in error is to insert an
explicit error message, such as error "debug me", and start stepping from
there, as in the following demonstration.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : load "Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2"                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : code f                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = /usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.                    |
|     m2:6:4-12:6: --source code:                                             |
|     f = t -> (                                                              |
|          x := 1;                                                            |
|          error "debug me";                                                  |
|          y := t+1;                                                          |
|          z := 1/t;                                                          |
|          w := x+t;                                                          |
|          )                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f 0                                                                     |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:8:10:(3):[2]: error   |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:8:10:(3): entering    |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:8:5                   |
|-8:21: --source code:                                                        |
|     error "debug me";                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|: debug me                                                                   |
|debugger (enter 'help' to see commands)                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii4 : return                                                                 |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:9:11:(3):[            |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:9:11:(3):             |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:9:5                   |
|-9:13: --source code:                                                        |
|     y := t+1;                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|2]: --stepping limit reached                                                 |
|entering debugger (enter 'help' to see commands)                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii5 : current                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|oo5 = local-assign 2 0 2-OP + local-fetch 0 0                                |
|                              1                                              |
|                                                                             |
|oo5 : PseudocodeClosure                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii6 : disassemble oo                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|oo6 = (local-assign 2 0 (2-OP + (local-fetch 0 0) 1))                        |
