assert -- check whether something is true, raise an error if not
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        assert x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note thing: Thing,, 

Description
===========

assert x raises an error if x isn't true.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : stopIfError = false;                     |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : assert( (2+2) === 4)                     |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert(rank matrix {{1, 2}, {2, 4}} == 2)|
|stdio:3:6:(3):[1]: error: assertion failed    |
+----------------------------------------------+

If x is an *note Expression: Expression, that evaluates to false, then a
partially evaluated form is printed with the error message to assist in
debugging.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert Equation(rank matrix {{1, 2}, {2, 4}}, 2)|
|stdio:4:6:(3):[1]: error: assertion failed:          |
|1 == 2 is false                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note generateAssertions: generateAssertions, -- generate assert statements
    from experimental input
  * *note stopIfError: stopIfError, -- whether to stop the program when an
    error occurs

Ways to use assert:
===================

  * "assert(Expression)"
  * "assert(Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

