benchmark -- accurate timing of execution
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        benchmark s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: String,, a string containing Macaulay2 code
  * Outputs:
      * a *note real number: RR,, the number of seconds it takes to evaluate
        the code in s

Description
===========

Produces an accurate timing for the code contained in the string s.  The value
returned is the number of seconds.
+------------------------------+
|i1 : benchmark "sqrt 2p100000"|
|                              |
|o1 = .0003130694860205697     |
|                              |
|o1 : RR (of precision 53)     |
+------------------------------+
The snippet of code provided will be run enough times to register meaningfully
on the clock, and the garbage collector will be called beforehand.

For the programmer
==================

The object *note benchmark: benchmark, is a *note function closure:
FunctionClosure,.

