breakpoint -- set a breakpoint to stop execution at a particular point in the code and enter the debugger
*********************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        breakpoint s
  * Consequences:
      * At the time the code including breakpoint s is executed, the execution
        will stop right before s, and the debugger will be entered.

Description
===========

Setting a breakpoint is a way to stop execution at a particular point in the
code and enter the debugger. Then, commands like step continue finish and so on
as in the following demonstration.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : load "Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2"                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : code h                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = /usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.                    |
|     m2:28:4-33:1: --source code:                                            |
|     h = t -> (                                                              |
|          x := 1;                                                            |
|          breakpoint y := t+1;                                               |
|          z := 1/t;                                                          |
|          w := x+t;                                                          |
|     )                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : h 1                                                                     |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:30:22:(3): entering   |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:30:                   |
|16-30:24: --source code:                                                     |
|     breakpoint y := t+1;                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|debugger (enter 'help' to see commands)                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii4 : step                                                                   |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:30:22:(3):[           |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:31:11:(3):[           |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:31:11:(3):            |
|/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/Macaulay2Doc/demos/demo2.m2:31:                   |
|5-31:13: --source code:                                                      |
|     z := 1/t;                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|2]: unhandled step command                                                   |
|2]: --stepping limit reached                                                 |
|entering debugger (enter 'help' to see commands)                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|ii5 : finish                                                                 |
|stdio:3:1:(3):[1]: --done stepping, returning to top level                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

