handleInterrupts
****************

  * Usage: 
        handleInterrupts = b
  * Inputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: Boolean,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, the value of b
  * Consequences:
      * If b is *note false: false,, then the default operating system actions
        for the signals SIGINT, and SIGALRM are restored, and thus typing
        CTRL-C or the triggering of an *note alarm: alarm, will result in the
        Macaulay2 process terminating immediately. If b is *note true: true,,
        then the default Macaulay2 signal handlers are installed, and thus
        control will be returned to top level after the code currently
        executing notices that the interrupt flag has been set.

Description
===========

The command line option --int has the same effect as handleInterrupts=false.

For the programmer
==================

The object *note handleInterrupts: handleInterrupts, is a *note Boolean value:
Boolean,.

