commandInterpreter -- the top level command interpreter
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        commandInterpreter f
  * Inputs:
      * f, () or a *note dictionary: Dictionary,, a *note symbol: Symbol,, an
        instance of the type *note Pseudocode: Pseudocode,, or a *note
        function: Function,
  * Consequences:
      * the top level command interpreter will be called with the symbols in
        the lexical scope of f visible to the user.

Description
===========

One more i will be added to prompt each time the command interpreter is
entered.  To leave it, type end or the end of file character.
+--------------------------+
|i1 : f = (x -> y -> 11) 13|
|                          |
|o1 = f                    |
|                          |
|o1 : FunctionClosure      |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : commandInterpreter f |
+--------------------------+
|ii3 : x                   |
|                          |
|oo3 = 13                  |
+--------------------------+
|ii4 : end                 |
+--------------------------+
|i5 : x                    |
|                          |
|o5 = x                    |
|                          |
|o5 : Symbol               |
+--------------------------+
This facility is useful as a debugging tool, and is used by the standard
debugger.

