on -- trace a function each time it's run
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        on f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note function: Function,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CallLimit => an *note integer: ZZ,, default value 100000, the maximum
        number of times to permit the function f to be called
      * Name => a *note string: String,, default value null, the name to use
        for the function, in case f is an anonymous function (not assigned to a
        global variable)
      * GenerateAssertions => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value
        false, whether to print assertion statements that can be used as input
        to Macaulay2 to check the behavior of the function remains the same.
        Arguments and values are prepared with *note toExternalString:
        toExternalString,, failure of which is silently ignored.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note function: Function,, a new function that returns the same
        values that f would have returned, but has a few side effects useful
        for debugging: upon entry, it prints its arguments, and upon exit it
        prints its return values.  The display includes the name of f, a
        sequence number in parentheses that tells how many times the function
        has been called, and a number in brackets that gives the nesting
        (recursion) depth. The sequence number allows the entry and exit
        reports to be connected.

Description
===========

Ideally, this function would replace f, i.e., we would write f = on f.
Unfortunately, all the pre-installed system functions are write-protected;
fortunately, their methods are not, and can be replaced.

