packages -- Macaulay2 packages
******************************

A package is a body of Macaulay2 source code devoted to a particular topic.
Many packages are distributed with Macaulay2, and others are available from the
author's homepage.

To load a package, say FirstPackage, use either of the following methods.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : loadPackage "FirstPackage" |
|                                |
|o1 = FirstPackage               |
|                                |
|o1 : Package                    |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : needsPackage "FirstPackage"|
|                                |
|o2 = FirstPackage               |
|                                |
|o2 : Package                    |
+--------------------------------+

For technical information about packages, see *note Package: Package,.

Macaulay2 searches for the file FirstPackage.m2 on your search *note path:
path,. The packages provided with Macaulay2 are on your search path, as is your
current working directory.

Using existing packages

  * *note loadPackage: loadPackage, -- load a package
  * *note needsPackage: needsPackage, -- load a package if not already loaded
  * *note dismiss: dismiss, -- dismiss a package
  * *note importFrom: importFrom, -- import symbols to the current private
    dictionary
  * *note loadedPackages: loadedPackages, -- the list of loaded packages

Creating a new package

  * *note creating a package: creating a package,
  * *note newPackage: newPackage, -- the preamble of a package
  * *note installPackage: installPackage, -- load and install a package and its
    documentation
  * *note uninstallPackage: uninstallPackage, -- uninstall a package and remove
    its documentation

Writing documentation for a package

  * *note writing documentation: writing documentation,
  * *note doc: (SimpleDoc)doc, -- a simple documentation function

Debugging a package

  * *note the debugger: the debugger,
  * *note debug(Package): debug_lpPackage_rp, -- open the private dictionary of
    a package
  * *note check(Package): check, -- perform tests of a package

Documentation for the packages provided with Macaulay2 is already installed. To
install documentation for another package, use *note installPackage:
installPackage,.

installPackage FirstPackage

You may see what packages have been loaded with the variable *note
loadedPackages: loadedPackages,.

See also
========

  * *note creating a package: creating a package,
  * *note packages provided with Macaulay2: packages provided with Macaulay2,
* Menu:

* Package::                     the class of all packages

Accessing packages
* loadedPackages::              the list of loaded packages
* package::                     get containing package
* loadPackage::                 load a package
* readPackage::                 read the package preamble
* needsPackage::                load a package if not already loaded
* installPackage::              load and install a package and its documentation
* installedPackages::
* uninstallPackage::            uninstall a package and remove its documentation
* uninstallAllPackages::

Interacting with packages
* importFrom::                  import symbols to the current private dictionary
* tests::                       locate a package's tests
* use::                         install or activate object
* use(Package): use_lpPackage_rp.  activate a previously dismissed package
* check(Package): check.        perform tests of a package
* debug(Package): debug_lpPackage_rp.  open the private dictionary of a package
* dismiss(Package): dismiss.    dismiss a package
* options(Package): options_lpPackage_rp.

Miscellaneous nodes
* makePackageIndex::            create an index of installed packages
* PackageDictionary::           the dictionary for names of packages
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

