loadPackage -- load a package
*****************************

  * Usage: 
        loadPackage PackageName
  * Inputs:
      * PackageName, a *note string: String,, the name of the package, or a
        *note Package: Package, object
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * FileName => a *note string: String,, default value null, the name of
        the file containing the source code of the package, from which it
        should be loaded
      * LoadDocumentation => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value
        false, whether to load the documentation of the package, too; see *note
        beginDocumentation: beginDocumentation,
      * DebuggingMode => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value null,
        the value of *note debuggingMode: debuggingMode, during loading the
        package; specifying it here overrides the value specified as an option
        to *note newPackage: newPackage, by the package itself; however, if
        *note debuggingMode: debuggingMode, is already false it will remain so.
      * Configuration => a *note list: List,, default value {}, the entries are
        options KEY => VALUE overriding the defaults specified in the source
        code of the package and the (possibly updated) values in the file in
        the user's application directory.
      * Reload => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value null, whether
        to reload the package, if it has been loaded before. If the input was
        an already loaded *note Package: Package,, this is automatically set to
        true.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note package: Package,, the package just loaded; if the input was an
        already loaded *note Package: Package,, this is the reloaded package
  * Consequences:
      * Loads (or reloads) the package PackageName that is in the file
        PackageName.m2.

Description
===========

The file PackageName.m2 should be on the load *note path: path, and should
contain a package named PackageName.

If the variable *note notify: notify, is set to true, then an informational
message is displayed after the file is loaded.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : notify = true                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : loadPackage "FirstPackage"                                              |
| -- loading FirstPackage.m2                                                  |
| -- opening database /usr/local/lib/Macaulay2/FirstPackage/cache/rawdocumenta|
| -- beginDocumentation: using documentation database, skipping the rest of /u|
| -- package "FirstPackage" loaded                                            |
| -- loaded /usr/local/share/Macaulay2/FirstPackage.m2                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = FirstPackage                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Package                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|tion-dcba-8.db                                                               |
|sr/local/share/Macaulay2/FirstPackage.m2                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If the input is a loaded package, then this command will reload the package
instead:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : loadPackage FirstPackage                                                |
| -- warning: reloading FirstPackage; recreate instances of types from this pa|
| -- closing database /usr/local/lib/Macaulay2/FirstPackage/cache/rawdocumenta|
| -- loading FirstPackage.m2                                                  |
| -- beginDocumentation: reading the rest of /usr/local/share/Macaulay2/FirstP|
| -- package "FirstPackage" loaded                                            |
| -- loaded /usr/local/share/Macaulay2/FirstPackage.m2                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = FirstPackage                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Package                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|ckage                                                                        |
|tion-dcba-8.db                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|ackage.m2                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In fact this version of the command is simply a convenient shortcut for
loadPackage with the option Reload overridden to true.

See also
========

  * *note packages: packages, -- Macaulay2 packages
  * *note readPackage: readPackage, -- read the package preamble
  * *note dismiss: dismiss, -- dismiss a package
  * *note needsPackage: needsPackage, -- load a package if not already loaded
  * *note packages provided with Macaulay2: packages provided with Macaulay2,

Ways to use loadPackage:
========================

  * "loadPackage(Package)"
  * "loadPackage(String)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note loadPackage: loadPackage, is a *note method function with
options: MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

