needsPackage -- load a package if not already loaded
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        needsPackage PackageName
  * Inputs:
      * PackageName, a *note string: String,, the name of the package
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * FileName => a *note string: String,, default value null, the name of
        the file containing the source code of the package, from which it
        should be loaded
      * LoadDocumentation => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value
        false, whether to load the documentation of the package, too; see *note
        beginDocumentation: beginDocumentation,
      * DebuggingMode => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value null,
        the value of the variable *note debuggingMode: debuggingMode, during
        loading the package; specifying it here overrides the value specified
        as an option to *note newPackage: newPackage, by the package itself
      * Configuration => a *note list: List,, default value {}, the entries are
        options KEY => VALUE overriding the defaults specified in the source
        code of the package and the (possibly updated) values in the file in
        the user's application directory.
      * Reload => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value null, whether
        to reload the package, if it has been loaded from a different source
        before
  * Outputs:
      * a *note package: Package,, the package requested
  * Consequences:
      * loads the package PackageName by loading the file PackageName.m2 which
        should appear in one of the directories occurring in the list *note
        path: path,, unless it has already been loaded, in which case it
        ensures that the package's dictionary of exported symbols occurs in
        *note dictionaryPath: dictionaryPath, and are thus available to the
        user. In addition, the function *note needsPackage: needsPackage, is
        applied to each of the packages whose names are specified by the *note
        newPackage(...,PackageExports=>...): newPackage, option for the
        requested package. If the variable *note notify: notify, is set to
        true, then an informational message is displayed after the file is
        loaded.

Description
===========

For example, to load the sample package FirstPackage:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : notify = true                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : needsPackage "FirstPackage"                                             |
| -- loading FirstPackage.m2                                                  |
| -- opening database /usr/local/lib/Macaulay2/FirstPackage/cache/rawdocumenta|
| -- beginDocumentation: using documentation database, skipping the rest of /u|
| -- package "FirstPackage" loaded                                            |
| -- loaded /usr/local/share/Macaulay2/FirstPackage.m2                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = FirstPackage                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Package                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|tion-dcba-8.db                                                               |
|sr/local/share/Macaulay2/FirstPackage.m2                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : needsPackage "FirstPackage"                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = FirstPackage                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Package                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The second time the package was not reloaded.

