installPackage -- load and install a package and its documentation
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        installPackage PackageName
  * Inputs:
      * PackageName, a *note string: String,, or *note Package: Package,, the
        package to install
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * FileName => a *note string: String,, default value null, the name of
        the file containing the source code of the package, from which it
        should be loaded
      * UserMode => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value null, if
        true, then do not give the -q option to the Macaulay2 executable when
        running examples, thereby allowing it to load the user's *note
        initialization file: initialization file,, allowing it to load packages
        previously installed in the user's *note application directory:
        applicationDirectory,, and allowing packages it loads to read their
        configuration files from the user's *note application directory:
        applicationDirectory,. If false, then do give the option. If *note
        null: null,, then propagate the option from the current *note
        commandLine: commandLine,, if one occurs there.
      * DebuggingMode => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value null,
        whether to enter *note the debugger: the debugger, if an error occurs
        during installation; however, if *note debuggingMode: debuggingMode, is
        already false, it will remain so.
      * RerunExamples => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value false,
        whether to rerun all the examples during installation
      * RunExamples => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value true,
        whether to run the examples during installation
      * IgnoreExampleErrors => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value
        false, whether to ignore errors that occur during the running of
        examples during installation
      * CheckDocumentation => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value
        true, whether to check the package's documentation for consistency and
        completeness
      * MakeDocumentation => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value
        true, whether to make the documentation for the package during
        installation
      * MakeHTML => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value true,
        whether to make HTML documentation. This is a form of the documentation
        that can be viewed using a browser.
      * MakeInfo => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value true,
        whether to make the info pages. This is a form of the documentation
        that can be viewed using the Unix command info or using emacs
      * MakePDF => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value false,
        whether to make PDF documentation
      * InstallPrefix => a *note string: String,, default value
        "/home/m2user/.Macaulay2/local/", the installation prefix for
        installation of the files of the package, in case encapsulation is not
        enabled, or for installation of the links to the files, in case
        encapsulation is enabled. The default value is the subdirectory named
        local of the user's *note application directory: applicationDirectory,.
      * RemakeAllDocumentation => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default
        value true, whether to regenerate all of the help pages for this
        package. The default action is to rebuild only the html pages of the
        documentation entries that have been changed since the last time the
        package was installed. However, some changes to an entry, such as to
        its headline, will change the html of other pages that cross-reference
        it.
      * CacheExampleOutput => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value
        null, whether to cache (newer) example output in a subdirectory of the
        *note auxiliary file directory: newPackage, named examples for use in a
        future installation. This value, if set to true or false, will override
        any value explicitly specified when *note newPackage: newPackage, is
        called. After the directory is created, it will be necessary for the
        user to specify AuxiliaryFiles => true with the *note newPackage:
        newPackage, command.
      * SeparateExec => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value false,
        whether to install the files of the package in two separate directory
        trees, one for the architecture independent files, and one for the
        architecture dependent files
      * Verbose => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value false,
        whether to display some details of the installation procedure. For even
        more information set *note debugLevel: debugLevel, to a number greater
        than 0 or a number greater than 5.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note package: Package,, the package that was installed
  * Consequences:
      * The package is installed in a local directory, so that in the future,
        one may simply use *note loadPackage: loadPackage,. Documentation for
        the package is also produced, running any Macaulay2 examples that are
        requested in the package documentation, with the random number seed
        initialized to 0.

Description
===========

The main action of this routine is to generate the documentation of the given
package and install the Macaulay2 package and documentation.

The actual file loaded is PackageName.m2, which should be on the load *note
path: path, and should contain a package named PackageName.

In order to accomplish this, several steps are performed (or bypassed,
depending on the values of the optional arguments).

  * load the package, if not already loaded (see *note loadPackage:
    loadPackage,)
  * determine which help pages have changed since last install
  * run any new or previously failed examples, or all examples, as specified by
    the RerunExamples option
  * generate the html pages, or not, as specified by the MakeHTML option, for
    the modified help pages, or all html pages if RemakeAllDocumentation is set
    to true
  * generate the info pages, or not, as specified by the MakeInfo option
  * install the documentation and package in the location specified by the
    InstallPrefix option
  * place a link to this html documentation in the file index.html in the
    user's *note application directory: applicationDirectory,; see *note
    makePackageIndex: makePackageIndex,

The current value of *note prefixPath: prefixPath, is used to determine how to
direct documentation hyperlinks; the link will be directed to the appropriate
file if one is found by searching the trees referred to by *note prefixPath:
prefixPath,. Otherwise, all documentation hyperlinks are relative to positions
within a single tree of directories, as describe by *note Layout:
currentLayout,.

It might be necessary to run *note installPackage: installPackage, twice if a
package with the same name is already installed: the second installation will
redirect the hyperlinks to the freshly installed documentation, because the
files will have been installed by the first installation. This applies, for
example, to those authors who are developing updates to packages already
included with Macaulay2.

The files of the package are placed in subdirectories of the appropriate prefix
directory as specified by *note Layout: currentLayout,, depending on the value
of the SeparateExec option:



Install paths given SeparateExec => false:

  * share/Macaulay2/PackageName.m2,
  * share/info/PackageName.info,
  * lib/Macaulay2/PackageName/,
  * share/Macaulay2/PackageName/, and
  * share/doc/Macaulay2/PackageName/;

Install paths given SeparateExec => true:

  * common/share/Macaulay2/PackageName.m2,
  * common/share/info/PackageName.info,
  * x86_64-Linux-Ubuntu-24.04/lib/Macaulay2/PackageName/,
  * common/share/Macaulay2/PackageName/, and
  * common/share/doc/Macaulay2/PackageName/.

Note that in the latter case, the paths reflect the type of your machine. In
addition, if no errors occurred during running the examples, then an empty file
whose name is lib/Macaulay2/PackageName/.installed or
x86_64-Linux-Ubuntu-24.04/lib/Macaulay2/PackageName/.installed is created, to
signify that installation was completed.



Caveat
======

Links from html files containing documentation to documentation in another
package not yet installed may go to the wrong place, because it is assumed that
the package not yet installed will be installed under the same prefix. By
contrast, if the other package has already been installed under some prefix
occurring in the value of *note prefixPath: prefixPath,, then the correct path
will be used.  To get two packages installed under different prefixes which
refer to each other's documentation correctly, it may be necessary to install
one of them twice.

See also
========

  * *note Layout: currentLayout, -- relative locations of Macaulay2 files
  * *note packages: packages, -- Macaulay2 packages
  * *note prefixPath: prefixPath, -- absolute locations of Macaulay2 files
  * *note installedPackages: installedPackages,
  * *note uninstallAllPackages: uninstallAllPackages,
  * *note uninstallPackage: uninstallPackage, -- uninstall a package and remove
    its documentation

Ways to use installPackage:
===========================

  * "installPackage(Package)"
  * "installPackage(String)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note installPackage: installPackage, is a *note method function
with options: MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

