importFrom -- import symbols to the current private dictionary
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        importFrom(pkg, {"symbol1", "symbol2"})
  * Inputs:
      * pkg, a *note package: Package, or a *note string: String,, the package
        containing the private symbols
      * a *note string: String, or a *note list: List,, of strings,
        corresponding to the private *note symbols: Symbol, to export from the
        package
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: List,, of *note symbols: Symbol,
  * Consequences:
      * package symbols provided in the list will be added to the private *note
        dictionary: Dictionary, of the *note current package: currentPackage,,
        but will not be exported

Description
===========

This function can be used to import specific symbols from the private
dictionary of another package into the private dictionary of the *note current
package: currentPackage,.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : importFrom_Core {"raw"}|
|                            |
|o1 = {raw}                  |
|                            |
|o1 : List                   |
+----------------------------+
|i2 : raw random(ZZ^2, ZZ^2) |
|                            |
|o2 = 8 3                    |
|     1 7                    |
|                            |
|                            |
|o2 : RawMatrix              |
+----------------------------+

To import all private symbols of a package, use *note debug(Package):
debug_lpPackage_rp, instead. The symbols imported with this function can then
be exported using *note export: export, or *note exportMutable: exportMutable,.

See also
========

  * *note debug(Package): debug_lpPackage_rp, -- open the private dictionary of
    a package
  * *note exportFrom: exportFrom, -- export symbols from a package's private
    dictionary
  * *note Dictionary: Dictionary, -- the class of all dictionaries

