tests -- locate a package's tests
*********************************

  * Usage: 
        tests pkg
        tests(i, pkg)
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: ZZ,, 
      * pkg, a *note package: Package, or a *note string: String,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note numbered vertical list: NumberedVerticalList, or a *note test
        input: tests,,

Description
===========

When an integer is not provided, this returns all the tests for the given
package.  The position of each element would be passed as the first argument of
*note check: check, to run the test. Each value is a TestInput object.  These
are printed with the location of the file so that you may quickly jump to the
source code of the test when using Emacs.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : tests "FirstPackage"                                                    |
| -- warning: reloading FirstPackage; recreate instances of types from this   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {0 => TestInput[../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/FirstPackage.m2:54:5  |
|     {1 => TestInput[../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/FirstPackage.m2:58:5  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : NumberedVerticalList                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|package                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|-56:3]}                                                                      |
|-60:3]}                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If the test number is also provided, then the corresponding TestInput object is
returned.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : t = tests(0, "FirstPackage")                                          |
|                                                                           |
|o2 = TestInput[../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/FirstPackage.m2:54:5-56:3]|
|                                                                           |
|o2 : TestInput                                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The *note locate: locate, and *note code: code, functions do the expected thing
when given a TestInput object.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : locate t                                                             |
|                                                                          |
|o3 = ../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/FirstPackage.m2:54:5-56:3          |
|                                                                          |
|o3 : FilePosition                                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : code t                                                               |
|                                                                          |
|o4 = ../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/FirstPackage.m2:54:5-56:3: --source|
|     code:                                                                |
|     TEST ///                                                             |
|         assert ( firstFunction 2 == "D'oh!" )                            |
|     ///                                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Passing only the key of the desired test to *note code: code, is supported as
well.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : code 0                                                               |
|                                                                          |
|o5 = ../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/FirstPackage.m2:54:5-56:3: --source|
|     code:                                                                |
|     TEST ///                                                             |
|         assert ( firstFunction 2 == "D'oh!" )                            |
|     ///                                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

You may also pass a TestInput object to *note edit: edit, to open the code in
your favorite editor.

Ways to use tests:
==================

  * "tests(Package)"
  * "tests(String)"
  * "tests(ZZ,Package)"
  * "tests(ZZ,String)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note tests: tests, is a *note method function: MethodFunction,.

