check -- perform tests of a package
***********************************

  * Usage: 
        check pkg
        check(i, pkg)
        check(L, pkg)
  * Inputs:
      * pkg, a *note package: Package, or a *note string: String,, the package
        to test
      * i, an *note integer: ZZ,, the index of a test to run
      * L, a *note list: List,, containing indices of tests to run, or {} to
        run all tests
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * UserMode => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value null, if
        true, do not use the -q in arguments to the Macaulay2 executable when
        running tests, thereby allowing it to load the user's *note
        initialization file: initialization file,, allowing it to load packages
        previously installed in the user's *note application directory:
        applicationDirectory, and allowing packages it loads to read their
        configuration files from the user's *note application directory:
        applicationDirectory,. If false, the -q argument is added. If *note
        null: null,, then add -q if it appears as an option in *note
        commandLine: commandLine,.
      * Verbose => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value false, if
        true, then print the output of all failing tests
  * Consequences:
      * the tests in the package pkg are run (in separate Macaulay2 processes,
        with the random number seed initialized to 0), and any errors are
        reported.
      * if i is given, only the i-th test in the package is run and any errors
        are reported.

Description
===========

It is important for package authors to provide tests to ensure that the package
is functioning properly. One provides tests using the *note TEST: TEST,
function following the *note beginDocumentation: beginDocumentation, call in
the source of the package.

Optionally, one can add files to the tests directory under the auxiliary
subdirectory of the package.  The contents of each file will automatically be
included as one of the package's tests.

For example, to run the tests for the *note FirstPackage: (FirstPackage)Top,
package, use:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : needsPackage "FirstPackage"                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = FirstPackage                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Package                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : check_1 FirstPackage                                                    |
| -- warning: reloading FirstPackage; recreate instances of types from this   |
| -- capturing check(1, "FirstPackage")        -- .145875s elapsed            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|package                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : check FirstPackage                                                      |
| -- capturing check(0, "FirstPackage")        -- .142468s elapsed            |
| -- capturing check(1, "FirstPackage")        -- .141647s elapsed            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Alternatively, if the package is installed somewhere accessible, one can do the
following.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : check_1 "FirstPackage"                                      |
| -- capturing check(1, "FirstPackage")        -- .141795s elapsed|
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : check "FirstPackage"                                        |
| -- capturing check(0, "FirstPackage")        -- .142449s elapsed|
| -- capturing check(1, "FirstPackage")        -- .141607s elapsed|
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

A *note TestInput: tests, object (or a list of such objects) can also be run
directly.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : tests(1, "FirstPackage")                                              |
|                                                                           |
|o6 = TestInput[/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/FirstPackage.m2:58:5-60:3]       |
|                                                                           |
|o6 : TestInput                                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : check oo                                                              |
| -- capturing check(1, "FirstPackage")        -- .142331s elapsed          |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : tests "FirstPackage"                                                  |
|                                                                           |
|o8 = {0 => TestInput[/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/FirstPackage.m2:54:5-56:3]}|
|     {1 => TestInput[/usr/local/share/Macaulay2/FirstPackage.m2:58:5-60:3]}|
|                                                                           |
