TEST -- add a test for a package
********************************

  * Usage: 
        TEST s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: String,, containing Macaulay2 code; 
  * Consequences:
      * registers the string s as a test of the *note current package:
        currentPackage,.

Description
===========

This function should only occur in the documentation section of a package;
i.e., after *note beginDocumentation: beginDocumentation,. Use *note check:
check, to run all of the tests associated to a package.

For an example, see *note docExample: (SimpleDoc)docExample, and *note an
example of a package: an example of a package,.

If a test should be skipped when running *note check: check,, e.g., it is known
to fail under certain circumstances, then the comment -* no-check-flag *- may
be added to s.

Caveat
======

When creating tests, try to ensure that they run relatively quickly.

See also
========

  * *note assert: assert, -- check whether something is true, raise an error if
    not
  * *note beginDocumentation: beginDocumentation, -- start documentation
    section of a package
  * *note check: check, -- perform tests of a package

