hypertext list format
*********************

Documentation text is composed of a list of text and hypertext items. A single
text string, even though it is not a list, is generally accepted as a hypertext
list. Macaulay2 examples may be included in the list using the *note EXAMPLE:
EXAMPLE, tag. See *note Text: (Text)Top, for the full list of hypertext types.

Each element of the list may be a text string, or one of the elements below.
The following items are used by themselves:

  * *note BR: (Text)BR, -- line break
  * *note HR: (Text)HR, -- hypertext HR element (horizontal rule)

Items that take a text string (or other hypertext list) as argument:

  * *note HEADER1: (Text)HEADER1, -- hypertext HEADER1 item
  * *note HEADER2: (Text)HEADER2, -- hypertext HEADER2 item
  * *note HEADER3: (Text)HEADER3, -- hypertext HEADER3 item
  * *note HEADER4: (Text)HEADER4, -- hypertext HEADER4 item
  * *note HEADER5: (Text)HEADER5, -- hypertext HEADER5 item
  * *note HEADER6: (Text)HEADER6, -- hypertext HEADER6 item
  * *note HEADER2: (Text)HEADER2, -- hypertext HEADER2 item
  * *note PARA: (Text)PARA, -- hypertext paragraph container
  * *note SPAN: (Text)SPAN, -- hypertext span
  * *note ITALIC: (Text)ITALIC, -- hypertext italic font
  * *note TT: (Text)TT, -- hypertext TT item
  * *note EM: (Text)EM, -- hypertext EM item
  * *note PRE: (Text)PRE, -- preformatted text
  * *note SUB: (Text)SUB, -- hypertext subscript
  * *note SUP: (Text)SUP, -- hypertext superscript

Items that place hyperlinks into the documentation:

  * *note HREF: (Text)HREF, -- hypertext link
  * *note TO: (Text)TO, -- hypertext documentation link
  * *note TO2: (Text)TO2, -- labeled hypertext documentation link
  * *note TOH: (Text)TOH, -- hypertext documentation link followed by a
    headline

Other useful hypertext elements:

  * *note OL: (Text)OL, -- hypertext OL item
  * *note UL: (Text)UL, -- hypertext UL item
  * *note LI: (Text)LI, -- hypertext list item
  * *note DL: (Text)DL, -- hypertext DL element
  * *note DT: (Text)DT, -- hypertext DT element
  * *note DD: (Text)DD, -- hypertext DD element
  * *note CODE: (Text)CODE, -- hypertext CODE item
  * *note EXAMPLE: EXAMPLE, -- construct a hypertext item from a Macaulay2
    input string



Example
=======

For example, the hypertext list:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|{  HR{}, "When referring to a ", EM "Macaulay2", " identifier such as ", TT  |
|        ", use the TT element, or use a cross-reference, as in ", TO matrix, |
|        " examples (during ", TO (installPackage,String), ") as illustrated  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|"matrix",                                                                    |
| ".  Incorporate ", EM "Macaulay2",                                          |
|here.", EXAMPLE "matrix{{1,2},{3,4}}", HR{} }                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

when used as the input to *note document: document, produces:

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
When referring to a Macaulay2 identifier such as matrix, use the TT element, or
use a cross-reference, as in *note matrix: matrix,.  Incorporate Macaulay2
examples (during *note installPackage(String): installPackage,) as illustrated
here.
+------------------------+
|i1 : matrix{{1,2},{3,4}}|
|                        |
|o1 = | 1 2 |            |
|     | 3 4 |            |
|                        |
|              2       2 |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ  |
+------------------------+
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

