html -- convert to HTML format
******************************

  * Usage: 
        html x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note thing: Thing,, any Macaulay2 object
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: String,, the HTML rendering of x

Description
===========

html x converts x to HTML format.

The return value is a string that is suitable for use in a .html file readable
by a browser. *note hypertext: hypertext, elements are translated into the
corresponding HTML elements. When no HTML conversion is available, *note tex:
tex, is called. $\LaTeX$ can be rendered in the browser using MathJax or
$\KaTeX$.

See also
