net -- format for printing, as a net
************************************

  * Usage: 
        net o
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note thing: Thing,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note net: Net,, obtained by formatting o for printing

Description
===========

This function is the primary function called upon by *note <<: <<, to format
expressions for printing. The default method provided by the system is to
convert o to an *note Expression: Expression, with *note expression:
expression, and then to convert that to a *note Net: Net,.

A new method for formatting expressions of type T may be installed as follows:

+-----------------+
|net T := x -> ...|
+-----------------+

The function provided by the user should return a *note Net: Net, or a *note
String: String,.

There are various such methods for formatting, but we don't document them
separately.

See also
========

  * *note String: String, -- the class of all strings
  * *note Expression: Expression, -- the class of all expressions
  * *note AfterPrint: AfterPrint, -- top level method applied after printing
  * *note toString: toString, -- convert to a string
  * *note toExternalString: toExternalString, -- convert to a readable string
  * *note expression: expression, -- convert to an expression

