document -- create a documentation node
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        document { Key => key, ... }
  * Inputs:
      * a *note list: List,, with *note Hypertext: (Text)Hypertext,, *note
        String: String,, and special documentation entries as optional
        arguments such as Key => "..." (required)
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Key: Key, => a *note list: List,, default value null, key of a
        documentation node
      * *note Headline: Headline, => a *note list: List,, default value null,
        headline of a documentation node
      * *note BaseFunction: BaseFunction, => a *note list: List,, default value
        null, the basename of a function in a documentation node
      * *note Usage: Usage, => a *note list: List,, default value null, ways to
        use a function in a documentation node
      * *note Inputs: Inputs, => a *note list: List,, default value null,
        inputs for a function in a documentation node
      * *note Outputs: Outputs, => a *note list: List,, default value null,
        outputs for a function in a documentation node
      * *note Consequences: Consequences, => a *note list: List,, default value
        null, side-effects of a function in a documentation node
      * *note Acknowledgement: Acknowledgement, => a *note list: List,, default
        value null, acknowledgements listed in a documentation node
      * *note Contributors: Contributors, => a *note list: List,, default value
        null, non-author contributors listed in a documentation node
      * *note References: References, => a *note list: List,, default value
        null, references listed in a documentation node
      * *note Caveat: Caveat, => a *note list: List,, default value null,
        warnings or limitations listed in a documentation node
      * *note SeeAlso: SeeAlso, => a *note list: List,, default value null,
        cross-references to other documentation nodes
      * *note Subnodes: Subnodes, => a *note list: List,, default value null, a
        menu of documentation nodes
      * *note SourceCode: SourceCode, => a *note list: List,, default value
        null, sources displayed in a documentation node
      * *note ExampleFiles: ExampleFiles, => a *note list: List,, default value
        null, data files corresponding to a documentation node
      * *note Citation: Citation, => a *note list: List,, default value null,
        package citation information
  * Consequences:
      * formatted documentation is created and stored in the *note current
        package: currentPackage,

Description
===========

There are two basic types of documentation:

  0. Documenting a function or a method, as in *note ideal(List):
     ideal_lpList_rp,.
  1. documenting an overview or functions with methods, as in *note ideals:
     ideals, or *note ideal: ideal, respectively.

The headings *note Usage: Usage,, *note BaseFunction: BaseFunction,, *note
Inputs: Inputs,, *note Outputs: Outputs,, and *note Consequences:
Consequences,, are useful only for documentation of the first type, as well as
in a call to *note SYNOPSIS: SYNOPSIS,.



Templates for using the *note document(List): document, method

  * *note package documentation template: package documentation template,
  * *note function documentation template: function documentation template,
  * *note optional argument documentation template: optional argument
    documentation template,
  * *note overview documentation template: overview documentation template,

Here is a basic template:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|    document {                                                               |
|        Key          => {myFunc, (myFunc, MyType), [myFunc, MyOption], ...}, |
|        Headline     => "one line description of myFunc", -- not needed for  |
|        BaseFunction => myFunc, -- usually not needed                        |
|        Usage        => "myFunc x",                                          |
|        Inputs       => { inputs, ... },                                     |
|        Outputs      => { outputs, ... },                                    |
|        SourceCode   => { METHOD1, ... }, -- usually not needed              |
|        Consequences => { side-effects, ... },                               |
|        "A list of strings containing names of files in the auxiliary        |
|        directory of the package can go here; the files will be visible      |
|        in the current directory while example code is run.",                |
|        ExampleFiles => {"datafile1", "datafile2"},                          |
|        "There can be explanatory prose here in the form of a hypertext list |
|        EXAMPLE lines ///                                                    |
|          m2code                                                             |
|          m2code                                                             |
|          m2code                                                             |
|        ///,                                                                 |
|        "There can be explanatory prose here in the form of a hypertext list |
|        Caveat       => {"warning"},                                         |
|        SeeAlso      => {"other things"},                                    |
|        Subnodes     => {                                                    |
|            "subheading a",                                                  |
|            TO "node 1",                                                     |
|            TO "node 2",                                                     |
|            "subheading b",                                                  |
|            TO "node 3",                                                     |
|            ...                                                              |
|            },                                                               |
|        }                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|overviews                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|.",                                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|.",                                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

