Inputs -- inputs for a function in a documentation node
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        document { ... , Inputs => { inputs, ... }, ... }

Description
===========

The entries should consist of items in one of the following forms.

  * hypertext
  * class
  * symbolname
  * class => hypertext
  * symbolname => class
  * symbolname => hypertext
  * symbolname => class => hypertext

As an example, here is the Inputs entry of the method *note resolution(Ideal):
(OldChainComplexes)resolution_lpIdeal_rp,:

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|Inputs => { "I" => { "an ideal in a ring ", TT "R", ", say" } }|
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

Here is an example of the Inputs entry of the function *note sin: sin,:

+------------------------+
|Inputs => { "x" => RR },|
+------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Outputs: Outputs, -- outputs for a function in a documentation node
  * *note Usage: Usage, -- ways to use a function in a documentation node

