Outputs -- outputs for a function in a documentation node
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        document { ... , Outputs => { outputs, ... }, ... }

Description
===========

The entries should consist of items in one of the following forms.

  * hypertext
  * class => hypertext (or null)
  * symbolname => hypertext (or null)
  * symbolname => class => hypertext (or null)

As an example, here is the Outputs entry of the method *note resolution(Ideal):
(OldChainComplexes)resolution_lpIdeal_rp,:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|Outputs => { {"a resolution of ", TT "R/I", " by projective ", TT "R",       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|"-modules" } }                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that the hypertext list needs to be bounded by { and } as there is only
one output for *note resolution(Ideal):
(OldChainComplexes)resolution_lpIdeal_rp,. Without the braces, multiple outputs
are defined. Note also that the *note Type: Type, of the output is
automatically added in this case.

Here is an example of the Outputs entry of the function *note sin: sin,:

+---------------------------------------------+
|Outputs => { { "the sine of ", TT "x", "" } }|
+---------------------------------------------+

