Subnodes -- a menu of documentation nodes
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        document { ... , Subnodes => { ... }, ... }
  * Consequences:
      * the documentation subnodes listed will appear as descendents of this
        node in the documentation tree

Description
===========

This option inserts into a documentation page a menu of subnodes and defines
how the tree structure of the documentation is constructed. This is relevant
when printing the documentation.

Example of usage as an optional argument to *note document(List): document,
===========================================================================

+---------------------------------+
|Subnodes => {                    |
|        "An example of subnodes",|
|        TO "a link name",        |
|        TO "another link name"   |
|        },                       |
+---------------------------------+

Example of usage as a keyword in *note doc(String): (SimpleDoc)doc,
===================================================================

When used as a main section of a documentation node, Subnodes can be used as
follows:

+-------------------------------------------------+
|Subnodes                                         |
|    :Heading 1                                   |
|      myFunction                                 |
|      "a link name"                              |
|      :A subheading about @TO "mySecondFunction"@|
|        mySecondFunction                         |
|    :Heading 2                                   |
|      "another link name"                        |
+-------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note TOH: (Text)TOH, -- hypertext documentation link followed by a
    headline
  * *note doc(String): (SimpleDoc)doc, -- a simple documentation function

