EXAMPLE -- construct a hypertext item from a Macaulay2 input string
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        EXAMPLE x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note string: String,, a *note visible list: VisibleList,, or an
        instance of the type *note PRE: (Text)PRE,, containing strings or
        objects of class *note PRE: (Text)PRE,
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note TABLE: (Text)TABLE,, a table containing
        the examples

Description
===========

If the table is included in the input provided to *note document: document,,
the input string will be evaluated by *note installPackage: installPackage, and
the result will be displayed in the documentation. Each object of class *note
PRE: (Text)PRE, will be inserted unchanged into the documentation as example
output. For example, the code

EXAMPLE { "1+1" }

produces a display that looks like this:

+--------+
|i1 : 1+1|
|        |
|o1 = 2  |
+--------+

See also
========

  * *note examples: examples, -- list the examples in documentation
  * *note hypertext: hypertext, -- prepare hypertext for display
  * *note document: document, -- create a documentation node
  * *note installPackage: installPackage, -- load and install a package and its
    documentation

