SYNOPSIS -- a standardized synopsis for use in documentation nodes
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        SYNOPSIS ( ..., Usage => "...", ... )
  * Inputs:
      * a *note list: List,, with *note Hypertext: (Text)Hypertext,, *note
        String: String,, and special documentation entries as optional
        arguments such as Usage => "..." (required)
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * BaseFunction => a *note function: Function,, default value null, see
        *note document(...,BaseFunction=>...): BaseFunction, -- the basename of
        a function in a documentation node
      * Heading => a *note list: List,, default value "Synopsis", see *note
        document(...,Headline=>...): Headline, -- specifies a subheading for
        the synopsis
      * Usage => a *note list: List,, default value "", see *note
        document(...,Usage=>...): Usage, -- ways to use a function in a
        documentation node
      * Inputs => a *note list: List,, default value {}, see *note
        document(...,Inputs=>...): Inputs, -- inputs for a function in a
        documentation node
      * Outputs => a *note list: List,, default value {}, see *note
        document(...,Outputs=>...): Outputs, -- outputs for a function in a
        documentation node
      * Consequences => a *note list: List,, default value {}, see *note
        document(...,Consequences=>...): Consequences, -- side-effects of a
        function in a documentation node
  * Outputs:
      * a *note markup list: (Text)Hypertext,, usable as an input of *note
        document(List): document,

Description
===========

This function prepares a standardized synopsis in hypertext for use in
documentation nodes. Here is an empty template for use with SYNOPSIS.

+------------------------------+
|SYNOPSIS (                    |
|        BaseFunction => fn,   |
|        Heading      => "",   |
|        Usage        => "",   |
|        Inputs       => {},   |
|        Outputs      => {},   |
|        Consequences => {},   |
|        PARA { ... },         |
|        EXAMPLE lines " ... ")|
+------------------------------+

The options are used just as with *note document: document,. Here is an example
of its use.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|SYNOPSIS {                                                                   |
|        Heading => "using binary methods for method functions",              |
|        Usage   => "f(x,y)",                                                 |
|        Inputs  => {                                                         |
|            "f" => { "a method function" },                                  |
|            "x" => { "an object of type ", TT "X" },                         |
|            "y" => { "an object of type ", TT "Y" }},                        |
|        Outputs => {                                                         |
|            { "the previously installed method for ", TT "f(X, Y)", " is call|
|                ", and the return value is returned. If no such method has be|
|                searches for a method for ", TT "f(X',Y')", ", where ", TT "X|
|                " and ", TT "Y'", " is an ancestor of ", TT "Y", "(see ", TO |
|        "The second line of the following example illustrates the syntax abov|
|        using ", TO "source", ", which happens to be a method function.",    |
|        EXAMPLE lines ///                                                    |
|          source(String, String) := peek;                                    |
|          source("foo", "bar")///,                                           |
|        PARA "The same syntax works for 3 or 4 arguments."}                  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|ed with arguments ", TT "(x, y)",                                            |
|en installed, then Macaulay2                                                 |
|'", " is an ancestor of ", TT "X",                                           |
|"inheritance", " for details)."}},                                           |
|e,                                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See the Synopsis keyword in *note doc(String): (SimpleDoc)doc, for usage as a
keyword in that format.

