addDependencyTask(Task,Task) -- schedule a task, but ensure that it will not run until another task finishes
************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note addDependencyTask: addDependencyTask_lpTask_cmTask_rp,
  * Usage: 
        addDependencyTask(t,u)
  * Inputs:
      * t, a *note task: Task,, 
      * u, a *note task: Task,, 
  * Consequences:
      * the task t will be scheduled for execution, but execution will not
        begin until the task u finishes

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : for i to 5 do t_i = createTask(() -> i)               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : for i from 1 to 5 do addDependencyTask(t_i, t_(i - 1))|
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : schedule t_0                                          |
|                                                           |
|o3 = <<task, created>>                                     |
|                                                           |
|o3 : Task                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : sleep 1                                               |
|                                                           |
|o4 = 0                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : taskResult t_5                                        |
|                                                           |
|o5 = 5                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note addDependencyTask(Task,Task): addDependencyTask_lpTask_cmTask_rp, --
    schedule a task, but ensure that it will not run until another task
    finishes
