addStartTask(Task,Task) -- schedule a task upon completion of another
*********************************************************************

  * Function: *note addStartTask: addStartTask_lpTask_cmTask_rp,
  * Usage: 
        addStartTask(t,u)
  * Inputs:
      * t, a *note task: Task,, 
      * u, a *note task: Task,, 
  * Consequences:
      * After task t finishes, task u will be scheduled for execution.

Description
===========

+-------------------------+
|i1 : f = () -> "f value";|
+-------------------------+
|i2 : g = () -> "g value";|
+-------------------------+
|i3 : F = createTask f    |
|                         |
|o3 = <<task, created>>   |
|                         |
|o3 : Task                |
+-------------------------+
|i4 : G = createTask g    |
|                         |
|o4 = <<task, created>>   |
|                         |
|o4 : Task                |
+-------------------------+
|i5 : addStartTask(F,G)   |
+-------------------------+
|i6 : schedule F          |
|                         |
|o6 = <<task, created>>   |
|                         |
|o6 : Task                |
+-------------------------+
|i7 : taskResult F        |
|                         |
|o7 = f value             |
+-------------------------+
|i8 : taskResult G        |
|                         |
|o8 = g value             |
+-------------------------+

