isRegularFile -- whether a file is a regular file
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isRegularFile fn
  * Inputs:
      * fn, a *note string: String,, a filename or path
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, whether fn is the path to a regular
        file

Description
===========

In UNIX, a regular file is one that is not special in some way.  Special files
include symbolic links and directories.  A regular file is a sequence of bytes
stored permanently in a file system.
+------------------------------+
|i1 : fn = temporaryFileName() |
|                              |
|o1 = /tmp/M2-33376-0/0        |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : fn << "hi there" << close|
|                              |
|o2 = /tmp/M2-33376-0/0        |
|                              |
|o2 : File                     |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : isRegularFile fn         |
|                              |
|o3 = true                     |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : removeFile fn            |
+------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isDirectory: isDirectory, -- whether a file is a directory
  * *note readlink: readlink, -- get the resolved value a symbolic link

For the programmer
==================

