temporaryFileName -- make a temporary file name
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        temporaryFileName()
  * Outputs:
      * a unique temporary file name.

Description
===========

The file name is so unique that even with various suffixes appended, no
collision with existing files will occur.  The files will be removed when the
program terminates, unless it terminates as the result of an error.
+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : temporaryFileName () | ".tex" |
|                                   |
|o1 = /tmp/M2-33335-0/0.tex         |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : temporaryFileName () | ".html"|
|                                   |
|o2 = /tmp/M2-33335-0/1.html        |
+-----------------------------------+

This function will work under Unix, and also under Windows if you have a
directory on the same drive called /tmp.

If the name of the temporary file will be given to an external program, it may
be necessary to concatenate it with *note rootPath: rootPath, or *note rootURI:
rootURI, to enable the external program to find the file.

The temporary file name is derived from the value of the environment variable
TMPDIR, if it has one.

If *note fork: fork, is used, then the parent and child Macaulay2 processes
will each remove their own temporary files upon termination, with the parent
removing any files created before *note fork: fork, was called.

See also
========

  * *note File: File, -- the class of all files
  * *note rootPath: rootPath,
  * *note rootURI: rootURI,

