Program -- external program object
**********************************

Description
===========

A hash table returned by *note findProgram: findProgram, with the following
strings as keys:

  * "name", the name of the loaded program.  This comes from the first argument
    passed to *note findProgram: findProgram,.  It is also what is displayed
    when printing a Program.
  * "path", the path to the program as determined by *note findProgram:
    findProgram,.
  * "prefix", a sequence of two strings identifying the prefix prepended to the
    binary executables.  See *note findProgram: findProgram,, specifically the
    description of the Prefix option, for more.
  * "version", a string containing the version number of the program.  Only
    present if *note findProgram: findProgram, was called with the
    MinimumVersion option.

See also
========

  * *note findProgram: findProgram, -- load external program
  * *note runProgram: runProgram, -- run an external program
  * *note programPaths: programPaths, -- user-defined external program paths

Functions and methods returning an object of class Program:
===========================================================

  * *note findProgram: findProgram, -- load external program

Methods that use an object of class Program:
============================================

  * *note Program << Thing: Program << Thing, -- run program with input
    redirection
  * "runProgram(Program,String)" -- see *note runProgram: runProgram, -- run an
    external program
  * "runProgram(Program,String,String)" -- see *note runProgram: runProgram, --
    run an external program

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Program: Program, is a *note type: Type,, with ancestor
classes *note HashTable: HashTable, < *note Thing: Thing,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in
Macaulay2Doc/functions/findProgram-doc.m2:30:0.

File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: programPaths, Prev: Program, Up: findProgram

programPaths -- user-defined external program paths
***************************************************

Description
===========

A mutable hash table containing user-defined paths to external programs used by
Macaulay2.  Its keys are strings containing the names of programs and must
coincide with the first argument of *note findProgram: findProgram,.

It is only necessary to define a path in this way if a program is installed in
a non-standard location.  In particular, *note findProgram: findProgram,
already checks prefixDirectory | currentLayout#"programs", (where the programs
shipped with Macaulay2 are installed) and all of the directories in the user's
PATH environment variable.

If you use a particular program frequently and it is installed in a
non-standard location, then it may be useful to add a line to your *note
initialization file: initialization file, defining its path in this way.

See also
========

  * *note Program: Program, -- external program object
  * *note path: path, -- list of directories to look in

For the programmer
==================

The object *note programPaths: programPaths, is a *note mutable hash table:
MutableHashTable,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in
Macaulay2Doc/functions/findProgram-doc.m2:58:0.

