runProgram -- run an external program
*************************************

  * Usage: 
        runProgram(program, args)
        runProgram(program, exe, args)
  * Inputs:
      * program, an instance of the type *note Program: Program,, the program
        to run, generated by *note findProgram: findProgram,.
      * exe, a *note string: String,, the specific executable file to run. This
        is only necessary if the program consists of multiple such files.  If
        not given, then program#"name" is used.
      * args, a *note string: String,, the command line arguments passed to the
        program.
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * KeepFiles => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value false,
        whether to keep the temporary files containing the program's output.
      * RaiseError => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value true,
        whether to raise an error if the program returns a nonzero value.
      * RunDirectory => a *note string: String,, default value null, the
        directory from which to run the program.  If it does not exist, then it
        will be created.  If *note null: null,, then the program will be run
        from the current working directory (see *note currentDirectory:
        currentDirectory,).
      * Verbose => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value false,
        whether to print the command line input and the program's output.

Description
===========

This method runs an external program which has already been loaded using *note
findProgram: findProgram,.  The results of this run are available in a *note
ProgramRun: ProgramRun, object.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : gfan = findProgram("gfan", "gfan --help")           |
|                                                         |
|o1 = gfan                                                |
|                                                         |
|o1 : Program                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : runProgram(gfan, "_version")                        |
|                                                         |
|o2 = 0                                                   |
|                                                         |
|o2 : ProgramRun                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : oo#"output"                                         |
|                                                         |
|o3 = Gfan version:                                       |
|     gfan0.8beta                                         |
|                                                         |
|     Forked from source tree on:                         |
|     1778184367 Thu May 07 22:06:07 2026                 |
|                                                         |
|     Linked libraries:                                   |
|     GMP 6.3.0                                           |
|     Cddlib       YES                                    |
|     SoPlex        NO                                    |
|     Singular      NO                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : runProgram(gfan, "_foo", RaiseError => false)       |
|                                                         |
|o4 = 256                                                 |
|                                                         |
|o4 : ProgramRun                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : oo#"error"                                          |
|                                                         |
|o5 = UNKNOWN OPTION: _foo.                               |
|     USE --help AS A SINGLE OPTION TO VIEW THE HELP TEXT.|
+---------------------------------------------------------+

The value corresponding to the "output" key may also be obtained using *note
toString: toString,.

+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : toString runProgram(gfan, "_version")|
|                                          |
|o6 = Gfan version:                        |
|     gfan0.8beta                          |
|                                          |
|     Forked from source tree on:          |
|     1778184367 Thu May 07 22:06:07 2026  |
|                                          |
|     Linked libraries:                    |
|     GMP 6.3.0                            |
|     Cddlib       YES                     |
|     SoPlex        NO                     |
|     Singular      NO                     |
+------------------------------------------+

It is also possible to skip *note findProgram: findProgram, and just provide
two strings: the name of the program and the command line arguments.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : runProgram("normaliz", "--version")                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = 0                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : ProgramRun                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : peek oo                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = ProgramRun{command => /usr/bin/normaliz --version                       |
|                error =>                                                     |
|                output => Normaliz 3.10.2                                    |
|                          ---------------------------------------------------|
|                          with package(s) Flint e-antic nauty                |
|                          Copyright (C) 2007-2022  The Normaliz Team, Univers|
|                          This program comes with ABSOLUTELY NO WARRANTY; Thi|
|                          and you are welcome to redistribute it under certai|
|                          See COPYING for details.                           |
|                                                                             |
|                return value => 0                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                   }                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|---------                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|ity of Osnabrueck.                                                           |
|s is free software,                                                          |
|n conditions;                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Internally, this routine uses *note run: run,. Another way to interact with
programs is to pass a string beginning with "!" to *note get: get,, *note
openIn: openIn_lpString_rp,, *note openOut: openOut_lpString_rp,, or *note
openInOut: openInOut,.

