load -- read Macaulay2 commands
*******************************

Description
===========

load "f" -- reads and executes Macaulay2 expressions found in the file named f.

The file is sought in the directory containing the file currently being loaded,
if any, and then along the *note path: path,, unless the name of the file
begins with /, $, or !. If the file begins with ./ or ../, then it looks
instead in the directory of the file currently being loaded (see *note
currentFileDirectory: currentFileDirectory,).  If no file is being loaded it
will look in the current directory (see *note currentDirectory:
currentDirectory,).

The file is read without echoing the input, printing the values, or
incrementing the line number.

If one of the top level expressions in the file evaluates to the symbol *note
end: end, the reading of the file is stopped at that point.

If the variable *note notify: notify, is set to true, then an informational
message is displayed after the file is loaded.

