top level loop
**************

The top level evaluation loop of the interpreter contains hooks so the user can
control how printing of the results of evaluation is done.  If the result is
*note null: null, then nothing is printed.  Otherwise, the appropriate method
associated with the symbol *note Print: Print, is applied to perform the
printing, unless the printing is to be suppressed, as indicated by a semicolon
at the end of the statement, in which case the *note NoPrint: NoPrint, method
is applied.

See also
========

  * *note Print: Print, -- top level method for printing results
  * *note NoPrint: NoPrint, -- top level method for non-printing results
  * *note BeforePrint: BeforePrint, -- top level method applied before printing
    results
  * *note AfterPrint: AfterPrint, -- top level method applied after printing
  * *note AfterNoPrint: AfterNoPrint, -- top level method applied after not
    printing
* Menu:

* value::                       evaluate
* capture::                     evaluate Macaulay2 code and capture the output
* oo::                          the last output value
* ooo::                         the next to the last output value
* oooo::                        the third to the last output value
* OutputDictionary::            the dictionary for output values
* clearAll::                    forget everything
* clearOutput::                 forget output values
* topLevelMode::                the current top level mode
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

