capture -- evaluate Macaulay2 code and capture the output
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (err, output) := capture str
  * Inputs:
      * str, a *note net: Net,, a *note list: List,, a *note string: String,,
        or a *note test input: tests,, the Macaulay2 code to be evaluated
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * UserMode => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value true,
        indicates whether currently loaded packages and exported symbols should
        be accessible while str is being evaluated.
      * PackageExports => a *note list: List,, default value null, of packages
        to be loaded before evaluating str.  The current package, as given by
        *note Macaulay2Doc: Top,, will be included.
  * Outputs:
      * err, a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, whether the evaluation was
        interrupted because of an error
      * output, a *note string: String,, the result of the evaluation

