If UserMode => false given, the dictionaries available to the user will not be
affected by the evaluation and *note collectGarbage: collectGarbage, is called
afterwards.

Errors occurred while evaluating str do not cause an error outside of capture.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (err, output) = capture /// stderr << "Checking a false statement:" <<  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = (true,                                                            )     |
|            i1 :  stderr << "Checking a false statement:" << endl; 1/0       |
|            Checking a false statement:                                      |
|            currentString:1:51:(3):[4]: error: division by zero              |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Sequence                                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|endl; 1/0 ///                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert err                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Certain examples or tests might not be compatible with capture. In such cases,
use the string -* no-capture-flag *- somewhere within str so that the code is
run in a separate Macaulay2 subprocess instead.

See also
========

  * *note check: check, -- perform tests of a package
  * *note examples: examples, -- list the examples in documentation

Ways to use capture:
====================

  * "capture(List)"
  * "capture(Net)"
  * "capture(String)"
  * "capture(TestInput)"

