currentTime -- get the current time
***********************************

  * Usage: 
        currentTime()
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,, the current time, in seconds since 00:00:00
        1970-01-01 UTC, the beginning of the epoch

Description
===========

+------------------+
|i1 : currentTime()|
|                  |
|o1 = 1786067132   |
+------------------+

We can compute, roughly, how many years ago the epoch began as follows.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : currentTime() /( (365 + 97./400) * 24 * 60 * 60 )|
|                                                      |
|o2 = 56.59821430155866                                |
|                                                      |
|o2 : RR (of precision 53)                             |
+------------------------------------------------------+

We can also compute how many months account for the fractional part of that
number.

+-------------------------+
|i3 : 12 * (oo - floor oo)|
|                         |
|o3 = 7.178571618703955   |
|                         |
|o3 : RR (of precision 53)|
+-------------------------+

Compare that to the current date, available from a standard Unix command.

+----------------------------+
|i4 : run "date"             |
|Fri Aug  7 01:45:32 UTC 2026|
|                            |
|o4 = 0                      |
+----------------------------+

For the programmer
==================

The object *note currentTime: currentTime, is a *note compiled function:
CompiledFunction,.

