alarm -- set an alarm
*********************

  * Usage: 
        alarm n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,
  * Consequences:
      * the alarm will be sounded after n seconds; it can be intercepted with
        *note try: try,

Description
===========

If n is zero, then no alarm is scheduled, and any previously scheduled alarm is
cancelled. Any pending alarm will be cancelled when any other error occurs, or
when the top level loop offers an input prompt to the user.


The value returned is the number of seconds remaining until any previously
scheduled alarm was due to be delivered, or zero if there was no previously
scheduled alarm.


This command may interfere with *note time: time, or *note sleep: sleep, on
some systems.

For the programmer
==================

The object *note alarm: alarm, is a *note compiled function: CompiledFunction,.

