fork -- fork the process
************************

  * Usage: 
        fork()
  * Outputs:
      * When successful, it returns the process id of the child in the parent,
        and returns 0 in the child.  When unsuccessful, it returns -1.

Description
===========

Platforms that do not have a built-in fork() function will always return -1.

Warning: in multithreaded programs like Macaulay2, very few operations can be
safely done in the child.  This is especially true when the user has been *note
parallel programming with threads and tasks: parallel programming with threads
and tasks,. Even allocating memory in the child may hang the process.

For the programmer
==================

The object *note fork: fork, is a *note compiled function: CompiledFunction,.

