Database -- the class of all database files
*******************************************

Description
===========

A database file is just like a hash table, except both the keys and values have
to be strings.  In this example we create a database file, store a few entries,
remove an entry with *note remove: remove,, close the file, and then remove the
file.
+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : filename = temporaryFileName () | ".dbm"|
|                                             |
|o1 = /tmp/M2-32798-0/0.dbm                   |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : x = openDatabaseOut filename            |
|                                             |
|o2 = /tmp/M2-32798-0/0.dbm                   |
|                                             |
|o2 : Database                                |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : x#"first" = "hi there"                  |
|                                             |
|o3 = hi there                                |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : x#"first"                               |
|                                             |
|o4 = hi there                                |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : x#"second" = "ho there"                 |
|                                             |
|o5 = ho there                                |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i6 : scanKeys(x,print)                       |
|second                                       |
|first                                        |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i7 : remove(x,"second")                      |
|                                             |
|o7 = ho there                                |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i8 : scanKeys(x,print)                       |
|first                                        |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i9 : close x                                 |
|                                             |
|o9 = 0                                       |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i10 : removeFile filename                    |
+---------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note HashTable: HashTable, -- the class of all hash tables
  * *note String: String, -- the class of all strings
  * *note removeFile: removeFile, -- remove a file

Functions and methods returning a database:
===========================================

  * "openDatabase(String)" -- see *note openDatabase: openDatabase, -- open a
    database file
  * "openDatabaseOut(String)" -- see *note openDatabaseOut: openDatabaseOut, --
    open a database file for writing

Methods that use a database:
============================

  * "Database #? String" -- see *note #?: #?, -- check existence of value in a
    list, hash table, database, or string
  * "isOpen(Database)" -- see *note isOpen: isOpen, -- whether a file or
    database is open
  * "keys(Database)" -- see *note keys: keys, -- keys used in a hash table,
    dictionary, or database
  * "Database # String" -- see *note List # ZZ: List # ZZ, -- get value from
    list, hash table, database, dictionary, or string
  * "Manipulator Database" -- see *note Manipulator: Manipulator, -- the class
    of all file manipulators
  * "remove(Database,String)" -- see *note remove: remove, -- remove an entry
    from a mutable hash table, list, or database
  * "scanKeys(Database,Function)" -- see *note scanKeys: scanKeys, -- apply a
    function to each key in a hash table or database

