GCstats -- information about the status of the garbage collector
****************************************************************

Description
===========

Macaulay2 uses the Hans Boehm *note garbage collector: GC garbage collector, to
reclaim unused memory.  The function GCstats provides information about its
status, such as the total number of bytes allocated, the current heap size, the
number of garbage collections done, the number of threads used in each
collection, the total cpu time spent in garbage collection, etc.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : s = GCstats()                                 |
|                                                   |
|o1 = HashTable{"bytesAlloc" => 67946571546        }|
|               "GC_free_space_divisor" => 3        |
|               "GC_LARGE_ALLOC_WARN_INTERVAL" => 1 |
|               "gcCpuTimeSecs" => 0                |
|               "heapSize" => 217415680             |
|               "numGCs" => 1452                    |
|               "numGCThreads" => 4                 |
|                                                   |
|o1 : HashTable                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------+

The value returned is a hash table, from which individual bits of information
can be easily extracted, as follows.

+-----------------+
|i2 : s#"heapSize"|
|                 |
|o2 = 217415680   |
+-----------------+

Any entries whose keys are all upper case give the values of environment
variables affecting the operation of the garbage collector that have been
specified by the user.

For further information about the individual items in the table, we refer the
user to the source code and documentation of the garbage collector.

See also
========

  * *note GC garbage collector: GC garbage collector,

For the programmer
==================

The object *note GCstats: GCstats, is a *note compiled function:
CompiledFunction,.

