registerFinalizer -- register a string that will be displayed when an object is garbage collected
*************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        registerFinalizer(x,str)
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note thing: Thing,
      * str, a *note string: String,
  * Consequences:
      * A finalizer is registered with the garbage collector to print a string
        when that object is collected as garbage

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : for i from 1 to 9 do (x := 0 .. 10000 ; registerFinalizer(x, "--        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|finalizing sequence #"|i|" --"))                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : collectGarbage()                                                        |
|--finalization: (1)[7]: -- finalizing sequence #8 --                         |
|--finalization: (2)[2]: -- finalizing sequence #3 --                         |
|--finalization: (3)[0]: -- finalizing sequence #1 --                         |
|--finalization: (4)[4]: -- finalizing sequence #5 --                         |
|--finalization: (5)[6]: -- finalizing sequence #7 --                         |
|--finalization: (6)[3]: -- finalizing sequence #4 --                         |
|--finalization: (7)[5]: -- finalizing sequence #6 --                         |
|--finalization: (8)[1]: -- finalizing sequence #2 --                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This function should mainly be used for debugging.  Having a large number of
finalizers might degrade the performance of the program.  Moreover, registering
two or more objects that are members of a circular chain of pointers for
finalization will result in a memory leak, with none of the objects in the
chain being freed, even if nothing else points to any of them.

See also
========

  * *note collectGarbage: collectGarbage, -- collect the garbage in memory

Ways to use registerFinalizer:
==============================

  * registerFinalizer(Thing,String) (missing documentation)

