File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: prefixDirectory, Next: applicationDirectory, Prev: prefixPath, Up: how Macaulay2 finds its files

prefixDirectory -- the prefix directory
***************************************

Description
===========

When Macaulay2 is successfully installed, its files are installed in a
directory tree whose layout, relative to the root, is determined by the hash
table *note Layout: currentLayout,.  When M2 starts up, it detects whether it
is running in such a layout, and sets *note prefixDirectory: prefixDirectory,
to the root of that directory tree.  The way it does that is that it locates
the running M2 executable and determines whether it is located in a directory
whose name is bin that has a sibling directory called share that leads to a
directory called share/Macaulay2/Core/.

The prefix directory can be set by the user at an early stage when M2 starts up
with the --prefix command line option.  This will affect the value of *note
path: path, and thus the locations of the files loaded initially.  Use the
--notify command line option to display the locations of files as they are
loaded.

See also
========

  * *note prefixPath: prefixPath, -- absolute locations of Macaulay2 files
  * *note invoking the Macaulay2 program: invoking the Macaulay2 program,

For the programmer
==================

The object *note prefixDirectory: prefixDirectory, is a *note string: String,.

