Thing -- the class of all things
********************************

Description
===========

Everything in Macaulay2 is a thing.  This includes numbers, strings, and lists.
More complicated things such as polynomials, groups, rings, and chain complexes
are implemented as hash tables.  See *note Type: Type, for information about
what types of things there are.
* Menu:

* NetFile::                     the class of all net files
* Boolean::                     the class of boolean values
* Dictionary::                  the class of all dictionaries
* Nothing::                     the empty class
* Number::                      the class of all numbers
* File::                        the class of all files
* AtomicInt::                   the class of atomic integers
* Mutex::                       the class of mutexes
* Symbol::                      the class of all symbols
* Pseudocode::                  the class of pseudocodes

Types of thing:
===============

  * *note AtomicInt: AtomicInt, -- the class of atomic integers
  * *note BasicList: BasicList, -- the class of all basic lists
  * *note Boolean: Boolean, -- the class of boolean values
  * *note Database: Database, -- the class of all database files
  * *note Dictionary: Dictionary, -- the class of all dictionaries
  * *note Error: Error, -- error information
  * *note File: File, -- the class of all files
  * *note Function: Function, -- the class of all functions
  * *note FunctionBody: FunctionBody, -- the class of function bodies
  * *note HashTable: HashTable, -- the class of all hash tables
  * *note Mutex: Mutex, -- the class of mutexes
  * *note Net: Net, -- the class of all nets and strings
  * *note NetFile: NetFile, -- the class of all net files
  * *note Nothing: Nothing, -- the empty class
  * *note Number: Number, -- the class of all numbers
  * *note Pseudocode: Pseudocode, -- the class of pseudocodes
  * *note Symbol: Symbol, -- the class of all symbols
  * "SymbolBody" -- see *note symbolBody: symbolBody, -- symbol bodies
  * *note Task: Task, -- the class of all tasks

