LocalDictionary -- the class of all local dictionaries
******************************************************

Description
===========

A local dictionary is one used in connection with a local scope, such as one
that is bounded by the body of a function closure. A local dictionary is
created on the fly by the interpreter, and after the scope has been closed, the
dictionary can be enlarged no further. Accessing local dictionaries can be a
useful debugging tool.  The local dictionaries accessible to the user come with
frames, so their symbols have values; thus they may be referred to as
dictionary closures.

See also
========

  * *note localDictionaries: localDictionaries, -- get local dictionaries
  * *note GlobalDictionary: GlobalDictionary, -- the class of all global
    dictionaries

Methods that use an object of class LocalDictionary:
====================================================

  * *note debug(LocalDictionary): debug_lpLocalDictionary_rp, -- open a local
    or global dictionary to the user

For the programmer
==================

The object *note LocalDictionary: LocalDictionary, is a *note type: Type,, with
ancestor classes *note Dictionary: Dictionary, < *note Thing: Thing,.

