isANumber -- whether a number is not not-a-number
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isANumber x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note number: Number,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, whether x is not not a number.

Description
===========

For a discussion of the notion of not-a-number in floating point arithmetic,
see http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NaN.

+-------------------------+
|i1 : isANumber 3.        |
|                         |
|o1 = true                |
+-------------------------+
|i2 : inf = 1/0.          |
|                         |
|o2 = infinity            |
|                         |
|o2 : RR (of precision 53)|
+-------------------------+
|i3 : isANumber inf       |
|                         |
|o3 = true                |
+-------------------------+
|i4 : nan = inf - inf     |
|                         |
|o4 = NotANumber          |
|                         |
|o4 : RR (of precision 53)|
+-------------------------+
|i5 : isANumber nan       |
|                         |
|o5 = false               |
+-------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isFinite: isFinite, -- whether a number is finite
  * *note isInfinite: isInfinite, -- whether a number is infinite

Ways to use isANumber:
======================

  * "isANumber(Number)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isANumber: isANumber, is a *note compiled function:
CompiledFunction,.

