File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: InexactNumber, Next: InexactNumber', Prev: IndeterminateNumber, Up: Number

InexactNumber
*************

Description
===========

This type of number is intended to serve as a parent class for those types of
numbers that are inexactly represented in the computer.
* Menu:

* precision::
* numeric::                     convert to floating point
* round::                       round a number
* size2::                       number of binary digits to the left of the point
* clean::                       set to zero elements that are approximately zero
* norm::                        l^p norm
* minExponent::
* maxExponent::

Types of inexact number:
========================

  * *note CC: CC, -- the class of all complex numbers
  * *note CCi: CCi, -- the class of all complex intervals
  * *note RR: RR, -- the class of all real numbers
  * *note RRi: RRi, -- the class of all real intervals

