GlobalAssignHook -- hook for assignment to global variables
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        X.GlobalAssignHook = f
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note type: Type,
      * f, a *note function: Function,,  of two variables: the symbol to which
        a value is about to be assigned, and the value being assigned
  * Consequences:
      * f will be called just before an assignment to a global variable of an
        instance of class X occurs

Description
===========

This technique is used, for example, for instances of *note Type: Type, and
*note Ring: Ring, to arrange for the name of the type or ring to be set to the
name of the global variable to which it is first assigned.  The functions *note
globalAssignFunction: globalAssignFunction, and *note globalReleaseFunction:
globalReleaseFunction, may installed as methods for this purpose.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : RR.GlobalAssignHook = (sym,val) -> << "--about to assign " << val << "  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|to " << sym << endl;                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : a = 4.5                                                                 |
|--about to assign 4.5 to a                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = 4.5                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : RR (of precision 53)                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note GlobalReleaseHook: GlobalReleaseHook,

