globalAssignment -- install standard global assignment method
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        globalAssignment X
  * Inputs:
      * X, a *note type: Type,
  * Consequences:
      * the functions *note globalAssignFunction: globalAssignFunction, and
        *note globalReleaseFunction: globalReleaseFunction, are installed in
        the type X under *note GlobalAssignHook: GlobalAssignHook, and *note
        GlobalReleaseHook: GlobalReleaseHook,, respectively.  The effect is
        that when an object of type X is assigned to a global variable, the
        function *note use: use, is called on it, and thereafter that object
        will print out as the name of the variable.

Description
===========

One type for which this has been done is *note Ring: Ring,, as illustrated in
the following example.
+-----------------------+
|i1 : S := QQ[x]        |
|                       |
|o1 = QQ[x]             |
|                       |
|o1 : PolynomialRing    |
+-----------------------+
|i2 : S                 |
|                       |
|o2 = QQ[x]             |
|                       |
|o2 : PolynomialRing    |
+-----------------------+
|i3 : S^3               |
|                       |
|            3          |
|o3 = (QQ[x])           |
|                       |
|o3 : QQ[x]-module, free|
+-----------------------+
|i4 : R = S             |
|                       |
|o4 = R                 |
|                       |
|o4 : PolynomialRing    |
+-----------------------+
|i5 : S                 |
|                       |
|o5 = R                 |
|                       |
|o5 : PolynomialRing    |
+-----------------------+
|i6 : S^3               |
|                       |
|      3                |
|o6 = R                 |
|                       |
|o6 : R-module, free    |
+-----------------------+

