Type -- the class of all mutable types
**************************************

Description
===========

Everything in the system is classified, and the class that a thing belongs to
is a type. A type is implemented as a *note mutable hash table:
MutableHashTable, containing method functions for its instances.


The list of types known to the system is displayed below.
* Menu:


mathematical mutable types
* Monoid::                      the class of all monoids
* Ring::                        the class of all rings
* RingFamily::

other mutable types
* SelfInitializingType::        the class of all self initializing types
* WrapperType::                 a class of lists with abbreviated constructors
* HeaderType::                  a class of lists with abbreviated constructors

Types of type:
==============

  * *note HeaderType: HeaderType, -- a class of lists with abbreviated
    constructors
  * *note Monoid: Monoid, -- the class of all monoids
  * *note Ring: Ring, -- the class of all rings
  * *note RingFamily: RingFamily,
  * *note SelfInitializingType: SelfInitializingType, -- the class of all self
    initializing types
  * *note WrapperType: WrapperType, -- a class of lists with abbreviated
    constructors

Functions and methods returning a type:
=======================================

  * "class(Thing)" -- see *note class: class, -- class of an object
  * "parent(Thing)" -- see *note parent: parent, -- parent type of an object

Methods that use a type:
========================

  * "? Type" -- see *note ? Symbol: ? Symbol, -- view brief documentation of a
    symbol
  * "about(Type)" -- see *note about: about, -- search the documentation
  * *note ancestor(Type,Type): ancestor_lpType_cmType_rp, -- whether one type
    is an ancestor of another
  * "instance(Thing,Type)" -- see *note instance: instance, -- whether
    something has a certain type
  * "instances(Type)" -- see *note instances: instances,
  * "isQuotientOf(Type,QuotientRing)" -- see *note isQuotientOf(Type,Ring):
    isQuotientOf_lpType_cmRing_rp, -- whether one ring is a quotient of a ring
    of a given type
  * *note isQuotientOf(Type,Ring): isQuotientOf_lpType_cmRing_rp, -- whether
    one ring is a quotient of a ring of a given type
  * "methods(Type)" -- see *note methods: methods, -- list methods
  * "ofClass(Type)" -- see *note ofClass: ofClass, -- English phrases for types
  * *note random(Type): random_lpType_rp, -- get a random object of a type
  * *note select(BasicList,Type): select_lpBasicList_cmType_rp, -- select
    elements of a given type in a list

Protected objects of class Type:
================================

  * *note AngleBarList: AngleBarList, -- the class of lists delimited by <| ...
    |>
  * *note Array: Array, -- the class of all arrays -- [...]
  * *note AssociativeExpression: AssociativeExpression, -- the class of
    associative expressions
  * *note AtomicInt: AtomicInt, -- the class of atomic integers
  * *note BasicList: BasicList, -- the class of all basic lists
  * *note BettiTally: BettiTally, -- the class of all Betti tallies
  * *note Boolean: Boolean, -- the class of boolean values
