File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: GF, Next: order, Up: GaloisField

GF -- make a finite field
*************************

Description
===========

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        GF(p,n)
        GF(q)
  * Inputs:
      * p, a prime number
      * n
      * *note Variable: GF, => a *note symbol: Symbol,, default value null, the
        name to use for the generator of the field.  If null, then a is used.
      * *note SizeLimit: GF, => an *note integer: ZZ,, default value 10000, the
        limit on the size of a Galois field whose elements will be represented
        internally as powers of the primitive element
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Galois field: GaloisField,, a finite field with q = p^n
        elements
The generator of this ring is a primitive element: it generates the
multiplicative group of non-zero elements.

If the single argument form GF(q) is given, q should be a prime power q = p^n

+-----------------------------+
|i1 : A = GF(3,2,Variable=>b);|
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : ambient A               |
|                             |
|        ZZ                   |
|        --[b]                |
|         3                   |
|o2 = ----------              |
|      2                      |
|     b  - b - 1              |
|                             |
|o2 : QuotientRing            |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : b^8                     |
|                             |
|o3 = 1                       |
|                             |
|o3 : A                       |
+-----------------------------+
|i4 : b^4                     |
|                             |
|o4 = -1                      |
|                             |
|o4 : A                       |
+-----------------------------+
+----------------+
|i5 : K = GF 8   |
|                |
|o5 = K          |
|                |
|o5 : GaloisField|
+----------------+
|i6 : a^3+a      |
|                |
|o6 = 1          |
|                |
|o6 : K          |
+----------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        GF R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,, A quotient of a polynomial ring over ZZ/p in
        one variable, modulo an irreducible polynomial
      * *note PrimitiveElement: GF, => ..., default value FindOne, either an
        element of R, or the symbol *note FindOne: FindOne,.  An element is
        primitive if it generates the multiplicative group of non-zero elements
        of R
      * *note SizeLimit: GF, => an *note integer: ZZ,, default value 10000, the
        limit on the size of a Galois field whose elements will be represented
        internally as powers of the primitive element
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Galois field: GaloisField,, a finite field isomorphic to R
+--------------------------------+
|i7 : A = ZZ/5[a]/(a^3-a-2)      |
|                                |
|o7 = A                          |
|                                |
|o7 : QuotientRing               |
+--------------------------------+
|i8 : B = GF A                   |
|                                |
|o8 = B                          |
|                                |
|o8 : GaloisField                |
+--------------------------------+
|i9 : C = ZZ/5[b]/(b^3+1+3*b^2+b)|
|                                |
|o9 = C                          |
|                                |
|o9 : QuotientRing               |
+--------------------------------+
|i10 : D = GF C                  |
|                                |
|o10 = D                         |
|                                |
|o10 : GaloisField               |
+--------------------------------+
|i11 : map(B,D,{a^2})            |
|                                |
|                   2            |
|o11 = map (B, D, {a })          |
|                                |
|o11 : RingMap B <-- D           |
+--------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note toField: toField_lpRing_rp, -- declare that a ring is a field
  * *note finite fields: finite fields,

