hilbertSeries(PolynomialRing) -- compute the Hilbert series of a ring
*********************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertSeries: hilbertSeries,
  * Usage: 
        hilbertSeries R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: PolynomialRing,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Order: hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value infinity, display the truncated power series expansion
      * *note Reduce: hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmReduce=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, reduce the Hilbert series
  * Outputs:
      * a *note divide expression: Divide,, the Hilbert series

Description
===========

We compute the *note Hilbert series: hilbertSeries, of a ring.
+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, Degrees => {2}]/ideal(x^2);|
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : s = hilbertSeries R                      |
|                                              |
|           4                                  |
|      1 - T                                   |
|o2 = --------                                 |
|           2                                  |
|     (1 - T )                                 |
|                                              |
|o2 : Expression of class Divide               |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : numerator s                              |
|                                              |
|          4                                   |
|o3 = 1 - T                                    |
|                                              |
|o3 : ZZ[T]                                    |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : poincare R                               |
|                                              |
|          4                                   |
|o4 = 1 - T                                    |
|                                              |
|o4 : ZZ[T]                                    |
+----------------------------------------------+
Recall that the variables of the power series are the variables of the *note
degrees ring: degreesRing,.
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R=ZZ/101[x, Degrees => {{1,1}}]/ideal(x^2);|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : s = hilbertSeries R                        |
|                                                |
|           2 2                                  |
|      1 - T T                                   |
|           0 1                                  |
|o6 = ----------                                 |
|     (1 - T T )                                 |
|           0 1                                  |
|                                                |
|o6 : Expression of class Divide                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : numerator s                                |
|                                                |
|          2 2                                   |
|o7 = 1 - T T                                    |
|          0 1                                   |
|                                                |
|o7 : ZZ[T ..T ]                                 |
|         0   1                                  |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : poincare R                                 |
|                                                |
|          2 2                                   |
|o8 = 1 - T T                                    |
|          0 1                                   |
|                                                |
|o8 : ZZ[T ..T ]                                 |
|         0   1                                  |
+------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note hilbertSeries(PolynomialRing): hilbertSeries_lpPolynomialRing_rp, --
    compute the Hilbert series of a ring
