codim(QuotientRing) -- compute the codimension
**********************************************

  * Function: *note codim: codim,
  * Usage: 
        codim R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note quotient ring: QuotientRing,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Generic: codim_lpIdeal_cmGeneric=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value false,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,, the codimension of R

Description
===========

Computes the codimension of the presentation ideal of R over its ambient
polynomial ring.
+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]/(ideal(x,y) * ideal(x-1))|
|                                          |
|o1 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : codim R                              |
|                                          |
|o2 = 1                                    |
+------------------------------------------+
However, the following may not be the expected result.
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R = QQ[x,y]/(ideal(x,y) * ideal(x-1))|
|                                          |
|o3 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o3 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : codim R                              |
|                                          |
|o4 = 1                                    |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : codim (R/x)                          |
|                                          |
|o5 = 2                                    |
+------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note dim(QuotientRing): dim_lpRing_rp, -- compute the Krull dimension

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "codim(PolynomialRing)"
  * *note codim(QuotientRing): codim_lpQuotientRing_rp, -- compute the
    codimension
