presentation(PolynomialRing,QuotientRing) -- presentation of a quotient ring
****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note presentation: presentation,
  * Usage: 
        presentation B
        presentation(A,B)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note polynomial ring: PolynomialRing,
      * B, a *note quotient ring: QuotientRing,, a quotient ring of A
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, whose image is the ideal of A defining B

Description
===========

If A is not present, then it is understood to be the ultimate ambient
polynomial ring of B. In general, A may be any ring of which B is a quotient.


In the examples below, A is the ultimate ambient polynomial ring of A, B and C.
+-------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ[a..d];             |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : B = A/(a^2,b^3);          |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : C = B/(a*b*c,b*c*d, b^2); |
+-------------------------------+
|i4 : presentation A            |
|                               |
|o4 = 0                         |
|                               |
|             1                 |
|o4 : Matrix A  <-- 0           |
+-------------------------------+
|i5 : presentation B            |
|                               |
|o5 = | a2 b3 |                 |
|                               |
|             1      2          |
|o5 : Matrix A  <-- A           |
+-------------------------------+
|i6 : presentation C            |
|                               |
|o6 = | abc bcd b2 a2 b3 |      |
|                               |
|             1      5          |
|o6 : Matrix A  <-- A           |
+-------------------------------+
|i7 : presentation(B,C)         |
|                               |
|o7 = | abc bcd b2 |            |
|                               |
|             1      3          |
|o7 : Matrix B  <-- B           |
+-------------------------------+
|i8 : presentation(A,C)         |
|                               |
|o8 = | abc bcd b2 a2 b3 |      |
|                               |
|             1      5          |
|o8 : Matrix A  <-- A           |
+-------------------------------+
|i9 : minimalPresentation C     |
|                               |
|              QQ[a..d]         |
|o9 = --------------------------|
|       2   3                 2 |
|     (a , b , a*b*c, b*c*d, b )|
|                               |
|o9 : QuotientRing              |
+-------------------------------+


Caveat
======

The given presentation is often not minimal

See also
========

  * *note minimalPresentation: minimalPresentation, -- compute a minimal
    presentation

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note presentation(PolynomialRing,QuotientRing):
    presentation_lpPolynomialRing_cmQuotientRing_rp, -- presentation of a
    quotient ring
  * "presentation(QuotientRing)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

