ambient(Ring) -- ambient polynomial ring
****************************************

  * Function: *note ambient: ambient,
  * Usage: 
        ambient R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,, a polynomial ring or a quotient of a polynomial
        ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: Ring,, the polynomial ring of which this ring is a
        quotient

Description
===========

+---------------------+
|i1 : A = ZZ[a..d];   |
+---------------------+
|i2 : B = A/(3*a^2-1);|
+---------------------+
|i3 : C = B/(a*b-3);  |
+---------------------+
|i4 : describe C      |
|                     |
|        B            |
|o4 = -------         |
|     a*b - 3         |
+---------------------+
|i5 : ambient C       |
|                     |
|o5 = B               |
|                     |
|o5 : QuotientRing    |
+---------------------+
If R is not a quotient of a polynomial ring, an error is given.

Caveat
======

If the ring is a *note GaloisField: GaloisField,, then the meaning is
different.  See *note ambient(GaloisField): ambient_lpGaloisField_rp,.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "ambient(PolynomialRing)"
  * "ambient(QuotientRing)"
  * *note ambient(Ring): ambient_lpRing_rp, -- ambient polynomial ring
