degreesRing -- the ring or monoid of degrees
********************************************

  * Usage: 
        degreesRing A
        degreesMonoid A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note ring: Ring, or a *note monoid: Monoid,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note polynomial ring: PolynomialRing, or a *note monoid: Monoid,, a
        Laurent polynomial ring or monoid with inverses;

Description
===========

Given a ring or monoid A with *note degree length: degreeLength, $n$,
degreesRing and degreesMonoid produce a Laurent polynomial ring or monoid of
Laurent monomials in $n$ variables, respectively, whose monomials correspond to
the degrees of elements of A. The variable has no subscript when $n=1$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = ZZ[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : degreesRing A                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = ZZ[T]                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : degreesMonoid A                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = monoid[T, Degrees => {1}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32},        |
|                                                {Weights => {-1}   }         |
|                                                {GroupLex => 1     }         |
|                                                {Position => Up    }         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : GeneralOrderedMonoid                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Inverses => true, Global => false]                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : degrees oo                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {{1}}                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : heft A                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {1}                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = QQ[x,y, Degrees => {{1,-2}, {2,-1}}];                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : degreesRing R                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = ZZ[T ..T ]                                                              |
|         0   1                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : degreesMonoid R                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = monoid[T ..T , Degrees => {1, 0}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32},|
|             0   1                                      {Weights => {-1..0}} |
|                                                        {GroupLex => 2     } |
|                                                        {Position => Up    } |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : GeneralOrderedMonoid                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Inverses => true, Global => false]                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : degrees oo                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = {{1}, {0}}                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : heft R                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = {1, 0}                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : S = QQ[x,y, Degrees => {-2,1}];                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : degreesRing S                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = ZZ[T]                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o12 : PolynomialRing                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : degreesMonoid S                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o13 = monoid[T, Degrees => {{}}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32},      |
|                                                  {Weights => {-1}   }       |
|                                                  {GroupLex => 1     }       |
|                                                  {Position => Up    }       |
|                                                                             |
|o13 : GeneralOrderedMonoid                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Inverses => true, Global => false]                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : degrees oo                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o14 = {{}}                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o14 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : heft S                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that in the last example the ring does not have a *note heft vector: heft
vectors,.

*note Hilbert series: hilbertSeries, and *note polynomials: hilbertPolynomial,
of modules over A are elements of its degrees ring over *note ZZ: ZZ,.  The
monomial ordering is chosen so that the Hilbert series, which has an infinite
number of terms, is bounded above by the weight. Elements of this ring are also
used as variables for Poincare polynomials generated by *note poincare:
poincare, and *note poincareN: poincareN,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : R = QQ[x,y, Degrees => {{1,-2,0}, {2,-1,1}}];              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : use degreesRing R                                          |
|                                                                 |
|o17 = ZZ[T ..T ]                                                 |
|          0   2                                                  |
|                                                                 |
|o17 : PolynomialRing                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : hilbertSeries module ideal vars R                          |
|                                                                 |
|         -2    2 -1      3 -3                                    |
|      T T   + T T  T  - T T  T                                   |
|       0 1     0 1  2    0 1  2                                  |
|o18 = -------------------------                                  |
|             2 -1           -2                                   |
|       (1 - T T  T )(1 - T T  )                                  |
|             0 1  2       0 1                                    |
|                                                                 |
|o18 : Expression of class Divide                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i19 : (1+T_1+T_2^2)^3                                            |
|                                                                 |
|       3     2 2     2       4       2          6     4     2    |
|o19 = T  + 3T T  + 3T  + 3T T  + 6T T  + 3T  + T  + 3T  + 3T  + 1|
|       1     1 2     1     1 2     1 2     1    2     2     2    |
|                                                                 |
|o19 : ZZ[T ..T ]                                                 |
|          0   2                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note use: use, -- install or activate object
  * *note heft: heft, -- heft vector of ring or monoid
  * *note poincare: poincare, -- assemble degrees of a ring, module, or ideal
    into a polynomial
  * poincareN (missing documentation)
  * *note hilbertFunction: hilbertFunction, -- the Hilbert function
  * *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial, -- compute the Hilbert
    polynomial
  * *note hilbertSeries: hilbertSeries, -- compute the Hilbert series
  * *note degreeLength: degreeLength, -- the length of the degree vector
  * *note monoid(...,DegreeRank=>...):
    monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegrees=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- specify the degrees of the
    variables
* Menu:

* degreesRing(List): degreesRing_lpList_rp.  the ring or monoid of degrees

