degreesRing(List) -- the ring or monoid of degrees
**************************************************

  * Function: *note degreesRing: degreesRing,
  * Usage: 
        degreesRing L
        degreesMonoid L
        degreesRing n
        degreesMonoid n
  * Inputs:
      * a *note list: List, or an *note integer: ZZ,, see *note heft vectors:
        heft vectors, or *note degreeLength: degreeLength,;
  * Outputs:
      * A, a *note monoid: Monoid, or a *note polynomial ring: PolynomialRing,,
        a monoid of Laurent monomials or ring of Laurent polynomials.

Description
===========

These functions produce either a monoid of Laurent monomials or Laurent
polynomial ring $A$ in n variables, where n is the length of the list L, which
is typically a *note heft vector: heft vectors,. Each monomial in the output
corresponds to a degree vector for a ring with heft vector L or degree length n
and no heft vector.

When a list is given, the variables of the output have degrees given by the
elements of L and weights are the negative of the degrees. When an integer is
given, then the number of variables is n, the degrees are all {}, and the
weights are all -1.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : degreesMonoid {1,2,3}                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = monoid[T ..T , Degrees => {1..3}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32  |
|             0   2                                      {Weights => {-1, -2, |
|                                                        {GroupLex => 3       |
|                                                        {Position => Up      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : GeneralOrderedMonoid                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|   }, Inverses => true, Global => false]                                     |
|-3}}                                                                         |
|   }                                                                         |
|   }                                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : degreesMonoid 3                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = monoid[T ..T , Degrees => {3:{}}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32},|
|             0   2                                      {Weights => {3:-1} } |
|                                                        {GroupLex => 3     } |
|                                                        {Position => Up    } |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : GeneralOrderedMonoid                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Inverses => true, Global => false]                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The monomial ordering used in the degrees ring is RevLex so the polynomials in
it will be displayed with the smallest exponents first, because such
polynomials are often used as Hilbert series.

Assign the degrees ring to a global variable or call *note use(Monoid):
use_lpRing_rp, to assign the indeterminates of the ring or monoid to global
variables.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert instance(T_0, IndexedVariable)                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : use degreesMonoid 3                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = monoid[T ..T , Degrees => {3:{}}, MonomialOrder => {MonomialSize => 32},|
|             0   2                                      {Weights => {3:-1} } |
|                                                        {GroupLex => 3     } |
|                                                        {Position => Up    } |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : GeneralOrderedMonoid                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Inverses => true, Global => false]                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert instance(T_0, degreesMonoid 3)                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : A = degreesRing 4                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = A                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert instance(T_0, degreesRing 4)                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

