numgens(Ring) -- number of generators of a polynomial ring
**********************************************************

  * Function: *note numgens: numgens,
  * Usage: 
        numgens R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,, number of generators of R over the coefficient
        ring

Description
===========

If the ring R is a fraction ring or a (quotient of a) polynomial ring, the
number returned is the number of generators of R over the coefficient ring. In
all other cases, the number of generators is zero.
+-------------------+
|i1 : numgens ZZ    |
|                   |
|o1 = 0             |
+-------------------+
|i2 : A = ZZ[a,b,c];|
+-------------------+
|i3 : numgens A     |
|                   |
|o3 = 3             |
+-------------------+
|i4 : KA = frac A   |
|                   |
|o4 = KA            |
|                   |
|o4 : FractionField |
+-------------------+
|i5 : numgens KA    |
|                   |
|o5 = 3             |
+-------------------+
If the ring is polynomial ring over another polynomial ring, then only the
outermost variables are counted.
+-----------------+
|i6 : B = A[x,y]; |
+-----------------+
|i7 : numgens B   |
|                 |
|o7 = 2           |
+-----------------+
|i8 : C = KA[x,y];|
+-----------------+
|i9 : numgens C   |
|                 |
|o9 = 2           |
+-----------------+
In this case, use the *note CoefficientRing: CoefficientRing, option to *note
generators: generators, to obtain the complete set of generators.
+--------------------------------------------+
|i10 : g = generators(B, CoefficientRing=>ZZ)|
|                                            |
|o10 = {x, y, a, b, c}                       |
|                                            |
|o10 : List                                  |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i11 : #g                                    |
|                                            |
|o11 = 5                                     |
+--------------------------------------------+
Galois fields created using *note GF: GF, have zero generators, but their
underlying polynomial ring has one generators.
+---------------------------+
|i12 : K = GF(9,Variable=>a)|
|                           |
|o12 = K                    |
|                           |
|o12 : GaloisField          |
+---------------------------+
|i13 : numgens K            |
|                           |
|o13 = 1                    |
+---------------------------+
|i14 : R = ambient K        |
|                           |
|o14 = R                    |
|                           |
|o14 : QuotientRing         |
+---------------------------+
|i15 : numgens R            |
|                           |
|o15 = 1                    |
+---------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note generators: generators, -- provide matrix or list of generators
  * *note minimalPresentation: minimalPresentation, -- compute a minimal
    presentation
  * *note GF: GF, -- make a finite field
  * *note ambient: ambient, -- ambient free module of a subquotient, or ambient
    ring

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "numgens(EngineRing)"
  * "numgens(FractionField)"
  * "numgens(MonomialIdeal)"
  * "numgens(PolynomialRing)"
  * "numgens(QuotientRing)"
  * *note numgens(Ring): numgens_lpRing_rp, -- number of generators of a
    polynomial ring
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

