vars(Ring) -- row matrix of the variables
*****************************************

  * Function: *note vars: vars,
  * Usage: 
        vars R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, a matrix with one row whose entries are the
        variables of the ring R

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[w,x,y,z];                  |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : vars S                            |
|                                       |
|o2 = | w x y z |                       |
|                                       |
|             1      4                  |
|o2 : Matrix S  <-- S                   |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : ideal vars S                      |
|                                       |
|o3 = ideal (w, x, y, z)                |
|                                       |
|o3 : Ideal of S                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : coker vars S                      |
|                                       |
|o4 = cokernel | w x y z |              |
|                                       |
|                            1          |
|o4 : S-module, quotient of S           |
+---------------------------------------+
|i5 : res coker vars S                  |
|                                       |
|      1      4      6      4      1    |
|o5 = S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S     |
|                                       |
|     0      1      2      3      4     |
|                                       |
|o5 : Complex                           |
+---------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = S/(x^2-w*y, x*y-w*z, x*z-y^2);|
+---------------------------------------+
|i7 : vars R                            |
|                                       |
|o7 = | w x y z |                       |
|                                       |
|             1      4                  |
|o7 : Matrix R  <-- R                   |
+---------------------------------------+
|i8 : use S;                            |
+---------------------------------------+
|i9 : Q = S/(x^2-w*y, z);               |
+---------------------------------------+
|i10 : vars S                           |
|                                       |
|o10 = | w x y z |                      |
|                                       |
|              1      4                 |
|o10 : Matrix S  <-- S                  |
+---------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

