flattenRing(...,CoefficientRing=>...) -- specify the coefficient ring of the flattened ring
*******************************************************************************************

Description
===========

Use this option to change the default behavior of *note flattenRing:
flattenRing,, by setting the option to the desired *note coefficientRing:
coefficientRing, of the output ring.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : k = toField (QQ[x]/(x^2+x+1));                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = k[y]/(x-y+2);                                            |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (S, f) = flattenRing(R); describe S                          |
|                                                                  |
|         k[y]                                                     |
|o4 = -----------                                                  |
|     - y + x + 2                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : (S2, f2) = flattenRing(R, CoefficientRing => QQ); describe S2|
|                                                                  |
|              QQ[y, x]                                            |
|o6 = -------------------------                                    |
|       2                                                          |
|     (x  + x + 1, - y + x + 2)                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

See *note flattenRing: flattenRing, documentation for more examples and
details.

See also
========

  * *note flattenRing: flattenRing, -- write a ring as a (quotient of a)
    polynomial ring

