File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: generators, Prev: flattenRing, Up: Ring

generators -- provide matrix or list of generators
**************************************************

  * Usage: 
        generators x
        gens x
  * Inputs:
      * x
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientRing: generators_lpRing_rp, => ..., default value
        null, only used if x is a ring
  * Outputs:
      * provides the generators of x in a convenient form, as a list or a
        matrix, depending on the type

Description
===========


Produces the generators of a Gröbner basis, a polynomial ring, an ideal, a free
module, a free group, a submodule given by means of generators (or for which
generators have been computed), or a free monoid.


Usually the result is a list of generators, but the generators of a module or
Gröbner basis are provided as the columns in a matrix. The matrix is stored in
a module M under M.generators, unless the matrix is the identity matrix.


The symbol gens is a synonym for generators.

See also
========

  * *note numgens: numgens, -- the number of generators
  * *note Monoid: Monoid, -- the class of all monoids
  * *note GroebnerBasis: GroebnerBasis, -- the class of all Gröbner bases
  * *note Module: Module, -- the class of all modules
  * *note relations: relations, -- the defining relations
  * *note subquotient: subquotient, -- make a subquotient module

Ways to use generators:
=======================

  * *note generators(GroebnerBasis): generators_lpGroebnerBasis_rp, -- the
    generator matrix of a Gröbner basis
  * *note generators(Ideal): generators_lpIdeal_rp, -- the generator matrix of
    an ideal
  * "generators(MonomialIdeal)" -- see *note generators(Ideal):
    generators_lpIdeal_rp, -- the generator matrix of an ideal
  * *note generators(Module): generators_lpModule_rp, -- the generator matrix
    of a module
  * *note generators(Monoid): generators_lpMonoid_rp, -- list of generators
  * *note generators(Ring): generators_lpRing_rp, -- the list of generators of
    a ring

For the programmer
