InexactFieldFamily -- the class of all families of inexact fields
*****************************************************************

Description
===========

All real numbers have the same class, *note RR: RR,, but the rings they belong
to depends on the number of binary digits of precision used to represent them.
Similarly for complex numbers, which all belong to the class *note CC: CC,.
Thus *note RR: RR, and *note CC: CC, are regarded not as inexact fields, but as
families of inexact fields.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : x = 1/3.                                                      |
|                                                                   |
|o1 = .3333333333333333                                             |
|                                                                   |
|o1 : RR (of precision 53)                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : class x                                                       |
|                                                                   |
|o2 = RR                                                            |
|                                                                   |
|o2 : InexactFieldFamily                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : ring x                                                        |
|                                                                   |
|o3 = RR                                                            |
|       53                                                          |
|                                                                   |
|o3 : RealField                                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : x = 1/3.p200                                                  |
|                                                                   |
|o4 = .3333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333333334|
|                                                                   |
|o4 : RR (of precision 200)                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : class x                                                       |
|                                                                   |
|o5 = RR                                                            |
|                                                                   |
|o5 : InexactFieldFamily                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : ring x                                                        |
|                                                                   |
|o6 = RR                                                            |
|       200                                                         |
|                                                                   |
|o6 : RealField                                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note InexactField: InexactField, -- the class of inexact fields

Methods that use an inexact field family:
=========================================

  * "default(InexactFieldFamily)" -- see *note default: default, -- default
    member of a family
  * "InexactFieldFamily Array" -- see *note Ring Array: Ring Array, -- the
    standard way to make a polynomial ring
  * "InexactFieldFamily List" -- see *note Ring List: Ring List, -- make a
    local polynomial ring
  * "InexactFieldFamily Monoid" -- see *note Ring Monoid: Ring Monoid, -- make
    a polynomial ring

Protected objects of class InexactFieldFamily:
==============================================

  * *note CC: CC, -- the class of all complex numbers
  * *note CCi: CCi, -- the class of all complex intervals
  * *note RR: RR, -- the class of all real numbers
  * *note RRi: RRi, -- the class of all real intervals

