isPrime -- whether a integer or polynomial is prime
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isPrime f
  * Inputs:
      * f, an *note integer: ZZ,, or an element in a *note polynomial ring:
        PolynomialRing,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, *note true: true, if f is either a
        prime integer or an irreducible polynomial and *note false: false,
        otherwise

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : ZZ/2[t];                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isPrime(t^2+t+1)                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isPrime(t^2+1)                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isPrime 101                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isPrime 1581741965468191654681185746811965468118567481185674811856695018|
|                                                                             |
|o5 = true                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|56749                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isPrime 1581741965468191654681185746811965468118567481185674811856695018|
|                                                                             |
|o6 = false                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|56749^2                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Since *note factor: factor, returns factors guaranteed only to be pseudoprimes,
it may be useful to check their primality, as follows.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : f = factor 28752093487520394720397634653456                             |
|                                                                             |
|      4                                                                      |
|o7 = 2 109*1831*3014311519*2987077659845341                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : Expression of class Product                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : peek'_2 f                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = Product{Power{2, 4}, Power{109, 1}, Power{1831, 1}, Power{3014311519,   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     1}, Power{2987077659845341, 1}}                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : first \ toList f                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = {2, 109, 1831, 3014311519, 2987077659845341}                            |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : isPrime \ oo                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = {true, true, true, true, true}                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Primality testing for integers is handled by *note FLINT: FLINT,.

See also
========

  * *note factor: factor, -- factor a ring element or a ZZ-module
  * *note isPseudoprime: isPseudoprime_lpZZ_rp, -- whether an integer is
    probably prime
  * *note isPrime(Ideal): (MinimalPrimes)isPrime_lpIdeal_rp, -- whether an
    ideal is prime

Ways to use isPrime:
====================

  * "isPrime(RingElement)"
  * "isPrime(ZZ)"
  * isPrime(Ideal) (missing documentation)

