toRR -- convert to high-precision real number
*********************************************

  * Usage: 
        toRR(prec,x)
  * Inputs:
      * prec, an *note integer: ZZ,, the number of bits of precision desired
      * x, a *note real number: RR,, an *note integer: ZZ,, or a *note rational
        number: QQ,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note real number: RR,, the result of converting x to a
        high-precision real number

Description
===========

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : toRR(200,1/7)                                                 |
|                                                                   |
|o1 = .1428571428571428571428571428571428571428571428571428571428571|
|                                                                   |
|o1 : RR (of precision 200)                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : precision oo                                                  |
|                                                                   |
|o2 = 200                                                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

For the programmer
==================

The object *note toRR: toRR, is a *note compiled function: CompiledFunction,.

