toRRi -- construct an interval
******************************

  * Usage: 
        I = toRRi(n)
        I = toRRi(l,r)
        I = toRRi(prec,l,r)
  * Inputs:
      * n, a *note number: Number,, 
      * l, a *note number: Number,, 
      * r, a *note number: Number,, 
      * prec, an *note integer: ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * I, a *note real interval: RRi,, 

Description
===========

Returns an interval as small as possible containing n or from l to r.  Note
that if l is to the right of r, the constructed interval is empty.  This is a
more low-level function and *note interval: interval, or span should be used
instead.

