diameter -- diameter of an interval
***********************************

  * Usage: 
        x = diameter I
  * Inputs:
      * I, a *note real interval: RRi, or a *note complex interval: CCi,, 
  * Outputs:
      * x, a *note real number: RR,, 

Description
===========

Returns the diameter (the difference between the endpoints) of the input
interval.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : interval (2, 7)      |
|                          |
|o1 = [2,7]                |
|                          |
|o1 : RRi (of precision 53)|
+--------------------------+
|i2 : diameter oo          |
|                          |
|o2 = 5                    |
|                          |
|o2 : RR (of precision 53) |
+--------------------------+

For a complex interval, the length of the diagonal in the complex plane is
returned.

+---------------------------+
|i3 : interval (0, 3 + 4*ii)|
|                           |
|o3 = [0,3]+[0,4]*ii        |
|                           |
|o3 : CCi (of precision 53) |
+---------------------------+
|i4 : diameter oo           |
|                           |
|o4 = 5                     |
|                           |
|o4 : RR (of precision 53)  |
+---------------------------+

