toCC -- convert to high-precision complex number
************************************************

Description
===========

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        toCC(prec,x,y)
        toCC(prec,x)
  * Inputs:
      * prec, an *note integer: ZZ,, the number of bits of precision desired
      * x, an *note integer: ZZ,, a *note rational number: QQ,, or a *note real
        number: RR,
      * y, an *note integer: ZZ,, a *note rational number: QQ,, or a *note real
        number: RR,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex number: CC,, the complex number with real part x and
        complex part y.  If y is omitted, the imaginary part is zero.
+--------------------------+
|i1 : toCC(200,7)          |
|                          |
|o1 = 7                    |
|                          |
|o1 : CC (of precision 200)|
+--------------------------+
|i2 : toCC(100,7,3.)       |
|                          |
|o2 = 7+3*ii               |
|                          |
|o2 : CC (of precision 100)|
+--------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        toCC(x,y)
        toCC x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note real number: RR,
      * y, a *note real number: RR,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex number: CC,, the complex number with real part x and
        complex part y.  If y is omitted, the imaginary part is zero.  The
        precision of the result is the minimum precision of the arguments.
+--------------------------+
|i3 : toCC(3.,4.)          |
|                          |
|o3 = 3+4*ii               |
|                          |
|o3 : CC (of precision 53) |
+--------------------------+
|i4 : toCC(3.p100,4.p200)  |
|                          |
|o4 = 3+4*ii               |
|                          |
|o4 : CC (of precision 100)|
+--------------------------+

Ways to use toCC:
=================

  * "toCC(CC)"
  * "toCC(QQ)"
