toCCi -- construct an interval
******************************

  * Usage: 
        I = toCCi(n)
        I = toCCi(re,im)
        I = toCCi(prec,re,im)
  * Inputs:
      * n, a *note complex number: CC,, 
      * re, a *note real interval: RRi,, 
      * im, a *note real interval: RRi,, 
      * prec, an *note integer: ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * I, a *note complex interval: CCi,, 

Description
===========

Returns an interval as small as possible containing n or from l to r.  Note
that if l is to the right of r, the constructed interval is empty.  This is a
more low-level function and *note interval: interval, or span should be used
instead.

See also
========

  * *note span(List): span, -- construct smallest interval
  * *note span(Sequence): span, -- construct smallest interval
  * *note interval: interval, -- construct an interval

For the programmer
==================

The object *note toCCi: toCCi, is a *note compiled function: CompiledFunction,.

