integers modulo a prime
***********************

Create the ring of integers modulo a prime number p as follows.
+-----------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101  |
|                 |
|o1 = R           |
|                 |
|o1 : QuotientRing|
+-----------------+
We can create elements of the ring as follows.
+----------+
|i2 : 9_R  |
|          |
|o2 = 9    |
|          |
|o2 : R    |
+----------+
|i3 : 103_R|
|          |
|o3 = 2    |
|          |
|o3 : R    |
+----------+
The usual arithmetic operations are available.
+-----------------------+
|i4 : 9_R * 11_R        |
|                       |
|o4 = -2                |
|                       |
|o4 : R                 |
+-----------------------+
|i5 : 9_R ^ 11          |
|                       |
|o5 = 49                |
|                       |
|o5 : R                 |
+-----------------------+
|i6 : 9_R * 11_R == -2_R|
|                       |
|o6 = true              |
+-----------------------+
Find the inverse of an integer modulo a prime as follows.
+------------+
|i7 : 17_R^-1|
|            |
|o7 = 6      |
|            |
|o7 : R      |
+------------+
To view this element as an element of ZZ use the *note lift: lift, command.
+-----------------------+
|i8 : lift (17_R^-1, ZZ)|
|                       |
|o8 = 6                 |
+-----------------------+
* Menu:

* char::                        get the characteristic of the ring or field
* getPrimeWithRootOfUnity::     find a prime p with a primitive n-th root of unity r in ZZ/p
