getPrimeWithRootOfUnity -- find a prime p with a primitive n-th root of unity r in ZZ/p
***************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (p,r)=getPrimeWithRootOfUnity(n,r1)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,, the exponent of the root of unity
      * r1, an *note integer: ZZ,, tentative root of unity
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Range => ..., default value (10000,30000), (a,b), specifying an
        integral interval in which we search for a prime number with desired
        properties. If $b < a + 2*\log a$ an error message will be returned.
  * Outputs:
      * p, an *note integer: ZZ,, a prime in the specified range. The default
        range is $(10^4,3*10^4)$
      * r, an *note integer: ZZ,, a primitive n-th root of unity mod p

Description
===========

We compute the prime p as a larger prime factor of $r1^n-1$. If the largest p
in the desired range does not work, we pass to $r1+1$ and repeat.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 12                                                 |
|                                                            |
|o1 = 12                                                     |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : (p,r) = getPrimeWithRootOfUnity(n,5)                   |
|                                                            |
|o2 = (20593, 12)                                            |
|                                                            |
|o2 : Sequence                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : factor(r^n-1)                                          |
|                                                            |
|o3 = 5*7*11*13*19*29*157*20593                              |
|                                                            |
|o3 : Expression of class Product                            |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : r^12%p==1, r^6%p==1, r^4%p==1                          |
|                                                            |
|o4 = (true, false, false)                                   |
|                                                            |
|o4 : Sequence                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : (p,r) = getPrimeWithRootOfUnity(12,11,Range=>(100,200))|
|                                                            |
|o5 = (157, 22)                                              |
|                                                            |
|o5 : Sequence                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : factor(r^n-1)                                          |
|                                                            |
|      2      2                                              |
|o6 = 3 5*7*13 23*97*157*463*1489                            |
|                                                            |
|o6 : Expression of class Product                            |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : r^12%p==1, r^6%p==1, r^4%p==1                          |
|                                                            |
|o7 = (true, false, false)                                   |
|                                                            |
|o7 : Sequence                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note nextPrime: nextPrime, -- compute the smallest prime greater than or
    equal to a given number

Ways to use getPrimeWithRootOfUnity:
====================================

  * "getPrimeWithRootOfUnity(ZZ,ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note getPrimeWithRootOfUnity: getPrimeWithRootOfUnity, is a *note
method function with options: MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

