Ring Array -- the standard way to make a polynomial ring
********************************************************

  * Operator: *note SPACE: SPACE,

Description
===========

R[...] -- produces the monoid ring from a ring R and the ordered monoid
specified by [...].


This is the customary way to make a polynomial ring.


Optional arguments (placed inside the array):
  * *note DegreeGroup: DegreeGroup, -- an optional argument
  * *note Variables: Variables, -- an optional argument
  * *note DegreeLift: DegreeLift, -- an optional argument
  * *note VariableBaseName: VariableBaseName, -- an optional argument
  * *note DegreeRank: DegreeRank, -- an optional argument
  * *note Weights: Weights, -- assigning weights to the variables
  * *note Inverses: Inverses, -- an optional argument
  * *note Global: MonomialOrder, -- monomial ordering
  * *note MonomialOrder: MonomialOrder, -- monomial ordering
  * *note WeylAlgebra: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeylAlgebra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, --
    specify differential operators in the ring
  * *note Degrees: Degrees, -- an optional argument
  * *note Join: Join, -- an optional argument
  * *note MonomialSize: MonomialSize, -- an optional argument
  * *note Local: Local, -- an optional argument
  * *note Heft: Heft, -- an optional argument
  * *note Constants: Constants, -- an optional argument
  * *note SkewCommutative: SkewCommutative, -- an optional argument
  * *note DegreeMap: DegreeMap, -- an optional argument

See also
========

  * *note polynomial rings: polynomial rings,

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "InexactFieldFamily Array"
  * *note Ring Array: Ring Array, -- the standard way to make a polynomial ring
