get a ring variable by index -- get a ring variable by index
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        R_i
  * Inputs:
      * R
      * i
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: RingElement,, the i-th generator of the ring R
The indexing of generators is based on 0, so R_0 would be the first one, and so
on.
+-------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[a..d]  |
|                   |
|o1 = R             |
|                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing|
+-------------------+
|i2 : R_2           |
|                   |
|o2 = c             |
|                   |
|o2 : R             |
+-------------------+


If the coefficient ring is a polynomial ring, then the numbering matches that
in the list returned by *note generators: generators,.
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = R[x,y,z]                     |
|                                      |
|o3 = S                                |
|                                      |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                   |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : generators(S,CoefficientRing=>ZZ)|
|                                      |
|o4 = {x, y, z, a, b, c, d}            |
|                                      |
|o4 : List                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : S_2                              |
|                                      |
|o5 = z                                |
|                                      |
|o5 : S                                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : S_6                              |
|                                      |
|o6 = d                                |
|                                      |
|o6 : S                                |
+--------------------------------------+

