monoid(Ring) -- make or retrieve a monoid
*****************************************

  * Function: *note monoid: monoid,
  * Usage: 
        monoid R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Constants: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmJoin=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, specify how to handle degrees in the coefficient
        ring
      * *note DegreeGroup: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegrees=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, specify the degrees of the variables
      * *note DegreeLift: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLift=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null, specify maps between degree groups
      * *note DegreeMap: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLift=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, specify maps between degree groups
      * *note DegreeRank: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegrees=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, specify the degrees of the variables
      * *note Degrees: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegrees=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, specify the degrees of the variables
      * *note Global: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLocal=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value true, specify local or global monomial order
      * *note Heft: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmHeft=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value null, specify a heft vector
      * *note Inverses: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmInverses=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, allow negative exponents in monomials
      * *note Join: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmJoin=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value null, specify how to handle degrees in the coefficient ring
      * *note Local: monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLocal=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
