monoid(...,Inverses=>...) -- allow negative exponents in monomials
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        monoid[X,Y, Inverses => P]

Description
===========

The optional argument Inverses specifies whether negative exponents will be
allowed, making the monoid into a group. This option is mainly used by *note
degreesMonoid: degreesRing, and *note degreesRing: degreesRing, functions to
allow negative exponents in the monomials.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x,y, Inverses => true, MonomialOrder => Lex]|
|                                                        |
|o1 = S                                                  |
|                                                        |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S_{1,-1} + S_{-1,1}                                |
|                                                        |
|        -1    -1                                        |
|o2 = x*y   + x  y                                       |
|                                                        |
|o2 : S                                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

This option may also be used when creating a new ring from an existing ring,
creating a tensor product ring, or symmetric algebra.

