monoid(...,Weights=>...) -- specify weights of the variables
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        monoid[a,b,c, Weights => {w1, w2, w3}]

Description
===========

This option specifies the weights of the variables in the monoid. The orderings
by these weight vectors is prepended to the list of orderings provided by the
*note monoid(...,MonomialOrder=>...):
monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMonomialOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, option. The value must be a
list integers when the degree length is one, or a list of lists of integers
otherwise.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]                   |
|                                   |
|o1 = R                             |
|                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : leadTerm matrix {{x+y, x^2+y}}|
|                                   |
|o2 = | x x2 |                      |
|                                   |
