File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: MonomialOrder, Next: obtaining the monomial order of a ring, Prev: NCLex, Up: monomial orderings

MonomialOrder -- monomial ordering
**********************************

Description
===========

MonomialOrder -- an optional argument used with polynomial rings and monoids to
indicate a monomial ordering other than the default (graded reverse
lexicographic).


In Macaulay2, each polynomial ring (and also each monoid) is equipped with a
monomial order, which is used for display of polynomials (terms are listed in
descending monomial order), and also for Gröbner basis computations.


In the most general setting, a monomial ordering is given by a list of ordering
tests, of various types listed and described below, each of which provides a
partial ordering on the monomials.  The ordering tests are applied
sequentially, starting with the first one, until one monomial is judged greater
than the other. At the end, if necessary, the graded reverse lexicographic
order is used to compare the monomials. For examples, see below, or see *note
monomial orderings: monomial orderings,.


Permissible elements:
  * *note GRevLex: GRevLex, => n -- A graded reverse lexicographic block of
    variables
  * *note Lex: Lex, => n
  * *note Weights: Weights, => {...}
  * *note Position: MonomialOrder, => Up  or  Position => Down
  * *note RevLex: RevLex, => n
  * *note GroupLex: GroupLex, => n
  * *note GroupRevLex: GroupRevLex, => n
  * *note MonomialSize: MonomialSize, => n, n being 8,16,32, or 64.  Set the
    packing size for exponents for further variables


Some examples of monomial orders.  Note that if only one item is in the list,
we can dispense with the list.
  * MonomialOrder => {GRevLex=>2, GRevLex=>3} -- a product order
  * MonomialOrder => {2, 3} -- same
  * MonomialOrder => {Weights=>{1,13,6,2}} -- a weight order
  * MonomialOrder => Weights=>{1,13,6,2} -- same
If any monomials will be less than 1 in the ordering, then the option Global =>
false should be used.
+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : QQ[x,y, Weights => {-1,1}, Global => false]|
|                                                |
|o1 = QQ[x..y]                                   |
|                                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                             |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : x<1                                        |
|                                                |
|o2 = true                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : y<1                                        |
|                                                |
|o3 = false                                      |
+------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note monomial orderings: monomial orderings,
  * *note weightGrevlex: (QthPower)weightGrevlex, -- transform a weight matrix
    into a monomial ordering matrix
  * *note grevlexWeight: (QthPower)grevlexWeight, -- transform a weight matrix
    into a monomial ordering matrix

Functions with optional argument named MonomialOrder:
=====================================================

  * "graphIdeal(...,MonomialOrder=>...)" -- see *note graphIdeal(RingMap):
    graphIdeal_lpRingMap_rp, -- the ideal of the graph of the regular map
    corresponding to a ring map
  * "graphRing(...,MonomialOrder=>...)" -- see *note graphRing(RingMap):
    graphRing_lpRingMap_rp, -- the coordinate ring of the graph of the regular
    map corresponding to a ring map
  * *note monoid(...,MonomialOrder=>...):
    monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMonomialOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- specify the monomial
    ordering
  * "newRing(...,MonomialOrder=>...)" -- see *note newRing: newRing, -- make a
    copy of a ring, with some features changed
  * "pushForward(...,MonomialOrder=>...)" -- see *note
    pushForward(RingMap,Module): pushForward_lpRingMap_cmModule_rp, -- compute
    the pushforward of a module along a ring map
  * *note rsort(...,MonomialOrder=>...):
    rsort_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMonomialOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- specify Ascending or
    Descending monomial order
  * *note sort(...,MonomialOrder=>...):
    sort_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMonomialOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- specify Ascending or
    Descending monomial order
  * *note sortColumns(...,MonomialOrder=>...):
    sortColumns_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMonomialOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- specify Ascending
    or Descending monomial order
  * "symmetricAlgebra(...,MonomialOrder=>...)" -- see *note symmetricAlgebra:
    symmetricAlgebra, -- the symmetric algebra of a module
  * "tensor(Monoid,Monoid,MonomialOrder=>...)" -- see *note
    tensor(Monoid,Monoid): tensor_lpMonoid_cmMonoid_rp, -- tensor product of
    monoids
  * "tensor(Ring,Ring,MonomialOrder=>...)" -- see *note tensor(Monoid,Monoid):
    tensor_lpMonoid_cmMonoid_rp, -- tensor product of monoids

