standardForm -- convert to standard form
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        standardForm f
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: HashTable,, the polynomial or monomial in a form
        involving hash tables.

Description
===========

A polynomial is represented by hash tables in which the keys are hash tables
representing the monomials and the values are the coefficients. The monomials
themselves are represented by hash tables in which the keys are the variables
and the values are the corresponding exponents.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y,z];                   |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : standardForm (x^2 - 7 + x*y*z^11 + y)|
|                                          |
|o2 = HashTable{HashTable{} => -7      }   |
|               HashTable{0 => 1 } => 1    |
|                         1 => 1           |
|                         2 => 11          |
|               HashTable{0 => 2} => 1     |
|               HashTable{1 => 1} => 1     |
|                                          |
|o2 : HashTable                            |
+------------------------------------------+

Code
====

../../../../../Macaulay2/m2/monoids.m2:146:30-150:86: --source code:
standardForm RingElement   := f -> (
    R := ring f;
    k := coefficientRing R;
    (cc, mm) := rawPairs(raw k, raw f);
    new HashTable from toList apply(cc, mm, (c, m) -> (standardForm m, new k
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
from c)))

See also
========

  * *note listForm: listForm, -- convert to list form
  * *note content: content, -- the content of a polynomial
  * *note coefficients: coefficients, -- get the monomials and coefficients of
    a polynomial or matrix
  * *note exponents: exponents, -- the exponents of a polynomial
  * *note monomials: monomials, -- matrix of monomials in a ring element or
    matrix

Ways to use standardForm:
=========================

  * "standardForm(MonoidElement)"
  * "standardForm(RingElement)"

