factoring polynomials
*********************

Polynomials can be factored with *note factor: factor,.  Factorization works in
polynomial rings over prime finite fields, ZZ, or QQ.
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/10007[a,b];                                         |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = (2*a+3)^4 + 5                                          |
|                                                                |
|        4      3       2                                        |
|o2 = 16a  + 96a  + 216a  + 216a + 86                            |
|                                                                |
|o2 : R                                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : g = (2*a+b+1)^3                                            |
|                                                                |
|       3      2        2    3      2             2              |
|o3 = 8a  + 12a b + 6a*b  + b  + 12a  + 12a*b + 3b  + 6a + 3b + 1|
|                                                                |
|o3 : R                                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : S = factor f                                               |
|                                                                |
|                         2                                      |
|o4 = (a - 402)(a + 405)(a  + 3a - 2301)(16)                     |
|                                                                |
|o4 : Expression of class Product                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : T = factor g                                               |
|                                                                |
|                       3                                        |
|o5 = (a - 5003b - 5003) (8)                                     |
|                                                                |
|o5 : Expression of class Product                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+


The results have been packaged for easy viewing.  The number of factors is
obtained using
+-------+
|i6 : #T|
|       |
|o6 = 2 |
+-------+
Each factor is represented as a power (exponents equal to 1 don't appear in the
display.)  The parts can be extracted with *note #: #,.
+------------------------------+
|i7 : T#0                      |
|                              |
|                       3      |
|o7 = (a - 5003b - 5003)       |
|                              |
|o7 : Expression of class Power|
+------------------------------+
|i8 : T#0#0                    |
|                              |
|o8 = a - 5003b - 5003         |
|                              |
|o8 : R                        |
+------------------------------+
|i9 : T#0#1                    |
|                              |
|o9 = 3                        |
+------------------------------+
* Menu:

* roots(RingElement): roots_lpRingElement_rp.  compute the roots of a polynomial
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/ov_rings.m2:1175:0.

