setupLift -- set up lift from one ring to another
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        setupLift (f,R,S)
        setupLift g
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note function: Function,, 
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,, 
      * S, a *note ring: Ring,, 
      * g, a *note ring map: RingMap,, 

Description
===========

There are two possible ways of implementing *note lift: lift, using setupLift.
In the first one, we use a function:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x]                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S=QQ[y]                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : setupPromote map(R,S,{x^2})                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : setupLift(a->sum(listForm a, (e,c)->if odd first e then error "not      |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|liftable" else c*y^(first e//2)),R,S)                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : promote(y^2+2,R)                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|      4                                                                      |
|o5 = x  + 2                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : lift(oo,S)                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|      2                                                                      |
|o6 = y  + 2                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : S                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : lift(x,S,Verify=>false)                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In the second one, we define a ring map which is a partial inverse to the
promotion map:

+------------------------------------------+
|i8 : R=QQ[x,y]                            |
|                                          |
|o8 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o8 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i9 : S=R[s]                               |
|                                          |
|o9 = S                                    |
|                                          |
|o9 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i10 : setupPromote map(R,S,{x+y})         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i11 : setupLift map(S,R,{s,0})            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i12 : promote(s^3+2*s-1,R)                |
|                                          |
|       3     2        2    3              |
|o12 = x  + 3x y + 3x*y  + y  + 2x + 2y - 1|
|                                          |
|o12 : R                                   |
+------------------------------------------+
|i13 : lift(oo,S)                          |
|                                          |
|       3                                  |
|o13 = s  + 2s - 1                         |
|                                          |
|o13 : S                                   |
+------------------------------------------+
|i14 : lift(x,S,Verify=>false)             |
+------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note setupPromote: setupPromote, -- set up promote from one ring to
    another

Ways to use setupLift:
======================

  * "setupLift(Function,Ring,Ring)"
  * "setupLift(RingMap)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note setupLift: setupLift, is a *note method function:
MethodFunction,.

