newRing -- make a copy of a ring, with some features changed
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = newRing(R, options)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: PolynomialRing, or a *note quotient ring:
        QuotientRing,,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Variables => a *note list: List,, default value nothing, see *note
        monoid(...,Variables=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariables=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * VariableBaseName => a *note symbol: Symbol,, default value nothing, see
        *note monoid(...,VariableBaseName=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariables=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * Global => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value nothing, see
        *note monoid(...,Global=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLocal=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * Local => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value nothing, see
        *note monoid(...,Local=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmLocal=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * Inverses => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value nothing, see
        *note monoid(...,Inverses=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmInverses=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * Weights => a *note list: List,, default value nothing, see *note
        monoid(...,Weights=>...): monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeights=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * Degrees => a *note list: List,, default value nothing, see *note
        monoid(...,Degrees=>...): monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegrees=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * DegreeMap => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value nothing,
        see *note monoid(...,DegreeMap=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLift=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * DegreeLift => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value nothing,
        see *note monoid(...,DegreeLift=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLift=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * DegreeRank => an *note integer: ZZ,, default value nothing, see *note
        monoid(...,DegreeRank=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegrees=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * Heft => a *note list: List,, default value nothing, see *note
        monoid(...,Heft=>...): monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmHeft=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * Join => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value nothing, see
        *note monoid(...,Join=>...): monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmJoin=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * Constants => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value nothing,
        see *note monoid(...,Join=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmJoin=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * MonomialOrder => a *note list: List,, default value nothing, see *note
        monoid(...,MonomialOrder=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMonomialOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * MonomialSize => an *note integer: ZZ,, default value nothing, see *note
        monoid(...,MonomialSize=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMonomialSize=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * SkewCommutative => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value
        nothing, see *note monoid(...,SkewCommutative=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSkewCommutative=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * WeylAlgebra => a *note list: List,, default value nothing, see *note
        monoid(...,WeylAlgebra=>...):
        monoid_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmWeylAlgebra=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,;
      * DegreeGroup => ..., default value nothing
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note ring: Ring,, a new ring, constructed in the same way R was,
        over the same coefficient ring, but with the newly specified options
        overriding those used before. See *note monoid: monoid, for a
        description of those options. If R was a quotient ring, then the number
        of variables must be the same, and S will be a quotient ring, too, with
        defining ideal obtained from the old by substituting the new variables
        for the old, preserving their order.

Description
===========

If a different number of variables is given with *note Variables: Variables,,
then the list of degrees in R will be ignored.  If a new degree rank is
specified with *note DegreeRank: DegreeRank, then the list of degrees and the
heft vector of R will be ignored.  If a new nonempty list of degrees is
specified with *note Degrees: Degrees,, then the degree rank and the heft
vector of R will be ignored.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y, MonomialOrder => Lex, Degrees => {3,5}];                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : describe newRing(R, MonomialOrder => GRevLex)                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = QQ[x..y, Degrees => {3, 5}, Heft => {1}, MonomialOrder =>               |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{MonomialSize => 32}]                                                        |
|{GRevLex => {3, 5} }                                                         |
|{Position => Up    }                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : describe newRing(R, Variables => 4)                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = QQ[p ..p , Degrees => {4:1}, Heft => {1}, MonomialOrder =>              |
|         0   3                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{MonomialSize => 32}]                                                        |
|{Lex => 2          }                                                         |
|{Position => Up    }                                                         |
|{GRevLex => {2:1}  }                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : describe newRing(R, Heft => {2})                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = QQ[x..y, Degrees => {3, 5}, Heft => {2}, MonomialOrder =>               |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{MonomialSize => 32}]                                                        |
|{Lex => 2          }                                                         |
|{Position => Up    }                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S = R/(x^2+y^3);                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : describe newRing(R, Variables => 2)                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = QQ[p ..p , Degrees => {3, 5}, Heft => {1}, MonomialOrder =>             |
|         0   1                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{MonomialSize => 32}]                                                        |
|{Lex => 2          }                                                         |
|{Position => Up    }                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

