kernel(RingMap) -- kernel of a ringmap
**************************************

  * Function: *note kernel: kernel,
  * Usage: 
        kernel f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring map: RingMap,, R --> S
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note SubringLimit: kernel_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSubringLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        an *note integer: ZZ,, default value infinity, stop the computation
        after this many elements of the kernel have been found
      * DegreeLimit (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: Ideal,, an ideal of R

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = QQ[s,t];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : F = map(S,R,{s^3, s^2*t, s*t^2, t^3})                                   |
|                                                                             |
|                  3   2      2   3                                           |
|o3 = map (S, R, {s , s t, s*t , t })                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : RingMap S <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : ker F                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|             2                    2                                          |
|o4 = ideal (c  - b*d, b*c - a*d, b  - a*c)                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : G = map(S,R,{s^5, s^3*t^2-t, s*t-s, t^5})                               |
|                                                                             |
|                  5   3 2                5                                   |
|o5 = map (S, R, {s , s t  - t, s*t - s, t })                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : RingMap S <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : ker(G, SubringLimit=>1)                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|            2 10      2   7     2 7      2 2 4     3 5         6       3 3   |
|o6 = ideal(a c   + 10a b*c  - 5a c  + 25a b c  + 2a c  - 5a*b*c  - 5a*b c  + |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|         6      5      2 3       3   2       2 3       4      2 2      3 2   |
|     5a*c  - a*b  + 10a b c - 15a b*c  - 5a*b c  - 5a*b  + 25a b c - 5a c  - |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      5    4        3      2           2     2                               |
|     c  + a  - 10a*b  + 20a b*c - 10a*b  + 5a c - 5a*b - a)                  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
In the case when everything is homogeneous, Hilbert functions are used to speed
up the computations.

Caveat
======

It should be possible to interrupt the computation and restart it, but this has
not yet been implemented.

See also
========

  * *note substitution and maps between rings: substitution and maps between
    rings,
  * *note elimination of variables: elimination of variables,
  * *note monomialCurveIdeal: monomialCurveIdeal, -- make the ideal of a
    monomial curve
* Menu:

* kernel(...,SubringLimit=>...): kernel_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSubringLimit=>_pd_pd_pd_rp.  stop after finding enough elements of a subring

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note kernel(RingMap): kernel_lpRingMap_rp, -- kernel of a ringmap
