newCoordinateSystem -- change variables
***************************************

Description
===========

newCoordinateSystem(S,m) -- takes a one-rowed matrix m of independent linear
forms over a ring R and returns a pair (f,g), where f is a ring map given by
some linear change of coordinates from R to S which sends the last variables of
R to the forms in m, and g is the inverse of f.


The ring S should have the same number of variables as S.
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a..d]                                     |
|                                                          |
|o1 = R                                                    |
|                                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = ZZ/101[p..s]                                     |
|                                                          |
|o2 = S                                                    |
|                                                          |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (f,g) = newCoordinateSystem(S,matrix{{a+2*b,3*c-d}});|
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f                                                    |
|                                                          |
|o4 = map (S, R, {50p, 3r, p + 2q, 3r - s})                |
|                                                          |
|o4 : RingMap S <-- R                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : g                                                    |
|                                                          |
|o5 = map (R, S, {-2a, a - 50c, 34b, b - d})               |
|                                                          |
|o5 : RingMap R <-- S                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

