isField -- whether something is a field
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        isField R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, *note true: true, if R was explicitly
        constructed as a field (no computation is done) and *note false: false,
        otherwise

Description
===========

This function recognizes basic fields, *note Galois fields: GaloisField, and
*note fraction fields: FractionField,.
+---------------------------+
|i1 : isField QQ            |
|                           |
|o1 = true                  |
+---------------------------+
|i2 : isField CC_53         |
|                           |
|o2 = true                  |
+---------------------------+
|i3 : isField GF(2,3)       |
|                           |
|o3 = true                  |
+---------------------------+
|i4 : isField(frac(QQ[x,y]))|
|                           |
|o4 = true                  |
+---------------------------+
This function will not recognize other rings as fields.
+----------------------+
|i5 : R = QQ[x]/(x^2+1)|
|                      |
|o5 = R                |
|                      |
|o5 : QuotientRing     |
+----------------------+
|i6 : isUnit x         |
|                      |
|o6 = true             |
+----------------------+
|i7 : isField R        |
|                      |
|o7 = false            |
+----------------------+
|i8 : F = toField R    |
|                      |
|o8 = F                |
|                      |
|o8 : PolynomialRing   |
+----------------------+
|i9 : isField F        |
|                      |
|o9 = true             |
+----------------------+

See also
