toField(Ring) -- declare that a ring is a field
***********************************************

  * Function: *note toField: toField_lpRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        L = toField R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,
  * Outputs:
      * L, a new ring, isomorphic to R, declared to be a field. Polynomial
        rings over it will support Gröbner basis operations.

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ[i]/(i^2+1);                |
+---------------------------------------+
|i2 : L = toField A                     |
|                                       |
|o2 = L                                 |
|                                       |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                    |
+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : B = L[x,y,z]                      |
|                                       |
|o3 = B                                 |
|                                       |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                    |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = ideal(i*x^2-y-i, i*y^2-z-i)   |
|                                       |
|               2             2         |
|o4 = ideal (i*x  - y - i, i*y  - z - i)|
|                                       |
|o4 : Ideal of B                        |
+---------------------------------------+
|i5 : gens gb I                         |
|                                       |
|o5 = | y2+iz-1 x2+iy-1 |               |
|                                       |
|             1      2                  |
|o5 : Matrix B  <-- B                   |
+---------------------------------------+

If the engine eventually discovers that some nonzero element of L is not a
unit, an error will be signalled.  The user may then use *note getNonUnit:
getNonUnit, to obtain a non-invertible element of L. If a ring probably is a
field, it can be used as a field until a contradiction is found, and this may
be a good way of discovering whether a ring is a field.

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : A = ZZ[a]/(a^2+3);                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : L = toField A                                           |
|                                                             |
|o7 = L                                                       |
|                                                             |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : L[x,y,z]                                                |
|                                                             |
|o8 = L[x..z]                                                 |
|                                                             |
|o8 : PolynomialRing                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : try gb ideal (a*x^2-y^2-z^2, y^3, z^3) else getNonUnit L|
|                                                             |
|o9 = a                                                       |
|                                                             |
|o9 : L                                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note getNonUnit: getNonUnit, -- retrieve a previously discovered non-unit
  * *note try: try, -- catch an error

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note toField(Ring): toField_lpRing_rp, -- declare that a ring is a field
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

