getNonUnit -- retrieve a previously discovered non-unit
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getNonUnit R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,, in which division by a non-unit may have been
        attempted
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: RingElement,, the non-unit, if any, or *note
        null: null,

Description
===========

If a ring has been declared to be a field, using *note toField:
toField_lpRing_rp, or *note frac: frac,, but a nonzero element is found to not
be a unit, this routine will return that element, otherwise *note null: null,
is returned.
+---------------------------+
|i1 : A = ZZ/101[a]/(a^2-1);|
+---------------------------+
|i2 : toField A             |
|                           |
|o2 = A[]                   |
|                           |
|o2 : PolynomialRing        |
+---------------------------+
|i3 : 1//(a-1)              |
|                           |
|o3 = 0                     |
|                           |
|o3 : A                     |
+---------------------------+
|i4 : getNonUnit A          |
+---------------------------+
Warning: this function does not work yet for divisions attempted in the course
of computing a Gröbner basis or resolution.

See also
========

  * *note toField: toField_lpRing_rp, -- declare that a ring is a field
  * *note frac: frac, -- construct a fraction field

