ideals
******

An overview
===========

In Macaulay2, once a ring (see *note rings: rings,) is defined, ideals are
constructed in the usual way by giving a set of generators.


For those operations where we consider an ideal as a module, such as computing
Hilbert functions and polynomials, syzygies, free resolutions, see *note
modules: modules,.


For additional common operations and a comprehensive list of all routines in
Macaulay2 which return or use ideals, see *note Ideal: Ideal,.


The following link differs from the previous one in case only: *note ideal:
ideal,.
* Menu:

* Ideal::                       the class of all ideals
* ideal::                       make an ideal
* isIdeal::                     whether something is an ideal
* creating an ideal::

