The ring of a monomial ideal must be a commutative polynomial ring.  This ring
must not be a skew commuting ring, and/or a quotient ring.
* Menu:

* monomialIdeal::               make a monomial ideal
* monomialSubideal::            find the largest monomial ideal in an ideal
* independentSets(MonomialIdeal): independentSets.  some size-maximal independent subsets of variables modulo an ideal
* standardPairs(MonomialIdeal): standardPairs.  find the standard pairs of a monomial ideal
* polarize(MonomialIdeal): polarize.  compute the polarization of a monomial ideal
* codim(MonomialIdeal): codim_lpMonomialIdeal_rp.  compute the codimension
* MonomialIdeal - MonomialIdeal::  monomial ideal difference
* dual(MonomialIdeal,List): dual_lpMonomialIdeal_cmList_rp.  the Alexander dual
* dual(MonomialIdeal,RingElement): dual_lpMonomialIdeal_cmRingElement_rp.  the Alexander dual
* dual(MonomialIdeal): dual_lpMonomialIdeal_rp.  the Alexander dual of a monomial ideal
* lcm(MonomialIdeal): lcm_lpMonomialIdeal_rp.  least common multiple of all minimal generators

