Ideal ^ ZZ -- power of an ideal
*******************************

  * Operator: *note ^: ^,
  * Usage: 
        I^n
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: Ideal,
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,, at least zero
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: Ideal,, the ideal I^n

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^2, b^2-c*d);                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I^3                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|             6   4 2    4      2 4     2 2       2 2 2   6     4        2 2 2|
|o3 = ideal (a , a b  - a c*d, a b  - 2a b c*d + a c d , b  - 3b c*d + 3b c d |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        3 3                                                                  |
|     - c d )                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
The generators produced are often not minimal.  Use *note trim(Ideal): trim, or
*note mingens(Ideal): mingens_lpModule_rp, to find a smaller generating set.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : trim I^3                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|             6     4        2 2 2    3 3   2 4     2 2       2 2 2   4 2     |
|o4 = ideal (b  - 3b c*d + 3b c d  - c d , a b  - 2a b c*d + a c d , a b  -   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      4      6                                                               |
|     a c*d, a )                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ideals: ideals,

