leadTerm(ZZ,Ideal) -- get the ideal of lead polynomials
*******************************************************

  * Function: *note leadTerm: leadTerm,
  * Usage: 
        leadTerm(n,I)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,
      * I, an *note ideal: Ideal,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, The ideal of all possible lead polynomials of
        I using the first n parts of the monomial order

Description
===========

Compute a *note Gröbner basis: Gröbner bases, and return the ideal generated by
the lead terms of the Gröbner basis elements using the first n.
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d,MonomialOrder=>ProductOrder{1,3}];|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a*b-c*d, a*c-b*d)                   |
|                                                   |
|o2 = ideal (a*b - c*d, a*c - b*d)                  |
|                                                   |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : leadTerm(1,I)                                 |
|                                                   |
|             2     2                               |
|o3 = ideal (b d - c d, a*c, a*b)                   |
|                                                   |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

