codim(Ideal) -- compute the codimension
***************************************

  * Function: *note codim: codim,
  * Usage: 
        codim I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: Ideal,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Generic: codim_lpIdeal_cmGeneric=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value false,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,, dim(R) - dim(R/I), where R is the ring
        containing I.

Description
===========

When R is equidimensional, this quantity is the codimension of the ideal I.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a..e];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialCurveIdeal(R,{2,3,5,7})                                     |
|                                                                             |
|             2                               2     2    3           3      2 |
|o2 = ideal (d  - c*e, b*d - a*e, b*c - a*d, c d - b e, c  - a*b*e, b  - a*c )|
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : J = ideal presentation singularLocus(R/I);                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : codim J                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 4                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : radical J                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = ideal (d, c, b, a*e)                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
The following may not be the expected result, because the ring is not
equidimensional.
+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = QQ[x,y]/(ideal(x,y) * ideal(x-1))|
|                                          |
|o6 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o6 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i7 : codim ideal(x,y)                     |
|                                          |
|o7 = 1                                    |
+------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note dim(Ideal): dim_lpIdeal_rp, -- compute the Krull dimension
  * *note dim(MonomialIdeal): dim_lpIdeal_rp, -- compute the Krull dimension
  * *note codim(MonomialIdeal): codim_lpMonomialIdeal_rp, -- compute the
    codimension

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note codim(Ideal): codim_lpIdeal_rp, -- compute the codimension
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/functions/codim-doc.m2:106:0.

