degree(Ideal)
*************

  * Function: *note degree: degree,
  * Usage: 
        degree I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: Ideal,, in a polynomial ring or quotient of a
        polynomial ring
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,, the degree of the zero set of I

Description
===========

The degree of an ideal I in a ring S is the degree of the module S/I.  See
*note degree(Module): degree_lpModule_rp, for more details.
+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[a..f];                      |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^5, b^5, c^5, d^5, e^5);|
|                                        |
|o2 : Ideal of S                         |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : degree I                           |
|                                        |
|o3 = 3125                               |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : degree(S^1/I)                      |
|                                        |
|o4 = 3125                               |
+----------------------------------------+
If the ideal is not homogeneous, then the degree returned is the degree of the
ideal of initial monomials (which is homogeneous).  If the monomial order is a
degree order (the default), this is the same as the degree of the projective
closure of the zero set of I.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I = intersect(ideal(a-1,b-1,c-1),ideal(a-2,b-1,c+1),ideal(a-4,b+7,c-3/4 |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : Ideal of S                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|));                                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : degree I                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = 3                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note dim: dim, -- compute the Krull dimension
  * *note codim: codim, -- compute the codimension
  * *note genus: genus,
  * *note genera: genera,
  * *note hilbertSeries: hilbertSeries, -- compute the Hilbert series
  * *note reduceHilbert: reduceHilbert, -- reduce a Hilbert series expression
  * *note poincare: poincare, -- assemble degrees of a ring, module, or ideal
    into a polynomial
  * *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial, -- compute the Hilbert
    polynomial

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note degree(Ideal): degree_lpIdeal_rp,
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

