dim(Ideal) -- compute the Krull dimension
*****************************************

  * Function: *note dim: dim,
  * Usage: 
        dim I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: Ideal,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,

Description
===========

Computes the Krull dimension of the base ring of I mod I.


The ideal of 3x3 commuting matrices:
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x_(0,0)..x_(2,2),y_(0,0)..y_(2,2)]|
|                                                  |
|o1 = R                                            |
|                                                  |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = genericMatrix(R,x_(0,0),3,3)             |
|                                                  |
|o2 = | x_(0,0) x_(1,0) x_(2,0) |                  |
|     | x_(0,1) x_(1,1) x_(2,1) |                  |
|     | x_(0,2) x_(1,2) x_(2,2) |                  |
|                                                  |
|             3      3                             |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = genericMatrix(R,y_(0,0),3,3)             |
|                                                  |
|o3 = | y_(0,0) y_(1,0) y_(2,0) |                  |
|     | y_(0,1) y_(1,1) y_(2,1) |                  |
|     | y_(0,2) y_(1,2) y_(2,2) |                  |
|                                                  |
|             3      3                             |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = ideal flatten(M*N-N*M);                  |
|                                                  |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : dim I                                        |
|                                                  |
|o5 = 12                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------+
The dimension of a Stanley-Reisner monomial ideal associated to a simplicial
complex.


A hollow tetrahedron:
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : needsPackage "SimplicialComplexes"             |
|                                                    |
|o6 = SimplicialComplexes                            |
|                                                    |
|o6 : Package                                        |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : R = QQ[a..d]                                   |
|                                                    |
|o7 = R                                              |
|                                                    |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : D = simplicialComplex {a*b*c,a*b*d,a*c*d,b*c*d}|
|                                                    |
|o8 = simplicialComplex | bcd acd abd abc |          |
|                                                    |
|o8 : SimplicialComplex                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : I = monomialIdeal D                            |
|                                                    |
|o9 = monomialIdeal(a*b*c*d)                         |
|                                                    |
|o9 : MonomialIdeal of R                             |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : facets D                                      |
|                                                    |
|o10 = {b*c*d, a*c*d, a*b*d, a*b*c}                  |
|                                                    |
|o10 : List                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : dim D                                         |
|                                                    |
|o11 = 2                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : dim I                                         |
|                                                    |
|o12 = 3                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------+
Note that the dimension of the zero ideal is -1.

See also
========

  * *note ideal: ideal, -- make an ideal
  * *note monomialIdeal: monomialIdeal, -- make a monomial ideal
  * *note SimplicialComplexes: (SimplicialComplexes)Top, -- exploring abstract
    simplicial complexes within commutative algebra

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note dim(Ideal): dim_lpIdeal_rp, -- compute the Krull dimension
  * "dim(MonomialIdeal)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/functions/dim-doc.m2:108:0.

