generator -- provide a single generator
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        generator I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: Ideal, or a *note module: Module,
  * Outputs:
      * the single generator of I, if it has just one

Description
===========

If the number of apparent generators is greater than 1, then *note trim: trim,
will be called.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : I = ideal (4,6)               |
|                                   |
|o1 = ideal (4, 6)                  |
|                                   |
|o1 : Ideal of ZZ                   |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : generator I                   |
|                                   |
|o2 = 2                             |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : M = image matrix {{4,6},{0,0}}|
|                                   |
|o3 = image | 4 6 |                 |
|           | 0 0 |                 |
|                                   |
|                               2   |
|o3 : ZZ-module, submodule of ZZ    |
+-----------------------------------+
|i4 : generator M                   |
|                                   |
|o4 = | 2 |                         |
|     | 0 |                         |
|                                   |
|o4 : Vector                        |
+-----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note generators: generators, -- provide matrix or list of generators

