hilbertSeries(Ideal) -- compute the Hilbert series of the quotient of the ambient ring by the ideal
***************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertSeries: hilbertSeries,
  * Usage: 
        hilbertSeries I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: Ideal,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Order: hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value infinity, display the truncated power series expansion
      * *note Reduce: hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmReduce=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, reduce the Hilbert series
  * Outputs:
      * a *note divide expression: Divide,, the Hilbert series

Description
===========

We compute the *note Hilbert series: hilbertSeries, of R/I, the quotient of the
ambient ring by the ideal. Caution: For an ideal I running hilbertSeries I
calculates the Hilbert series of R/I.
+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, Degrees => {2}];|
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal x^2                 |
|                                   |
|            2                      |
|o2 = ideal x                       |
|                                   |
|o2 : Ideal of R                    |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : s = hilbertSeries I           |
|                                   |
|           4                       |
|      1 - T                        |
|o3 = --------                      |
|           2                       |
|     (1 - T )                      |
|                                   |
|o3 : Expression of class Divide    |
+-----------------------------------+
|i4 : numerator s                   |
|                                   |
|          4                        |
|o4 = 1 - T                         |
|                                   |
|o4 : ZZ[T]                         |
+-----------------------------------+
|i5 : poincare I                    |
|                                   |
|          4                        |
|o5 = 1 - T                         |
|                                   |
|o5 : ZZ[T]                         |
+-----------------------------------+
|i6 : reduceHilbert s               |
|                                   |
|          2                        |
|     1 + T                         |
|o6 = ------                        |
|        1                          |
|                                   |
|o6 : Expression of class Divide    |
+-----------------------------------+
Recall that the variables of the power series are the variables of the *note
degrees ring: degreesRing,.
+-------------------------------------+
|i7 : R=ZZ/101[x, Degrees => {{1,1}}];|
+-------------------------------------+
|i8 : I = ideal x^2;                  |
|                                     |
|o8 : Ideal of R                      |
+-------------------------------------+
|i9 : s = hilbertSeries I             |
|                                     |
|           2 2                       |
|      1 - T T                        |
|           0 1                       |
|o9 = ----------                      |
|     (1 - T T )                      |
|           0 1                       |
|                                     |
|o9 : Expression of class Divide      |
+-------------------------------------+
|i10 : numerator s                    |
|                                     |
|           2 2                       |
|o10 = 1 - T T                        |
|           0 1                       |
|                                     |
|o10 : ZZ[T ..T ]                     |
|          0   1                      |
+-------------------------------------+
|i11 : poincare I                     |
|                                     |
|           2 2                       |
|o11 = 1 - T T                        |
|           0 1                       |
|                                     |
|o11 : ZZ[T ..T ]                     |
|          0   1                      |
+-------------------------------------+
|i12 : reduceHilbert s                |
|                                     |
|      1 + T T                        |
|           0 1                       |
|o12 = --------                       |
|          1                          |
|                                     |
|o12 : Expression of class Divide     |
+-------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

As is often the case, calling this function on an ideal I actually computes it
for R/I where R is the ring of I.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note hilbertSeries(Ideal): hilbertSeries_lpIdeal_rp, -- compute the
    Hilbert series of the quotient of the ambient ring by the ideal
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in
Macaulay2Doc/functions/hilbertSeries-doc.m2:115:0.

