isSubset(Ideal,Ideal) -- whether one object is a subset of another
******************************************************************

  * Function: *note isSubset: isSubset,
  * Usage: 
        isSubset(I,J)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: Ideal,
      * J, an *note ideal: Ideal,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, whether I is contained in J

Description
===========

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                    |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^2-b*c-1,a*c-1,b^3-1);|
|                                      |
|o2 : Ideal of R                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : isSubset(I^2,I)                  |
|                                      |
|o3 = true                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : isSubset(I,I^2)                  |
|                                      |
|o4 = false                            |
+--------------------------------------+
In polynomial rings, this is accomplished by computing a Gröbner basis of J and
testing whether every element of I reduces to 0 modulo I.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isSubset(Ideal,Ideal): isSubset_lpIdeal_cmIdeal_rp, -- whether one
    object is a subset of another
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

