minimalPresentation(Ideal) -- compute a minimal presentation of the quotient ring defined by an ideal
*****************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note minimalPresentation: minimalPresentation,
  * Usage: 
        J = minimalPresentation I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: Ideal,, in a ring S
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Exclude: minimalPresentation_lpRing_rp, => ..., default value {},
        compute a minimal presentation of a quotient ring
  * Outputs:
      * J, an *note ideal: Ideal,,  in a new ring Q with S/I isomorphic to Q/J
  * Consequences:
      * minimalPresentation stores the isomorphism  from S/I to Q/J as
        I.cache.minimalPresentationMap , where I is the input ideal and the
        inverse of this map as I.cache.minimalPresentationMapInv

Description
===========

If the ideal I is homogeneous, then the ideal J, in a new ring Q is the
defining ideal for a minimal presentation of the ring S/I where S is the ring
of I. This is accomplished as follows. If a variable occurs as a term of a
generator of I and in no other terms of the same polynomial, then the variable
is replaced by the remaining terms and removed from the ring. A minimal
generating set for the resulting ideal is then computed. If I is not
homogeneous, then an attempt is made to improve the presentation of S/I.
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : C = ZZ/101[x,y,z,u,w];                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x-x^2-y,z+x*y,w^2-u^2);                  |
|                                                        |
|o2 : Ideal of C                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : minPres I                                          |
|                                                        |
|              2    2                                    |
|o3 = ideal(- u  + w )                                   |
|                                                        |
|               ZZ                                       |
|o3 : Ideal of ---[x, u, w]                              |
|              101                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I.cache.minimalPresentationMap                     |
|                                                        |
|           ZZ                     2       3    2        |
|o4 = map (---[x, u, w], C, {x, - x  + x, x  - x , u, w})|
|          101                                           |
|                                                        |
|              ZZ                                        |
|o4 : RingMap ---[x, u, w] <-- C                         |
|             101                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I.cache.minimalPresentationMapInv                  |
|                                                        |
|              ZZ                                        |
|o5 = map (C, ---[x, u, w], {x, u, w})                   |
|             101                                        |
|                                                        |
|                    ZZ                                  |
|o5 : RingMap C <-- ---[x, u, w]                         |
|                   101                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
If the Exclude option is present, then those variables with the given indices
are not simplified away (remember that ring variable indices start at 0).
+-----------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = ZZ/101[x,y,z,u,w];              |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i7 : I = ideal(x-x^2-y,z+x*y,w^2-u^2);   |
|                                         |
|o7 : Ideal of R                          |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i8 : minimalPresentation(I, Exclude=>{1})|
|                                         |
|               2             2    2      |
|o8 = ideal (- x  + x - y, - u  + w )     |
|                                         |
|               ZZ                        |
|o8 : Ideal of ---[x..y, u, w]            |
|              101                        |
+-----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note minimalPresentation(Ring): minimalPresentation_lpRing_rp, -- compute
    a minimal presentation of a quotient ring
  * *note trim(Ideal): trim, -- minimize generators and relations

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note minimalPresentation(Ideal): minimalPresentation_lpIdeal_rp, --
    compute a minimal presentation of the quotient ring defined by an ideal
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in
Macaulay2Doc/functions/minimalPresentation-doc.m2:96:0.

