isIdeal -- whether something is an ideal
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        isIdeal I
  * Inputs:
      * I, a *note thing: Thing,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, *note true: true, if I is either an
        *note ideal: Ideal,, a *note monomial ideal: MonomialIdeal, or a *note
        module: Module, which is a submodule of a free module of rank 1 with
        generators in degree 0 and *note false: false, otherwise

Description
===========

+------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x,y,z];           |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2, y^2)      |
|                              |
|             2   2            |
|o2 = ideal (x , y )           |
|                              |
|o2 : Ideal of S               |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : isIdeal I                |
|                              |
|o3 = true                     |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : J = monomialIdeal I      |
|                              |
|                     2   2    |
|o4 = monomialIdeal (x , y )   |
|                              |
|o4 : MonomialIdeal of S       |
+------------------------------+
|i5 : isIdeal J                |
|                              |
|o5 = true                     |
+------------------------------+
|i6 : R = QQ[a..d]/(a*b*c*d);  |
+------------------------------+
|i7 : I = ideal(a^2,b^2) * R^1 |
|                              |
|o7 = image | a2 b2 |          |
|                              |
|                             1|
|o7 : R-module, submodule of R |
+------------------------------+
|i8 : isIdeal I                |
|                              |
|o8 = true                     |
+------------------------------+
|i9 : J = a^2 * R^2 + a*b * R^2|
|                              |
|o9 = image | a2 0  ab 0  |    |
|           | 0  a2 0  ab |    |
|                              |
|                             2|
