comodule -- submodule to quotient module
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        comodule M
        quotient M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,, or an *note ideal: Ideal,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: Module,, the quotient module N/M, if M is given as a
        submodule $M \subset N$, where N is either a free module or a quotient
        of a free module.

Description
===========

+-----------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];           |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a,b,c,d^3);   |
|                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R              |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : comodule I              |
|                             |
|o3 = cokernel | a b c d3 |   |
|                             |
|                            1|
|o3 : R-module, quotient of R |
+-----------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note image: image, -- image of a map
  * *note cokernel: cokernel, -- cokernel of a map
  * *note kernel: kernel, -- kernel of a map

Ways to use comodule:
=====================

  * "comodule(Ideal)"
  * "comodule(Module)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note comodule: comodule, is a *note method function:
MethodFunction,.

