File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: Matrix, Next: matrix, Up: matrices

Matrix -- the class of all matrices
***********************************

Description
===========

A matrix is a homomorphism between two modules, together with an integer (or
vector of integers) called its degree, which is used when determining whether
the map is homogeneous.  The matrix is stored in the usual way as a rectangular
array of ring elements. When the source or target modules are not free, the
matrix is interpreted as a linear transformation in terms of the generators of
the modules.


A matrix f is an immutable object, so if you want to cache information about
it, put it in the hash table f.cache.


Common ways to make a matrix:
  * *note map: map, -- make a map
  * *note matrix: matrix, -- make a matrix
Common ways to get information about matrices:
  * degree(Matrix) (missing documentation)
  * *note isHomogeneous(Matrix): isHomogeneous, -- whether something is
    homogeneous (graded)
  * *note matrix(Matrix): matrix_lpMatrix_rp, -- the matrix between generators
Common operations on matrices:
  * *note Matrix + Matrix: +, -- a unary or binary operator, usually used for
    addition
