leadTerm(Matrix) -- get the greatest term of each column
********************************************************

  * Function: *note leadTerm: leadTerm,
  * Usage: 
        leadTerm f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,, in a polynomial ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, the lead term matrix of f

Description
===========

In Macaulay2, each free module over a polynomial ring comes equipped with a
*note monomial order: monomial orderings, and this routine returns the matrix
whose i-th column is the lead term of the i th column of f.
+----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : f = matrix{{0,a^2-b*c},{c,d}}|
|                                  |
|o2 = | 0 a2-bc |                  |
|     | c d     |                  |
|                                  |
|             2      2             |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R              |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : leadTerm f                   |
|                                  |
|o3 = | 0 a2 |                     |
|     | c 0  |                     |
|                                  |
|             2      2             |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R              |
+----------------------------------+
Coefficients are included in the result:
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = ZZ[a..d][x,y,z];                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : f = matrix{{0,(a+b)*x^2},{c*x, (b+c)*y}}|
|                                             |
|o5 = | 0  (a+b)x2 |                          |
|     | cx (b+c)y  |                          |
|                                             |
|             2      2                        |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R                         |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i6 : leadTerm f                              |
|                                             |
|o6 = | 0  ax2 |                              |
|     | cx 0   |                              |
|                                             |
|             2      2                        |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R                         |
+---------------------------------------------+
The argument f can also be a *note Gröbner basis: GroebnerBasis,, in which case
the lead term matrix of the generating matrix of f is returned.

See also
========

  * *note leadCoefficient: leadCoefficient, -- the coefficient of the leading
    term
  * *note leadMonomial: leadMonomial, -- the leading monomial of a ring element
  * *note leadComponent: leadComponent, -- the leading component(s) of a vector
    or matrix

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "leadTerm(GroebnerBasis)"
  * *note leadTerm(Matrix): leadTerm_lpMatrix_rp, -- get the greatest term of
    each column
  * "leadTerm(Vector)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/doc7.m2:54:0.

