leadTerm(ZZ,Matrix) -- get the matrix of lead polynomials of each column
************************************************************************

  * Function: *note leadTerm: leadTerm,
  * Usage: 
        leadTerm(n,f)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,, in a polynomial ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, the lead term matrix of f using the first n
        parts of the monomial order

Description
===========

Returns the matrix whose i-th column is the lead term of the i-th column of f,
using the first n parts of the monomial order.
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z,a..d,MonomialOrder=>ProductOrder{3,4}];|
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = matrix{{0,x^2*(a+b)}, {a*x+2*b*y, y^2*(c+d)}}   |
|                                                         |
|o2 = | 0      x2a+x2b |                                  |
|     | xa+2yb y2c+y2d |                                  |
|                                                         |
|             2      2                                    |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : leadTerm(1,f)                                       |
|                                                         |
|o3 = | 0  x2a+x2b |                                      |
|     | xa 0       |                                      |
|                                                         |
|             2      2                                    |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

