borel(Matrix) -- make a Borel fixed submodule
*********************************************

  * Function: *note borel: borel_lpMatrix_rp,

Description
===========

borel m -- make a Borel fixed submodule


Yields the matrix with the same target as the matrix m, whose columns generate
the smallest Borel fixed submodule containing the lead monomials of the columns
of m.  If m is a monomial ideal, then the minimal Borel fixed monomial ideal
containing it is returned.


For example, if R = ZZ/101[a..f], then
+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a..e]                |
|                                     |
|o1 = R                               |
|                                     |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                  |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : borel matrix {{a*d*e, b^2}}     |
|                                     |
|o2 = | a2 ab b2 ac2 acd ad2 ace ade ||
|                                     |
|             1      8                |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                 |
+-------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note borel(Matrix): borel_lpMatrix_rp, -- make a Borel fixed submodule
  * "borel(MonomialIdeal)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/doc7.m2:159:0.

