modulo -- find the pre-image (pullback) of image of a map (low level version)
*****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        modulo(f,g)
  * Inputs:
      * f
      * g
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,,  whose image is the pre-image (pullback) of
        the image of g under f

Description
===========

The maps f and g must have the same target, and their sources and targets must
be free. If f is *note null: null,, then it is taken to be the identity.  If g
is *note null: null,, it is taken to be zero.

This function is mainly for internal use.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                              |
|                                                |
|o1 = R                                          |
|                                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                             |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = matrix {{x,y}}                         |
|                                                |
|o2 = | x y |                                    |
|                                                |
|             1      2                           |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                            |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : g = matrix {{y,z}}                         |
|                                                |
|o3 = | y z |                                    |
|                                                |
|             1      2                           |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                            |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : modulo(f,g)                                |
|                                                |
|o4 = {1} | 0 z y |                              |
|     {1} | 1 0 0 |                              |
|                                                |
|             2      3                           |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                            |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : kernel( inducedMap(coker g, target g) * f )|
|                                                |
|o5 = image {1} | 0 z y |                        |
|           {1} | 1 0 0 |                        |
|                                                |
|                             2                  |
|o5 : R-module, submodule of R                   |
+------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use modulo:
===================

  * "modulo(Matrix,Matrix)"
  * "modulo(Matrix,Nothing)"
  * "modulo(Nothing,Matrix)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note modulo: modulo, is a *note method function with options:
MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

