Matrix ** RingElement
*********************

  * Operator: *note **: _st_st,
  * Usage: 
        f ** r
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,
      * r, a *note ring element: RingElement,
  * Outputs:
      * the tensor product of f with r

Description
===========

+-----------------------------+
|i1 : f = matrix "2,3,4;5,6,7"|
|                             |
|o1 = | 2 3 4 |               |
|     | 5 6 7 |               |
|                             |
|              2       3      |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ       |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : f ** 10                 |
|                             |
|o2 = | 20 30 40 |            |
|     | 50 60 70 |            |
|                             |
|              2       3      |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ       |
+-----------------------------+

When the ring element is homogeneous, the degrees of the source module can
change, which is what makes this operation different from scalar
multiplication.

+---------------------------------------+
|i3 : QQ[x,y]                           |
|                                       |
|o3 = QQ[x..y]                          |
|                                       |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                    |
+---------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = matrix "x,y"                  |
|                                       |
|o4 = | x y |                           |
|                                       |
|                      1               2|
|o4 : Matrix (QQ[x..y])  <-- (QQ[x..y]) |
+---------------------------------------+
|i5 : g = f ** y^7                      |
|                                       |
|o5 = | xy7 y8 |                        |
|                                       |
|                      1               2|
|o5 : Matrix (QQ[x..y])  <-- (QQ[x..y]) |
+---------------------------------------+
|i6 : h = f * y^7                       |
|                                       |
|o6 = | xy7 y8 |                        |
|                                       |
|                      1               2|
|o6 : Matrix (QQ[x..y])  <-- (QQ[x..y]) |
+---------------------------------------+
|i7 : degrees g                         |
|                                       |
|o7 = {{{0}}, {{8}, {8}}}               |
|                                       |
|o7 : List                              |
+---------------------------------------+
|i8 : degrees h                         |
|                                       |
|o8 = {{{0}}, {{1}, {1}}}               |
|                                       |
|o8 : List                              |
+---------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note Matrix ** RingElement: Matrix _st_st RingElement,
