smithNormalForm(Matrix) -- smith normal form for a matrix over a PID
********************************************************************

  * Function: *note smithNormalForm: smithNormalForm_lpMatrix_rp,
  * Usage: 
        (D,P,Q) = smithNormalForm M
        (D,P) = smithNormalForm(M,ChangeMatrix=>{true,false})
        (D,Q) = smithNormalForm(M,ChangeMatrix=>{false,true})
        D = smithNormalForm(M,ChangeMatrix=>{false,false})
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: Matrix,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * ChangeMatrix => a *note list: List,, default value {true, true}, of two
        Boolean elements. This determines whether the change of basis matrices
        P and/or Q are computed
      * KeepZeroes => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value true,
        whether to keep rows and columns that are completely zero
  * Outputs:
      * D, a *note matrix: Matrix,, The Smith normal form of M
      * P, a *note matrix: Matrix,, invertible (left) change of basis matrix
      * Q, a *note matrix: Matrix,, invertible (right) change of basis matrix

Description
===========

This function produces a diagonal matrix D, and invertible matrices P and Q
such that D = PMQwith diagonal entries d1, d2, ..., dn of D satisfying
d1|d2|...|dn.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = matrix{{1,2,3},{1,34,45},{2213,1123,6543},{0,0,0}}                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = | 1    2    3    |                                                      |
|     | 1    34   45   |                                                      |
|     | 2213 1123 6543 |                                                      |
|     | 0    0    0    |                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|              4       3                                                      |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : (D,P,Q) = smithNormalForm M                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = (| 1 0 0      |, | 1  -102182 -43292 0 |, | 129506 17567889865          |
|      | 0 1 0      |  | -1 102183  -92361 0 |  | 70085  9507247241           |
|      | 0 0 135654 |  | 1  -102183 92362  0 |  | -55831 -7573648009          |
|      | 0 0 0      |  | 0  0       0      1 |                                |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     2383136963911713  |)                                                    |
|     1289686610013066  |                                                     |
|     -1027388073388531 |                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D == P * M * Q                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (D,P) = smithNormalForm(M, ChangeMatrix=>{true,false},                  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = (| 1 0 0      |, | 1  -102182 -43292 0 |)                               |
|      | 0 1 0      |  | -1 102183  -92361 0 |                                |
|      | 0 0 135654 |  | 1  -102183 92362  0 |                                |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Sequence                                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|KeepZeroes=>false)                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D = smithNormalForm(M, ChangeMatrix=>{false,false})                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = | 1 0 0      |                                                          |
|     | 0 1 0      |                                                          |
|     | 0 0 135654 |                                                          |
|     | 0 0 0      |                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|              4       3                                                      |
|o5 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This function is the underlying routine used by *note minimalPresentation:
minimalPresentation, in the case when the ring is *note ZZ: ZZ,, or a
polynomial ring in one variable over a field.

+-------------------------------+
|i6 : prune coker M             |
|                               |
|o6 = cokernel | 135654 |       |
|              | 0      |       |
|                               |
|                              2|
|o6 : ZZ-module, quotient of ZZ |
+-------------------------------+
In the following example, we test the result be checking that the entries of
D1, P1 M Q1 are the same. The degrees associated to these matrices do not match
up, so a simple test of equality would return false.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : S = ZZ/101[t]                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : D = diagonalMatrix{t^2+1, (t^2+1)^2, (t^2+1)^3, (t^2+1)^5}              |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = | t2+1 0        0            0                       |                  |
|     | 0    t4+2t2+1 0            0                       |                  |
|     | 0    0        t6+3t4+3t2+1 0                       |                  |
|     | 0    0        0            t10+5t8+10t6+10t4+5t2+1 |                  |
|                                                                             |
|             4      4                                                        |
|o8 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : P = random(S^4, S^4)                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = | 24  19  -8  -38 |                                                     |
|     | -36 19  -22 -16 |                                                     |
|     | -30 -10 -29 39  |                                                     |
|     | -29 -29 -24 21  |                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|             4      4                                                        |
|o9 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : Q = random(S^4, S^4)                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = | 34  -18 -28 16  |                                                    |
|      | 19  -13 -47 22  |                                                    |
|      | -47 -43 38  45  |                                                    |
|      | -39 -15 2   -34 |                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|              4      4                                                       |
|o10 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : M = P*D*Q                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o11 = | -33t10+37t8+46t6+48t4-24t2+5 -36t10+22t8-16t6+21t4+27t2+33           |
|      | 18t10-11t8+2t6+7t4-37t2-13   38t10-12t8+13t6+42t4-50t2-29            |
|      | -6t10-30t8-10t6+t4+33t2+46   21t10+4t8+43t6+41t4+19                  |
|      | -11t10+46t8+8t6-4t4+29t2-16  -12t10+41t8+3t6+20t4-31t2               |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|      25t10+24t8+47t6-40t4-13t2-26  -21t10-4t8+36t6+37t4+35t2+17 |           |
|      -32t10+42t8-45t6+16t4-12t2-46 39t10-7t8+6t6-41t4+10t2+2    |           |
|      -23t10-14t8-19t6-36t4-25t2-17 -13t10+36t8-21t6-23t4+49t2+2 |           |
|      42t10+8t8+13t6-44t4+2t2-8     -7t10-35t8-39t6-9t4+35t2+33  |           |
|                                                                             |
|              4      4                                                       |
|o11 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : (D1,P1,Q1) = smithNormalForm M;                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : D1 - P1*M*Q1 == 0                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o13 = true                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : prune coker M                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o14 = cokernel | t2+1 0        0            0                       |        |
|               | 0    t4+2t2+1 0            0                       |        |
|               | 0    0        t6+3t4+3t2+1 0                       |        |
|               | 0    0        0            t10+5t8+10t6+10t4+5t2+1 |        |
|                                                                             |
|                             4                                               |
|o14 : S-module, quotient of S                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
The key idea of the current implementation is as follows: compute a Gröbner
basis, transpose the generators, and repeat, until we encounter a matrix whose
transpose is already a Gröbner basis.

Caveat
======

The behavior of this function is not defined when the ring is not a PID.

See also
========

  * *note minimalPresentation(Module): minimalPresentation_lpModule_rp, --
    minimal presentation of a module

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note smithNormalForm(Matrix): smithNormalForm_lpMatrix_rp, -- smith normal
    form for a matrix over a PID
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

