matrix -- make a matrix
***********************

Description
===========

The simplest use of this function is to define a matrix by giving a doubly
nested list of ring elements.  One may also explicitly provide the ring, or
give a matrix as a doubly-nested list of matrices.
+----------------------------+
|i1 : matrix{{1,2,3},{4,5,6}}|
|                            |
|o1 = | 1 2 3 |              |
|     | 4 5 6 |              |
|                            |
|              2       3     |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ      |
+----------------------------+
|i2 : R = QQ[x,y,z];         |
+----------------------------+
|i3 : matrix{{x,0,2},{1,2,y}}|
|                            |
|o3 = | x 0 2 |              |
|     | 1 2 y |              |
|                            |
|             2      3       |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R        |
+----------------------------+
The *note map: map, function provides other methods to define a matrix.

See also
========

  * *note map: map, -- make a map
  * *note matrix(String): (Classic)matrix_lpString_rp, -- make a matrix using
    classic Macaulay syntax
* Menu:

* matrix(List): matrix_lpList_rp.  create a matrix from a doubly-nested list of ring elements or matrices
* matrix(Ring,List): matrix_lpRing_cmList_rp.  create a matrix from a doubly nested list of ring elements or matrices
* matrix(Matrix): matrix_lpMatrix_rp.  the matrix between generators
* matrix(MutableMatrix): matrix_lpMutableMatrix_rp.  make a matrix from a mutable one
* matrix(RingElement): matrix_lpRing_cmRingElement_rp.  make a matrix from a ring element
* matrix(Vector): matrix_lpVector_rp.  make a matrix
* matrix(RingMap): matrix_lpRingMap_rp.  the matrix associated to a ring map

