matrix(Ring,RingElement) -- make a matrix from a ring element
*************************************************************

  * Function: *note matrix: matrix,
  * Usage: 
        matrix(R, f)
        matrix f
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring, or an instance of the type *note RingFamily:
        RingFamily,,
      * f, a *note ring element: RingElement, or a *note number: Number,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: matrix_lpList_rp, => ..., default value null, create a
        matrix from a doubly-nested list of ring elements or matrices
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, the one by one matrix with f as its single
        entry;

Description
===========

+-----------------------+
|i1 : matrix 48         |
|                       |
|o1 = | 48 |            |
|                       |
|              1       1|
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ |
+-----------------------+
|i2 : R = QQ[x,y]       |
|                       |
|o2 = R                 |
|                       |
|o2 : PolynomialRing    |
+-----------------------+
|i3 : matrix(x^2 - y^2) |
|                       |
|o3 = | x2-y2 |         |
|                       |
|             1      1  |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R   |
+-----------------------+

Specify a ring R to get a matrix over R instead of the ring of f.

+-----------------------+
|i4 : matrix(QQ, 48)    |
|                       |
|o4 = | 48 |            |
|                       |
|              1       1|
|o4 : Matrix QQ  <-- QQ |
+-----------------------+
|i5 : matrix(R, 48)     |
|                       |
|o5 = | 48 |            |
|                       |
|             1      1  |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R   |
+-----------------------+

