genericSymmetricMatrix -- make a generic symmetric matrix
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        genericSymmetricMatrix(R,r,n)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,
      * r, a *note ring element: RingElement,, which is a variable in the ring
        R (this input is optional)
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,
  * Outputs:
      * a symmetric *note matrix: Matrix, with n rows whose entries on and
        above the diagonal are the variables of R starting with r

Description
===========

A square *note matrix: Matrix, M is symmetric if transpose(M) - M == 0.
+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[a..z];                    |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = genericSymmetricMatrix(R,a,3)|
|                                      |
|o2 = | a b c |                        |
|     | b d e |                        |
|     | c e f |                        |
|                                      |
|             3      3                 |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : transpose(M) - M == 0            |
|                                      |
|o3 = true                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : genericSymmetricMatrix(R,d,5)    |
|                                      |
|o4 = | d e f g h |                    |
|     | e i j k l |                    |
|     | f j m n o |                    |
|     | g k n p q |                    |
|     | h l o q r |                    |
|                                      |
|             5      5                 |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                  |
+--------------------------------------+


Omitting the input r is the same as having r be the first variable in R.
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : genericSymmetricMatrix(R,3)|
|                                |
|o5 = | a b c |                  |
|     | b d e |                  |
|     | c e f |                  |
|                                |
|             3      3           |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R            |
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : genericSymmetricMatrix(R,5)|
|                                |
|o6 = | a b c d e |              |
|     | b f g h i |              |
|     | c g j k l |              |
|     | d h k m n |              |
|     | e i l n o |              |
|                                |
|             5      5           |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R            |
+--------------------------------+

