MutableMatrix -- the class of all mutable matrices
**************************************************

Description
===========

A mutable matrix in Macaulay2 is a rectangular array of elements of a specific
ring, whose entries can be modified.


A mutable matrix is different from a *note Matrix: Matrix, in that a matrix
contains degree information for the target and source of the matrix, while a
mutable matrix has no such information.  Also, more operations are provided for
matrices.


For an overview of mutable matrices, see *note mutable matrices: mutable
matrices,.


Mutable matrices can either be encoded in a sparse manner (the matrix only
encodes the non-zero elements), or in a dense manner (all elements are stored
-- even zeros).  The distinction is an option to several of the routines that
create mutable matrices (*note mutableMatrix: mutableMatrix,, *note
mutableIdentity: mutableIdentity_lpRing_cmZZ_rp,). Certain operations over RR
or CC are performed using the LAPACK library and require dense encoding of
matrices: *note LUdecomposition: LUdecomposition,, *note SVD: SVD,, *note
solve: solve,, *note eigenvalues: eigenvalues,, *note eigenvectors:
eigenvectors,.

row and column operations
-------------------------

  * *note rowAdd: rowAdd, -- add a multiple of one row to another
  * *note rowSwap: rowSwap, -- interchange rows
  * *note rowPermute: rowPermute, -- permute some rows
  * *note rowMult: rowMult, -- multiply a row by a ring element
  * *note columnAdd: columnAdd, -- add a multiple of one column to another
  * *note columnSwap: columnSwap, -- interchange columns
  * *note columnPermute: columnPermute, -- permute some columns
  * *note columnMult: columnMult, -- multiply a column by a ring element

matrix arithmetic
-----------------

Many matrix arithmetic routines are only available for immutable matrices, not
mutable matrices.  It is necessary to use *note matrix: matrix, to make an
immutable matrix first.

Functions and methods returning a mutable matrix:
=================================================

  * "cover(MutableMatrix)" -- see *note cover(Matrix): cover_lpMatrix_rp, --
    get the map between the covering free modules
  * "MutableMatrix ^ ZZ" -- see *note Matrix ^ ZZ: Matrix ^ ZZ, -- power
  * "mutableIdentity" -- see *note mutableIdentity(Ring,ZZ):
    mutableIdentity_lpRing_cmZZ_rp, -- make a mutable identity matrix
  * *note mutableMatrix: mutableMatrix, -- make a mutable matrix
  * "randomMutableMatrix" -- see *note randomMutableMatrix(ZZ,ZZ,RR,ZZ):
    randomMutableMatrix_lpZZ_cmZZ_cmRR_cmZZ_rp, -- a random mutable matrix of
    integers
  * RingMap MutableMatrix (missing documentation)

