Matrix _ List -- select columns
*******************************

  * Operator: *note _: _us,
  * Usage: 
        f_cols
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,, a matrix between free modules
      * cols, a *note list: List,, a list of integers denoting the choice of
        columns
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, the submatrix of f corresponding to the
        columns cols.

Description
===========

This is the same as calling *note submatrix(f,cols):
submatrix_lpMatrix_cmVisibleList_rp,.
+---------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..f];               |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : p = matrix {{a,b,c},{d,e,f}}|
|                                 |
|o2 = | a b c |                   |
|     | d e f |                   |
|                                 |
|             2      3            |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R             |
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : p_{1}                       |
|                                 |
|o3 = | b |                       |
|     | e |                       |
|                                 |
|             2      1            |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R             |
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : p_{1,2,0}                   |
|                                 |
|o4 = | b c a |                   |
|     | e f d |                   |
|                                 |
|             2      3            |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R             |
+---------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note submatrix: submatrix, -- select part of a matrix
  * *note Matrix ^ List: Matrix ^ List, -- select rows

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note Matrix _ List: Matrix _us List, -- select columns
  * "MutableMatrix _ List"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/functions/submatrix-doc.m2:25:0.

