diff(Matrix,RingElement) -- differentiation
*******************************************

  * Function: *note diff: diff,
  * Usage: 
        diff(f,g)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,, a matrix
      * g, a *note ring element: RingElement,, a polynomial with the same ring
        as f
  * Outputs:
      * the result of differentiating g by the differential operator
        corresponding to each entry of f.

Description
===========

The shape of the resulting matrix is the same as the shape of f, but the
degrees of the source module are different in an attempt to ensure that the
result is homogeneous.
+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z,q];                 |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = vars R                       |
|                                      |
|o2 = | x y z q |                      |
|                                      |
|             1      4                 |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : diff(f, (x+y-z)^2)               |
|                                      |
|o3 = | 2x+2y-2z 2x+2y-2z -2x-2y+2z 0 ||
|                                      |
|             1      4                 |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : f2 = genericMatrix(R,2,2)        |
|                                      |
|o4 = | x z |                          |
|     | y q |                          |
|                                      |
|             2      2                 |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : diff(f2, (x+y-z)^2)              |
|                                      |
|o5 = | 2x+2y-2z -2x-2y+2z |           |
|     | 2x+2y-2z 0         |           |
|                                      |
|             2      2                 |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R                  |
+--------------------------------------+

