SVD -- singular value decomposition of a matrix
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        (S,U,Vt) = SVD M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: Matrix,,  over *note RR: RR, or *note CC: CC,, of
        size m by n
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note DivideConquer: SVD_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDivideConquer=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value true, whether to use the LAPACK divide and conquer
        SVD algorithm
  * Outputs:
      * S, a *note vertical list: VerticalList,, the list of singular values
      * U, a *note matrix: Matrix,, an orthogonal (unitary) matrix of size m by
        m
      * Vt, a *note matrix: Matrix,, an orthogonal (unitary) matrix of size n
        by n

Description
===========

If Sigma is the diagonal m by n matrix whose (i,i) entry is the i-th element of
S, then M = U Sigma Vt.  This is the singular value decomposition of M.  The
entries of S are (up to roundoff error) the eigenvalues of the Hermitian matrix
M * (conjugate transpose M)


M may also be a *note MutableMatrix: MutableMatrix, in which case the returned
values U and Vt are also *note mutable matrices: MutableMatrix,.


If M is over *note CC: CC,, then U and Vt are unitary matrices over *note CC:
CC,. If M is over *note RR: RR,, U and Vt are orthogonal over RR.
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : printingPrecision=2;                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = map(RR^3, RR^5, (i,j) -> (i+1)^j * 1.0)                   |
|                                                                   |
|o2 = | 1 1 1 1  1  |                                               |
|     | 1 2 4 8  16 |                                               |
|     | 1 3 9 27 81 |                                               |
|                                                                   |
|                3         5                                        |
|o2 : Matrix RR    <-- RR                                           |
|              53        53                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (S,U,V) = SVD(M)                                              |
|                                                                   |
|o3 = ({88 }, | -.016 -.4  -.92  |, | -.014 -.038 -.11 -.32 -.94  |)|
|      {3.9}  | -.21  -.89 .4    |  | -.28  -.41  -.57 -.59 .29   | |
|      {.8 }  | -.98  .2   -.068 |  | -.74  -.41  .066 .51  -.15  | |
|                                   | .084  .33   -.81 .47  -.081 | |
|                                   | -.61  .74   .077 -.27 .062  | |
|                                                                   |
|o3 : Sequence                                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M' = (transpose U) * M * (transpose V)                        |
|                                                                   |
|o4 = | 88      -3.1e-15 1.3e-14  -3.9e-15 -8.9e-16 |               |
|     | 4.9e-15 3.9      -6.8e-15 -5.8e-16 -2.2e-15 |               |
|     | 7.7e-15 1.2e-14  .8       2.6e-16  6.1e-16  |               |
|                                                                   |
|                3         5                                        |
|o4 : Matrix RR    <-- RR                                           |
|              53        53                                         |
