Now let's try the divide and conquer algorithm and compare answers.
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : (S', U', V') = SVD(M, DivideConquer => true)             |
|                                                               |
|o10 = ({88 }, | -.02 -.4  -.92 |, | -.01 -.04 -.11 -.32 -.94 |)|
|       {3.9}  | -.21 -.89 .4   |  | -.28 -.41 -.57 -.59 .29  | |
|       {.8 }  | -.98 .2   -.07 |  | -.74 -.41 .07  .51  -.15 | |
|                                  | .08  .33  -.81 .47  -.08 | |
|                                  | -.61 .74  .08  -.27 .06  | |
|                                                               |
|o10 : Sequence                                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : norm \ ({S', U', V'}-{S, U, V})                          |
|                                                               |
|o11 = {0, 0, 0}                                                |
|                                                               |
|o11 : List                                                     |
