minors(ZZ,Matrix) -- ideal generated by minors
**********************************************

  * Function: *note minors: minors_lpZZ_cmMatrix_rp,
  * Usage: 
        minors(n,M)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,, order of the minor
      * M, a *note matrix: Matrix,, a map between free modules
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * First => a *note list: List,, default value null, if given, should be a
        list of two integer lists, which will be the first minor computed
      * Limit => an *note integer: ZZ,, default value infinity, the maximum
        number of minors to find
      * *note Strategy: minors_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, choose between Bareiss, Cofactor and Dynamic
        algorithms
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: Ideal,, the ideal generated by the n by n minors of the
        matrix M

Description
===========

Minors are generated in the same order as that used by *note subsets(ZZ,ZZ):
subsets,.
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[a..f];                                |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = matrix{{a,b,c},{d,e,f}}                  |
|                                                  |
|o2 = | a b c |                                    |
|     | d e f |                                    |
|                                                  |
|             2      3                             |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : minors(2,M)                                  |
|                                                  |
|o3 = ideal (- b*d + a*e, - c*d + a*f, - c*e + b*f)|
|                                                  |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : minors(2,M,Limit=>1)                         |
|                                                  |
|o4 = ideal(- b*d + a*e)                           |
|                                                  |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------+

When n is negative, the unit ideal is returned, to preserve the expected
ordering among the resulting ideals.

+-----------------------------+
|i5 : minors(1,M)             |
|                             |
|o5 = ideal (a, d, b, e, c, f)|
|                             |
|o5 : Ideal of R              |
+-----------------------------+
|i6 : minors(0,M)             |
|                             |
|o6 = ideal 1                 |
|                             |
|o6 : Ideal of R              |
+-----------------------------+
|i7 : minors(-1,M)            |
|                             |
|o7 = ideal 1                 |
|                             |
|o7 : Ideal of R              |
+-----------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note exteriorPower: exteriorPower, -- exterior power
  * *note determinant: determinant, -- determinant of a matrix
* Menu:

* minors(...,Strategy=>...): minors_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp.  choose between Bareiss, Cofactor and Dynamic algorithms

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note minors(ZZ,Matrix): minors_lpZZ_cmMatrix_rp, -- ideal generated by
    minors
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

