permanents -- ideal generated by square permanents of a matrix
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        permanents(n,M)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,, the size of the permanents
      * M, a *note matrix: Matrix,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: Ideal,,  generated by the permanents of the n by n
        subpermanents of M

Description
===========

The permanent of a square matrix N has the Laplace transform similar to the
Laplace transform of the determinant of N: but all signs are positive.
Permanents are used in combinatorics and in probability. They are
computationally difficult.
+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[a..f];                          |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = genericMatrix(R,a,2,3)             |
|                                            |
|o2 = | a c e |                              |
|     | b d f |                              |
|                                            |
|             2      3                       |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                        |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : permanents(2,M)                        |
|                                            |
|o3 = ideal (b*c + a*d, b*e + a*f, d*e + c*f)|
|                                            |
|o3 : Ideal of R                             |
+--------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======



