exteriorPower(ZZ,Matrix) -- exterior power of a matrix
******************************************************

  * Function: *note exteriorPower: exteriorPower,
  * Usage: 
        exteriorPower(i,f)
        exteriorPower_i f
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: ZZ,
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: exteriorPower_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null, choose between Bareiss, Cofactor and Dynamic
        algorithms
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, the i-th exterior power of f.

Description
===========

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/2[x,y];             |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : f = random(R^3,R^{3:-1})   |
|                                |
|o2 = | x   y   y   |            |
|     | x+y y   x   |            |
|     | x   x+y x+y |            |
|                                |
|             3      3           |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R            |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : exteriorPower_2 f          |
|                                |
|o3 = | y2       x2+xy+y2 xy+y2 ||
|     | x2       x2       0     ||
|     | x2+xy+y2 y2       x2+y2 ||
|                                |
|             3      3           |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R            |
+--------------------------------+
The matrix may be a more general homomorphism of modules.  For example,
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : g = map(coker matrix {{x^2},{x*y},{y^2}}, R^3, id_(R^3))|
|                                                             |
|o4 = | 1 0 0 |                                               |
|     | 0 1 0 |                                               |
|     | 0 0 1 |                                               |
|                                                             |
|o4 : Matrix                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : g2 = exteriorPower(2,g)                                 |
|                                                             |
|o5 = | 1 0 0 |                                               |
|     | 0 1 0 |                                               |
|     | 0 0 1 |                                               |
|                                                             |
|o5 : Matrix                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : target g2                                               |
|                                                             |
|o6 = cokernel | xy x2 0  |                                   |
|              | y2 0  x2 |                                   |
|              | 0  y2 xy |                                   |
|                                                             |
|                            3                                |
|o6 : R-module, quotient of R                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note exteriorPower(ZZ,Module): exteriorPower_lpZZ_cmModule_rp, -- exterior
    power of a module

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note exteriorPower(ZZ,Matrix): exteriorPower_lpZZ_cmMatrix_rp, -- exterior
    power of a matrix
