printingAccuracy -- current accuracy for printing numbers
*********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        printingAccuracy = n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,
  * Consequences:
      * Henceforth, inexact numbers are printed with at most n digits to the
        right of the decimal point displayed. The special case where n=-1 is
        interpreted as meaning n=infinity, and this case is used when a number
        appears alone on an output line.

Description
===========

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : printingPrecision,printingAccuracy                |
|                                                       |
|o1 = (6, -1)                                           |
|                                                       |
|o1 : Sequence                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : 1p100e-5/3                                        |
|                                                       |
|o2 = .000003333333333333333333333333333333             |
|                                                       |
|o2 : RR (of precision 100)                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : x = {1p100e-5/3,1p100e-4/3,1p100e-3/3,1p100e-2/3} |
|                                                       |
|o3 = {.00000333333, .0000333333, .000333333, .00333333}|
|                                                       |
|o3 : List                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : printingAccuracy = 8                              |
|                                                       |
|o4 = 8                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : x                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o5 = {.00000333, .00003333, .00033333, .00333333}      |
|                                                       |
|o5 : List                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : printingAccuracy = 4                              |
|                                                       |
|o6 = 4                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : x                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o7 = {0, 0, .0003, .0033}                              |
|                                                       |
|o7 : List                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note printingAccuracy: printingAccuracy, -- current accuracy for printing
    numbers
  * *note printingLeadLimit: printingLeadLimit, -- maximum number of leading
    zeroes to use when printing real numbers
  * *note printingTrailLimit: printingTrailLimit, -- maximum number of
    additional trailing digits to use when printing real numbers
  * *note printingSeparator: printingSeparator, -- string used to separate
    mantissa from exponent when printing real numbers
  * *note format: format, -- format a string or real number

For the programmer
==================

The object *note printingAccuracy: printingAccuracy, is an *note integer: ZZ,.

