modules
*******

In Macaulay2, modules are implemented as *note subquotient modules: subquotient
modules,. Submodules and quotients of free modules are perhaps the most common
and important modules, and subquotients form the smallest class of modules that
naturally includes these cases.


See *note Tutorial_colon_ Modules in Macaulay2: Tutorial_co Modules in
Macaulay2, for an overview tutorial on modules.


For additional common operations and a comprehensive list of all routines in
Macaulay2 which return or use modules, see *note Module: Module,.
* Menu:

* Module::                      the class of all modules
* module::                      make or get a module
* isModule::                    whether something is a module

construction of modules
