Module -- the class of all modules
**********************************

Description
===========


For basic information about modules in Macaulay2, see *note modules: modules,.


Common ways to make a module:
  * *note Ring ^ ZZ: Ring ^ ZZ, -- make a free module
  * *note Ring ^ List: Ring ^ List, -- make a free module
  * *note cokernel(Matrix): cokernel_lpMatrix_rp, -- cokernel of a map of
    modules
  * *note image(Matrix): image_lpMatrix_rp, -- image of a map
  * *note kernel(Matrix): kernel_lpMatrix_rp, -- kernel of a matrix
Common ways to get information about modules:
  * *note ring(Module): ring, -- get the associated ring of an object
  * *note numgens(Module): numgens_lpModule_rp, -- number of generators of a
    module
  * *note degrees(Module): degrees_lpRing_rp, -- degrees of generators
  * *note generators(Module): generators_lpModule_rp, -- the generator matrix
    of a module
  * *note relations(Module): relations, -- the defining relations
  * *note isFreeModule: isFreeModule, -- whether something is a free module
  * *note isHomogeneous(Module): isHomogeneous, -- whether something is
    homogeneous (graded)
Numerical information about a module:
  * *note codim(Module): codim_lpModule_rp, -- codimension of the support of a
    module
  * *note dim(Module): dim_lpModule_rp, -- compute the Krull dimension
  * *note rank(Module): rank, -- compute the rank
Submodules, quotients, and subquotient modules:
  * *note ambient(Module): ambient_lpModule_rp, -- ambient free module
  * *note cover(Module): cover_lpModule_rp, -- get the covering free module
  * *note super(Module): super, -- get the ambient module
  * *note Module / Module: Module / Module, -- quotient module
  * *note subquotient(Matrix,Matrix): subquotient, -- make a subquotient module
  * *note isSubset(Module,Module): isSubset_lpModule_cmModule_rp, -- whether
    one object is a subset of another
Common operations on modules:
  * *note Module + Module: Module + Module, -- sum of submodules
  * *note Module == Module: equality and containment of modules,
  * *note Module ++ Module: Module ++ Module, -- direct sum of modules
  * *note Module ^ List: Module ^ List, -- projection onto summand
  * *note Module ** Module: tensor_lpModule_cmModule_rp, -- tensor product of
    modules
  * *note Module ^** ZZ: Module ^_st_st ZZ, -- tensor power
  * *note Module _ List: Module _us List, -- map from free module to some
    generators
Minimalization:
  * *note mingens(Module): mingens_lpModule_rp, -- minimal generator matrix
  * *note trim(Module): trim, -- minimize generators and relations
  * *note minimalPresentation(Module): minimalPresentation_lpModule_rp, --
    minimal presentation of a module
Graded modules:
  * *note basis: basis, -- basis or generating set of all or part of a ring,
    ideal or module
  * *note truncate(ZZ,Module): (Truncations)truncate_lpList_cmModule_rp, --
    truncation of the graded ring, ideal or module at a specified degree or set
    of degrees
  * *note degree(Module): degree_lpModule_rp, -- get the degree of a module
  * *note genera(Module): (Varieties)genera_lpCoherentSheaf_rp,
  * *note hilbertSeries(Module): hilbertSeries_lpModule_rp, -- compute the
    Hilbert series of the module
  * *note hilbertFunction(ZZ,Module): hilbertFunction, -- the Hilbert function
  * *note poincare(Module): poincare, -- assemble degrees of a ring, module, or
    ideal into a polynomial
  * *note regularity(Module): regularity, -- compute the Castelnuovo-Mumford
    regularity
Annihilators, quotients and Gröbner bases:
  * *note gb(Module): gb, -- compute a Gröbner basis
  * *note Ideal _colon_ Ideal: (Saturation)quotient_lpModule_cmModule_rp, --
    ideal or submodule quotient
