symmetricAlgebra -- the symmetric algebra of a module
*****************************************************

Description
===========

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        symmetricAlgebra M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: Ring,, the symmetric algebra of M
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                                |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = image matrix{{a,b,c}}                    |
|                                                  |
|o2 = image | a b c |                              |
|                                                  |
|                             1                    |
|o2 : R-module, submodule of R                     |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : symmetricAlgebra M                           |
|                                                  |
|                       R[p ..p ]                  |
|                          0   2                   |
|o3 = ---------------------------------------------|
|     (- b*p  + a*p , - c*p  + b*p , - c*p  + a*p )|
|           0      1       1      2       0      2 |
|                                                  |
|o3 : QuotientRing                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : symmetricAlgebra(R^{1,2,3})                  |
|                                                  |
|o4 = R[p ..p ]                                    |
|        0   2                                     |
|                                                  |
|o4 : PolynomialRing                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+

Most of the optional arguments for monoids (see *note Ring Array: Ring Array,
or *note monoid: monoid,) are available here as well, as in the following
example.  They apply to the variables that correspond to the generators of the
module.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : A = symmetricAlgebra(M, Variables=>{x,y,z})                   |
|                                                                   |
|o5 = A                                                             |
|                                                                   |
|o5 : QuotientRing                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : describe A                                                    |
|                                                                   |
|                     R[x..z]                                       |
|o6 = ---------------------------------------                       |
|     (- b*x + a*y, - c*y + b*z, - c*x + a*z)                       |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : B = symmetricAlgebra(M, VariableBaseName=>G, MonomialSize=>16)|
|                                                                   |
|o7 = B                                                             |
|                                                                   |
|o7 : QuotientRing                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : describe B                                                    |
|                                                                   |
|                       R[G ..G ]                                   |
|                          0   2                                    |
|o8 = ---------------------------------------------                 |
|     (- b*G  + a*G , - c*G  + b*G , - c*G  + a*G )                 |
|           0      1       1      2       0      2                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : symmetricAlgebra(M, Degrees=> {3:1})                          |
|                                                                   |
|                       R[p ..p ]                                   |
|                          0   2                                    |
|o9 = ---------------------------------------------                 |
|     (- b*p  + a*p , - c*p  + b*p , - c*p  + a*p )                 |
|           0      1       1      2       0      2                  |
|                                                                   |
|o9 : QuotientRing                                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        symmetricAlgebra f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring map: RingMap,, the map between symmetric algebras induced
        by f
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : symmetricAlgebra vars R                                     |
|                                                                  |
|o10 = map (R[p ], R[p ..p ], {a*p , b*p , c*p , d*p , a, b, c, d})|
|              0      0   3       0     0     0     0              |
|                                                                  |
|o10 : RingMap R[p ] <-- R[p ..p ]                                 |
|                 0         0   3                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        symmetricAlgebra(A,B,f)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note ring: Ring,, the symmetric algebra of the target of f,
        previously computed.  Optional.
      * B, a *note ring: Ring,, the symmetric algebra of the source of f,
        previously computed.  Optional.
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring map: RingMap,, the map between the specified symmetric
        algebras induced by f

This form of functoriality is needed, because various options are available
when computing symmetric algebras.

For a linear map that is an isomorphism, and is known to be so, e.g., by having
had its inverse computed, the inverse of the corresponding map between
symmetric algebras is precomputed and made available.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : symmetricAlgebra vars R                                     |
|                                                                  |
|o11 = map (R[p ], R[p ..p ], {a*p , b*p , c*p , d*p , a, b, c, d})|
|              0      0   3       0     0     0     0              |
|                                                                  |
|o11 : RingMap R[p ] <-- R[p ..p ]                                 |
|                 0         0   3                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : p = symmetricAlgebra(A,B,id_M)                              |
|                                                                  |
|o12 = map (A, B, {x, y, z, a, b, c, d})                           |
|                                                                  |
|o12 : RingMap A <-- B                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : p^-1                                                        |
|                                                                  |
|o13 = map (B, A, {G , G , G , a, b, c, d})                        |
|                   0   1   2                                      |
|                                                                  |
|o13 : RingMap B <-- A                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : p * p^-1 === id_A                                           |
|                                                                  |
|o14 = true                                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : p^-1 * p === id_B                                           |
|                                                                  |
|o15 = true                                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use symmetricAlgebra:
=============================

  * "symmetricAlgebra(Matrix)"
  * "symmetricAlgebra(Module)"
  * "symmetricAlgebra(Nothing,Nothing,Matrix)"
  * "symmetricAlgebra(Nothing,Ring,Matrix)"
  * "symmetricAlgebra(Ring,Nothing,Matrix)"
  * "symmetricAlgebra(Ring,Ring,Matrix)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note symmetricAlgebra: symmetricAlgebra, is a *note method function
with options: MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

