formation -- recover the methods used to make a module
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        formation M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,, a module
  * Outputs:
      * an *note expression: Expression,, an *note expression: Expression,
        whose value is the module itself

Description
===========

If the module was created as a direct sum, tensor product, of Hom-module, then
the expression will reflect that. In each case, the result is a function
application, and the sequence of arguments is easily obtained.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : M = ZZ^2 ++ ZZ^3                          |
|                                               |
|       5                                       |
|o1 = ZZ                                        |
|                                               |
|o1 : ZZ-module, free                           |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : t = formation M                           |
|                                               |
|                  2    3                       |
|o2 = directSum (ZZ , ZZ )                      |
|                                               |
|o2 : Expression of class FunctionApplication   |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : peek t                                    |
|                                               |
|                                       2    3  |
|o3 = FunctionApplication{directSum, (ZZ , ZZ )}|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : t#1                                       |
|                                               |
|        2    3                                 |
|o4 = (ZZ , ZZ )                                |
|                                               |
|o4 : Sequence                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : value t                                   |
|                                               |
|       5                                       |
|o5 = ZZ                                        |
|                                               |
|o5 : ZZ-module, free                           |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : M = directSum(ZZ^2, ZZ^3, ZZ^4)           |
|                                               |
|       9                                       |
|o6 = ZZ                                        |
|                                               |
|o6 : ZZ-module, free                           |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : t = formation M                           |
|                                               |
|                  2    3    4                  |
|o7 = directSum (ZZ , ZZ , ZZ )                 |
|                                               |
|o7 : Expression of class FunctionApplication   |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i8 : t#1                                       |
|                                               |
|        2    3    4                            |
|o8 = (ZZ , ZZ , ZZ )                           |
|                                               |
|o8 : Sequence                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i9 : M = ZZ^2 ** ZZ^3                          |
|                                               |
|       6                                       |
|o9 = ZZ                                        |
|                                               |
|o9 : ZZ-module, free                           |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i10 : t = formation M                          |
|                                               |
|                2    3                         |
|o10 = tensor (ZZ , ZZ )                        |
|                                               |
|o10 : Expression of class FunctionApplication  |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i11 : t#1                                      |
|                                               |
|         2    3                                |
|o11 = (ZZ , ZZ )                               |
|                                               |
|o11 : Sequence                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------+

If the module was not obtained that way, then *note null: null, is returned.

+--------------------+
|i12 : formation ZZ^6|
+--------------------+

The same remarks apply to certain other types of objects, such as chain
complexes.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : R = QQ[x,y];                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : C = res coker vars R;                         |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : D = C ++ C                                    |
|                                                    |
|       2      4      2                              |
|o15 = R  <-- R  <-- R                               |
|                                                    |
|      0      1      2                               |
|                                                    |
|o15 : Complex                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : formation D                                   |
|                                                    |
|                  1      2      1   1      2      1 |
|o16 = directSum (R  <-- R  <-- R , R  <-- R  <-- R )|
|                                                    |
|                 0      1      2   0      1      2  |
|                                                    |
|o16 : Expression of class FunctionApplication       |
+----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note directSum: directSum, -- direct sum of modules or maps
  * *note Module ++ Module: Module ++ Module, -- direct sum of modules
  * *note Module ** Module: tensor_lpModule_cmModule_rp, -- tensor product of
    modules
  * *note Hom(Module,Module): Hom, -- module of homomorphisms
  * *note FunctionApplication: FunctionApplication, -- the class of all
    function application expressions
  * *note Expression: Expression, -- the class of all expressions

Ways to use formation:
======================

  * "formation(Module)"

