ambient -- ambient free module of a subquotient, or ambient ring
****************************************************************

Description
===========

Each module M in Macaulay2 is a quotient, submodule or subquotient of a free
module, called the ambient free module of M.


The ambient ring of a quotient ring R/I is the polynomial ring of that it is a
quotient.  The ambient ring of a Galois field is the quotient ring that it was
constructed from.


See also
========

  * *note GF: GF, -- make a finite field
  * *note cover: cover, -- get the covering free module
  * *note super: super, -- get the ambient module

Ways to use ambient:
====================

  * *note ambient(GaloisField): ambient_lpGaloisField_rp, -- corresponding
    quotient ring
  * *note ambient(Matrix): ambient_lpMatrix_rp, -- get the map between the
    ambient free modules
  * *note ambient(Module): ambient_lpModule_rp, -- ambient free module
  * "ambient(PolynomialRing)" -- see *note ambient(Ring): ambient_lpRing_rp, --
    ambient polynomial ring
  * "ambient(QuotientRing)" -- see *note ambient(Ring): ambient_lpRing_rp, --
    ambient polynomial ring
  * *note ambient(Ring): ambient_lpRing_rp, -- ambient polynomial ring

