length(Module) -- compute the length of a module
************************************************

  * Function: *note length: length,
  * Usage: 
        l = length M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,, 
  * Outputs:
      * l, an *note integer: ZZ,, the length of M
  * Consequences:
      * In the local case, the length of the module is stored in
        M.cache.length.

Description
===========

If M is a graded module over a singly graded polynomial ring or a quotient of a
polynomial ring over a field k then length is the same as the degree.

If M is over a local ring then length is computed by summing the output of the
Hilbert-Samuel function until it vanishes. Note that in this case the *note
LocalRings: (LocalRings)Top, package must be loaded first.

Caveat
======

In the local case, the input is assumed to have finite length.

See also
========

  * *note degree(Module): degree_lpModule_rp, -- get the degree of a module

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note length(Module): length_lpModule_rp, -- compute the length of a module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

