dim(Module) -- compute the Krull dimension
******************************************

  * Function: *note dim: dim,
  * Usage: 
        dim M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,

Description
===========

Computes the Krull dimension of the module M
+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/31991[a,b,c,d]                |
|                                          |
|o1 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialCurveIdeal(R,{1,2,3})    |
|                                          |
|             2                    2       |
|o2 = ideal (c  - b*d, b*c - a*d, b  - a*c)|
|                                          |
|o2 : Ideal of R                           |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = Ext^1(I,R)                       |
|                                          |
|o3 = cokernel {-3} | a -b c |             |
|              {-3} | b -c d |             |
|                                          |
|                            2             |
|o3 : R-module, quotient of R              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : dim M                                |
|                                          |
|o4 = 2                                    |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : N = Ext^0(I,R)                       |
|                                          |
|o5 = image {-2} | c2-bd |                 |
|           {-2} | bc-ad |                 |
|           {-2} | b2-ac |                 |
|                                          |
|                             3            |
|o5 : R-module, submodule of R             |
+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : dim N                                |
|                                          |
|o6 = 4                                    |
+------------------------------------------+
Note that the dimension of the zero module is -1.

See also
========

  * *note dim(Ring): dim_lpRing_rp, -- compute the Krull dimension
  * *note dim(Ideal): dim_lpIdeal_rp, -- compute the Krull dimension

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note dim(Module): dim_lpModule_rp, -- compute the Krull dimension
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/functions/dim-doc.m2:62:0.

