Module ++ Module -- direct sum of modules
*****************************************

  * Operator: *note ++: ++,

Description
===========

M++N -- computes the direct sum of two modules (or coherent sheaves).
+----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a..c];            |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : image vars R ++ kernel vars R|
|                                  |
|o2 = image {0} | a b c 0  0  0  | |
|           {1} | 0 0 0 -b 0  -c | |
|           {1} | 0 0 0 a  -c 0  | |
|           {1} | 0 0 0 0  b  a  | |
|                                  |
|                             4    |
|o2 : R-module, submodule of R     |
+----------------------------------+

The projection and inclusion maps for direct sums can be obtained with the
following methods.

  * *note Module ^ Array: Module ^ Array, -- projection onto summand
  * *note Module _ Array: Module _us Array, -- inclusion from summand

The components can be recovered later with *note components: components, or
with *note formation: formation,.

See also
========

  * *note directSum: directSum, -- direct sum of modules or maps

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note Module ++ Module: Module ++ Module, -- direct sum of modules
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/functions/directSum-doc.m2:48:0.

