hilbertPolynomial(Module) -- compute the Hilbert polynomial of the module
*************************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial,
  * Usage: 
        hilbertPolynomial M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Projective: hilbertPolynomial_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmProjective=>_pd_pd_pd
        _rp, => ..., default value true, choose how to display the Hilbert
        polynomial
  * Outputs:
      * a *note projective Hilbert polynomial: ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial,,
        unless the option Projective is false

Description
===========

We compute the *note Hilbert polynomial: hilbertPolynomial, of a module.
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                             |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = module monomialCurveIdeal(R, {1,3,4});|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : h = hilbertPolynomial M                   |
|                                               |
|o3 = 3*P  - 4*P  + P                           |
|        0      1    3                          |
|                                               |
|o3 : ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial               |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hilbertPolynomial(M, Projective=>false)   |
|                                               |
|     1 3    2   13                             |
|o4 = -i  + i  - --i                            |
|     6           6                             |
|                                               |
|o4 : QQ[i]                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------+


