minimalPresentation(Module) -- minimal presentation of a module
***************************************************************

  * Function: *note minimalPresentation: minimalPresentation,
  * Usage: 
        N = minimalPresentation M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Exclude: minimalPresentation_lpRing_rp, => ..., default value {},
        compute a minimal presentation of a quotient ring
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note module: Module,, isomorphic to M
  * Consequences:
      * The isomorphism from N to M as g = N.cache.pruningMap unless
        M.cache.pruningMap already exists, in which case N is the same as M.
        The inverse isomorphism can be obtained as g^-1

Description
===========

If the Module M is graded then the module N is a minimal presentation of M.  If
not, then an attempt is made to improve the presentation of M.  An example
follows.
+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/32003[a..d];                    |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = coker matrix {{a,1,b},{c,3,b+d}}   |
|                                            |
|o2 = cokernel | a 1 b   |                   |
|              | c 3 b+d |                   |
|                                            |
|                            2               |
|o2 : R-module, quotient of R                |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = minimalPresentation M              |
|                                            |
|o3 = cokernel | b+16001d a-10668c |         |
|                                            |
|                            1               |
|o3 : R-module, quotient of R                |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : peek N.cache                           |
|                                            |
|o4 = CacheTable{cache => MutableHashTable{}}|
|                pruningMap => | -10668 |    |
|                              | 0      |    |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : g = N.cache.pruningMap                 |
|                                            |
|o5 = | -10668 |                             |
|     | 0      |                             |
|                                            |
|o5 : Matrix M <-- N                         |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i6 : g^-1                                   |
|                                            |
|o6 = | -3 1 |                               |
|                                            |
|o6 : Matrix N <-- M                         |
+--------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note minimalPresentation(Matrix): minimalPresentation_lpMatrix_rp, --
    minimally present source and target of a matrix
  * *note trim(Module): trim, -- minimize generators and relations
  * *note mingens(Module): mingens_lpModule_rp, -- minimal generator matrix

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note minimalPresentation(Module): minimalPresentation_lpModule_rp, --
    minimal presentation of a module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in
Macaulay2Doc/functions/minimalPresentation-doc.m2:171:0.

