pdim(Module) -- compute the projective dimension of a module
************************************************************

  * Function: *note pdim: pdim,
  * Usage: 
        pdim M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,, the projective dimension

Description
===========

+------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];           |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2, x*y, y*z);|
|                              |
|o2 : Ideal of R               |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : M = R^1/I                |
|                              |
|o3 = cokernel | x2 xy yz |    |
|                              |
|                            1 |
|o3 : R-module, quotient of R  |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : res M                    |
|                              |
|      1      3      2         |
|o4 = R  <-- R  <-- R          |
|                              |
|     0      1      2          |
|                              |
|o4 : Complex                  |
+------------------------------+
|i5 : pdim M                   |
|                              |
|o5 = 2                        |
+------------------------------+
Notice this is one more than the projective dimension of I as an R-module.
+-------------------+
|i6 : res(module I) |
|                   |
|      3      2     |
|o6 = R  <-- R      |
|                   |
|     0      1      |
|                   |
|o6 : Complex       |
+-------------------+
|i7 : pdim(module I)|
|                   |
|o7 = 1             |
+-------------------+

