presentation(Module) -- presentation of a module
************************************************

  * Function: *note presentation: presentation,
  * Usage: 
        presentation M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, a presentation matrix of M

Description
===========

A presentation of M is a map p so that coker p is isomorphic to M.  The
presentation obtained is expressed in terms of the given generators, i.e., the
modules cover M and target p are identical. The isomorphism can be obtained as
map(M,coker p,1).


Since a module M may be described as a submodule or a subquotient module of a
free module, some computation may be required to produce a presentation.  See
also *note trim: trim,, or *note minimalPresentation: minimalPresentation,,
which do a bit more work to try to eliminate redundant generators.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal"a2-b2,abc"                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|             2    2                                                          |
|o2 = ideal (a  - b , a*b*c)                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = I/(I^2+a*I)                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = subquotient (| a2-b2 abc |, | a4-2a2b2+b4 a3bc-ab3c a2b2c2 a3-ab2 a2bc  |
|                                                                             |
|                               1                                             |
|o3 : R-module, subquotient of R                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
||)                                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : presentation M                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {2} | a b2 0 0  |                                                       |
|     {3} | 0 0  a b2 |                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|             2      4                                                        |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note minimalPresentation: minimalPresentation, -- compute a minimal
    presentation
  * *note trim: trim, -- minimize generators and relations
  * *note generators: generators, -- provide matrix or list of generators
  * *note relations: relations, -- the defining relations
  * *note cover: cover, -- get the covering free module

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note presentation(Module): presentation_lpModule_rp, -- presentation of a
    module
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

