tensor(Module,Module) -- tensor product of modules
**************************************************

  * Function: *note tensor: tensor,
  * Usage: 
        M ** N
        tensor(M, N)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,, 
      * N, a *note module: Module,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: Module,, the tensor product of $M$ and $N$

Description
===========

If $M$ has generators $m_1, $m_2, \dots, $m_r$, and $N$ has generators $n_1,
n_2, \dots, n_s$, then $M \otimes N$ has generators $m_i\otimes n_j$ for
$0<i\leq r$ and $0<j\leq s$.

+---------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[a..d];               |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : M = image matrix {{a,b}}    |
|                                 |
|o2 = image | a b |               |
|                                 |
|                             1   |
|o2 : R-module, submodule of R    |
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : N = image matrix {{c,d}}    |
|                                 |
|o3 = image | c d |               |
|                                 |
|                             1   |
|o3 : R-module, submodule of R    |
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : M ** N                      |
|                                 |
|o4 = cokernel {2} | -d 0  -b 0  ||
|              {2} | c  0  0  -b ||
|              {2} | 0  -d a  0  ||
|              {2} | 0  c  0  a  ||
|                                 |
|                            4    |
|o4 : R-module, quotient of R     |
+---------------------------------+
|i5 : N ** M                      |
|                                 |
|o5 = cokernel {2} | -b 0  -d 0  ||
|              {2} | a  0  0  -d ||
|              {2} | 0  -b c  0  ||
|              {2} | 0  a  0  c  ||
|                                 |
|                            4    |
|o5 : R-module, quotient of R     |
+---------------------------------+

Use *note trim: trim, or *note minimalPresentation: minimalPresentation, if a
more compact presentation is desired.

Use *note flip: flip, to produce the isomorphism $M \otimes N \to N \otimes M$.

To recover the factors from the tensor product, use the function *note
formation: formation,.

See also
========

  * *note flip: flip, -- isomorphism map of commutativity of tensor product
  * *note tensor(Module,Matrix): tensor_lpMatrix_cmModule_rp, -- tensor product
  * *note tensor(Matrix,Matrix): tensor_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, -- tensor product
  * *note formation: formation, -- recover the methods used to make a module

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note tensor(Module,Module): tensor_lpModule_cmModule_rp, -- tensor product
    of modules
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

