Module ** Ring -- tensor product
********************************

  * Operator: *note **: _st_st,
  * Usage: 
        M ** R
        R ** M
        tensor(M, R)
        tensor(R, M)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module, or an *note ideal: Ideal,, 
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: Module,, over $R$, obtained by forming the tensor
        product of the module $M$ with $R$

Description
===========

If the ring of $M$ is a base ring of $R$ then the matrix presenting the module
will be simply promoted (see *note promote: promote,). Otherwise, a ring map
from the ring of M to R will be constructed by examining the names of the
variables, as described in *note map(Ring,Ring): map_lpRing_cmRing_rp,.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x,y];                |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = coker vars R                |
|                                     |
|o2 = cokernel | x y |                |
|                                     |
|                            1        |
|o2 : R-module, quotient of R         |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : M ** R[t]                       |
|                                     |
|o3 = cokernel | x y |                |
|                                     |
|                                    1|
|o3 : R[t]-module, quotient of (R[t]) |
+-------------------------------------+

