Ring ^ List -- make a free module
*********************************

  * Operator: *note ^: ^,
  * Usage: 
        M = R^{i,j,k,...}
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: Ring,
      * {i,j,k, ...}, a *note list: List,, of integers or lists of integers
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: Module,, , a free module over R whose generators have
        degrees -i, -j, -k, ...

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d]                        |
|                                         |
|o1 = R                                   |
|                                         |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                      |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : R^{-1}                              |
|                                         |
|      1                                  |
|o2 = R                                   |
|                                         |
|o2 : R-module, free, degrees {1}         |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : R^{-1,2:-2,-3}                      |
|                                         |
|      4                                  |
|o3 = R                                   |
|                                         |
|o3 : R-module, free, degrees {1..2, 2..3}|
+-----------------------------------------+


If i, j, ... are lists of integers, then they represent multi-degrees, as in
*note graded and multigraded polynomial rings: graded and multigraded
polynomial rings,.
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = QQ[x,y,z,Degrees=>{{1,0},{1,-1},{1,-2}}]|
|                                                 |
|o4 = R                                           |
|                                                 |
|o4 : PolynomialRing                              |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R^{{1,2}}                                   |
|                                                 |
|      1                                          |
|o5 = R                                           |
|                                                 |
|o5 : R-module, free, degrees {{-1, -2}}          |
+-------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note degrees: degrees, -- degrees of generators
  * *note free modules: free modules,
  * *note graded and multigraded polynomial rings: graded and multigraded
    polynomial rings,

