isFreeModule -- whether something is a free module
**************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isFreeModule M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note thing: Thing,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, *note true: true, if the given
        representation of M is a free module and *note false: false, otherwise

Description
===========

This function checks if the module M is equal to its *note ambient: ambient,
free module by examining its matrix of *note generators:
generators_lpModule_rp, and its matrix of *note relations: relations,.


To determine whether M is isomorphic to a free module, use *note prune: prune,
M.
+------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/7[x,y];           |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : M = kernel vars R        |
|                              |
|o2 = image {1} | -y |         |
|           {1} | x  |         |
|                              |
|                             2|
|o2 : R-module, submodule of R |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : isFreeModule M           |
|                              |
|o3 = false                    |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : isFreeModule prune M     |
|                              |
|o4 = true                     |
+------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ambient: ambient, -- ambient free module of a subquotient, or ambient
    ring
  * *note prune(Module): minimalPresentation_lpModule_rp, -- minimal
    presentation of a module

Ways to use isFreeModule:
=========================

  * "isFreeModule(Module)"
  * "isFreeModule(Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isFreeModule: isFreeModule, is a *note method function:
MethodFunction,.

