cokernel(Matrix) -- cokernel of a map of modules
************************************************

  * Function: *note cokernel: cokernel,
  * Usage: 
        cokernel f
  * Inputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, f : A --> Ba *note matrix: Matrix, or a *note
        ring element: RingElement,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: Module,, the object B/(image f)

Description
===========

coker is a synonym for cokernel.

The generators of the cokernel are provided by the generators of the target of
f.  In other words, cover target f and cover cokernel f are equal.

An argument f that is a *note RingElement: RingElement, is interpreted as a one
by one matrix.

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[a..d];                               |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = cokernel matrix{{2*a-b,3*c-5*d,a^2-b-3}}|
|                                                 |
|o2 = cokernel | 2a-b 3c-5d a2-b-3 |              |
|                                                 |
|                            1                    |
|o2 : R-module, quotient of R                     |
+-------------------------------------------------+
If f is a matrix, and the target of f is a submodule, the resulting module will
be a *note subquotient: subquotient, module.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(a*M, M, a^3+a^2*b)                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {1} | a+10b+18 |                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Matrix                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (target f,source f)                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = (subquotient (| a |, | 2a-b 3c-5d a2-b-3 |), cokernel | 2a-b 3c-5d      |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     a2-b-3 |)                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : N = cokernel f                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = subquotient (| a |, | a2+10ab+18a 2a-b 3c-5d a2-b-3 |)                  |
|                                                                             |
|                               1                                             |
|o5 : R-module, subquotient of R                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : minimalPresentation N                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = cokernel | 81 27d 3c-5d 3b-18 a+b-9 9d2 bd-6d b2-b-30 3d3 d4 |          |
|                                                                             |
|                            1                                                |
|o6 : R-module, quotient of R                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note cover: cover, -- get the covering free module
  * *note image: image, -- image of a map
  * *note kernel: kernel, -- kernel of a map
  * *note coimage: coimage, -- coimage of a map
  * *note comodule: comodule, -- submodule to quotient module
  * *note minimalPresentation: minimalPresentation, -- compute a minimal
    presentation
  * *note matrices to and from modules: matrices to and from modules, --
    including kernel, cokernel and image

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note cokernel(Matrix): cokernel_lpMatrix_rp, -- cokernel of a map of
    modules
  * "cokernel(RingElement)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/functions/cokernel-doc.m2:42:0.

