isQuotientModule -- whether something is evidently a quotient of a free module
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isQuotientModule M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note thing: Thing,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, *note true: true, if the given
        representation of M a quotient of a free module.

Description
===========

This function checks if the module M is a quotient of its *note ambient:
ambient, free module by examining its matrix of *note generators:
generators_lpModule_rp,.
+-----------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c];      |
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : M = R^1/(a^2,b^2,c^2)   |
|                             |
|o2 = cokernel | a2 b2 c2 |   |
|                             |
|                            1|
|o2 : R-module, quotient of R |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : isQuotientModule M      |
|                             |
|o3 = true                    |
+-----------------------------+
The image of a map from a free module to the first generator of M yields an
equivalent module that is not presented as a quotient.
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = M_{0}                        |
|                                      |
|o4 = | 1 |                            |
|                                      |
|                   1                  |
|o4 : Matrix M <-- R                   |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : N = image f                      |
|                                      |
|o5 = subquotient (| 1 |, | a2 b2 c2 |)|
|                                      |
|                               1      |
|o5 : R-module, subquotient of R       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : M == N                           |
|                                      |
|o6 = true                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i7 : isQuotientModule N               |
|                                      |
|o7 = false                            |
+--------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Module _ List: Module _us List, -- map from free module to some
    generators
  * *note ambient: ambient, -- ambient free module of a subquotient, or ambient
    ring
  * *note isFreeModule: isFreeModule, -- whether something is a free module

Ways to use isQuotientModule:
=============================

  * "isQuotientModule(Module)"
  * "isQuotientModule(Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isQuotientModule: isQuotientModule, is a *note method
function: MethodFunction,.

