constructing maps between modules
*********************************

Let's start with a free module.
+---------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/5[x,y,z];|
+---------------------+
|i2 : F = R^3         |
|                     |
|      3              |
|o2 = R               |
|                     |
|o2 : R-module, free  |
+---------------------+
A list of indices can be used to produce homomorphisms corresponding to the
corresponding basis vectors.
+---------------------+
|i3 : F_{0,1,2}       |
|                     |
|o3 = | 1 0 0 |       |
|     | 0 1 0 |       |
|     | 0 0 1 |       |
|                     |
|             3      3|
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R |
+---------------------+
|i4 : F_{0,1}         |
|                     |
|o4 = | 1 0 |         |
|     | 0 1 |         |
|     | 0 0 |         |
|                     |
|             3      2|
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R |
+---------------------+
|i5 : F_{1,2}         |
|                     |
|o5 = | 0 0 |         |
|     | 1 0 |         |
|     | 0 1 |         |
|                     |
|             3      2|
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R |
+---------------------+
Matrices are viewed as linear transformations.
+------------------------+
|i6 : f = matrix{{x,y,z}}|
|                        |
|o6 = | x y z |          |
|                        |
|             1      3   |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R    |
+------------------------+
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

