codim(Module) -- codimension of the support of a module
*******************************************************

  * Function: *note codim: codim,
  * Usage: 
        codim M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,, a module over a ring R
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Generic: codim_lpIdeal_cmGeneric=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value false,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,

Description
===========

Computes the codimension of the support of the module as given by dim(R) -
dim(M).
+----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a..d];            |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : M = coker matrix{{a,b},{c,d}}|
|                                  |
|o2 = cokernel | a b |             |
|              | c d |             |
|                                  |
|                            2     |
|o2 : R-module, quotient of R      |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : codim M                      |
|                                  |
|o3 = 1                            |
+----------------------------------+

The returned value is the usual codimension if R is an integral domain or, more
generally, equidimensional.

See also
========

  * *note dim(Module): dim_lpModule_rp, -- compute the Krull dimension

