hilbertSeries(Module) -- compute the Hilbert series of the module
*****************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertSeries: hilbertSeries,
  * Usage: 
        hilbertSeries M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Order: hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value infinity, display the truncated power series expansion
      * *note Reduce: hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmReduce=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value false, reduce the Hilbert series
  * Outputs:
      * a *note divide expression: Divide,, the Hilbert series

Description
===========

We compute the *note Hilbert series: hilbertSeries, of a module.
+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x, Degrees => {2}];|
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : M = module ideal x^2          |
|                                   |
|o2 = image | x2 |                  |
|                                   |
|                             1     |
|o2 : R-module, submodule of R      |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : s = hilbertSeries M           |
|                                   |
|         4                         |
|        T                          |
|o3 = --------                      |
|           2                       |
|     (1 - T )                      |
|                                   |
|o3 : Expression of class Divide    |
+-----------------------------------+
|i4 : numerator s                   |
|                                   |
|      4                            |
|o4 = T                             |
|                                   |
|o4 : ZZ[T]                         |
+-----------------------------------+
|i5 : poincare M                    |
|                                   |
|      4                            |
|o5 = T                             |
|                                   |
|o5 : ZZ[T]                         |
+-----------------------------------+
Recall that the variables of the power series are the variables of the *note
degrees ring: degreesRing,.
+-------------------------------------+
|i6 : R=ZZ/101[x, Degrees => {{1,1}}];|
+-------------------------------------+
|i7 : M = module ideal x^2;           |
+-------------------------------------+
|i8 : s = hilbertSeries M             |
|                                     |
|         2 2                         |
|        T T                          |
|         0 1                         |
|o8 = ----------                      |
|     (1 - T T )                      |
|           0 1                       |
|                                     |
|o8 : Expression of class Divide      |
+-------------------------------------+
|i9 : numerator s                     |
|                                     |
|      2 2                            |
|o9 = T T                             |
|      0 1                            |
|                                     |
|o9 : ZZ[T ..T ]                      |
|         0   1                       |
+-------------------------------------+
|i10 : poincare M                     |
|                                     |
|       2 2                           |
|o10 = T T                            |
|       0 1                           |
|                                     |
|o10 : ZZ[T ..T ]                     |
|          0   1                      |
+-------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note hilbertSeries(Module): hilbertSeries_lpModule_rp, -- compute the
    Hilbert series of the module
