map -- make a map
*****************

  * Usage: 
        map(Y,X,d) or map(Y,X)
  * Inputs:
      * Y, an object, such as a ring, module, or chain complex
      * X, another object of the same type
      * d, a specification, such as a function, list, or matrix, or if omitted,
        understood to specify the identity map
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value null, specify the degree of a map
      * *note DegreeLift: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
      * *note DegreeMap: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
  * Outputs:
      * a map to Y from X defined by data d.

Description
===========

The function map provides a general mechanism for constructing a map
(homomorphism) between rings (a *note ring map: RingMap,), modules (a *note
matrix: Matrix,), or between objects in other categories.


See also the function *note matrix: matrix,, which focuses on creating new
matrices from rectangular arrays of ring elements or matrices.
* Menu:


Getting information about a map
* source::                      source of a map
* target::                      target of a map

Creating a map (matrix) between modules
* map(Module,Module,Function): map_lpModule_cmModule_cmFunction_rp.  create a matrix by specifying a function that gives each entry
* map(Module,Module,List): map_lpModule_cmModule_cmList_rp.  create a matrix by giving a sparse or dense list of entries
* map(Module,Module,RingElement): map_lpModule_cmModule_cmRingElement_rp.  construct the map induced by multiplication by a ring element on the generators
* map(Module,Module,Matrix): map_lpModule_cmModule_cmMatrix_rp.  create the matrix induced on generators by a given matrix

Creating a map between modules, where the source module is computed
* map(Module,ZZ,Function): map_lpModule_cmZZ_cmFunction_rp.  create a matrix from a free module by specifying a function that gives each entry
* map(Module,Nothing,List): map_lpModule_cmNothing_cmList_rp.  create a matrix by giving a doubly nested list of ring elements
* map(Module,ZZ,List): map_lpModule_cmZZ_cmList_rp.  create a matrix by giving a sparse or dense list of entries
* map(Module,Nothing,Matrix): map_lpModule_cmNothing_cmMatrix_rp.  recast a matrix to have a new target, and a free module as source

Creating a map with a different degree
* map(Matrix): map_lpMatrix_rp.  make a matrix with a different degree

Creating a map between modules over different rings
* map(Module,Module,RingMap,Matrix): map_lpModule_cmModule_cmRingMap_cmMatrix_rp.  homomorphism of modules over different rings

Creating a map between rings
* map(Ring,Ring): map_lpRing_cmRing_rp.  make a ring map, using the names of the variables
* map(Ring,Ring,List): map_lpRing_cmRing_cmList_rp.  make a ring map
* map(Ring,Ring,Matrix): map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp.  make a ring map

The Hom and End modules
* Hom::                         module of homomorphisms
* End::                         module of endomorphisms

Ways to use map:
================

  * map(GaloisField,GaloisField) (missing documentation)
  * *note map(Matrix): map_lpMatrix_rp, -- make a matrix with a different
    degree
  * *note map(Module): map_lpModule_rp, -- identity map
  * *note map(Module,Module,Function): map_lpModule_cmModule_cmFunction_rp, --
    create a matrix by specifying a function that gives each entry
  * *note map(Module,Module,List): map_lpModule_cmModule_cmList_rp, -- create a
    matrix by giving a sparse or dense list of entries
  * *note map(Module,Module,Matrix): map_lpModule_cmModule_cmMatrix_rp, --
    create the matrix induced on generators by a given matrix
  * "map(Module,Module,Number)" -- see *note map(Module,Module,RingElement):
    map_lpModule_cmModule_cmRingElement_rp, -- construct the map induced by
    multiplication by a ring element on the generators
  * *note map(Module,Module,RingElement):
    map_lpModule_cmModule_cmRingElement_rp, -- construct the map induced by
    multiplication by a ring element on the generators
  * "map(Module,Module,ZZ)" -- see *note map(Module,Module,RingElement):
