map(Module,Module,Function) -- create a matrix by specifying a function that gives each entry
*********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: map,
  * Usage: 
        map(M,N,f)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
      * N, a *note module: Module,
      * f, a *note function: Function,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value null, specify the degree of a map
      * *note DegreeLift: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
      * *note DegreeMap: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, a map from the module N to the module M whose
        matrix entry h_(i,j) is obtained from the function f by evaluating
        f(i,j).

Description
===========

Recall that all indices in Macaulay2 start at 0, so the upper left-most entry
of a matrix f is f_(0,0).


This function is often used when you already know the source and target
modules, including their gradings.  If you wish Macaulay2 to compute the column
degrees for you (so the resulting matrix will be homogeneous if possible), use
*note map(Module,ZZ,Function): map_lpModule_cmZZ_cmFunction_rp,.
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ[a..c];                             |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = map(R^3,R^{0,-1,-2,-3},(i,j) -> R_i^j)|
|                                               |
|o2 = | 1 a a2 a3 |                             |
|     | 1 b b2 b3 |                             |
|     | 1 c c2 c3 |                             |
|                                               |
|             3      4                          |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                           |
+-----------------------------------------------+
We specified the degrees of the source basis elements explicitly to ensure the
matrix would be homogeneous.
+--------------------+
|i3 : isHomogeneous f|
|                    |
|o3 = true           |
+--------------------+

Alternate approaches
====================

We could have let Macaulay2 take care of that for us, by replacing the source
module by its desired rank.
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : g = map(R^3,4,(i,j) -> R_i^j)          |
|                                            |
|o4 = | 1 a a2 a3 |                          |
|     | 1 b b2 b3 |                          |
|     | 1 c c2 c3 |                          |
|                                            |
|             3      4                       |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                        |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : degrees g                              |
|                                            |
|o5 = {{{0}, {0}, {0}}, {{0}, {1}, {2}, {3}}}|
|                                            |
|o5 : List                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isHomogeneous g                        |
|                                            |
|o6 = true                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+


Another way would be to let *note matrix: matrix, take care of that for us.
+--------------------------------------------+
|i7 : h = matrix table(3,4,(i,j) -> R_i^j)   |
|                                            |
|o7 = | 1 a a2 a3 |                          |
|     | 1 b b2 b3 |                          |
|     | 1 c c2 c3 |                          |
|                                            |
|             3      4                       |
|o7 : Matrix R  <-- R                        |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i8 : degrees h                              |
|                                            |
|o8 = {{{0}, {0}, {0}}, {{0}, {1}, {2}, {3}}}|
|                                            |
|o8 : List                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isHomogeneous h                        |
|                                            |
|o9 = true                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+

