map(Module,Module,RingElement) -- construct the map induced by multiplication by a ring element on the generators
*****************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: map,
  * Usage: 
        map(M,N,r)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
      * N, a *note module: Module,, over the same ring R as M.  An integer here
        stands for the free module of that rank.
      * r, a *note ring element: RingElement,, in the ring R
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value null, specify the degree of a map
      * *note DegreeLift: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
      * *note DegreeMap: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, The map induced by multiplication by r on the
        generators

Description
===========

If r is not zero, then either M and N should be equal, or they should have the
same number of generators.  This gives the same map as r * map(M,N,1).
map(M,N,1) is the map induced by the identity on the generators of M and N.
+---------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x];            |
+---------------------------+
|i2 : map(R^2,R^3,0)        |
|                           |
|o2 = 0                     |
|                           |
|             2      3      |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R       |
+---------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(R^2,R^2,x)    |
|                           |
|o3 = | x 0 |               |
|     | 0 x |               |
|                           |
|             2      2      |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R       |
+---------------------------+
|i4 : f == x *map(R^2,R^2,1)|
|                           |
|o4 = true                  |
+---------------------------+

Caveat
======

If M or N is not free, then we do not check that the result is a well defined
homomorphism.

See also
========

  * *note inducedMap: inducedMap, -- compute an induced map

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "map(Module,Module,Number)"
  * *note map(Module,Module,RingElement):
    map_lpModule_cmModule_cmRingElement_rp, -- construct the map induced by
    multiplication by a ring element on the generators
  * "map(Module,Module,ZZ)"
  * "map(Module,ZZ,ZZ)"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

