map(Module,Module,Matrix) -- create the matrix induced on generators by a given matrix
**************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: map,
  * Usage: 
        map(M,N,p)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
      * N, a *note module: Module,
      * p, a *note matrix: Matrix,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value null, specify the degree of a map
      * *note DegreeLift: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
      * *note DegreeMap: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, A matrix with the same entries as p, but whose
        target is M and source is N

Description
===========

M and N should be modules over the same ring, and have the same number of
generators as target p and source p, respectively.
+-------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];      |
+-------------------------+
|i2 : p = matrix {{x,y,z}}|
|                         |
|o2 = | x y z |           |
|                         |
|             1      3    |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R     |
+-------------------------+
|i3 : q = map(R^1,R^3,p)  |
|                         |
|o3 = | x y z |           |
|                         |
|             1      3    |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R     |
+-------------------------+
|i4 : degrees source p    |
|                         |
|o4 = {{1}, {1}, {1}}     |
|                         |
|o4 : List                |
+-------------------------+
|i5 : degrees source q    |
|                         |
|o5 = {{0}, {0}, {0}}     |
|                         |
|o5 : List                |
+-------------------------+

Caveat
======

If M or N is not free, then we do not check that the result is a well defined
homomorphism.

See also
========

  * *note inducedMap: inducedMap, -- compute an induced map

