map(Module,ZZ,Function) -- create a matrix from a free module by specifying a function that gives each entry
************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: map,
  * Usage: 
        map(M,n,f)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: Module,
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ,
      * f, a *note function: Function,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value null, specify the degree of a map
      * *note DegreeLift: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
      * *note DegreeMap: map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        null, make a ring map
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, a map from a graded free module of rank n to
        the module M whose matrix entry h_(i,j) is obtained from the function f
        by evaluating f(i,j).

Description
===========

This is the same as calling map(M,R^n,f), except that the degrees of the basis
elements of the source module are chosen in an attempt to ensure that the
resulting map is homogeneous of degree zero.
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = GF(9,Variable=>a)[x,y,z];                |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = map(R^1, 3, (i,j) -> (a^j * x - y)^(j+1))|
|                                                  |
|o2 = | x-y (a+1)x2+axy+y2 (-a-1)x3-y3 |           |
|                                                  |
|             1      3                             |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : source f                                     |
|                                                  |
|      3                                           |
|o3 = R                                            |
|                                                  |
|o3 : R-module, free, degrees {1..3}               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isHomogeneous f                              |
|                                                  |
|o4 = true                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------+

