map(...,Degree=>...) -- specify the degree of a map
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        map(..., Degree=>d)

Description
===========

Specifies that the degree of the map created should be d. The degree may be an
integer or a list of integers (multidegree). The length of the list should be
the same as the length of a degree for the ring, see *note degreeLength:
degreeLength,.


+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[x]                          |
|                                            |
|o1 = R                                      |
|                                            |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                         |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : p = map(R^1, R^1, {{x^4}})             |
|                                            |
|o2 = | x4 |                                 |
|                                            |
|             1      1                       |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                        |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isHomogeneous p                        |
|                                            |
|o3 = false                                  |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i4 : q = map(R^1, R^1, {{x^4}}, Degree => 4)|
|                                            |
|o4 = | x4 |                                 |
|                                            |
|             1      1                       |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                        |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isHomogeneous q                        |
|                                            |
|o5 = true                                   |
+--------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note map: map, -- make a map
  * *note matrix: matrix, -- make a matrix
  * *note inducedMap(...,Degree=>...):
    inducedMap_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, -- specify the degree of a
    map
  * *note matrix(...,Degree=>...): matrix_lpList_rp, -- create a matrix from a
    doubly-nested list of ring elements or matrices

