homomorphism' -- get the element of Hom from a homomorphism
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        homomorphism' f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,, of the form $M \to N$
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * DegreeLimit => an *note integer: ZZ, or a *note list: List,, default
        value null, see *note Hom(...,DegreeLimit=>...): Hom,
      * MinimalGenerators => a *note Boolean value: Boolean,, default value
        true, see *note Hom(...,MinimalGenerators=>...): Hom,
      * Strategy => a *note thing: Thing,, default value null, see *note
        Hom(...,Strategy=>...): Hom,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, the map $R^1 \to \mathrm{Hom}(M,N)$,
        corresponding to the map $f \in \mathrm{Hom}(M,N)$

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                       |
|                                         |
|o1 = R                                   |
|                                         |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                      |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = vars R ++ vars R                |
|                                         |
|o2 = | x y z 0 0 0 |                     |
|     | 0 0 0 x y z |                     |
|                                         |
|             2      6                    |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                     |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : g = homomorphism' f                 |
|                                         |
|o3 = {-1} | x |                          |
|     {-1} | 0 |                          |
|     {-1} | y |                          |
|     {-1} | 0 |                          |
|     {-1} | z |                          |
|     {-1} | 0 |                          |
|     {-1} | 0 |                          |
|     {-1} | x |                          |
|     {-1} | 0 |                          |
|     {-1} | y |                          |
|     {-1} | 0 |                          |
|     {-1} | z |                          |
|                                         |
|             12      1                   |
|o3 : Matrix R   <-- R                    |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i4 : target g === Hom(source f, target f)|
|                                         |
|o4 = true                                |
+-----------------------------------------+

We can undo the process with *note homomorphism: homomorphism,.

+------------------------+
|i5 : f' = homomorphism g|
|                        |
|o5 = | x y z 0 0 0 |    |
|     | 0 0 0 x y z |    |
|                        |
|             2      6   |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R    |
+------------------------+
|i6 : f === f'           |
|                        |
|o6 = true               |
+------------------------+

