Singular Book 1.3.3 -- properties of ring maps
**********************************************

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[a,b,c];               |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : R = QQ[x,y,z];               |
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : phi = map(R,S,{x,y,x^2-y^3}) |
|                                  |
|                          3    2  |
|o3 = map (R, S, {x, y, - y  + x })|
|                                  |
|o3 : RingMap R <-- S              |
+----------------------------------+
|i4 : isInjective phi              |
|                                  |
|o4 = false                        |
+----------------------------------+
|i5 : ker phi                      |
|                                  |
|            3    2                |
|o5 = ideal(b  - a  + c)           |
|                                  |
|o5 : Ideal of S                   |
+----------------------------------+
Packaged code for computing preimage is missing, but it's easy to do, as
follows.
+----------------------------------------+
|i6 : psi = map(R,S,{x,x+y,z-x^2+y^3})   |
|                                        |
|                            3    2      |
|o6 = map (R, S, {x, x + y, y  - x  + z})|
|                                        |
|o6 : RingMap R <-- S                    |
+----------------------------------------+
|i7 : isInjective psi                    |
|                                        |
|o7 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+
|i8 : ker psi                            |
|                                        |
|o8 = ideal ()                           |
|                                        |
|o8 : Ideal of S                         |
+----------------------------------------+
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/M2-Singular-Book.m2:278:0.

