Singular Book 1.8.1 -- ideal membership
***************************************

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ[x,y];                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^10+x^9*y^2, y^8-x^2*y^7);|
|                                          |
|o2 : Ideal of A                           |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = x^2*y^7+y^14;                    |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f % I                                |
|                                          |
|          12    8                         |
|o4 = - x*y   + y                          |
|                                          |
|o4 : A                                    |
+------------------------------------------+
So this f is not in the ideal I.
+---------------------+
|i5 : f = x*y^13+y^12;|
+---------------------+
|i6 : f % I           |
|                     |
|o6 = 0               |
|                     |
|o6 : A               |
+---------------------+
This f is in the ideal I.


Check inclusion and equality of ideals.
+-------------------------------+
|i7 : K = ideal(f,x^2*y^7+y^14);|
|                               |
|o7 : Ideal of A                |
+-------------------------------+
|i8 : (gens K) % I              |
|                               |
|o8 = | 0 -xy12+y8 |            |
|                               |
|             1      2          |
|o8 : Matrix A  <-- A           |
+-------------------------------+
In Macaulay2, inclusion of ideals can be tested using *note
isSubset(Ideal,Ideal): isSubset_lpIdeal_cmIdeal_rp, and equality can be checked
using *note Ideal == Ideal: equality and containment,.  In both cases the
necessary Gröbner bases are computed, if they have not already been computed.
+------------------+
|i9 : isSubset(K,I)|
|                  |
|o9 = false        |
+------------------+
|i10 : K == I      |
|                  |
|o10 = false       |
+------------------+
+-------------------------------+
|i11 : K = ideal(f,y^14+x*y^12);|
|                               |
|o11 : Ideal of A               |
+-------------------------------+
|i12 : (gens K) % I             |
|                               |
|o12 = 0                        |
|                               |
|              1      2         |
|o12 : Matrix A  <-- A          |
+-------------------------------+
|i13 : isSubset(K,I)            |
|                               |
|o13 = true                     |
+-------------------------------+
|i14 : K == I                   |
|                               |
|o14 = false                    |
+-------------------------------+
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

