Singular Book 1.8.7 -- solving equations
****************************************

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ[x,y,z,MonomialOrder=>Lex];          |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2+y+z-1, x+y^2+z-1, x+y+z^2-1);|
|                                                |
|o2 : Ideal of A                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : transpose gens gb I                        |
|                                                |
|o3 = {-6} | z6-4z4+4z3-z2 |                     |
|     {-4} | 2yz2+z4-z2    |                     |
|     {-2} | y2-y-z2+z     |                     |
|     {-2} | x+y+z2-1      |                     |
|                                                |
|             4      1                           |
|o3 : Matrix A  <-- A                            |
+------------------------------------------------+
Now we need to implement the solver!
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/M2-Singular-Book.m2:582:0.

