Singular Book 2.1.10 -- submodules of A^n
*****************************************

A common method of creating a submodule of A^n in Macaulay2 is to take the
image of a matrix.  This will be a submodule generated by the columns of the
matrix.
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ[x,y,z];                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = matrix{{x*y-1,y^4},{z^2+3,x^3},{x*y*z,z^2}}|
|                                                    |
|o2 = | xy-1 y4 |                                    |
|     | z2+3 x3 |                                    |
|     | xyz  z2 |                                    |
|                                                    |
|             3      2                               |
|o2 : Matrix A  <-- A                                |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = image f                                    |
|                                                    |
|o3 = image | xy-1 y4 |                              |
|           | z2+3 x3 |                              |
|           | xyz  z2 |                              |
|                                                    |
|                             3                      |
|o3 : A-module, submodule of A                       |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : numgens M                                      |
|                                                    |
|o4 = 2                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : ambient M                                      |
|                                                    |
|      3                                             |
|o5 = A                                              |
|                                                    |
|o5 : A-module, free                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
A submodule can easily be moved to quotient rings.
+------------------------------+
|i6 : Q = A/(x^2+y^2+z^2);     |
+------------------------------+
|i7 : substitute(M,Q)          |
|                              |
|o7 = image | xy-1 y4       |  |
|           | z2+3 -xy2-xz2 |  |
|           | xyz  z2       |  |
|                              |
|                             3|
|o7 : Q-module, submodule of Q |
+------------------------------+
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

