Singular Book 2.1.20 -- sum, intersection, module quotient
**********************************************************

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ[x,y,z];                   |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = image matrix{{x*y,x},{x*z,x}}|
|                                      |
|o2 = image | xy x |                   |
|           | xz x |                   |
|                                      |
|                             2        |
|o2 : A-module, submodule of A         |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = image matrix{{y^2,x},{z^2,x}}|
|                                      |
|o3 = image | y2 x |                   |
|           | z2 x |                   |
|                                      |
|                             2        |
|o3 : A-module, submodule of A         |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : M + N                            |
|                                      |
|o4 = image | xy x y2 x |              |
|           | xz x z2 x |              |
|                                      |
|                             2        |
|o4 : A-module, submodule of A         |
+--------------------------------------+
Notice that, in Macaulay2, each module comes equipped with a list of
generators, and operations such as sum do not try to simplify the list of
generators.


Intersection, quotients, annihilators are found using standard notation:
+-------------------------------+
|i5 : intersect(M,N)            |
|                               |
|o5 = image | x xy2-xz2 |       |
|           | x 0       |       |
|                               |
|                             2 |
|o5 : A-module, submodule of A  |
+-------------------------------+
|i6 : M : N                     |
|                               |
|o6 = ideal x                   |
|                               |
|o6 : Ideal of A                |
+-------------------------------+
|i7 : N : M                     |
|                               |
|o7 = ideal(y + z)              |
|                               |
|o7 : Ideal of A                |
+-------------------------------+
|i8 : Q = A/x^5;                |
+-------------------------------+
|i9 : M = substitute(M,Q)       |
|                               |
|o9 = image | xy x |            |
|           | xz x |            |
|                               |
|                             2 |
|o9 : Q-module, submodule of Q  |
+-------------------------------+
|i10 : ann M                    |
|                               |
|             4                 |
|o10 = ideal x                  |
|                               |
|o10 : Ideal of Q               |
+-------------------------------+
|i11 : M : x                    |
|                               |
|o11 = image | 1 y-z x4 |       |
|            | 1 0   0  |       |
|                               |
|                              2|
|o11 : Q-module, submodule of Q |
+-------------------------------+
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

