GroebnerBasis -- the class of all Gröbner bases
***********************************************

Description
===========

A Gröbner basis in Macaulay2 consists of a Gröbner basis computation, and
several associated matrices. Normally you don't need to refer to these objects
directly, as many operations on matrices and modules create them, and refer to
them.  For more information, see *note Gröbner bases: Gröbner bases,.
* Menu:

* returnCode::
* generators(GroebnerBasis): generators_lpGroebnerBasis_rp.  the generator matrix of a Gröbner basis
* mingens(GroebnerBasis): mingens_lpGroebnerBasis_rp.  (partially constructed) minimal generator matrix
* syz(GroebnerBasis): syz_lpGroebnerBasis_rp.  retrieve the syzygy matrix
* target(GroebnerBasis): target_lpGroebnerBasis_rp.  find target of a Gröbner basis
* getChangeMatrix(GroebnerBasis): getChangeMatrix.  get the change of basis matrix

Functions and methods returning a Gröbner basis:
================================================

  * *note forceGB: forceGB, -- declare that the columns of a matrix are a
    Gröbner basis
  * "forceGB(Matrix)" -- see *note forceGB: forceGB, -- declare that the
    columns of a matrix are a Gröbner basis
  * *note gb: gb, -- compute a Gröbner basis
  * "gb(Ideal)" -- see *note gb: gb, -- compute a Gröbner basis
  * "gb(Matrix)" -- see *note gb: gb, -- compute a Gröbner basis
  * "gb(Module)" -- see *note gb: gb, -- compute a Gröbner basis
  * "markedGB" -- see *note markedGB(Matrix,Matrix):
    markedGB_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, -- make a marked Gröbner basis
  * *note markedGB(Matrix,Matrix): markedGB_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, -- make a
    marked Gröbner basis

Methods that use a Gröbner basis:
=================================

  * "Number % GroebnerBasis" -- see *note %: %, -- a binary operator, usually
    used for remainder and reduction
  * "betti(GroebnerBasis)" -- see *note betti: betti, -- display or modify a
    Betti diagram
  * "status(GroebnerBasis)" -- see *note gb: gb, -- compute a Gröbner basis
  * *note generators(GroebnerBasis): generators_lpGroebnerBasis_rp, -- the
    generator matrix of a Gröbner basis
  * "getChangeMatrix(GroebnerBasis)" -- see *note getChangeMatrix:
    getChangeMatrix, -- get the change of basis matrix
  * "leadTerm(GroebnerBasis)" -- see *note leadTerm(Matrix):
    leadTerm_lpMatrix_rp, -- get the greatest term of each column
  * "leadTerm(ZZ,GroebnerBasis)" -- see *note leadTerm(ZZ,Matrix):
    leadTerm_lpZZ_cmMatrix_rp, -- get the matrix of lead polynomials of each
    column
  * *note Matrix % GroebnerBasis: Matrix % GroebnerBasis, -- compute the normal
    form of a ring element or matrix using a Gröbner basis
  * "RingElement % GroebnerBasis" -- see *note Matrix % GroebnerBasis: Matrix %
    GroebnerBasis, -- compute the normal form of a ring element or matrix using
    a Gröbner basis
  * *note mingens(GroebnerBasis): mingens_lpGroebnerBasis_rp, -- (partially
    constructed) minimal generator matrix
  * "Matrix // GroebnerBasis" -- see *note quotient(Matrix,Matrix):
    quotient_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, -- factor a map through another with the
    same target
  * "quotient(Matrix,GroebnerBasis)" -- see *note quotient(Matrix,Matrix):
    quotient_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, -- factor a map through another with the
    same target
  * "RingElement // GroebnerBasis" -- see *note quotient(Matrix,Matrix):
    quotient_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, -- factor a map through another with the
    same target
  * "quotientRemainder(Matrix,GroebnerBasis)" -- see *note quotientRemainder:
    quotientRemainder, -- matrix quotient and remainder
  * "remainder(Matrix,GroebnerBasis)" -- see *note remainder: remainder, --
    matrix remainder
  * "ring(GroebnerBasis)" -- see *note ring: ring, -- get the associated ring
    of an object
  * *note syz(GroebnerBasis): syz_lpGroebnerBasis_rp, -- retrieve the syzygy
    matrix
  * *note target(GroebnerBasis): target_lpGroebnerBasis_rp, -- find target of a
    Gröbner basis

