mingens(GroebnerBasis) -- (partially constructed) minimal generator matrix
**************************************************************************

  * Function: *note mingens: mingens,
  * Usage: 
        mingens G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note Gröbner basis: GroebnerBasis,
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: Complement, => ..., default value null, a Strategy
        option value
  * Outputs:
      * whose columns form a (partially computed) minimal generating set, a
        *note matrix: Matrix,

Description
===========

Every GroebnerBasis computation in Macaulay2 computes a generator matrix, in
the process of constructing the Gröbner basis.  If the original ideal or module
is homogeneous, then the columns of this matrix form a minimal set of
generators.  In the inhomogeneous case, the columns generate, and an attempt is
made to keep the size of the generating set small.


If the Gröbner basis is only partially constructed, the returned result will be
a partial answer.  In the graded case this set can be extended to a minimal set
of generators for the ideal or module.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..f]                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = genericSymmetricMatrix(R,a,3)                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = | a b c |                                                               |
|     | b d e |                                                               |
|     | c e f |                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|             3      3                                                        |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = minors(2,M)                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|               2                                                  2          |
|o3 = ideal (- b  + a*d, - b*c + a*e, - c*d + b*e, - b*c + a*e, - c  + a*f, - |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                             2                               |
|     c*e + b*f, - c*d + b*e, - c*e + b*f, - e  + d*f)                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : G = gb(I, PairLimit=>5)                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = GroebnerBasis[status: PairLimit; all S-pairs handled up to degree 1]    |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : GroebnerBasis                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : mingens G                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = | e2-df ce-bf cd-be |                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|             1      3                                                        |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : mingens I                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = | e2-df ce-bf cd-be c2-af bc-ae b2-ad |                                 |
|                                                                             |
|             1      6                                                        |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note GroebnerBasis: GroebnerBasis, -- the class of all Gröbner bases
  * *note gb: gb, -- compute a Gröbner basis
  * *note genericSymmetricMatrix: genericSymmetricMatrix, -- make a generic
    symmetric matrix
  * *note minors: minors_lpZZ_cmMatrix_rp, -- ideal generated by minors

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note mingens(GroebnerBasis): mingens_lpGroebnerBasis_rp, -- (partially
    constructed) minimal generator matrix
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

