syz(GroebnerBasis) -- retrieve the syzygy matrix
************************************************

  * Function: *note syz: syz,
  * Usage: 
        syz G
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note Gröbner basis: GroebnerBasis,, the Gröbner basis of a matrix
        h
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Algorithm: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value Inhomogeneous,
        compute the syzygy matrix
      * *note BasisElementLimit: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        infinity, compute the syzygy matrix
      * *note DegreeLimit: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value {}, compute
        the syzygy matrix
      * *note GBDegrees: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value null, compute
        the syzygy matrix
      * *note HardDegreeLimit: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value null,
        compute the syzygy matrix
      * *note MaxReductionCount: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value 10,
        compute the syzygy matrix
      * *note PairLimit: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value infinity,
        compute the syzygy matrix
      * *note StopBeforeComputation: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value
        false, compute the syzygy matrix
      * *note Strategy: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value {}, compute the
        syzygy matrix
      * *note SyzygyLimit: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value infinity,
        compute the syzygy matrix
      * *note SyzygyRows: syz_lpMatrix_rp, => ..., default value infinity,
        compute the syzygy matrix
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, the matrix of syzygies among the columns of h

Description
===========

Warning: the result may be zero if syzygies were not to be retained during the
calculation, or if the computation was not continued to a high enough degree.

The matrix of syzygies is returned without removing non-minimal syzygies.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..g];                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal"ab2-c3,abc-def,ade-bfg"              |
|                                                    |
|               2    3                               |
|o2 = ideal (a*b  - c , a*b*c - d*e*f, a*d*e - b*f*g)|
|                                                    |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : G = gb(I, Syzygies=>true);                     |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : syz G                                          |
|                                                    |
|o4 = {3} | -abc+def 0        -ade+bfg -d2e2f+b2cfg ||
|     {3} | ab2-c3   -ade+bfg 0        c3de-b3fg    ||
|     {3} | 0        abc-def  ab2-c3   -bc4+b2def   ||
|                                                    |
|             3      4                               |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                                |
+----------------------------------------------------+
There appear to be 4 syzygies, but the last one is a combination of the first
three:
+---------------------------------------+
|i5 : syz gens I                        |
|                                       |
|o5 = {3} | -abc+def 0        -ade+bfg ||
|     {3} | ab2-c3   -ade+bfg 0        ||
|     {3} | 0        abc-def  ab2-c3   ||
|                                       |
|             3      3                  |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R                   |
+---------------------------------------+
|i6 : mingens image syz G               |
|                                       |
|o6 = {3} | -abc+def 0        -ade+bfg ||
|     {3} | ab2-c3   -ade+bfg 0        ||
|     {3} | 0        abc-def  ab2-c3   ||
|                                       |
|             3      3                  |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R                   |
