"F4" is given for the Strategy, then experimental code (written by Bjarke Roune
and M. Stillman) is used. The plan is for this to become the default version
for Gröbner bases in later versions of Macaulay2.  But for now, it is
experimental.

These strategies only work for ideals in polynomial rings over a finite field
ZZ/p. In other cases, either an error will be given, or the current default
Gröbner basis algorithm will be used.

