forceGB(...,ChangeMatrix=>...) -- specify the change of basis matrix from a Gröbner basis to the generators of a module
***********************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        forceGB(...,ChangeMatrix=>m)
  * Inputs:
      * m, a *note matrix: Matrix,
  * Consequences:
      * Set the change of basis matrix from the Gröbner basis to the original
        generators

Description
===========

The matrix m should have size a by b, where a is the number of columns of the
original matrix, and b is the number of columns of f.
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : gbTrace = 3                                 |
|                                                 |
|o1 = 3                                           |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = ZZ[x,y,z];                              |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = matrix{{x^2-3, y^3-1, z^4-2}};          |
|                                                 |
|             1      3                            |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                             |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : g = forceGB(f, ChangeMatrix=>id_(source f));|
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : x^2*y^3 // g                                |
|                                                 |
|o5 = {2} | y3 |                                  |
|     {3} | 3  |                                  |
|     {4} | 0  |                                  |
|                                                 |
|             3      1                            |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R                             |
+-------------------------------------------------+

