forceGB(...,SyzygyMatrix=>...) -- specify the syzygy matrix
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        forceGB(f,SyzygyMatrix=>z,...)
  * Inputs:
      * z, a *note matrix: Matrix,
  * Consequences:
      * A request for the syzygy matrix of f will return z

Description
===========

In the following example, the only computation being performed when asked to
compute the *note kernel: kernel, or *note syz: syz, of f is the minimal
generator matrix of z.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : gbTrace = 3                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = 3                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = ZZ[x,y,z];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = matrix{{x^2-3, y^3-1, z^4-2}};                                      |
|                                                                             |
|             1      3                                                        |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : z = koszul(2,f)                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {2} | -y3+1 -z4+2 0     |                                               |
|     {3} | x2-3  0     -z4+2 |                                               |
|     {4} | 0     x2-3  y3-1  |                                               |
|                                                                             |
|             3      3                                                        |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : g = forceGB(f, SyzygyMatrix=>z);                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : syz g -- no extra computation                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {2} | -y3+1 -z4+2 0     |                                               |
|     {3} | x2-3  0     -z4+2 |                                               |
|     {4} | 0     x2-3  y3-1  |                                               |
|                                                                             |
|             3      3                                                        |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : syz f                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|   -- registering gb 0 at 0x7f2128f3b540                                     |
|                                                                             |
|   -- [gb]{2}(1)m{3}(1)m{4}(1)m{5}(1)z{6}(1)z{7}(1)znumber of (nonminimal) gb|
|   -- number of monomials                = 9                                 |
|   -- #reduction steps = 6                                                   |
|   -- #spairs done = 6                                                       |
|   -- ncalls = 0                                                             |
|   -- nloop = 0                                                              |
|   -- nsaved = 0                                                             |
|   --                                                                        |
|o7 = {2} | -y3+1 -z4+2 0     |                                               |
|     {3} | x2-3  0     -z4+2 |                                               |
|     {4} | 0     x2-3  y3-1  |                                               |
|                                                                             |
|             3      3                                                        |
|o7 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|elements = 3                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : kernel f                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = image {2} | -y3+1 -z4+2 0     |                                         |
|           {3} | x2-3  0     -z4+2 |                                         |
|           {4} | 0     x2-3  y3-1  |                                         |
|                                                                             |
|                             3                                               |
|o8 : R-module, submodule of R                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
If you know that the columns of z already form a set of minimal generators,
then one may use *note forceGB: forceGB, once again.

Caveat
======

If the columns of z do not generate the syzygy module of f, nonsensical answers
may result

