hilbertSeries -- compute the Hilbert series
*******************************************

Description
===========

The Hilbert series is the formal power series in the variables of the degrees
ring whose coefficients are the dimensions of the corresponding graded
component.Note that the series is provided as a type of expression called a
*note Divide: Divide,.

See also
========

  * *note degreesRing: degreesRing, -- the ring or monoid of degrees
  * *note reduceHilbert: reduceHilbert, -- reduce a Hilbert series expression
  * *note poincare: poincare, -- assemble degrees of a ring, module, or ideal
    into a polynomial
  * poincareN (missing documentation)
  * *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial, -- compute the Hilbert
    polynomial
  * *note hilbertFunction: hilbertFunction, -- the Hilbert function
* Menu:

* hilbertSeries(...,Order=>...): hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOrder=>_pd_pd_pd_rp.  display the truncated power series expansion
* hilbertSeries(...,Reduce=>...): hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmReduce=>_pd_pd_pd_rp.  reduce the Hilbert series

Ways to use hilbertSeries:
==========================

  * "hilbertSeries(ZZ,BettiTally)" -- see *note BettiTally: BettiTally, -- the
    class of all Betti tallies
  * *note hilbertSeries(Ideal): hilbertSeries_lpIdeal_rp, -- compute the
    Hilbert series of the quotient of the ambient ring by the ideal
  * *note hilbertSeries(Module): hilbertSeries_lpModule_rp, -- compute the
    Hilbert series of the module
  * *note hilbertSeries(PolynomialRing): hilbertSeries_lpPolynomialRing_rp, --
    compute the Hilbert series of a ring
  * "hilbertSeries(QuotientRing)" -- see *note hilbertSeries(PolynomialRing):
    hilbertSeries_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- compute the Hilbert series of a ring
  * *note hilbertSeries(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial):
    hilbertSeries_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp, -- compute the Hilbert
    series of a projective Hilbert polynomial

For the programmer
==================

The object *note hilbertSeries: hilbertSeries, is a *note method function with
options: MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

