hilbertPolynomial -- compute the Hilbert polynomial
***************************************************

Description
===========

In a singly graded ambient ring, the *note Hilbert function: hilbertFunction,
eventually is a polynomial called the Hilbert polynomial. By default this
polynomial is written in terms of the Hilbert polynomials of projective spaces
because it is a good form for extracting geometric information from the
polynomial. The Hilbert polynomial of P^i is z |--> binomial(z + i, i).

See also
========

  * *note degreesRing: degreesRing, -- the ring or monoid of degrees
  * *note reduceHilbert: reduceHilbert, -- reduce a Hilbert series expression
  * *note poincare: poincare, -- assemble degrees of a ring, module, or ideal
    into a polynomial
  * poincareN (missing documentation)
  * *note hilbertSeries: hilbertSeries, -- compute the Hilbert series
  * *note hilbertFunction: hilbertFunction, -- the Hilbert function
* Menu:

* hilbertPolynomial(...,Projective=>...): hilbertPolynomial_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmProjective=>_pd_pd_pd_rp.  choose how to display the Hilbert polynomial
* ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial::  the class of all Hilbert polynomials
* projectiveHilbertPolynomial::  Hilbert polynomial of projective space

Ways to use hilbertPolynomial:
==============================

  * "hilbertPolynomial(ZZ,BettiTally)" -- see *note BettiTally: BettiTally, --
    the class of all Betti tallies
  * *note hilbertPolynomial(Ideal): hilbertPolynomial_lpIdeal_rp, -- compute
    the Hilbert polynomial of the quotient of the ambient ring by the ideal
  * *note hilbertPolynomial(Module): hilbertPolynomial_lpModule_rp, -- compute
    the Hilbert polynomial of the module
  * *note hilbertPolynomial(Ring): hilbertPolynomial_lpRing_rp, -- compute the
    Hilbert polynomial of the ring

For the programmer
==================

The object *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial, is a *note method
function with options: MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

