ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial -- the class of all Hilbert polynomials
*******************************************************************

Description
===========

For convenience, these polynomials are expressed in terms of the Hilbert
polynomials of projective space.


The functions *note degree: degree, and *note dim: dim, are designed so they
correspond the degree and dimension of the algebraic variety that may have been
used to produce the Hilbert polynomial.
+-------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Z = Proj(QQ[x_0..x_12]/(x_0^3+x_12^3))|
|                                           |
|o1 = Z                                     |
|                                           |
|o1 : ProjectiveVariety                     |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i2 : hilbertPolynomial Z                   |
|                                           |
|o2 = P  - 3*P   + 3*P                      |
|      9      10      11                    |
|                                           |
|o2 : ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial           |
+-------------------------------------------+
* Menu:

* ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial ZZ::  value of polynomial
* degree(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial): degree_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp.
* dim(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial): dim_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp.  the degree of the Hilbert polynomial
* euler(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial): euler_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp.  constant term of the Hilbert polynomial
* hilbertSeries(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial): hilbertSeries_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp.  compute the Hilbert series of a projective Hilbert polynomial

Functions and methods returning a projective Hilbert polynomial:
================================================================

  * "ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial * ZZ" -- see *note *: _st, -- a binary
    operator, usually used for multiplication
  * "ZZ * ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial" -- see *note *: _st, -- a binary
    operator, usually used for multiplication
  * *note diff(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial):
    diff_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp,
  * *note diff(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial,ZZ):
    diff_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_cmZZ_rp,
  * *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial, -- compute the Hilbert
    polynomial
  * *note projectiveHilbertPolynomial: projectiveHilbertPolynomial, -- Hilbert
    polynomial of projective space

Methods that use a projective Hilbert polynomial:
=================================================

