degree(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial)
***********************************

  * Function: *note degree: degree,
  * Usage: 
        degree f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note projective Hilbert polynomial: ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial,,
        usually returned via *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,, the degree of any graded module having this
        Hilbert polynomial

Description
===========

This degree is obtained from the Hilbert polynomial f as follows: if f = d
z^e/e! + lower terms in z, then d is returned. This is the lead coefficient of
the highestP^e in the *note ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial:
ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial, display.
+--------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];              |
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^3, b^2, a*b*c);|
|                                |
|o2 : Ideal of R                 |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : F = hilbertPolynomial I    |
|                                |
|o3 = - 2*P  + 4*P               |
|          0      1              |
|                                |
|o3 : ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial|
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : degree F                   |
|                                |
|o4 = 4                          |
+--------------------------------+
The degree of this polynomial may be recovered using *note dim: dim,:
+----------+
|i5 : dim F|
|          |
|o5 = 1    |
+----------+
The dimension as a projective variety is also one less that the Krull dimension
of R/I
+--------------------------+
|i6 : (dim I - 1, degree I)|
|                          |
|o6 = (1, 4)               |
|                          |
|o6 : Sequence             |
+--------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial, -- compute the Hilbert
    polynomial

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note degree(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial):
    degree_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp,
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

