dim(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial) -- the degree of the Hilbert polynomial
************************************************************************

  * Function: *note dim: dim,
  * Usage: 
        dim P
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note projective Hilbert polynomial: ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,

Description
===========

The command *note dim: dim,is designed so that the result is the dimension of
the projective scheme that may have been used to produce the given Hilbert
polynomial.
+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : V = Proj(QQ[x_0..x_5]/(x_0^3+x_5^3))|
|                                         |
|o1 = V                                   |
|                                         |
|o1 : ProjectiveVariety                   |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : P = hilbertPolynomial V             |
|                                         |
|o2 = P  - 3*P  + 3*P                     |
|      2      3      4                    |
|                                         |
|o2 : ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial         |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : dim P                               |
|                                         |
|o3 = 4                                   |
+-----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial, -- compute the Hilbert
    polynomial
  * *note degree(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial):
    degree_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp,
  * *note euler(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial):
    euler_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp, -- constant term of the Hilbert
    polynomial

Ways to use this method:
========================

