euler(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial) -- constant term of the Hilbert polynomial
*****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note euler: euler,
  * Usage: 
        euler P
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note projective Hilbert polynomial: ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ,,  the constant term of the Hilbert polynomial

Description
===========

The command returns P(0) the constant term of P. This is also the Euler
characteristic of the sheaf of rings of a projective variety with Hilbert
polynomial P.


+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_0..x_3]                           |
|                                                |
|o1 = R                                          |
|                                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                             |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = Proj(R/monomialCurveIdeal(R, {1,3,4}));|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : P = hilbertPolynomial C                    |
|                                                |
|o3 = - 3*P  + 4*P                               |
|          0      1                              |
|                                                |
|o3 : ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial                |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : euler P                                    |
|                                                |
|o4 = 1                                          |
+------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note hilbertPolynomial: hilbertPolynomial, -- compute the Hilbert
    polynomial
  * *note eulers: eulers,
  * *note genus: genus,

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note euler(ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial):
    euler_lpProjectiveHilbertPolynomial_rp, -- constant term of the Hilbert
    polynomial
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

