Ext^ZZ(Matrix,Module) -- map between Ext modules
************************************************

  * Scripted functor: *note Ext: Ext,
  * Usage: 
        Ext^i(f,N)
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: ZZ,
      * f, a *note matrix: Matrix,, M1 --> M2
      * N, a *note module: Module,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: Matrix,, the map $Ext^i(M2,N) \rightarrow{}
        Ext^i(M1,N)$

Description
===========

If N is an ideal or ring, it is regarded as a module in the evident way.
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/32003[a..d];                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialCurveIdeal(R,{1,3,4})                 |
|                                                       |
|                        3      2     2    2    3    2  |
|o2 = ideal (b*c - a*d, c  - b*d , a*c  - b d, b  - a c)|
|                                                       |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M1 = R^1/I                                        |
|                                                       |
|o3 = cokernel | bc-ad c3-bd2 ac2-b2d b3-a2c |          |
|                                                       |
|                            1                          |
|o3 : R-module, quotient of R                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M2 = R^1/ideal(I_0,I_1)                           |
|                                                       |
|o4 = cokernel | bc-ad c3-bd2 |                         |
|                                                       |
|                            1                          |
|o4 : R-module, quotient of R                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : f = inducedMap(M1,M2)                             |
|                                                       |
|o5 = | 1 |                                             |
|                                                       |
|o5 : Matrix M1 <-- M2                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Ext^1(f,R)                                        |
|                                                       |
|o6 = 0                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o6 : Matrix 0 <-- 0                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : g = Ext^2(f,R)                                    |
|                                                       |
|o7 = {-5} | -d2 -cd c2 |                               |
|                                                       |
|o7 : Matrix                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : source g == Ext^2(M1,R)                           |
|                                                       |
|o8 = false                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : target g == Ext^2(M2,R)                           |
|                                                       |
|o9 = true                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : Ext^3(f,R)                                       |
|                                                       |
|o10 = 0                                                |
|                                                       |
|o10 : Matrix                                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note freeResolution: (Complexes)freeResolution, -- compute a free
    resolution of a module or ideal
  * *note resolution: (OldChainComplexes)resolution, -- projective resolution
  * *note Tor: Tor, -- Tor module
  * *note Hom: Hom, -- module of homomorphisms
  * *note Ext^ZZ(Module,Module): Ext^ZZ_lpModule_cmModule_rp, -- Ext module

