Schubert -- compute the Plücker ideal of a Schubert variety
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Schubert(k,n,sigma)
  * Inputs:
      * k
      * n
      * sigma, a subset of 0..n of size k+1 that indexes the Schubert variety
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing => a *note ring: Ring,, default value ZZ, the
        coefficient ring for the polynomial ring to be made
      * Variable => a *note symbol: Symbol,, default value "p", the base symbol
        for the indexed variables to be used.  The subscripts are the elements
        of subsets(n+1,k+1), converted to sequences and, if k is 0, converted
        to integers.
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: Ideal,, the ideal of the Schubert variety indexed by
        sigma

Description
===========

Given natural numbers $k \le{} n$, this routine finds the ideal of the Schubert
variety indexed by sigma in the Grassmannian of projective $k$-planes in $P^n$.

For example, the ideal of the Schubert variety indexed by $\{1,2,4\}$ in the
Grassmannian of projective planes in $P^4$ is displayed in the following
example.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : I = Schubert(2,4,{1,2,4},CoefficientRing => QQ)                         |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = ideal (p     , p     , p     , p     p      - p     p     , p     p     |
|             2,3,4   1,3,4   0,3,4   1,2,3 0,2,4    0,2,3 1,2,4   1,2,3 0,1,4|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     - p     p     , p     p      - p     p     )                            |
|        0,1,3 1,2,4   0,2,3 0,1,4    0,1,3 0,2,4                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Ideal of QQ[p     ..p     , p     , p     , p     , p     , p     , p   |
|                  0,1,2   0,1,3   0,2,3   1,2,3   0,1,4   0,2,4   1,2,4   0,3|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|  , p     , p     ]                                                          |
|,4   1,3,4   2,3,4                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = ring I;                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = res I                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|      1      6      14      16      9      2                                 |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R   <-- R   <-- R  <-- R                                  |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1      2       3       4      5                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : betti C                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|            0 1  2  3 4 5                                                    |
|o4 = total: 1 6 14 16 9 2                                                    |
|         0: 1 3  3  1 . .                                                    |
|         1: . 3 11 15 9 2                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : BettiTally                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

