Fano -- compute the ideal of a Fano scheme in the Grassmannian
**************************************************************

Description
===========

Fano scheme
===========

  * Usage: 
        Fano(k,I)
  * Inputs:
      * k, a positive integer less than r
      * I, an ideal representing a variety in projective r-space
  * Outputs:
      * the ideal of a Fano scheme in the Grassmannian
Given an ideal I representing a projective variety X in P^r, a positive integer
k<r, and optionally a ring GR with (exactly) r+1 choose k+1 variables,
representing the ambient space of the Grassmannian of k-planes in P^r, this
routine returns the ideal in GR of the Fano scheme that parametrizes the
k-planes lying on X.  If the optional third argument is not present, the
routine fabricates its own ring, and returns an ideal in it.

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        Fano(k,I,GR)
  * Inputs:
      * k, a positive integer less than r
      * I, an ideal representing a variety in projective r-space
      * GR, 
  * Outputs:
      * the ideal of a Fano scheme in the Grassmannian
Given an ideal I representing a projective variety X in P^r, a positive integer
k<r, and optionally a ring GR with (exactly) r+1 choose k+1 variables,
representing the ambient space of the Grassmannian of k-planes in P^r, this
routine returns the ideal in GR of the Fano scheme that parametrizes the
k-planes lying on X.  If the optional third argument is not present, the
routine fabricates its own ring, and returns an ideal in it.

