binomial -- binomial coefficient
********************************

  * Usage: 
        binomial(n,k)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: ZZ, or a *note ring element: RingElement,, 
      * k, an *note integer: ZZ,, must be non-negative; 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note number: Number,, the binomial coefficient, the coefficient of
        $x^k$ in $(1+x)^n$ or $n(n-1)...(n-k+1)/k!$.

Description
===========

+-------------------+
|i1 : binomial(13,6)|
|                   |
|o1 = 1716          |
+-------------------+
|i2 : binomial(-1,3)|
|                   |
|o2 = -1            |
+-------------------+

When either n or k are not *note ZZ: ZZ, objects, the *note Gamma: Gamma,
function is used, i.e., $\binom{n}{k} = \frac{\Gamma(n + 1)}{\Gamma(k +
1)\Gamma(n - k + 1)}$.

+-------------------------+
|i3 : binomial(7.5, pi)   |
|                         |
|o3 = 46.76478688243245   |
|                         |
|o3 : RR (of precision 53)|
+-------------------------+

A polynomial may also be used for n.

+-----------------------+
|i4 : R = QQ[x]         |
|                       |
|o4 = R                 |
|                       |
|o4 : PolynomialRing    |
+-----------------------+
|i5 : binomial(x + 3, 3)|
|                       |
|     1 3    2   11     |
|o5 = -x  + x  + --x + 1|
|     6           6     |
|                       |
|o5 : R                 |
+-----------------------+

Ways to use binomial:
=====================

  * "binomial(Number,Number)"
  * "binomial(RingElement,ZZ)"
  * "binomial(ZZ,ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note binomial: binomial, is a *note method function:
MethodFunction,.

