inversePermutation -- inverse permutation
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        y = inversePermutation x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note list: List,, a list of length n whose elements are the
        numbers 0, 1, 2, ..., n-1, in some order, representing the permutation
        defined by sending i to x#i
  * Outputs:
      * y, a *note list: List,, the list representing the inverse permutation
        of x

Description
===========

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : x = {1,2,3,4,5,0}         |
|                               |
|o1 = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 0}        |
|                               |
|o1 : List                      |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : y = inversePermutation x  |
|                               |
|o2 = {5, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4}        |
|                               |
|o2 : List                      |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : all(#x, i -> x#(y#i) == i)|
|                               |
|o3 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+
|i4 : all(#x, i -> y#(x#i) == i)|
|                               |
|o4 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+

We compose permutations with _; see *note VisibleList _ List: VisibleList _us
List,.

+-----------------------+
|i5 : x_x_x             |
|                       |
|o5 = {3, 4, 5, 0, 1, 2}|
|                       |
|o5 : List              |
+-----------------------+
|i6 : x_x_x_x_x_x       |
|                       |
|o6 = {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}|
|                       |
|o6 : List              |
+-----------------------+
|i7 : x_y               |
|                       |
|o7 = {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}|
|                       |
|o7 : List              |
+-----------------------+
|i8 : y_x               |
|                       |
|o8 = {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}|
|                       |
|o8 : List              |
+-----------------------+

Ways to use inversePermutation:
===============================

  * "inversePermutation(VisibleList)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note inversePermutation: inversePermutation, is a *note method
function: MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in
Macaulay2Doc/functions/permutations-doc.m2:63:0.

