random(QQ) -- get a random rational number
******************************************

  * Function: *note random: random,
  * Usage: 
        random x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note rational number: QQ,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Height: random_lpZZ_cmRing_rp, => an *note integer: ZZ,, default
        value 10, get a random homogeneous element from a graded ring
      * CoefficientRing (missing documentation) => ..., default value null, 
      * *note Density: random_lpModule_cmModule_rp, => ..., default value 1,
        get a random map of module
      * *note MaximalRank: random_lpModule_cmModule_rp, => ..., default value
        false, get a random map of module
      * *note UpperTriangular: random_lpModule_cmModule_rp, => ..., default
        value false, get a random map of module
  * Outputs:
      * a *note rational number: QQ,, randomly chosen from the interval $[0,
        x]$;

Description
===========

A random number is chosen from the uniform distribution on the interval $[0,
x]$ and then rounded (using the Farey sequence (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farey_sequence )) to the nearest rational number
with denominator bounded by the Height option.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : apply(10, i -> random(7_QQ, Height => 5))|
|                                              |
|      25  19     22  1     25  8  13  27      |
|o1 = {--, --, 2, --, -, 5, --, -, --, --}     |
|       4   4      5  5      4  5   4   5      |
|                                              |
|o1 : List                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note setRandomSeed: setRandomSeed, -- set starting point for random number
    generator

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note random(QQ): random_lpQQ_rp, -- get a random rational number
