Set - Set -- set difference
***************************

  * Operator: *note -: -,
  * Usage: 
        x - y
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note set: Set,,  or a *note list: List,
      * y, a *note set: Set,,  or a *note list: List,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note set: Set,, or a *note list: List,, consisting of those elements
        of x not in y

Description
===========

At least one of x, y must be a set, and the other may be a list.  If x is a
list, then so is the result.
+------------------------+
|i1 : set{a,b,c} - set{a}|
|                        |
|o1 = set {c, b}         |
|                        |
|o1 : Set                |
+------------------------+
|i2 : set{a,b,c} - {a}   |
|                        |
|o2 = set {c, b}         |
|                        |
|o2 : Set                |
+------------------------+
|i3 : {a,b,c} - set{a}   |
|                        |
|o3 = {b, c}             |
|                        |
|o3 : List               |
+------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Set: Set, -- the class of all sets

