sign -- sign (signum) function
******************************

  * Usage: 
        sign x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note number: Number,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: ZZ, or a *note complex number: CC,, 

Description
===========

When x is real, then this returns 1 if it is positive, -1 if it is negative,
and 0 if it is zero.

+--------------+
|i1 : sign 5   |
|              |
|o1 = 1        |
+--------------+
|i2 : sign (-3)|
|              |
|o2 = -1       |
+--------------+
|i3 : sign 0   |
|              |
|o3 = 0        |
+--------------+

If x is complex and nonzero, then this returns $x/|x|$.

+-------------------------+
|i4 : sign(-7*ii)         |
|                         |
|o4 = -ii                 |
|                         |
|o4 : CC (of precision 53)|
+-------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note sign(LieElement): (GradedLieAlgebras)sign_lpLieElement_rp, -- get the
    sign of a homogeneous element
  * *note sign(Permutation): (Permutations)sign_lpPermutation_rp, -- computes
    the sign of a permutation

Ways to use sign:
=================

  * "sign(Constant)"
  * "sign(Number)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note sign: sign, is a *note method function: MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in Macaulay2Doc/functions/sign-doc.m2:30:0.

