changes, 1.26.05
****************

  * new packages:
      * *note EliminationTemplates: (EliminationTemplates)Top,, a package by
        Manav Batavia, Cheng Chen, Wanchun / Rosie Shen, Anna Natalie
        Chlopecki, Tim Duff, Will Huang, and Aolong Li for elimination
        templates, has been added.
      * *note MacaulayPosets: (MacaulayPosets)Top,, a package by Penelope Beall
        and Yu Olivier Li for Macaulay posets, has been added.
      * *note MRDI: (MRDI)Top,, a package by Doug Torrance for serializing
        algebraic data with .mrdi files, has been added.
      * *note Padic: (Padic)Top,, a package by Doug Torrance for p-adic
        numbers, has been added.
      * *note SimplicialModules: (SimplicialModules)Top,, a package by Keller
        VandeBogert and Michael DeBellevue for working in the category of
        simplicial modules, has been added.
      * *note WittVectors: (WittVectors)Top,, a package by Anne Fayolle, Abhay
        Goel, Devlin Mallory, Eamon Quinlan-Gallego, and Teppei Takamatsu for
        computations with Witt vectors, Frobenius lifts, and
        quasi-F-splittings, has been added.
  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note ThinSincereQuivers: (ThinSincereQuivers)Top,, a
        package by Mary Barker and Patricio Gallardo for constructing flow
        polytopes and their associated quivers, has been published.
  * improved packages:
      * *note BettiCharacters: (BettiCharacters)Top, has been updated to
        version 2.6. Changes include significant optimizations of the core
        algorithm, a new option for semidirect products of finite groups acting
        on tori, and methods for hyperoctahedral groups. This version
        introduces breaking changes to the Character type, making it
        incompatible with previous versions.
      * *note CellularResolutions: (CellularResolutions)Top, has been updated
        to version 1.1 with improved documentation.
      * *note Complexes: (Complexes)Top, has been updated to version 1.0 and is
        now the default homological algebra package.  To construct a complex,
        use *note complex: (Complexes)complex_lpList_rp,, which returns a *note
        Complex: (Complexes)Complex, object.  This replaces *note chainComplex:
        (OldChainComplexes)chainComplex, and *note ChainComplex:
        (OldChainComplexes)ChainComplex,.  For the legacy behavior, the *note
        OldChainComplexes: (OldChainComplexes)Top, package is still available.
        Add HomologicalAlgebraPackage = "OldChainComplexes" to your *note
        initialization file: initialization file, to make it the default.
      * *note DGAlgebras: (DGAlgebras)Top, has been updated to version 2.0,
        introducing *note DGModule: (DGAlgebras)DGModule, and related types
        with core homological operations, adding minimal semifree DG
        resolutions, overhauling documentation of key constructors with
        examples, and expanding test coverage.
      * *note ForeignFunctions: (ForeignFunctions)Top, has been updated to
        version 0.7 with improved garbage collection of GMP and MPFR objects.
      * *note InvariantRing: (InvariantRing)Top, has been updated to version
        2.4, which includes a new algorithm for invariants of elementary
        abelian $p$-groups, as well as bugfixes and documentation improvements.
        The permutationMatrix method now takes arrays as inputs.
      * *note JSON: (JSON)Top, has been updated to version 0.6 with significant
        improvements to parsing speed thanks to the Jansson (see
        https://github.com/akheron/jansson ) library.
      * *note JSONRPC: (JSONRPC)Top, has been updated to version 0.2 with
        improved error messages.
      * *note LieAlgebraRepresentations: (LieAlgebraRepresentations)Top, has
        been updated to version 1.01, adding a dual construction for
        representations, fixing Cartan-basis inconsistencies in spin and
        half-spin matrix computations, and updating documentation to reflect a
        now-proven formula.
      * *note MatchingFields: (MatchingFields)Top, has been updated to version
        1.3 with overhauls to the internals of the main datatype, simpliyfing
        the logic and removing duplicated code.
      * *note PieriMaps: (PieriMaps)Top, has been updated to version 2.0,
        adding dual (projection-direction) Pieri and Littlewood-Richardson maps
        with point evaluators, supporting multiple basis conventions with
        conversions, and providing equivariance/well-definedness checks and
        symbolic representations of maps.
      * *note Probability: (Probability)Top, has been updated to version 0.7
        with minor updates.
      * *note RInterface: (RInterface)Top, has been updated to version 0.2,
        adding hash table-environment conversion, string-based evaluation via
        *note RValue: (RInterface)RValue,, a persistent *note RContext:
        (RInterface)RContext, for shared environments, formula construction
        with *note RObject ~ RObject: (RInterface)RObject ~ RObject,, and
        improved documentation and testing.
      * *note SchurComplexes: (SchurComplexes)Top, has been updated to version
        1.2, fixing a bug with function *note schurComplex:
        (SchurComplexes)schurComplex, keeps track of homological degree. Also,
        *note schurComplex: (SchurComplexes)schurComplex, has been updated to
        output a graded complex, based on the grading on the input complex.
      * *note SchurFunctors: (SchurFunctors)Top, has been updated to version
        1.0, adding a full Weyl-functor framework parallel to the Schur side
        (with new modules, operations, and characters), augmenting Schur-side
        utilities, fixing decomposition and predicate bugs, improving
        straightening performance, and expanding documentation.
      * *note SchurRings: (SchurRings)Top, has been updated to version 2.0,
        adding new character ring variants for symplectic, orthogonal, and
        rational GL groups (with full API support, branching/specialization
        maps, and inter-conversions), introducing a monomial-basis option with
        Kostka-based multiplication, and including minor efficiency
        improvements while preserving existing functionality.
      * *note SpecialFanoFourfolds: (SpecialFanoFourfolds)Top, has been updated
        to version 2.8, adding support for the *note
        DoublySpecialCubicFourfold:
        (SpecialFanoFourfolds)DoublySpecialCubicFourfold, class (cubic
        fourfolds in the intersection of two Hassett divisors).
      * *note SpectralSequences: (SpectralSequences)Top, has been updated to
        version 2.02 and now uses the *note Complexes: (Complexes)Top, package.
      * *note Tableaux: (Tableaux)Top, has been updated to version 0.6, merging
        the class SkewTableau into *note YoungTableau: (Tableaux)YoungTableau,
        and bringing in several features from the package *note SpechtModule:
        (SpechtModule)Top,.
      * *note TerraciniLoci: (TerraciniLoci)Top, has been updated to version
        0.5 with minor updates to citation and author info.
      * *note Visualize: (Visualize)Top, has been updated to version 1.9 and
        now uses updated versions of various JavaScript libraries.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * The *note Mutex: Mutex, class has been added to help prevent race
        conditions in multithreaded code.
      * Multiple assignment may now be used to assign to elements of mutable
        lists and hash tables and for using and installing assignment methods.
        In addition, null entries may be used on the left-hand side to skip
        assignment.  For example, if x is a mutable list and y is a mutable
        hash table, then (x#0, , y.a) = (1, 2, 3) is equivalent to x#0 = 1; y.a
        = 3, ignoring the 2.
      * The *note polylog: polylog, function has been added for computing
        polylogarithms.
      * The *note trap: trap, keyword and the except/do options to *note try:
        try, have been added for improved error handling.  In particular, it is
        now possible to "trap" an error as an *note Error: Error, object
        instead of raising it.
      * It is now possible to *note install: installMethod, a nullary
        (0-argument) method using the syntactic sugar f() := () -> ...
      * It is now possible to construct a mutable list with a specific number
        of null entries using *note new MutableList from ZZ: MutableList,.
      * The *note parse: parse, function has been added for viewing the parse
        tree of Macaulay2 code.
      * The *note norm: norm, function now supports computing $\ell^p$ norms
        for finite $p$.
      * The *note shuffle: shuffle, function has been added for shuffling lists
        and the *note randomElement: randomElement, function for selecting
        random elements from lists.  Note that *note random(List): shuffle,,
        which currently behaves like *note shuffle: shuffle,, will have its
        behavior changed to that of *note randomElement: randomElement, in a
        future release.
      * A new number type, *note CCi: CCi,, has been added for working with
        complex intervals.
  * functionality changed in a way that could break code:
      * The *note ~: ~, operator is now a binary or prefix unary operator
        instead of a postfix unary operator.  Use *note ^~: ^~, for
        sheafification.
      * The OldPolyhedra and OldToricVectorBundles packages are no longer
        distributed.  Use *note Polyhedra: (Polyhedra)Top, and *note
        ToricVectorBundles: (ToricVectorBundles)Top, instead.
      * It is no longer possible to *note promote: promote, from *note RR: RR,
        to *note QQ: QQ,.
      * Matrix multiplication now preserves degree.
      * The *note VisibleList _ List: VisibleList _us List, method for
        subsetting lists now preserves class, e.g., [1,2,3,4]_{0,1} now returns
        an *note Array: Array,, not a *note List: List,, as it did previously.
      * The NonminimalComplexes and PruneComplex packages have been removed.
        Their functionality has been moved to *note Complexes: (Complexes)Top,.
      * The resolution function (and its synonym, res) are now synonyms for
        *note freeResolution: (Complexes)freeResolution,.  The *note
        LengthLimit: LengthLimit, option is required for rings where there are
        infinite free resolutions such as quotients of polynomial rings and
        skew commutative polynomial rings.  Also, Strategy => Nonminimal
        replaces FastNonminimal => true.
