changes, 1.25.11
****************

  * upcoming breaking changes:
      * Beginning in the 1.26.05 release, current routines involving chain
        complexes and graded modules will be superseded by new functorial
        homological algebra routines in the *note Complexes: (Complexes)Top,
        package. Users and package developers are encouraged to preview the
        upcoming changes by adding HomologicalAlgebraPackage = "Complexes" to
        their *note initialization file: initialization file, and reporting any
        bugs via email or GitHub (see
        https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/issues/3778 ).
  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note ExteriorExtensions: (ExteriorExtensions)Top,, a
        package by Luke Oeding for building an algebra extending an exterior
        algebra, has been published.
      * a gold star *note MatrixSchubert: (MatrixSchubert)Top,, a package by
        Ayah Almousa, Sean Grate, Daoji Huang, Patricia Klein, Adam LaClair,
        Yuyuan Luo, and Joseph McDonough for functions for investigating ASM
        and matrix Schubert varieties, has been published.
      * a gold star *note MultigradedBGG: (MultigradedBGG)Top,, a package by
        Maya Banks, Michael K. Brown, Tara Gomes, Prashanth Sridhar, Eduardo
        Torres Davila, and Sasha Zotine for the multigraded BGG correspondence
        and differential modules, has been published.
  * new packages:
      * *note CpMackeyFunctors: (CpMackeyFunctors)Top,, a package by Thomas
        Brazelton, David Chan, Benjamin Mudrak, Ben Spitz, Chase Vogeli,
        Chenglu Wang, Michael R. Zeng, and Sasha Zotine for homological algebra
        with Mackey functors for cyclic groups of prime order, has been added.
      * *note ExteriorExtensions: (ExteriorExtensions)Top,, a package by Luke
        Oeding for building an algebra extending an exterior algebra, has been
        added.
      * *note JSONRPC: (JSONRPC)Top,, a package by Doug Torrance for
        implementing JSON-RPC servers, has been added.
      * *note MatrixFactorizations: (MatrixFactorizations)Top,, a package by
        David Favero, Sasha Pevzner, Timothy Tribone, and Keller VandeBogert
        for computing with matrix factorizations of different lengths, has been
        added.
      * *note NonPrincipalTestIdeals: (NonPrincipalTestIdeals)Top,, a package
        by Trung Chau, Karl Schwede, and Hunter Simper for singularities of
        pairs with non-principal ideals, has been added.
      * *note PathSignatures: (PathSignatures)Top,, a package by Felix Lotter,
        Oriol Reig, Angelo El Saliby, and Carlos Amendola for working with
        algebraic path signatures, has been added.
      * *note Tableaux: (Tableaux)Top,, a package by John Graf for constructing
        skew tableaux, has been added.
  * improved packages:
      * *note A1BrouwerDegrees: (A1BrouwerDegrees)Top, has been updated to
        version 2.0, with significant updates.
      * *note CharacteristicClasses: (CharacteristicClasses)Top, has been
        updated to version 2.1, with a new method to compute the Euler
        characteristic of a complex affine variety.
      * *note ForeignFunctions: (ForeignFunctions)Top, has been updated to
        version 0.6.
      * *note GeometricDecomposability: (GeometricDecomposability)Top, has been
        updated to version 1.4.3, adding aliases for methods with long names.
      * *note JSON: (JSON)Top, has been updated to version 0.5.
      * *note LieAlgebraRepresentations: (LieAlgebraRepresentations)Top,
        (formerly LieTypes) has been updated to version 1.0 with a major
        expansion.
      * *note Msolve: (Msolve)Top, has been updated to version 1.24.06, fixing
        a bug in *note msolveRUR: (Msolve)msolveRUR,.
      * *note MultigradedImplicitization: (MultigradedImplicitization)Top, has
        been updated to version 1.1, with an option to use interpolation to
        compute polynomials in multigraded components and changes to speed up
        multidegree and basis computation.
      * *note PolyominoIdeals: (PolyominoIdeals)Top, has been updated to
        version 2.0, including some functions that help with computations for
        collection of cells.
      * *note Probability: (Probability)Top, has been updated to version 0.6.
      * *note Python: (Python)Top, has been updated to version 1.0 with
        significant updates, including the new *note PythonContext:
        (Python)PythonContext, class and the method *note pythonRunScript:
        (Python)pythonRunScript,.
      * *note SCMAlgebras: (SCMAlgebras)Top, has been updated to version 1.1,
        adding new methods.  It can now compute the unmixed layer of an ideal,
        check for unmixedness, and check for canonical Cohen-Macaulayness.
      * *note SRdeformations: (SRdeformations)Top, has been updated to version
        0.53, using *note Polyhedra: (Polyhedra)Top, instead of OldPolyhedra.
      * *note TerraciniLoci: (TerraciniLoci)Top, has been updated to version
        0.4.
      * *note ToricHigherDirectImages: (ToricHigherDirectImages)Top, has been
        updated to version 1.1, fixing unexpected behavior from the output of
        *note HDI: (ToricHigherDirectImages)HDI,.
      * *note ToricTopology: (ToricTopology)Top, has been updated to version
        1.1, adding a new class *note MomentAngleComplex:
        (ToricTopology)MomentAngleComplex, and associated methods to compute
        equivariant cohomology, Betti numbers, and Euler characteristic, as
        well as minor fixes to the rest of the package.
      * *note VectorGraphics: (VectorGraphics)Top, has been updated to version
        1.1.1 with a bug fix and assorted minor changes.
      * *note VersalDeformations: (VersalDeformations)Top, has been updated to
        version 4.0, adding functionality for dealing with deformations of
        pairs of schemes or modules.
      * *note Visualize: (Visualize)Top, has been updated to version 1.8 with
        updates to the Javascript code.
      * *note WhitneyStratifications: (WhitneyStratifications)Top, has been
        updated to version 2.23, with several new methods to compute Whitney
        stratifications using polar varieties and to compute the Euler
        characteristic of the complex link and the local Euler obstruction
        using Whitney stratification.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * The method *note set(HashTable): set, has been added to create a set
        from the keys of a hash table.
      * The method *note toList(Tally): toList, has been added as a synonym for
        *note elements(Tally): elements,.
      * A new *note IFRAME: (Text)IFRAME, class has been added for using
        <iframe> tags in html.
      * Package authors may now add tests as individual files in the tests
        subdirectory of the package auxiliary directory without the need to use
        the *note TEST: TEST, keyword.  See *note check: check,.
      * A warning message is now displayed when reloading a package reminding
        users to recreate instances of any types from that package.
      * Negative numbers may now be used when getting matrices entries,
        creating submatrices, and getting ring variables to count backwards
        from the end.  For example, A_{-1} will return the last column of the
        matrix A.
      * The method *note sqrt(ZZ,ZZ): sqrt_lpZZ_cmZZ_rp, has been added for
        computing square roots in finite prime fields.
      * The method *note pfaffian: pfaffian, has been added for computing the
        pfaffian of a skew-symmetric matrix.
      * A new binary operator, *note @@?: @@?,, has been added.
  * functionality changed in a way that could break code:
      * The package LieTypes has been renamed as *note
        LieAlgebraRepresentations: (LieAlgebraRepresentations)Top,.
      * An error is now raised if a function parameter list contains a
        duplicate symbol.
      * Examples in package documentation are now generated using *note
        capture: capture,.  This speeds up installation considerably, but
        unexpected results may occur if, for example, one example sets a global
        variable that affects the behavior of another example.  To restore the
        old behavior of generating the example is a new M2 process, add the
        comment -* no-capture-flag *- to the example.
