changes, 1.25.05
****************

  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note AbstractSimplicialComplexes:
        (AbstractSimplicialComplexes)Top,, a package by Nathan Grieve for
        abstract simplicial complexes, has been published.
      * a gold star *note ForeignFunctions: (ForeignFunctions)Top,, a package
        by Doug Torrance providing a foreign function interface, has been
        published.
      * a gold star *note RealRoots: (RealRoots)Top,, a package by Jordy Lopez
        Garcia, Kelly Maluccio, Frank Sottile, and Thomas Yahl for symbolically
        exploring, counting, and locating real solutions to general polynomial
        systems, has been published.
  * new packages:
      * The package *note OldChainComplexes: (OldChainComplexes)Top, has been
        added to preserve the existing functionality of chain complexes, graded
        modules, and resolutions for backwards compatibility.
      * *note AllMarkovBases: (AllMarkovBases)Top,, a package by Alexander
        Milner and Oliver Clarke for computing all minimal Markov bases of a
        configuration matrix, has been added.
      * *note Brackets: (Brackets)Top,, a package by Dalton Bidleman, Tim Duff,
        Jack Kendrick, and Michael Zeng for brackets, Grassmann-Cayley
        algebras, and projective geometry, has been added.
      * *note ConnectionMatrices: (ConnectionMatrices)Top,, a package by Paul
        Goerlach, Joris Koefler, Mahrud Sayrafi, Anna-Laura Sattelberger,
        Hendrik Schroeder, Nicolas Weiss, and Francesca Zaffalon for connection
        matrices and integrable systems from D-ideals, has been added.
      * *note GameTheory: (GameTheory)Top,, a package by Erin Connelly,
        Vincenzo Galgano, Zhuang He, Lars Kastner, Giacomo Maletto, Elke
        Neuhaus, Irem Portakal, Hannah Tillmann-Morris, and Chenyang Zhao for
        computing equilibria in game theory, has been added.
      * *note IncidenceCorrespondenceCohomology:
        (IncidenceCorrespondenceCohomology)Top,, a package by Annet Kyomuhangi,
        Emanuela Marangone, Claudiu Raicu, and Ethan Reed for cohomology on the
        incidence correspondence, bundles of principal parts, and Lefschetz
        properties, has been added.
      * *note IntegerProgramming: (IntegerProgramming)Top,, a package by Mike
        Cummings for solving integer programs with Gröbner bases, has been
        added.
      * *note Oscillators: (Oscillators)Top,, a package by John Cobb, Hal
        Schenck, and Michael E. Stillman for analyzing graph oscillators, has
        been added.
      * *note ToricHigherDirectImages: (ToricHigherDirectImages)Top,, a package
        by Sasha Zotine for computations involving pushforwards and higher
        direct images of toric maps, has been added.
  * improved packages:
      * *note AbstractSimplicialComplexes: (AbstractSimplicialComplexes)Top,
        has been updated to version 1.1 with cosmetic updates.
      * *note ForeignFunctions: (ForeignFunctions)Top, has been updated to
        version 0.5.
      * *note GeometricDecomposability: (GeometricDecomposability)Top, has been
        updated to version 1.4.2 with minor updates.
      * *note JSON: (JSON)Top, has been updated to version 0.4.
      * *note LieTypes: (LieAlgebraRepresentations)Top, has been updated to
        version 0.9 with various improvements.
      * *note MatrixSchubert: (MatrixSchubert)Top, has been updated to version
        1.2 with a bug fix and documentation improvements.
      * *note MultigradedBGG: (MultigradedBGG)Top, has been updated to version
        1.2 with documentation improvements.
      * *note Permutations: (Permutations)Top, has been updated to version 1.1,
        adding several new methods.
      * *note RealRoots: (RealRoots)Top, has been updated to version 1.1.
      * *note Style: (Style)Top, has been updated to version 1.1 and now
        exports a *note generateGrammar: (Style)generateGrammar, method for
        generating grammars for syntax highlighting.
      * *note TerraciniLoci: (TerraciniLoci)Top, has been updated to version
        0.3.
      * *note ThinSincereQuivers: (ThinSincereQuivers)Top, has been updated to
        version 0.1 with expanded documentation, fixed typos, and functionality
        added.
      * *note ToricVectorBundles: (ToricVectorBundles)Top, has been updated to
        version 1.3 with a bug fix.
      * *note Varieties: (Varieties)Top, has been updated to version 0.3.
      * *note Visualize: (Visualize)Top, has been updated to version 1.7.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * The profiler has been updated significantly.  *note profile: profile,
        is now a keyword that will accept any Macaulay2 code.  Run *note
        profileSummary: profile, or *note coverageSummary: profile, to view the
        profiling results.
      * The *note random(QQ): random_lpQQ_rp, method has been added.
      * *note gcd: gcd, and *note lcm: lcm, now accept a single argument.
      * *note Vector: Vector, objects belonging to modules of rank 1 may now be
        added, subtracted, and tested for equality with elements from their
        underlying rings.
      * *note pairs: pairs, will now accept any instance of class for which an
        *note iterator: iterator, method is installed.
      * *note applyPairs: applyPairs,, *note scanPairs: scanPairs,, and *note
        selectPairs: selectPairs, will now accept any object that works with
        *note pairs: pairs,.
      * *note vector: vector, now accepts a ring as its first argument for
        constructing elements of free modules.
      * *note format: format, now escapes all control characters in a string.
      * It is now possible to write new ... from methods that accept 2 or 3
        arguments.  See *note new: new,.
      * intersection is now a synonym for *note intersect: intersect,.
      * *note directProduct: directProduct,, formerly exported by *note
        Polyhedra: (Polyhedra)Top,, has been moved to Core and now accepts any
        positive number of arguments.
      * The *note sign: sign, method has been added.
      * Package documentation pages now display BibTeX citation information,
        provided by *note cite: (PackageCitations)cite,.
      * There now exists a *note Citation: Citation, documentation keyword for
        overriding the default package citation information provided by *note
        cite: (PackageCitations)cite,.
      * There are now several additional *note round: round, methods.
      * *note needsPackage: needsPackage, will now reload a package if its
        source has been modified since the last time it was loaded.
      * Several new *note check: check, methods have been added.
      * *note randomSubset: randomSubset, has been added for generating random
        subsets of lists and sets.
  * functionality changed in a way that could break code:
      * The package Divisor has been renamed as *note WeilDivisors:
        (WeilDivisors)Top,.
      * The method *note isIsomorphic: (Isomorphism)isIsomorphic, now only
        returns true or false. To retrieved the computed isomorphism, use the
        method *note isomorphism: (Isomorphism)isomorphism,.
      * The method *note Matrix \\ Matrix: quotient', is now a shortcut for
        *note quotient'(Matrix,Matrix): quotient',. The previous functionality
        is still available via *note Matrix // Matrix:
        quotient_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_rp,, which is a shortcut for *note
        quotient(Matrix,Matrix): quotient_lpMatrix_cmMatrix_rp,. Additionally,
        both methods now work for maps of non-free modules.
      * *note leadTerm(Ideal): leadTerm_lpIdeal_rp, now returns an ideal
        instead of a matrix.
      * *note gcdCoefficients: gcdCoefficients, now returns a sequence instead
        of a list.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

