changes, 1.24.11
****************

  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note A1BrouwerDegrees: (A1BrouwerDegrees)Top,, a package
        by Nikita Borisov, Thomas Brazelton, Frenly Espino, Tom Hagedorn,
        Zhaobo Han, Jordy Lopez Garcia, Joel Louwsma, Wern Juin Gabriel Ong,
        and Andrew Tawfeek for A1-Brouwer degree computations, has been
        published.
      * a gold star *note SpecialFanoFourfolds: (SpecialFanoFourfolds)Top,, a
        package by Giovanni Staglianò for Hodge-special fourfolds, has been
        published.
      * a gold star *note SubalgebraBases: (SubalgebraBases)Top,, a package by
        Michael Burr, Oliver Clarke, Timothy Duff, Jackson Leaman, Nathan
        Nichols, and Elise Walker for Canonical subalgebra bases (aka
        SAGBI/Khovanskii bases), has been published.
  * new packages: 
      * *note AbstractSimplicialComplexes: (AbstractSimplicialComplexes)Top,, a
        package by Nathan Grieve for abstract simplicial complexes, has been
        added.
      * *note Msolve: (Msolve)Top,, a package by Martin Helmer, Mike Stillman,
        and Anton Leykin for interfacing with the msolve library for solving
        multivariate polynomial systems using Gröbner Bases, has been added.
      * *note MultigradedImplicitization: (MultigradedImplicitization)Top,, a
        package by Joseph Cummings and Benjamin Hollering for solving
        implicitization problems using multigradings, has been added.
      * *note NumericalSemigroups: (NumericalSemigroups)Top,, a package by
        David Eisenbud and Frank-Olaf Schreyer for computing the Apery set and
        invariants of a numerical semigroup ring, has been added.
      * *note Permutations: (Permutations)Top,, a package by Sean Grate for
        functions for working with permutations, has been added.
      * *note SCMAlgebras: (SCMAlgebras)Top,, a package by Ernesto Lax for
        sequentially Cohen-Macaulay modules or ideals, has been added.
  * improved packages:
      * *note A1BrouwerDegrees: (A1BrouwerDegrees)Top, has been updated to
        version 1.1 with bug fixes and improved documentation.
      * *note AssociativeAlgebras: (AssociativeAlgebras)Top, has been updated
        to version 0.9 with new functions related to derivation-quotient
        algebras, superpotentials, and Nakayama automorphisms of m-Koszul
        Artin-Schelter regular algebras.
      * *note ForeignFunctions: (ForeignFunctions)Top, has been updated to
        version 0.4 with improved documentation.
      * *note Jets: (Jets)Top, has been updated to version 1.2 with
        improvements and new methods for principal jets.
      * *note LieTypes: (LieAlgebraRepresentations)Top, has been updated to
        version 0.82 with bug fixes, improved documentation, and a new method,
        *note zeroModule: (LieAlgebraRepresentations)zeroModule,.
      * *note PositivityToricBundles: (PositivityToricBundles)Top, has been
        updated to version 1.9 with bug fixes and a new method, *note
        wellformedBundleFiltrations:
        (PositivityToricBundles)wellformedBundleFiltrations,.
      * *note Probability: (Probability)Top, has been updated to version 0.5
        with improved documentation.
      * *note Seminormalization: (Seminormalization)Top, has been updated to
        version 0.22 with several improvements.
      * *note TerraciniLoci: (TerraciniLoci)Top, has been updated to version
        0.2 with minor updates.
      * *note Triangulations: (Triangulations)Top, has been updated to version
        0.2 with a bug fix.
      * *note VectorGraphics: (VectorGraphics)Top, has been updated to version
        1.1 with several improvements.
      * *note Visualize: (Visualize)Top, has been updated to version 1.6 with
        improvements to the JavaScript code.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * A new function *note headlines: headlines, is now available for viewing
        a table of documentation headlines from a list produced by *note
        methods: methods,, *note about: about,, or *note apropos: apropos,.
      * It is now possible to construct an empty matrix by passing an empty
        list to *note matrix: matrix,.
      * *note LUdecomposition: LUdecomposition, now supports empty real and
        complex matrices.
      * The *note version: version, hash table now contains a "git branch" key.
      * The version number displayed in the startup banner now includes git
        information.
      * *note copyright: Copyright and license, is now a command that displays
        the *note Copyright and license: Copyright and license, documentation.
      * A number of improvements have been made to methods dealing with *note
        MonomialIdeal: MonomialIdeal, objects.
      * The function *note remove: remove,, which previously had no return
        value, now returns the value that was removed.
      * The function *note changeDirectory: changeDirectory,, for changing the
        working directory, has been added.
      * Many numerical functions that previously did not accept *note CC: CC,
        or *note RRi: RRi, arguments now do.
      * The functions *note selectKeys: selectKeys,, *note selectValues:
        selectValues,, and *note selectPairs: selectPairs, for selecting from
        hash tables have been added.
      * It is now possible to edit the list of packages that are loaded when
        Macaulay2 starts up by modifying the list Core#"preloaded packages" in
        init.m2.
      * The classes *note Constant: Constant,, *note InfiniteNumber:
        InfiniteNumber, and *note IndeterminateNumber: IndeterminateNumber, are
        now all subclasses of *note Number: Number,.
      * Hash codes are now unsigned 64-bit integers, vastly reducing the
        probability of running out when creating new types.
      * It is now possible to compare *note GroebnerBasis: GroebnerBasis,
        objects using *note ==: ==,.
      * Items in the "ways to use" section of documentation pages are now
        formatted using *note KBD: (Text)KBD,.
      * It is now possible to use *note try: try, with *note then: if,, but
        without *note else: if,.
      * When running Macaulay2 without the --no-readline option, command
        history is now saved between sessions.  This history can be found in
        the file history.m2 in the *note applicationDirectory:
        applicationDirectory,.
      * The error message is now more informative when a key is not found in a
        hash table.
      * New methods for scalar division, e.g., *note Matrix / Number: Matrix /
        Number, have been added.
      * The restriction on promotion/lifting has been relaxed so one can
        promote/lift between any two rings, and apply this to fraction fields
        and tensor products.
  * functionality changed in a way that could break code:
      * The behavior of *note basis: basis, over tower rings has changed.
        Previously basis was computed over the most recent coefficient ring,
        but now it is computed over the first coefficient ring. Previous
        behavior can be mimicked by passing the option basis(..., Variables =>
        gens R).
      * Testing equality of zero modules using *note ==: ==, so that two zero
        modules are equal if they are equal as cosets.  The only implication is
        that zero submodules of any free module are now the same, but zero
        submodules of arbitrary modules are only the same if they have the same
        ambient module.
      * The syntactic sugar T OP= f for *note installing augmented assignment
        methods: installing augmented assignment methods, has been removed.
      * *note TEST: TEST, is now a keyword instead of a method function.  It
        functionality remains essentially unchanged.  However, its *note
        FileName: FileName, option has been removed.  Use TEST get(...) instead
        when storing the code for a test in a file.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

