changes, 1.24.05
****************

  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note CotangentSchubert: (CotangentSchubert)Top,, a package
        by Paul Zinn-Justin for Cotangent Schubert calculus, has been
        published.
      * a gold star *note GeometricDecomposability:
        (GeometricDecomposability)Top,, a package by Mike Cummings and Adam Van
        Tuyl to check whether ideals are geometrically vertex decomposable, has
        been published.
      * a gold star *note InvariantRing: (InvariantRing)Top,, a package by
        Luigi Ferraro, Federico Galetto, Francesca Gandini, Hang Huang, Thomas
        Hawes, Matthew Mastroeni, and Xianglong Ni for invariants of group
        actions, has been published.
      * a gold star *note MultiplicitySequence: (MultiplicitySequence)Top,, a
        package by Justin Chen, Youngsu Kim, and Jonathan Montaño for computing
        the multiplicity sequence of an ideal, has been published.
      * a gold star *note Probability: (Probability)Top,, a package by Doug
        Torrance for basic probability functions, has been published.
      * a gold star *note TropicalToric: (TropicalToric)Top,, a package by
        Alessio Borzì on tropical methods for toric intersection theory, has
        been published.
  * new packages:
      * *note MultigradedBGG: (MultigradedBGG)Top,, a package by Maya Banks,
        Michael K. Brown, Tara Gomes, Prashanth Sridhar, Eduardo Torres Davila,
        and Sasha    Zotine for the multigraded BGG correspondence and
        differential modules, has been added.
      * *note TropicalToric: (TropicalToric)Top,, a package by Alessio Borzì on
        tropical methods for toric intersection theory, has been added.
      * *note VNumber: (VNumber)Top,, a package by Antonino Ficarra and
        Emanuele Sgroi to compute v-number of homogeneous ideals and v-function
        of monomial ideals, has been added.
  * improved packages:
      * Many *note FourTiTwo: (FourTiTwo)Top, methods now have a *note
        Precision: Precision, option for setting the integer precision used by
        4ti2.
      * *note GeometricDecomposability: (GeometricDecomposability)Top, has been
        updated to version 1.4.1 with minor updates.
      * *note NumericalAlgebraicGeometry: (NumericalAlgebraicGeometry)Top, has
        been updated to version 1.24 with small updates.
      * *note PositivityToricBundles: (PositivityToricBundles)Top, has been
        updated to version 1.7, adding several new methods, fixing bugs, and
        updating the documentation and tests.
      * *note ToricVectorBundles: (ToricVectorBundles)Top, has been updated to
        version 1.2 with updated documentation.
      * *note WhitneyStratifications: (WhitneyStratifications)Top, has been
        updated to version 2.03, adding new routines to stratify algebraic maps
        to the package. The update also includes several performance
        improvements and bug fixes.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * It is now possible to create a fraction field of an iterated polynomial
        ring using *note frac: frac,.
      * A number of new operators have been added that may be used for defining
        methods.  See *note ^!: ^!,, *note _!: _us!,, *note ^~: ^~,, *note _~:
        _us~,, *note ^>: ^>,, *note ^>=: ^>=,, *note ^<: ^<,, *note ^<=: ^<=,,
        *note _>: _us>,, *note _>=: _us>=,, *note _<: _us<,, *note _<=: _us<=,,
        *note |_: |_us,, and *note |_=: |_us=,.
      * A number of improvements have been made to parallelization. In
        particular:
          * The function *note getIOThreadMode: getIOThreadMode, has been added
            for determining the current I/O thread mode.
          * The functions *note setIOExclusive: setIOExclusive,, *note
            setIOSynchronized: setIOSynchronized,, and *note
            setIOUnSynchronized: setIOUnSynchronized, now also accept a file as
            an argument.
          * The default I/O thread mode has been changed from 0
            (unsynchronized) to 1 (synchronized).
          * Much of the code (e.g., reading mutable hash tables) is now thread
            safe.
          * The output of *note GCstats: GCstats, has been improved.
          * The initial heap size used by the garbage collector has been
            increased and the free space divisor has been decreased.
          * The *note taskResult: taskResult_lpTask_rp, function now waits
            until a task is finished before returning its result.
          * The *note parallelApply: parallelApply, function has been added for
            applying a function to a list in parallel.
          * The output when using the *note time: time, keyword now includes
            the time used by the current thread and in garbage collection.
          * The keyword threadVariable has been renamed to *note threadLocal:
            threadLocal,, although the former still exists as a synonym.
        See *note parallel programming with threads and tasks: parallel
        programming with threads and tasks, for more.
      * The hash counter for mutable hash tables increases much more slowly,
        decreasing the likelihood of overflowing.
      * The *note take: take, function will now accept a two-element list as
        its second element if the class of the first element has a *note
        iterator: iterator, method installed.
      * Broken links to the Journal of Software for Algebra and Geometry (see
        https://msp.org/jsag/ ) have been fixed in the documentation for older
        certified packages.
      * The documentation page for each certified package now includes its DOI.
      * The *note union: union, function has been added for sets.
      * The *note intersect: intersect, and *note intersect: intersect,
        functions now work for sets.
      * Creating integer quotient rings using ZZ/n now works when n is large
        and/or composite.
      * The syntax g \\ f as a synonym for f // g when f and g are matrices has
        been deprecated.  It will be replaced in the next release.
      * Modules may now be compared using *note <: <,, *note <=: <=,, *note >:
        >,, and *note >=: >=,, by their ranks and degrees.  In particular,
        lists of modules may now be sorted.
      * The method *note homomorphism(Vector): homomorphism, was added for
        getting the homomorphism from an element of a Hom module.
      * The method *note random(Module): random_lpList_cmModule_rp, was added
        for generating random elements of modules.
      * The method *note all(BasicList): all_lpBasicList_cmFunction_rp, was
        added for checking if all elements of a list of booleans are true.
      * The method *note position(ZZ,Function): position, was added for finding
        the smallest index for which a function returns true.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

