changes, 1.22
*************

  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note GraphicalModelsMLE: (GraphicalModelsMLE)Top,, a
        package by Carlos Amendola, Luis David Garcia Puente, Roser Homs Pons,
        Olga Kuznetsova, Harshit J Motwani, Elina Robeva, and David Swinarski,
        for maximum likelihood estimates for graphical statistical models, has
        been published.
      * a gold star *note LinearTruncations: (LinearTruncations)Top,, a package
        by Lauren Cranton Heller, David Eisenbud, and Navid Nemati for finding
        multigraded truncations that give linear resolutions, has been
        published.
      * a gold star *note RationalMaps: (RationalMaps)Top,, a package by Karl
        Schwede, Daniel Smolkin, S. Hamid Hassanzadeh, and C. J. Bott, for
        working with rational maps, has been published.
      * a gold star *note PseudomonomialPrimaryDecomposition:
        (PseudomonomialPrimaryDecomposition)Top,, a package by Alan A.
        Veliz-Cuba for primary decomposition of square free pseudomonomial
        ideals, has been published.
      * a gold star *note NoetherianOperators: (NoetherianOperators)Top,, a
        package by Robert Krone, Justin Chen, Marc Harkonen, Yairon Cid-Ruiz,
        and Anton Leykin, for numerically computing local dual spaces, Hilbert
        functions, and Noetherian operators, has been published.
      * a gold star *note Jets: (Jets)Top,, a package by Federico Galetto and
        Nicholas Iammarino, for computing jets of various algebraic, geometric
        and combinatorial objects, has been published.
  * new packages:
      * *note HolonomicSystems: (HolonomicSystems)Top,, a package by Mahrud
        Sayrafi, Christine Berkesch, Anton Leykin, and Harrison Tsai for
        holonomic systems, has been added.  The code was originally in the
        Dmodules package.
      * *note BernsteinSato: (BernsteinSato)Top,, a package by Anton Leykin and
        Harrison Tsai for Bernstein-Sato, has been added.  The code was
        originally in the Dmodules package.
      * *note PolyominoIdeals: (PolyominoIdeals)Top,, a package by Carmelo
        Cisto, Francesco Navarra, and Rizwan Jahangir for binomial ideals of
        collections of cells, has been added.
      * *note MatchingFields: (MatchingFields)Top,, a package by Oliver Clarke
        for matching fields, has been added.
      * *note CellularResolutions: (CellularResolutions)Top,, a package by Jay
        Yang and Aleksandra Sobieska for cellular resolutions of monomial
        ideals, has been added.
      * *note SagbiGbDetection: (SagbiGbDetection)Top,, a package by Viktoriia
        Borovik, Timothy Duff, and Elima Shehu for verifying whether the given
        generators of an ideal form the Gr"obner basis or whether the given
        generators of a finitely generated subalgebra of a polynomial ring are
        the SAGBI basis, has been added.
  * functionality added:
      * A *note RingMap: RingMap, object may now be raised to the 0th power if
        its *note source: source, and *note target: target, agree.
      * Matrices may now be joined with any type of number (not just integers)
        using *note |: Matrix | Matrix, and *note ||: Matrix || Matrix,.
      * The html documentation now syntax highlights Macaulay2 code by default
        using Prism (see https://prismjs.com/ ).
      * Some improvements have been made to *note findProgram: findProgram, and
        *note runProgram: runProgram,.
      * A specific test from a package may now be specified using *note
        tests(ZZ,Package): tests,.
      * The html documentation now uses the HTML5 specification.
  * functionality changed in a way that could break code:
      * The functions member and mutable have been renamed to *note isMember:
        isMember, and *note isMutable: isMutable,, respectively.  The old names
        still exist as synonyms, but they may be removed in a future release.
      * Raising a matrix to the 0th power will now raise an error if the *note
        source: source, and *note target: target, do not agree.
      * The value of a class's 1 key (used internally for getting
        multiplicative identities) should now be a function that takes an
        instance of the class and returns the multiplicative identity rather
        than the multiplicative identity itself.
      * The function *note urlEncode: urlEncode, has been moved from the *note
        OnlineLookup: (OnlineLookup)Top, package to *note Core: Core,, and its
        behavior has been slightly modified.
  * Emacs updates:
      * Several new functions have been added to for sending code to an M2
        process, and the code that is sent is now highlighted briefly as a
        visual indicator.  Refer to the "Macaulay2" dropdown menu in Emacs for
        more.
      * File locations that appear in Macaulay2 Interaction buffers are now
        handled using Compilation mode (see
        https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Compilation-
        Mode.html ).
      * Macaulay2 is now supported in Org Mode using ob-M2 (see
        https://github.com/d-torrance/ob-M2 ).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

