changes, 1.21
*************

  * new packages:
      * *note Triangulations: (Triangulations)Top,, a package by Mike Stillman
        for triangulations of polyhedra and point sets, has been added.
      * *note WhitneyStratifications: (WhitneyStratifications)Top,, a package
        by Martin Helmer for computing Whitney stratifications algebraically,
        has been added.
      * *note JSON: (JSON)Top,, a package by Doug Torrance for JSON encoding
        and decoding, has been added.
      * *note ForeignFunctions: (ForeignFunctions)Top,, a package by Doug
        Torrance for providing a foreign function interface, has been added.
      * *note GeometricDecomposability: (GeometricDecomposability)Top,, a
        package by Mike Cummings and Adam Van Tuyl for determining whether
        ideals are geometrically vertex decomposable, has been added.
      * *note PseudomonomialPrimaryDecomposition:
        (PseudomonomialPrimaryDecomposition)Top,, a package by Alan A.
        Veliz-Cuba for primary decomposition of square free pseudomonomial
        ideals, has been added.
  * improved packages:
      * The package *note BettiCharacters: (BettiCharacters)Top, has been
        updated to version 2.0, which introduces character tables,
        decompositions, and other methods for characters. The GradedCharacter
        type has been removed, and the Character type has been modified to
        accommodate both homological and internal grading in a simplified
        format.
  * functionality added:
      * New methods, *note iterator: iterator, and *note next: next,, and a new
        class, *note Iterator: Iterator, have been added to allow iteration
        over any Macaulay2 object.
      * *note for: for, loops, as well as the methods *note scan: scan,, *note
        apply: apply,, *note select: select,, *note fold: fold,, *note
        accumulate: accumulate,, *note take: take,, and *note join: join,, now
        work with any iterable object.
      * *note truncate(Number): truncate_lpNumber_rp, has been added, rounding
        numbers toward zero.
      * *note quotientRemainder(ZZ,ZZ):
        quotientRemainder_lpRingElement_cmRingElement_rp, has been added, for
        obtaining the quotient and remainder simultaneously when performing
        integer division.
      * The bitwise not operator, *note ~ ZZ: ~ ZZ, has been added.
      * A new strategy *note Dynamic: Dynamic, is implemented for *note
        determinant: determinant,, *note minors: minors_lpZZ_cmMatrix_rp,, and
        *note exteriorPower: exteriorPower,.
      * A new global variable *note blockMatrixForm: blockMatrixForm, which
        affects the display of matrices has been added.
      * Partial support for UTF-8 in strings has been added.
      * *note changeBase: changeBase, has been added for changing integer
        bases.
  * functionality changed in a way that could break code:
      * *note remove: remove, may now be used to remove elements from mutable
        lists.  Its previous (undocumented) behavior was equivalent to *note
        drop: drop,.
      * *note characters: characters, and *note width(Net): width_lpNet_rp, now
        split strings according to UTF-8 characters rather than bytes.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

