changes, 1.20
*************

  * new packages:
      * *note CotangentSchubert: (CotangentSchubert)Top,, a package by Paul
        Zinn-Justin for cotangent Schubert calculus, has been added.
      * *note OnlineLookup: (OnlineLookup)Top,, a package by Paul Zinn-Justin
        for looking up mathematical information online, has been added.
      * *note MergeTeX: (MergeTeX)Top,, a package by Paul Zinn-Justin for
        running Macaulay2 code and inserting the results into a LaTeX file, has
        been added.
      * *note Probability: (Probability)Top,, a package by Doug Torrance for
        basic probability, has been added.
      * *note Isomorphism: (Isomorphism)Top,, a package by David Eisenbud for
        probabilistic searching for isomorphisms between modules, has been
        added.
      * a gold star *note SchurVeronese: (SchurVeronese)Top,, a package by
        Juliette Bruce, Daniel Erman, Steve Goldstein and Jay Yang for
        examining data for Veronese embeddings of projective space, has been
        added and published.
      * a gold star *note CodingTheory: (CodingTheory)Top,, a package by Taylor
        Ball, Eduardo Camps, Henry Chimal-Dzul, Delio Jaramillo-Velez, Hiram H.
        Lopez, Nathan Nichols, Matthew Perkins, Ivan Soprunov, German Vera, and
        Gwyn Whieldon for coding theory, has been added and published.
  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note ThreadedGB: (ThreadedGB)Top,, a package by Sonja
        Petrovic and Shahrzad Zelenberg, for computing a Gröbner basis using
        the classical Buchberger algorithm with multiple threads, has been
        published.
      * a gold star *note MultiprojectiveVarieties:
        (MultiprojectiveVarieties)Top,, a package by Giovanni Staglianò for
        multi-projective varieties, has been published.
  * improved packages:
      * The package *note GraphicalModelsMLE: (GraphicalModelsMLE)Top, has been
        improved following many recommendations through its certification
        process. Several computations have been optimized. The names of several
        procedures and options have been modified.
      * The package *note Complexes: (Complexes)Top, has been improved.  The
        documentation has been enhanced, numerous minor bugs have been fixed,
        and free resolutions have been implemented independent of the current
        *note ChainComplex: (OldChainComplexes)ChainComplex, class.
      * The package *note HyperplaneArrangements: (HyperplaneArrangements)Top,
        has been improved.  It includes several improvements in the basic code,
        increased functionality with the Matroids package, completely rewritten
        documentation, numerous bug fixes, and better consistency with
        Macaulay2 conventions.
      * The package *note SimplicialComplexes: (SimplicialComplexes)Top, has
        been improved.  It adds constructors for many classic examples,
        implements a new data type for simplicial maps, incorporates many
        improvements to the methods, improves interoperability with *note
        Polyhedra: (Polyhedra)Top, and completely overhauls the documentation.
        Changes that break backwards compatibility include changing the output
        of faces and facets from Matrix to List, changing the output type of
        fVector from HashTable to List, and replacing == with === for
        SimplicialComplexes.
  * functionality added:
      * New functions *note memoizeValues: memoize, and *note memoizeClear:
        memoize, have been added for dealing with the values retained by
        functions created with memoize.
      * A new method *note uniquePermutations: uniquePermutations, has been
        added. Equivalent to unique @@ permutations except faster.
      * A number of unicode symbols have been added as synonyms, e.g., ℤ or ⊗.
      * New numeric functions *note Beta: Beta,, *note Digamma: Digamma,, *note
        inverseErf: inverseErf,, *note regularizedBeta: regularizedBeta,, *note
        inverseRegularizedBeta: inverseRegularizedBeta,, *note
        regularizedGamma: regularizedGamma,, and *note inverseRegularizedGamma:
        inverseRegularizedGamma,, new numeric constant *note CatalanConstant:
        CatalanConstant,.  *note Gamma: Gamma, now accepts two arguments, for
        the incomplete gamma function.  Numeric functions accept constants as
        arguments.
      * *note pack: pack,, *note reverse: reverse,, and *note tally: tally, now
        support strings.
      * *note unique: unique, now supports all visible lists.
      * Syntax highlighting of Macaulay2 code in the HTML documentation has
        been added as a build-time option.  Use *note M2CODE: (Text)M2CODE, to
        indicate code to be highlighted.
  * functionality changed in a way that could break code:
      * The update to SimplicialComplexes has several minor breaking changes,
        outlined above.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

