changes, 1.19
*************

  * new packages:
      * *note MonomialIntegerPrograms: (MonomialIntegerPrograms)Top,, a package
        by Lily Silverstein and Jay White for using integer programming for
        fast computations with monomial ideals, has been added.
      * *note ThinSincereQuivers: (ThinSincereQuivers)Top,, a package by Mary
        Barker and Patricio Gallardo for construction of flow polytopes and
        their associated quivers, has been added.
      * *note Python: (Python)Top,, a package by Daniel R. Grayson and Doug
        Torrance for an interface to Python, has been added.
      * *note BettiCharacters: (BettiCharacters)Top,, a package by Federico
        Galetto for finite group characters on free resolutions and graded
        modules, has been added.
      * *note Jets: (Jets)Top,, a package by Federico Galetto and Nicholas
        Iammarino, for computing jets of various algebraic, geometric and
        combinatorial objects, has been added.
      * *note FunctionFieldDesingularization:
        (FunctionFieldDesingularization)Top,, a package by Douglas A. Leonard
        for desingularization of function fields, has been added.
      * *note HomotopyLieAlgebra: (HomotopyLieAlgebra)Top,, a package by David
        Eisenbud for homotopy Lie algebra, has been added.
      * *note TSpreadIdeals: (TSpreadIdeals)Top,, a package by Luca Amata for
        t-spread ideals of a polynomial ring, has been added.
      * *note ExteriorModules: (ExteriorModules)Top,, a package by Luca Amata
        and Marilena Crupi for monomial modules over exterior algebras, has
        been added.
      * *note GroebnerStrata: (GroebnerStrata)Top,, a package by Kristine Jones
        and Mike Stillman for working with Gröbner families and subschemes of
        Hilbert schemes, has been added.
      * *note QuaternaryQuartics: (QuaternaryQuartics)Top,, a package by
        Kapustka, Kapustka, Ranestad, Schenck, Stillman and Yuan containing
        code and examples for their paper 'Quaternary Quartic Forms and
        Gorenstein Rings', has been added.
      * *note RealRoots: (RealRoots)Top,, a package by Jordy Lopez, Kelly
        Maluccio, Frank Sottile, and Thomas Yahl for symbolically exploring,
        counting, and locating real solutions to polynomial systems, has been
        added.
      * *note K3Surfaces: (K3Surfaces)Top,, a package by Michael Hoff and
        Giovanni Staglianò for explicit constructions of K3 surfaces, has been
        added.
  * improved packages:
      * The package *note Truncations: (Truncations)Top, has been improved to
        support modules over the Cox rings of simplicial *note normal toric
        varieties: (NormalToricVarieties)Top,.
      * The package *note MonodromySolver: (MonodromySolver)Top, includes
        several new convenience functions for manipulating systems and creating
        seed pairs.
      * The package *note Complexes: (Complexes)Top, has been improved.  The
        documentation is complete, and all methods involving Yoneda Ext and
        connecting maps have been written.  This package will soon replace the
        chain complex code from the Core.
  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note DecomposableSparseSystems:
        (DecomposableSparseSystems)Top,, a package by Taylor Brysiewicz, Jose
        Israel Rodriguez, Frank Sottile, and Thomas Yahl for solving
        decomposable sparse systems, has been published.
      * a gold star *note SparseResultants: (SparseResultants)Top,, a package
        by Giovanni Staglianò for computations with sparse resultants, has been
        published.
      * a gold star *note ExteriorModules: (ExteriorModules)Top,, a package by
        Luca Amata and Marilena Crupi for monomial modules over exterior
        algebras, has been published.
  * packages that have been renamed:
      * The package FastLinAlg has been renamed to *note FastMinors:
        (FastMinors)Top,.
      * The package RandomRationalPoints has been renamed to *note
        RandomPoints: (RandomPoints)Top,.
  * functionality added:
      * Integers may now be entered using the binary, octal, and hexadecimal
        numeral systems with the prefixes "0b", "0o", and "0x", respectively.
      * A new binary operator, *note ^^: ^^,, has been added for computing the
        bitwise XOR of two integers.  This replaces the "xor" method.
      * A new keyword, *note xor: xor,, has been added for finding the logical
        XOR of two boolean objects.
      * The function *note printerr: printerr,, for printing warning messages
        and logs to *note stderr: stderr,, is now exported.
