changes, 1.18
*************

  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note PhylogeneticTrees: (PhylogeneticTrees)Top,, a package
        by Nathaniel Bushek, Ruth Davidson, Elizabeth Gross, Pamela Harris,
        Robert Krone, Colby Long, AJ Stewart, and Robert Walker for invariants
        for group-based phylogenetic models, has been published.
      * a gold star *note GradedLieAlgebras: (GradedLieAlgebras)Top,, a package
        by Clas Löfwall and Samuel Lundqvist for computations in graded Lie
        algebras, has been published.
      * a gold star *note RelativeCanonicalResolution:
        (RelativeCanonicalResolution)Top,, a package by Christian Bopp and
        Michael Hoff for computation of the relative canonical resolution for
        g-nodal canonical curves with a fixed $g^1_k$, has been published.
      * a gold star *note FrobeniusThresholds: (FrobeniusThresholds)Top,, a
        package by Juliette Bruce, Daniel Hernández, Karl Schwede, Dan Smolkin,
        Pedro Teixeira, and Emily Witt, for calculations of F-thresholds, has
        been published.
  * new packages:
      * *note AssociativeAlgebras: (AssociativeAlgebras)Top,, a package by
        Frank Moore and Mike Stillman for noncommutative algebra, has been
        added.
      * *note RationalPoints2: (RationalPoints2)Top,, a package by Jieao Song
        for finding rational points on a variety, has been added.
      * *note SuperLinearAlgebra: (SuperLinearAlgebra)Top,, a package by
        Fereshteh Bahadorykhalily and Fatemeh Tarashi Kashani for computing
        with supermatrices, has been added.
      * *note SubalgebraBases: (SubalgebraBases)Top,, a package by Michael
        Burr, Oliver Clarke, Timothy Duff, Jackson Leaman, Nathan Nichols,
        Elise Walker, Mike Stillman, and Harrison Tsai, for computing canonical
        subalgebra bases, has been added.
      * *note AInfinity: (AInfinity)Top,, a package by David Eisenbud and Mike
        Stillman for A-infinity structures on free resolutions, has been added.
      * *note LinearTruncations: (LinearTruncations)Top,, a package by Lauren
        Cranton Heller, David Eisenbud, and Navid Nemati for finding
        multigraded truncations that give linear resolutions, has been added.
  * improved packages:
      * The package *note NumericalSchubertCalculus:
        (NumericalSchubertCalculus)Top, has been improved: several functions
        and options were added for user convenience. Output formats, verbosity,
        and documentation were greatly improved.
      * The package *note VirtualResolutions: (VirtualResolutions)Top, has been
        improved: a new strategy using a significantly faster algorithm has
        been added for the *note multigradedRegularity:
        (VirtualResolutions)multigradedRegularity, function.
      * The package *note NoetherianOperators: (NoetherianOperators)Top, has
        been improved: the *note DiffOp: (NoetherianOperators)DiffOp, type has
        been reworked, and support for Noetherian operators and differential
        primary decompositions of modules has been added.
      * Several packages (*note Chordal: (Chordal)Top,, *note Graphs:
        (Graphs)Top,, *note Markov: (Markov)Top,, and *note Posets:
        (Posets)Top,) that generate and display visualizations of mathematical
        objects using external image viewers have been modified so that they no
        longer require package-specific configuration of these viewers.
        Instead, *note show: show, is used, which opens the images using the
        system default viewer (using open on macOS and xdg-open on Linux).
  * functionality added:
      * A new type of real number, *note RRi: RRi, based on interval arithmetic
        has been added, based on the library mpfi, thanks to Michael Burr, with
        help from Anton Leykin.
      * The function *note tests: tests, has been added, for getting
        information about a package's tests.
      * A new type of list, *note AngleBarList: AngleBarList,, has been added,
        for use in forming free associative algebras. An instance can be
        created with the notation <|x,y,z|>.
      * The function *note assert: assert, now accepts an *note Expression:
        Expression, object as its argument. This provides more useful error
        messages for debugging, because they will contain the expression in
        unevaluated form, which might be something like d == 3.
      * In the function *note orbitRepresentatives:
        (MonomialOrbits)orbitRepresentatives, in the package *note
        MonomialOrbits: (MonomialOrbits)Top,, it is now possible to specify a
        subset of monomials from which the monomials that represent orbits are
        chosen, or from which the monomials that represent orbits are removed.
  * functionality removed
      * The type MatrixDegreeExpression has been removed.
      * The type ModuleMap has been removed.
