File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: changes_cm 1_pd17, Next: changes_cm 1_pd16, Prev: changes_cm 1_pd18, Up: changes to Macaulay2_cm by version

changes, 1.17
*************

  * functionality added:
      * The function *note importFrom: importFrom, has been added, for
        importing individual symbols from another package.
      * The function *note readPackage: readPackage, has been added, for
        retrieving the options in the preamble of a package quickly.
      * The function *note hooks: hooks, has been added, for retrieving the
        list of functions installed as hooks for handling computations of a
        specific type.
      * The function *note baseRing: baseRing, has been added, for retrieving
        the ring from which a ring was formed.
      * The functions *note findProgram: findProgram, and *note runProgram:
        runProgram, have been added, to provide a uniform way for packages to
        locate external programs. (The names and locations of such programs may
        vary from system to system.
      * The function *note formation: formation, has been added, for retrieving
        the way a module was formed, whether as a direct sum, tensor product,
        or Hom-module.
  * functionality improved:
      * The function *note capture: capture, is now used for generating most
        examples and tests.
      * The function *note installPackage: installPackage, accepts two new
        argument: *note installPackage(...,MakeHTML=>...): installPackage, and
        *note installPackage(...,MakePDF=>...): installPackage,. The PDF output
        will be improved in a future release.
      * The new optional argument name *note Keywords: Keywords, can now be
        used with packages to specify a list of key words (or phrases), useful
        for searching and organizing the packages by topic, as seen here: *note
        packages provided with Macaulay2: packages provided with Macaulay2,.
      * The functions *note addHook: addHook, and *note runHooks: runHooks,
        have been modified to accept a new syntax, allow giving names to hooks,
        and run specific hooks using the option Strategy. The symbol *note
        Default: Default, has been added for use as the name of hooks. The
        mutable hash table *note GlobalHookStore: addHook, has been added as a
        storage location for some hooks. For more information on *note using
        hooks: using hooks,, see that documentation node.
      * The functions *note code: code, is modified to also show the code for
        hooks listed by the function *note hooks: hooks,.
      * $\LaTeX$ typesetting for the web documentation is now rendered using
        $\KaTeX$ (see https://katex.org/ ), a JavaScript math typesetting
        library for browsers. As a result, $\LaTeX$ equations and matrices are
        rendered correctly. One notable change is that mathematical characters
        and equations now must be enclosed in \(...\), \[...\], $...$, or
        $$...$$ in order to be rendered. See *note html(TEX):
        (Text)html_lpTEX_rp, for more details and examples
      * The option *note Boxes: Boxes, of *note netList: netList, has been made
        more flexible to allow customization of the box; it now accepts as
        input a pair of lists of rows and columns.
      * A brief documentation of various types of objects can be viewed using
        *note ? Symbol: ? Symbol,.
      * The *note document: document, function now accepts three new options:
        *note Acknowledgement: Acknowledgement,, *note Contributors:
        Contributors,, and *note References: References,. The content of each
        will appear under a subsection of the same name in the documentation.
        Moreover, *note document(String): (SimpleDoc)doc, is now a synonym for
        *note doc(String): (SimpleDoc)doc,.
      * The *note regex: regex, function, as well as other functions that
        accept *note regular expressions: regular expressions,, have been
        rewritten to use the Perl regular expression syntax by default, which
        allows more fine-grained control of the matches. The *note POSIX:
        regex, extended flavor is still available as an option. The
        functionality is unchanged in almost all cases, except for regular
        expressions containing escaped special characters, where another
        backslash may be needed, and, in rare cases, where there are multiple
        options to match the regular expression. Internally, the new
        implementation incorporates the *note Boost.Regex: Boost, library.
  * new packages:
      * *note EagonResolution: (EagonResolution)Top,, a package by David
        Eisenbud and Mike Stillman for Eagon resolutions of residue fields, has
        been added.
      * *note EigenSolver: (EigenSolver)Top,, a package by Laurent Busé, Justin
        Chen, Kisun Lee, Anton Leykin, Tomas Pajdla, and Erika Pirnes for
        solving polynomial systems using eigen-computations, has been added.
      * *note GKMVarieties: (GKMVarieties)Top,, a package by Chris Eur and
        Ritvik Ramkumar for computations with GKM manifolds and moment graphs,
        has been added.
      * *note GraphicalModelsMLE: (GraphicalModelsMLE)Top,, a package by Carlos
        Amendola, Luis David Garcia Puente, Roser Homs Pons, Olga Kuznetsova,
        Harshit J Motwani, Elina Robeva, and David Swinarski, for maximum
        likelihood estimates for graphical statistical models, has been added.
      * *note Hadamard: (Hadamard)Top,, a package by Iman Bahmani Jafarloo for
        Hadamard products of projective subvarieties, has been added.
      * *note MonomialOrbits: (MonomialOrbits)Top,, a package by David Eisenbud
        and Mike Stillman for orbit representatives of monomial ideals, has
        been added.
      * *note MultiprojectiveVarieties: (MultiprojectiveVarieties)Top,, a
        package by Giovanni Staglianò for multi-projective varieties, has been
        added.
      * *note MultiplicitySequence: (MultiplicitySequence)Top,, a package by
        Justin Chen, Youngsu Kim, and Jonathan Montaño, for computing the
        multiplicity sequence of an ideal, has been added.
      * *note NoetherianOperators: (NoetherianOperators)Top,, a package by
        Robert Krone, Justin Chen, Marc Harkonen, Yairon Cid-Ruiz, and Anton
        Leykin, for numerically computing local dual spaces, Hilbert functions,
        and Noetherian operators, has been added. (The package NumericalHilbert
        has been absorbed into this new package.
      * *note NumericalLinearAlgebra: (NumericalLinearAlgebra)Top,, a package
        by Robert Krone, Marc Harkonen, and Anton Leykin for numerically
        compute local dual spaces and Hilbert functions, has been added.
      * *note RandomPoints: (RandomPoints)Top,, previously called
        RandomRationalPoints a package by Sankhaneel Bisui, Thai Nguyen, Karl
        Schwede, Sarasij Maitra, and Zhan Jiang, for computing a random point
        in a given variety over a finite field, has been added.
      * *note ResLengthThree: (ResLengthThree)Top,, a package by Lars Winther
        Christensen, Luigi Ferraro, Francesca Gandini, Frank Moore, and Oana
        Veliche, for multiplication in free resolutions of length three, has
        been added.
      * *note ResolutionsOfStanleyReisnerRings:
        (ResolutionsOfStanleyReisnerRings)Top,, a package by Ashleigh Adams for
        comparing resolutions of Stanley-Reisner rings and computing various
        systems of parameters, has been added.
      * *note Saturation: (Saturation)Top,, a package by Justin Chen, Mahrud
        Sayrafi, and Mike Stillman for computations involving quotients,
        saturations, and annihilators of modules and ideals, has been added.
        The package is preloaded, so the routines from this package will be
        used automatically. In particular, the new implementation supports
        caching of computations as well as new strategies, which can be listed
        using the *note hooks: hooks, function.
      * *note StatGraphs: (StatGraphs)Top,, a package by Carlos Amendola, Luis
        David Garcia Puente, Roser Homs Pons, Olga Kuznetsova, and Harshit J
        Motwani, for graphs used in algebraic statistics, has been added.
      * *note SwitchingFields: (SwitchingFields)Top,, a package by Zhan Jiang
        and Sarasij Maitra for switching base fields and obtaining natural
        maps, has been added.
  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note VirtualResolutions: (VirtualResolutions)Top,, a
        package by Ayah Almousa, Christine Berkesch, Juliette Bruce, David
        Eisenbud, Michael Loper, and Mahrud Sayrafi for virtual resolutions on
        products of projective spaces, has been published.
  * improved packages:
      * The *note doc(String): (SimpleDoc)doc, method from the *note SimpleDoc:
        (SimpleDoc)Top, package has been rewritten to support documenting
        multiple nodes at once. The following keywords were added: Node,
        Synopsis, Tree, Acknowledgement, Contributors, References, and
        SourceCode. Moreover, two new functions, *note arXiv: (SimpleDoc)arXiv,
        and *note stacksProject: (SimpleDoc)stacksProject, were added to help
        with referencing external documents.
      * The *note PrimaryDecomposition: (PrimaryDecomposition)Top, package has
        been improved to support computation of associated primes and primary
        decomposition of modules. In addition, partial computations in this
        package are now cached.
      * The *note MinimalPrimes: (MinimalPrimes)Top, package has been improved
        and the *note minimalPrimes: (MinimalPrimes)minimalPrimes, and *note
        isPrime(Ideal): (MinimalPrimes)isPrime_lpIdeal_rp, routines from that
        package are now used by default, deprecating the installMinprimes
        routine. A new routine *note radicalContainment:
        (MinimalPrimes)radicalContainment, has been added, and the function
        *note radical: (MinimalPrimes)radical, is moved to this package. In
        addition, partial computations in this package are now cached.
      * Version 2.0 of *note InvariantRing: (InvariantRing)Top, introduces
        types for different group actions as well as rings of invariants. It
        also contains new functionality for computing invariants of finite
        groups, diagonal actions (tori/abelian groups), and linearly reductive
        groups. The code from version 1.1.0 has been updated to work with the
        new types.
  * functionality changed:
      * The functions *note associatedPrimes:
        (PrimaryDecomposition)associatedPrimes,, *note topComponents:
        (PrimaryDecomposition)topComponents,, and *note removeLowestDimension:
        (PrimaryDecomposition)removeLowestDimension, have been moved to the
        package *note PrimaryDecomposition: (PrimaryDecomposition)Top,.
      * The destinations of the links at the tops of the web pages portraying
        documentation nodes in a package have been altered.  The links labeled
        next and previous have been interchanged with the links labelled
        forward and backward.  This was done to bring the terminology into
        agreement with that used in the info nodes portraying documentation
        nodes.  The result can be described as follows.  By virtue of the *note
        Subnodes: Subnodes, option, each node is provided with a certain number
        of subnodes, so the documentation as a whole may be regarded as an
        ordered union of rooted trees, with the top node of the package serving
        as the root of the first one. (Ideally it would be the only one.)  The
        next and previous links can be used to traverse the (sibling) subnodes
        of a given node, in sequence.  (The various roots are also regarded as
        siblings.)  The forward and backward links can be used to traverse all
        the nodes, in depth-first sequence.  Ideally, the documentation would
        be structured so such a traversal results in a readable document with
        topics presented in a logical sequence.
  * functionality changed in a way that could break code:
      * The variable backupFileRegexp has been replaced by the *note Exclude:
        Exclude, option to *note copyDirectory:
        copyDirectory_lpString_cmString_rp,.
      * The option *note installPackage(...,InstallPrefix=>...):
        installPackage, no longer accepts a function as input. only strings
        containing a path to the installation prefix are accepted.
      * The function localRing has been moved to the package *note LocalRings:
        (LocalRings)Top,.
  * functionality removed
      * The function removeHook has been removed.
      * The ForestNode and TreeNode types have been made internal.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

