File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: changes_cm 1_pd16, Next: changes_cm 1_pd15, Prev: changes_cm 1_pd17, Up: changes to Macaulay2_cm by version

changes, 1.16
*************

  * functionality added:
      * The location of Macaulay2's Emacs files has changed from site-lisp to
        site-lisp/Macaulay2, so users, after installing this version of
        Macaulay2, may once again need to run *note setupEmacs: setupEmacs, (or
        *note setup: setup,).
  * new packages:
      * *note SimplicialPosets: (SimplicialPosets)Top,, a package by Nathan
        Nichols for constructing Stanley simplicial poset rings, has been
        added.
      * *note SlackIdeals: (SlackIdeals)Top,, a package by Amy Wiebe and
        Antonio Macchia for slack ideals of polytopes and matroids, has been
        added.
      * *note PositivityToricBundles: (PositivityToricBundles)Top,, a package
        by Andreas Hochenegger for checking positivity of toric vector bundles,
        has been added.
      * *note SparseResultants: (SparseResultants)Top,, a package by Giovanni
        Staglianò for computations with sparse resultants, has been added.
      * *note DecomposableSparseSystems: (DecomposableSparseSystems)Top,, a
        package by Taylor Brysiewicz, Jose Israel Rodriguez, Frank Sottile, and
        Thomas Yahl for solving decomposable sparse systems, has been added.
      * *note MixedMultiplicity: (MixedMultiplicity)Top,, a package by Kriti
        Goel, Sudeshna Roy, and J. K. Verma for mixed multiplicities of ideals,
        has  been added.
      * *note ThreadedGB: (ThreadedGB)Top,, a package by Sonja Petrovic, Sara
        Jamshidi Zelenberg, and Tanner Zielinski for computing a Gröbner basis
        using the classical Buchberger algorithm with multiple threads, has
        been added.
      * *note PencilsOfQuadrics: (PencilsOfQuadrics)Top,, a package by
        Frank-Olaf Schreyer, David Eisenbud, and Yeongrak Kim for Clifford
        algebras of pencils of quadratic forms, has been added.
      * *note VectorGraphics: (VectorGraphics)Top,, a package by Paul
        Zinn-Justin for producing scalable vector graphics, has been added.
  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note DeterminantalRepresentations:
        (DeterminantalRepresentations)Top,, a package by Justin Chen and Papri
        Dey for computing determinantal representations, has been published.
      * a gold star *note Seminormalization: (Seminormalization)Top,, a package
        by Karl Schwede and Bernard Serbinowski for computing seminormalization
        of rings, has been published.
      * a gold star *note SumsOfSquares: (SumsOfSquares)Top,, a package by
        Diego Cifuentes, Thomas Kahle, Pablo A. Parrilo, and Helfried Peyrl for
        sums of squares, has been published.
  * functionality added:
      * The function *note installPackage: installPackage, now returns, as its
        value, the package that was installed. This makes it more convenient to
        both install and check a package, because one can type check
        installPackage "FOO".
      * The *note roots: roots_lpRingElement_rp, command is now handled by the
        *note MPSolve: MPSolve, library, and is more robust, but no longer
        takes an optional argument Unique.
      * The *note Complexes: (Complexes)Top, package has new data types and
        routines for homological algebra. Eventually, it will replace the
        current facilities for homological algebra. We are making this
        available in order to get feedback from users before making this
        change.  Please email the authors with any and all comments or
        suggestions.
  * functionality improved
      * The PARI library has been removed.  Its functionality has been subsumed
        by the *note MPSolve: MPSolve, library (for the *note roots:
        roots_lpRingElement_rp, function for finding roots of a univariate
        polynomial), and the *note FLINT: FLINT, library, for integer
        factorization and primality testing.
      * The *note Boost.Stacktrace: Boost, library has been added for printing
        stack traces in case of a crash.
      * Primality testing, provided by *note isPrime: isPrime,, is now handled
        by the *note FLINT: FLINT, library.
      * Probable prime testing, provided by *note isPseudoprime:
        isPseudoprime_lpZZ_rp,, is now handled by the *note FLINT: FLINT,
        library.
      * Factorization of integers, provided by *note factor(ZZ):
        factor_lpRingElement_rp,, is now handled by the *note FLINT: FLINT,
        library.
      * The *note FLINT: FLINT, library, and several others, no longer need to
        be patched while building Macaulay2. This involved a reorganization of
        the way memory management is done in the engine and the interpreter. As
        a result, we can use versions of several basic libraries as provided by
        the operating system, including *note GNU MP: GNU MP,,MPIR,*note MPFR:
        MPFR,, and the *note NTL library: NTL library,.
      * The *note CompleteIntersectionResolutions:
        (CompleteIntersectionResolutions)Top, package now has an implementation
        of the dual of the (infinite) Tate resolution of any module over a
        complete intersection $R$ as a finitely generated module over
        $R[t_1..t_c]$, the ring of Eisenbud operators.  As a byproduct, this
        gives another method for computing the global $Ext_R(M,N)$.  Also
        implemented layered resolutions (in the sense of Eisenbud-Peeva) of
        Cohen-Macaulay modules over $R$.
      * The *note ReesAlgebra: (ReesAlgebra)Top, has new functionality, with
        the defaults changed to make the computation faster.
