File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: changes_cm 1_pd13, Next: changes_cm 1_pd12, Prev: changes_cm 1_pd14, Up: changes to Macaulay2_cm by version

changes, 1.13
*************

  * functionality changed in a way that could break code:
      * Various packages have been preloaded for convenience when starting
        Macaulay2, but now they are no longer visible by default inside the
        source code of a package.  Developers of packages should add the names
        of the needed preloaded packages to the value of the *note
        newPackage(...,PackageImports=>...): newPackage, or *note
        newPackage(...,PackageExports=>...): newPackage, option, to ensure that
        needed definitions are visible.
      * the Schubert2 functions projectiveSpace and projectiveSpace'have been
        renamed *note abstractProjectiveSpace:
        (Schubert2)abstractProjectiveSpace,  and *note
        abstractProjectiveSpace': (Schubert2)abstractProjectiveSpace',.  The
        reason is that there were name conflicts with the *note
        NormalToricVarieties: (NormalToricVarieties)Top, package. Since PP is
        no longer protected, you may put PP = abstractProjectiveSpace in your
        init file and then use something like X = PP 4, although PP^4 will no
        longer work.
      * The deprecated old-style block comment syntax has been disabled.  Now
        one types -* COMMENT *- instead of {* COMMENT *}.
  * new packages:
      * *note Truncations: (Truncations)Top,, a package by David Eisenbud and
        Mike Stillman for truncating modules, has been added. It implements a
        better notion of truncation of a multigraded module.  Some bugs in the
        old function have been fixed. The function *note truncate(List,Module):
        (Truncations)truncate_lpList_cmModule_rp, has been made functorial, but
        it no longer allows partial degrees to be given.
      * *note FrobeniusThresholds: (FrobeniusThresholds)Top,, a package by Erin
        Bela, Alberto F. Boix, Juliette Bruce, Drew Ellingson, Daniel
        Hernandez, Zhibek Kadyrsizova, Moty Katzman, Sara Malec, Matthew
        Mastroeni, Maral Mostafazadehfard, Marcus Robinson, Karl Schwede, Dan
        Smolkin, Pedro Teixeira and Emily Witt for calculation of Frobenius
        thresholds, has been added.
      * *note ToricInvariants: (ToricInvariants)Top,, a package by Martin
        Helmer for computing Euclidean distance degrees, polar degrees, degree
        and codimension of the dual, and Chern-Mather classes of toric
        varieties, has been added.
      * *note SegreClasses: (SegreClasses)Top,, a package by Martin Helmer and
        Corey Harris for testing containment of varieties and computing
        algebraic multiplicity of subvarieties and Fulton-MacPherson
        intersection products, has been added.
      * *note SemidefiniteProgramming: (SemidefiniteProgramming)Top,, a package
        by Diego Cifuentes, Thomas Kahle, Pablo A. Parrilo, and Helfried Peyrl
        for semidefinite programming, has been added.
      * *note SumsOfSquares: (SumsOfSquares)Top,, a package by Diego Cifuentes,
        Thomas Kahle, Pablo A. Parrilo, and Helfried Peyrl for sums of squares,
        has been added.
      * *note MultiGradedRationalMap: (MultiGradedRationalMap)Top,, a package
        by Yairon Cid Ruiz for computing the degree and birationality of
        multigraded rational maps, has been added.
  * improved packages:
      * *note CompleteIntersectionResolutions:
        (CompleteIntersectionResolutions)Top, now has a full implementation of
        the Eisenbud-Shamash resolution, and using *note MCMApproximations:
        (MCMApproximations)Top,, now can compute the layered resolution of any
        Cohen-Macaulay module, not just a high syzygy.
  * new constants and operators:
      * The type *note Describe: Describe,, *note MapExpression:
        MapExpression,, MatrixDegreeExpression, SheafExpression, and *note
        VectorExpression: VectorExpression, have been added.
      * The top level mode *note WebApp: WebApp, has been added.
      * The function htmlWithTex has been added.
      * The function *note polarize: polarize, has been added.
