File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: changes_cm 1_pd12, Next: changes_cm 1_pd11, Prev: changes_cm 1_pd13, Up: changes to Macaulay2_cm by version

changes, 1.12
*************

  * new packages:
      * *note Seminormalization: (Seminormalization)Top,, a package by Bernard
        Serbinowski and Karl Schwede for computing seminormalization of rings,
        has been added.
      * *note CoincidentRootLoci: (CoincidentRootLoci)Top,, a package by M. C.
        Brambilla and G. Staglianò for computations with coincident root loci,
        has been added.
      * *note RelativeCanonicalResolution: (RelativeCanonicalResolution)Top,, a
        package by Christian Bopp and Michael Hoff for computation of the
        relative canonical resolution for g-nodal canonical curves with a fixed
        $g^1_k$, has been added.
      * *note RandomCurvesOverVerySmallFiniteFields:
        (RandomCurvesOverVerySmallFiniteFields)Top,, a package by Christian
        Bopp and Frank-Olaf Schreyer for computation of general canonical
        curves of genus $\le 15$ over fields with small characteristic, has
        been added.
      * *note StronglyStableIdeals: (StronglyStableIdeals)Top,, a package by
        Davide Alberelli and Paolo Lella for studying strongly stable ideals
        related to Hilbert polynomials, has been added.
      * *note SLnEquivariantMatrices: (SLnEquivariantMatrices)Top,, a package
        by Ada Boralevi, Daniele Faenzi and Paolo Lella for computations
        related to the paper "A construction of equivariant bundles on the
        space of symmetric forms", has been added.
      * *note CorrespondenceScrolls: (CorrespondenceScrolls)Top,, a package by
        David Eisenbud, Frank-Olaf Schreyer, and Alessio Sammartano, to compute
        and analyze examples of correspondence scrolls, has been added.
      * *note NCAlgebra: (NCAlgebra)Top,, a package by Frank Moore, Andrew
        Conner, and Courtney Gibbons, implementing data types for
        noncommutative algebras, has been added.
      * *note SpaceCurves: (SpaceCurves)Top,, a package by Frank Schreyer, Mike
        Stillman, and Mengyuan Zhang, for generation of space curves, has been
        added.
      * *note ExteriorIdeals: (ExteriorIdeals)Top,, a package by Marilena Crupi
        and Luca Amata for manipulating monomial ideals over exterior algebras,
        has been added.
  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note Resultants: (Resultants)Top,, a package by Giovanni
        Staglianò for resultants and discriminants for multivariate
        polynomials, has been published.
      * a gold star *note SpaceCurves: (SpaceCurves)Top,, a package by Frank
        Schreyer, Mike Stillman, and Mengyuan Zhang, for generation of space
        curves, has been published.
      * a gold star *note ReesAlgebra: (ReesAlgebra)Top,, a package by David
        Eisenbud, Amelia Taylor, and Sorin Popescu for computations with Rees
        algebras, has been published.
      * a gold star *note Cremona: (Cremona)Top,, a package by Giovanni
        Staglianò for computations for rational maps between projective
        varieties, has been published.
      * a gold star *note ExteriorIdeals: (ExteriorIdeals)Top,, a package by
        Marilena Crupi and Luca Amata for manipulating monomial ideals over
        exterior algebras, has been published.
  * improved packages:
      * The package *note VersalDeformations: (VersalDeformations)Top, has had
        a bug fixed.  The lifting algorithm would give an error or incorrect
        output if the tangent cone for the obstruction equations wasn't
        generated by the lowest order terms of the obstruction equations. This
        has been remedied by actually calculating the tangent cone, and making
        appropriate adjustments to the algorithm.
      * The package *note TateOnProducts: (TateOnProducts)Top, has been
        improved.  The package implements the method of Tate resolutions, for
        computing cohomology of sheaves on products of projective spaces, and
        also the pushforward complex of a sheaf under a map from a variety to a
        projective space. Tate resolutions on single projective spaces were
        treated in the package *note BGG: (BGG)Top,, but the case of a product
        of projective spaces is much more subtle, since no term of the full
        Tate resolution is finitely generated.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * The function *note about: about, has been added.  It allows one to
        search the documentation of all the packages that have been installed,
        optionally searching the contents, in addition to the keys. For
        example, the command help about X will display all the documentation
        about X.
      * The class *note NumberedVerticalList: NumberedVerticalList, has been
        added.  It's a new type of vertical list (see *note VerticalList:
        VerticalList,) that is also printed vertically, but with numbered
        entries, for ease of referring to them.
      * The option AbsoluteLinks to *note installPackage: installPackage, has
        been removed.  Better logic is now used internally, producing relative
        links only between files installed under the same prefix.
      * The layout of files into directories used by *note installPackage:
        installPackage, has been simplified, so it may be a good idea to
        reinstall any packages you have installed.  See *note Layout:
        currentLayout,.
      * Each directory listed in *note prefixPath: prefixPath, now has its own
        layout, which is detected at runtime. See *note Layout: currentLayout,.
      * Functionality for fast nonminimal free resolutions, *note
        FastNonminimal: (OldChainComplexes)FastNonminimal, has a number of bug
        fixes and improvements: (1) it now works for input modules, not just
        ideals (there was a monomial order mismatch which would often cause it
        to fail), (2) multigraded and inhomogeneous ideals/modules are allowed,
        (3) this function works over the exterior algebra as well (it has
        always done so, but that was not always realized), (4) it is possible
        to have M2 use an already created Gröbner basis, instead of recomputing
        one.  Use Strategy=>5 in the *note resolution:
        (OldChainComplexes)resolution, command, to tell the command that the
        provided ideal has generators which already form a Gröbner basis, not
        necessarily a reduced Gröbner basis, or a quotient module, whose
        presentation matrix forms a Gröbner basis. If the input is not, then
        this function can give incorrect answers or fail.  See *note
        FastNonminimal: (OldChainComplexes)FastNonminimal, for details and
        examples.
      * New types *note MethodFunctionSingle: MethodFunctionSingle, and *note
        MethodFunctionBinary: MethodFunctionBinary, were introduced to serve as
        classes of method functions with a single argument, such as *note code:
        code,, and of associative method functions based on methods with two
        arguments, such as *note gcd: gcd,, from other compiled functions.
      * We have removed the feature where typing an extra empty line ends
        multiline input in a terminal window or Emacs buffer. This will make it
        easier to feed input from a file into the interpreter with F-11 and
        encounter the same behavior, since in files we have permit empty lines.
        This change was requested at our Leipzig workshop, with Q2 at
        https://github.com/Macaulay2/Workshop-2018-Leipzig/wiki/Q&A-Thursday
        (see https://github.com/Macaulay2/Workshop-2018-Leipzig/wiki/Q&amp;A-
        Thursday ) being the question that prompted the discussion.
  * commits, issues, and pull requests on github
      * See closed 1.12 issues (see
        https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/issues?q=milestone%3A%22version+1.12%22
        +is%3Aclosed ), for the issues and pull requests incorporated into
        1.12.
      * See 1.12 commits (see https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/commits/release-
        1.12 ) for complete information about all changes to the code
        incorporated into 1.12.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

