changes, 1.10
*************

  * new packages:
      * *note SpectralSequences: (SpectralSequences)Top,, a package by Adam
        Boocher, Nathan Grieve, Eloisa Grifo, Gregory G. Smith, and Thanh Vu
        for spectral sequences, has been added.
      * *note SectionRing: (SectionRing)Top,, a package by Andrew Bydlon for
        computing the section ring of a Weil Divisor., has been added.
      * *note K3Carpets: (K3Carpets)Top,, a package by David Eisenbud,
        Frank-Olaf Schreyer for K3 double structure on scrolls, has been added.
      * *note ChainComplexOperations: (ChainComplexOperations)Top,, a package
        by David Eisenbud for sym2, wedge2, chi2 of a ChainComplex, has been
        added.
      * *note NumericalCertification: (NumericalCertification)Top,, a package
        by Kisun Lee for testing NumericalAlgebraicGeometry, has been added.
      * *note PhylogeneticTrees: (PhylogeneticTrees)Top,, a package by
        Nathaniel Bushek, Ruth Davidson, Elizabeth Gross, Pamela Harris, Robert
        Krone, Colby Long, AJ Stewart, Robert Walker, and Robert Walker for
        invariants for group-based phylogenetic models, has been added.
      * *note MonodromySolver: (MonodromySolver)Top,, a package by Cvetelina
        Hill, Anders Nedergaard Jensen, Kisun Lee, Anton Leykin, and Jeff
        Sommars for solving polynomial systems via monodromy, has been added.
      * *note ReactionNetworks: (ReactionNetworks)Top,, a package by Timothy
        Duff, Kisun Lee, and Anton Leykin for reaction networks, has been
        added.
      * *note PackageCitations: (PackageCitations)Top,, a package by Aaron Dall
        for citation of Macaulay2 packages, has been added.
      * *note NumericSolutions: (NumericSolutions)Top,, a package by Corrado
        Possieri, and Antonio Tornambe for solving systems of polynomial
        equalities, has been added.
      * *note GradedLieAlgebras: (GradedLieAlgebras)Top,, a package by Clas
        Löfwall and Samuel Lundqvist for computations in graded Lie algebras,
        has been added.
      * *note InverseSystems: (InverseSystems)Top,, a package by David Eisenbud
        for equivariant Macaulay inverse systems, has been added.
      * *note Pullback: (Pullback)Top,, a package by Drew Ellingson and Karl
        Schwede for pullback of rings, has been added.
      * *note EngineTests: (EngineTests)Top,, a package by Michael E. Stillman
        and Jakob Kroeker for a test suite for the Macaulay2 engine, has been
        added.
      * *note SVDComplexes: (SVDComplexes)Top,, a package by Frank Schreyer and
        Mike Stillman for SVD of a complex, including nonminimal resolutions
        over the reals, has been added.
      * *note RandomComplexes: (RandomComplexes)Top,, a package by Frank
        Schreyer and Mike Stillman for random complexes over fields or the
        integers, has been added.
  * improved packages:
      * *note Polyhedra: (Polyhedra)Top, has been rewritten by Lars Kastner for
        improved performance.  Many bugs have been fixed, and there are now a
        large number of tests. Some changes are not backward compatible.  Some
        changes include:
          * *note Fan: (Polyhedra)Fan,, is no longer a collection of Cone
            objects, but contains a matrix of rays (over ZZ), and a list of
            lists of integer indices, indicating the maximal cones.
            Well-defined-ness is no longer automatically checked.  Use *note
            isWellDefined(Fan): (Polyhedra)isWellDefined_lpCone_rp,
          * *note Polyhedron: (Polyhedra)Polyhedron,, is now a wrapper for the
            homogenized cone.
          * *note PolyhedralComplex: (Polyhedra)PolyhedralComplex,, is now a
            wrapper for the homogenized fan.
          * *note Cone: (Polyhedra)Cone,, has basically the same functionality,
            except that not everything is computed ahead of time.
          * *note faces: (Polyhedra)faces,, now returns a list of lists of
            integer indices.  There are two new functions for recovering the
            old behavior: *note facesAsCones: (Polyhedra)facesAsCones, (for
            fans and cones), and  *note facesAsPolyhedra:
            (Polyhedra)facesAsPolyhedra, for polyhedra and polyhedral
            complexes.
        An important difference is that objects of these classes can no longer
        be used as keys into hash tables, since these objects are implemented
        as mutable hash tables. In particular *note ===: ===, no longer works
        on cones.  Instead, use a sorted list of e.g. vertices and lineality
        space.

        If you need the old behavior, load the package OldPolyhedra. However,
        if possible, change your code to run with the new package.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * The functions *note toDual: (InverseSystems)toDual, and *note fromDual:
        (InverseSystems)fromDual, have been improved and moved to the new
        package *note InverseSystems: (InverseSystems)Top,: they are now
        compatible with linear changes of coordinates.
  * new constants and operators:
      * The function *note QRDecomposition: QRDecomposition, has been added.
      * The function *note isFinitePrimeField: isFinitePrimeField, has been
        added.
      * The function *note isWeylAlgebra: Weyl algebras, has been added.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

