changes, 1.9.1
**************

  * new packages:
      * *note ResidualIntersections: (ResidualIntersections)Top,, a package by
        Katie Ansaldi, David Eisenbud, Robert Krone, and Jay Yang, for studying
        conditions associated to residual intersection theory, has been added.
      * *note Visualize: (Visualize)Top,, a package by Brett Barwick, Thomas
        Enkosky, Branden Stone, and Jim Vallandingham, to help visualize
        algebraic objects in the browser using javascript, has been added.
      * *note EquivariantGB: (EquivariantGB)Top,, a package by Chris Hillar,
        Robert Krone, and Anton Leykin for equivariant Gröbner bases and
        related algorithms, has been added.
      * *note ExampleSystems: (ExampleSystems)Top,, a package by Anton Leykin
        for examples of polynomial systems in numerical algebraic geometry, has
        been added.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * The new function *note minimalBetti: minimalBetti, finds minimal Betti
        numbers of an ideal or module using the new *note FastNonminimal:
        (OldChainComplexes)FastNonminimal, functionality, avoiding unneeded
        computation of matrices in the free resolution.
      * The new function *note roots: roots_lpRingElement_rp,, provided by
        Guillem Blanco, finds roots of univariate polynomials numerically.
      * the new function *note splitWWW: splitWWW, takes an http response, e.g.
        from *note getWWW: getWWW, and unpacks it into the header, and the
        body.  Additionally, if the response indicates that this is a chunked
        response, then the body is unchunked (should be considered a bug fix
        from previous functionality).
  * functionality changed:
      * Some linear algebra functions, including *note LUdecomposition:
        LUdecomposition,, *note solve: solve,, *note nullSpace: nullSpace,, and
        *note columnRankProfile: columnRankProfile,,  when presented with
        matrices over *note ZZ: ZZ, would previously give occasional
        nonsensical answers.  These functions have been disabled for matrices
        over *note ZZ: ZZ,.  However, *note solve: solve, uses Gröbner basis
        methods to solve a linear system, so did not suffer this problem.
        Caveat: using these functions with a ring that is not a field, even if
        it runs, might give a nonsensical answer. This will be cleaned up in a
        later version.
