changes, 1.9
************

  * major improvements and additions:
      * Fast minimal betti number and non-minimal resolution code, for
        homogeneous ideals and modules over polynomial rings over finite prime
        fields.  Also is functional for ideals and modules over exterior
        algebras.  See *note FastNonminimal: (OldChainComplexes)FastNonminimal,
        and *note betti(...,Minimize=>...):
        (OldChainComplexes)betti_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmMinimize=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,.  For
        computing minimal betti numbers, on larger examples, this code is often
        hundreds to thousands of times faster than standard use of *note
        resolution: (Complexes)freeResolution, and is also, in many cases, much
        faster than the similar code in Singular version 4.0.2 described in
        Erocal, Motsak, Schreyer, Steenpass, Refined Algorithms to compute
        syzygies, arxiv 1502.01654.  A paper describing our algorithm and
        implementation is forthcoming.
  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note HighestWeights: (HighestWeights)Top,, a package by
        Federico Galetto for decomposing free resolutions and graded modules
        with a semisimple Lie group action, has been published.
      * a gold star *note Posets: (Posets)Top,, a package by David Cook II,
        Sonja Mapes, and Gwyn Whieldon, for processing partially ordered sets,
        has been published.
      * a gold star *note MultiplierIdeals: (MultiplierIdeals)Top,, a package
        by Zach Teitler for computing multiplier ideals of monomial ideals, has
        been published.
      * a gold star *note CharacteristicClasses: (CharacteristicClasses)Top,, a
        package by Christine Jost and Martin Helmer for computing
        characteristic classes on toric varieties, has been published.
  * new packages:
      * *note MCMApproximations: (MCMApproximations)Top,, a package by David
        Eisenbud for maximal Cohen-Macaulay approximations and complete
        intersections, has been added.
      * *note MultiplierIdealsDim2: (MultiplierIdealsDim2)Top,, a package by
        Ferran Dachs-Cadefau for computing multiplier ideals in 2-dimensional
        rings, has been added.
      * *note RunExternalM2: (RunExternalM2)Top,, a package by Brian Pike for
        running Macaulay2 functions outside the current Macaulay2 process, has
        been added.
      * *note SLPexpressions: (SLPexpressions)Top,, a package by Anton Leykin
        for straight line programs and algebraic circuits, has been added.
      * *note NumericalSchubertCalculus: (NumericalSchubertCalculus)Top,, a
        package by Anton Leykin, Abraham Martin del Campo, and Jan Verschelde,
        for numerical methods in Schubert Calculus, has been added.
      * *note ToricTopology: (ToricTopology)Top,, a package by Alvise Trevisan
        and Alexander I. Suciu for toric topology, has been added.
      * *note Cremona: (Cremona)Top,, a package by Giovanni Staglianò for
        rational maps between projective varieties, has been added.
      * *note Resultants: (Resultants)Top,, a package by Giovanni Staglianò for
        resultants and discriminants for multivariate polynomials, has been
        added (originally called MultipolynomialResultants).
      * *note VectorFields: (VectorFields)Top,, a package by Brian Pike for
        vector fields, has been added.
      * *note RandomIdeals: (RandomIdeals)Top,, a package by David Eisenbud for
        creating random ideals of various sorts, has been added.
      * *note Miura: (Miura)Top,, a package by Joe Suzuki for divisor class
        groups on curves, has been added.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * The new function *note installedPackages: installedPackages, returns a
        list of names of packages installed by the user with *note
        installPackage: installPackage,.
      * The new function *note uninstallAllPackages: uninstallAllPackages,
        uninstalls all the packages installed by the user with *note
        installPackage: installPackage,.
  * useful functions involving prime numbers, submitted by Frank Schreyer:
      * *note nextPrime: nextPrime,, a simple function to find the first prime
        number at least as large as a given number
      * *note getPrimeWithRootOfUnity: getPrimeWithRootOfUnity,, used to find a
        prime number p s.t. ZZ/p contains a n-th root of unity
      * *note randomKRationalPoint: randomKRationalPoint,, a function to find a
        random rational point on a variety over a finite field
