File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: changes_cm 1_pd6, Next: changes_cm 1_pd5, Prev: changes_cm 1_pd7, Up: changes to Macaulay2_cm by version

changes, 1.6
************

  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note VersalDeformations: (VersalDeformations)Top,, a
        package for calculating tangent and obstruction spaces as well as power
        series solutions for deformation problems involving isolated
        singularities and projective schemes, has been published.
      * a gold star *note KustinMiller: (KustinMiller)Top,, a package for
        unprojection and the Kustin-Miller complex, has been published.
  * new packages:
      * *note PushForward: (PushForward)Top,, a package for computing the
        push-forward functor for finite ring maps, has been added.  (It should
        have been added to the previous distribution.)
      * *note EliminationMatrices: (EliminationMatrices)Top,, a package for
        computing resultants, has been added.
      * *note EllipticIntegrals: (EllipticIntegrals)Top,, a package for
        numerical computation of elliptic integrals and elliptic functions, has
        been added.
      * *note Triplets: (Triplets)Top,, a package for computing Betti diagrams
        and hypercohomology tables associated to triplets of degree sequences,
        has been added.
      * *note CompleteIntersectionResolutions:
        (CompleteIntersectionResolutions)Top,, a package for analyzing the
        asymptotic structure of minimal resolutions over a complete
        intersection, has been added.
  * improved packages:
      * The package *note GraphicalModels: (GraphicalModels)Top, has been
        extended significantly by its authors. The previous version of this
        package was simply a basic extension of the package *note Markov:
        (Markov)Top,. Among the new algorithms implemented are procedures for
        computing the vanishing ideal of a graphical model and for checking for
        identifiable parameters in Gaussian mixed graph models. These
        procedures can be used to study fundamental problems about graphical
        models.
      * The package *note Schubert2: (Schubert2)Top, now handles intersection
        rings of isotropic flag bundles, with an algorithm based on a theorem
        in a paper of Grayson, Seceleanu, and Stillman.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * Factoring of polynomials over non-prime Galois fields has been added,
        using the *note Singular-Factory: Singular-Factory, library.
      * The methods for *note Hom(Matrix,Module): Hom_lpModule_cmMatrix_rp, and
        *note Hom(Module,Matrix): Hom_lpModule_cmMatrix_rp, now handle non-free
        modules. There is also a new method for *note Hom(Matrix,Matrix):
        Hom_lpModule_cmMatrix_rp,.
  * functionality changed:
      * changed the order of loading packages inside a package, as specified by
        *note newPackage(...,PackageImports=>...): newPackage, and *note
        newPackage(...,PackageExports=>...): newPackage, options, so that the
        order of loading is easy to specify (to avoid problems with shadowed
        variables).  The packages are loaded with *note needsPackage:
        needsPackage,, and now the imported packages are loaded before the
        exported packages.  So, if there is a problem, just replicate all the
        exported packages in the list of imports, and juggle the order of the
        list of imports.
      * The function *note temporaryFileName: temporaryFileName, now obeys the
        TMPDIR environment variable, the way other unix applications do, rather
        than putting temporary files into the directory /tmp.
  * new constants and operators:
      * New functions *note fileReadable: fileReadable,, *note fileWritable:
        fileWritable,, *note fileExecutable: fileExecutable, provide
        information about file permissions.
      * The class *note Task: Task, replaces Thread, and the function *note
        isCanceled: isCanceled_lpTask_rp, tells whether a task has been
        canceled.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

