File: Macaulay2Doc.info, Node: changes_cm 1_pd5, Next: changes_cm 1_pd4, Prev: changes_cm 1_pd6, Up: changes to Macaulay2_cm by version

changes, 1.5
************

  * major improvements and additions:
      * A facility for scheduling tasks to be performed in parallel (in
        threads) has been developed. See *note parallel programming with
        threads and tasks: parallel programming with threads and tasks,.
  * packages that have been published and certified:
      * a gold star *note Nauty: (Nauty)Top,, a package for an interface to the
        program nauty, which provides efficient methods for determining whether
        graphs are isomorphic, generating all graphs with particular
        properties, generating random graphs, and more, has been published.
      * a gold star *note NumericalAlgebraicGeometry:
        (NumericalAlgebraicGeometry)Top,, a package for using polynomial
        homotopy continuation to solve systems of polynomial equations and
        describing positive-dimensional complex algebraic varieties, has been
        published.
      * a gold star *note Binomials: (Binomials)Top,, a package for binomial
        ideals with a particular focus on intersection decompositions and
        associated primes, has been published.
  * new packages:
      * *note BIBasis: (BIBasis)Top,, a package for constructing reduced
        Pommaret and Gröbner bases in a Boolean ring, has been added.
      * *note CharacteristicClasses: (CharacteristicClasses)Top,, a package for
        degrees of Chern classes and other characteristic classes of projective
        schemes, has been added.
      * *note KustinMiller: (KustinMiller)Top,, a package for unprojection and
        the Kustin-Miller complex construction, has been added.
      * *note MonomialAlgebras: (MonomialAlgebras)Top,, a package for
        decomposing a monomial algebra as a module over a subalgebra, has been
        added.
      * *note MultiplierIdeals: (MultiplierIdeals)Top,, a package for computing
        multiplier ideals of monomial ideals, has been added (originally called
        MonomialMultiplierIdeals).
      * *note NautyGraphs: (NautyGraphs)Top,, a package for an interface to
        nauty (Graphs fork), has been added.
      * *note QthPower: (QthPower)Top,, a package for computing the integral
        closure of type I affine domains, has been added.
      * *note RandomObjects: (RandomObjects)Top,, *note RandomCanonicalCurves:
        (RandomCanonicalCurves)Top,, *note RandomCurves: (RandomCurves)Top,,
        *note RandomGenus14Curves: (RandomGenus14Curves)Top,, *note
        RandomPlaneCurves: (RandomPlaneCurves)Top,, and *note
        RandomSpaceCurves: (RandomSpaceCurves)Top,, packages for the
        construction of random points of unirational moduli spaces, have been
        added.
      * *note TensorComplexes: (TensorComplexes)Top,, a package for multilinear
        algebra for the construction of tensor complexes, has been added.
      * *note Units: (Units)Top,, a package for conversion of units of measure,
        has been added.
      * *note VersalDeformations: (VersalDeformations)Top,, a package for
        calculating versal deformations and local Hilbert schemes, has been
        added.
  * functionality added or improved:
      * The function *note temporaryFileName: temporaryFileName, now produces
        file names with no chance of collision, and deletes the files upon
        normal termination of the program.
      * The function *note newPackage: newPackage, now has two new options,
        *note newPackage(...,PackageExports=>...): newPackage, and *note
        newPackage(...,PackageImports=>...): newPackage,, which provide a more
        robust way to specify that other packages should be loaded when this
        new package is loaded.
      * The new functions *note limitFiles: limitFiles, and *note
        limitProcesses: limitProcesses, can be used to impose resource limits
        on the current process.
  * functionality changed:
      * Now F = GF p will return a ring of type *note GaloisField: GaloisField,
        when p is prime, instead of returning the quotient ring ZZ/p.  In
        particular, the generator F_0 will be a generator of the multiplicative
        group.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

