changes, 1.2
************

  * major improvements and additions:
      * Improved old documentation and added many new descriptions of
        functions.
      * Greatly improved the debugger. In particular, the debugger will put you
        directly onto the line of the program with an error, and allows the
        user to execute a given number of steps of the program (see *note step:
        step,) and to conveniently display and change values of variables as
        they evolve.
      * Improved the making of packages: made it much easier for a user to
        create a complete package, including documentation.
      * Improved the handling of symmetric algebras and Rees algebras; improved
        implementation of things like analytic spread.
      * Improved handling of finite fields: *note GF: GF, now uses *note Conway
        polynomials: (ConwayPolynomials)Top, when possible. Maps between Galois
        fields made with them are now easy to produce with map(E,F).  (Note:
        actually, the user must load the package manually.)
      * The function *note hilbertFunction: hilbertFunction, is now faster at
        computing power series expansions.
      * Homomorphisms (maps) of modules over different rings with respect to a
        ring homomorphism between them are now supported.  Composition, coimage
        (replacing pushForward1), and kernel work. An option has been added to
        *note basis: basis, to ask it to return such a homomorphism.  See *note
        map(Module,Module,RingMap,Matrix):
        map_lpModule_cmModule_cmRingMap_cmMatrix_rp,, *note
        map(Module,Nothing,RingMap,Matrix):
        map_lpModule_cmModule_cmRingMap_cmMatrix_rp,, and *note
        map(Module,RingMap): map_lpModule_cmModule_cmRingMap_cmMatrix_rp,.
      * The total Ext functor now accepts multigraded modules, see *note
        Ext(Module,Module): Ext_lpModule_cmModule_rp,.
      * Macaulay2 now incorporates PARI (see http://pari.math.u-bordeaux.fr/ ),
        a free library for computing in number theory. It is used by *note
        factor(ZZ): factor_lpRingElement_rp,, *note factor(QQ):
        factor_lpRingElement_rp,, *note isPseudoprime(ZZ):
        isPseudoprime_lpZZ_rp,, and *note isPrime(ZZ): isPrime,.
      * new packages, included:
          * *note BGG: (BGG)Top, -- Bernstein-Gelfand-Gelfand correspondence
          * *note BoijSoederberg: (BoijSoederberg)Top, -- Betti diagram
            operations useful for investigating the Boij-Soederberg conjectures
          * *note Bruns: (Bruns)Top, -- make a 3-generator ideal with an "any"
            resolution
          * *note ConwayPolynomials: (ConwayPolynomials)Top, -- a database of
            Conway polynomials
          * *note EdgeIdeals: (EdgeIdeals)Top, -- edge ideals
          * *note FourTiTwo: (FourTiTwo)Top, -- Interface to 4ti2
          * *note gfanInterface: (gfanInterface)Top, -- interface to Anders
