replacements for commands and scripts from Macaulay
***************************************************

Macaulay2 aims to provide all of the functionality of Macaulay, but the names
of the functions are not the same, and there are other differences.  One major
difference is the introduction of the notion of module, whereas in Macaulay,
the pervasive concept was the matrix.


Here is a list of old Macaulay functions, together with pointers to functions
in Macaulay2 that might be used to replace them.


